#description=Data from https://www.sanskrit-lexicon.uni-koeln.de/ as on 2026-06-01

a
A. As an indefinite article before nouns singular, for the<BR>most part not expressed in Sanskrit; as, ‘a lion,’ सिंहः;<BR>(One) एकः -का -कं.<BR>— (Some, a certain) कश्चित्; as, ‘a certain<BR>man,’ कश्चित् पुरुषः.<BR>— (Each, every) expressed by प्रति or अनु,<BR>before the acc. neut.; as, ‘a day,’ ‘each day,’ प्रतिदिनं or<BR>अनुदिनं. When ‘a’ comes before a participle, after a<BR>verb of motion, it is expressed by the dat. c.; as, ‘he went<BR>a hunting,’ मृगयायै गतः; or by अर्थं preceded by the crude<BR>form of a noun; as, मृगयार्थं गतः; or by the infinitive; as,<BR>मृगयां कर्त्तुं गतः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abaft
ABAFT, adv. (Towards the stern of the ship) नावः पश्चिमभागं प्रति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abandon
To ABANDON, v. a. त्यज् (c. 1. त्यजति, त्यक्तुं), परित्यज्, सन्त्यज्; हा (c. 3.<BR>जहाति, हातुं), अपहा, विहा, प्रहा, अपाहा; उत्सृज् (c. 6. -सृजति, -स्रष्टुं),<BR>अतिसृज्, व्यपसृज्; उज्झ् (c. 6. उज्झति, उज्झितुं), प्रोज्झ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abandoned
ABANDONED, p. p. त्यक्तः -क्ता -क्तं, परित्यक्तः -क्ता -क्तं, उत्त्पक्तः -क्ता -क्तं,<BR>हीनः -ना -नं, उत्सृष्टः -ष्टा -ष्टं, प्रोज्झितः -ता -तं, समुज्झितः -ता -तं, रहितः<BR>-ता -तं, विरहितः -ता -तं, विसर्ज्जितः -ता -तं, विनाकृतः -ता -तं.<BR>— (Re-<BR>probate) पापात्मा -त्मा -त्म (न्), पापमतिः -तिः -ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abandonment
ABANDONMENT, s. त्यागः, परित्यागः, उत्त्यागः, विरहः, प्रोज्झनं.<BR>— (Of<BR>worldly connexions) सन्न्यासः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abase
To ABASE v. a. स्वस्थानाद् अपकृष् (c. 1. -कर्षति, c. 6. -कृषति, -क्रष्टुं),<BR>स्वस्थानाद् भ्रंश् in caus. (भ्रंशयति, भ्रंशयितुं) or निपत् in caus.<BR>(-पातयति, -पातयितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abased
ABASED, p. p. भग्नदर्पः -र्पा -र्पं, अपकृष्टः -ष्टा -ष्टं, पराभूतः -ता -तं,<BR>अभिभूतः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abasement
ABASEMENT, s. (The act of bringing low) अपकर्षः, -र्षणं, अभिभवः.<BR>—<BR>(A low state), अपकृष्टता, -त्वं, अपकीर्त्तिः f.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abash
To ABASH, v. a. लज् in caus. (लाजयति, लाजयितुं), ह्री in caus.<BR>(ह्रेपयति, ह्रेपयितुं), त्रप् in caus. (त्रपयति, त्रपयितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abashed
ABASHED, p. p. लज्जितः -ता -तं, त्रपितः -ता -तं, व्रीडितः -ता -तं,<BR>ह्रीपरिगतः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abate
To ABATE, v. a. (To diminish) ह्रस् in caus. (ह्रासयति, ह्रासयितुं),<BR>कन् (nom. कनयति, कनयितुं), लघ् (nom. लघयति, लघयितुं), शम्<BR>in caus. (शमयति, शमयितुं).<BR>— (To let down the price in selling)<BR>मूल्यं न्यूनीकृ.<BR>— (To depress) अवसद् in caus. (-सादयति, -यितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abate
To ABATE, v. n. (To grow less) क्षि in pass. (क्षीयते), ह्रस् (c. 1.<BR>ह्रसति, ह्रसितुं).<BR>— (To subside) शम् (c. 4. शाम्यति, शमितुं), उपशम्,<BR>प्रशम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abated
ABATED, p. p. (Subsided) उपशान्तः -न्ता -न्तं, प्रशान्तः -न्ता -न्तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abbess
ABBESS, s. विहारस्य or मठस्य or आश्रमस्य प्रधाना स्त्री.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abbey
ABBEY, s. विहारः, धर्म्मचारिणां मठः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abbot
ABBOT, s. विहारस्य प्रधानपुरुषः, मठाध्यक्षः, गुरुः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abbreviate
To ABBREVIATE, v. a. (To shorten by contraction) संहृ (c. 1.<BR>-हरति, -हर्त्तुं), सङ्क्षिप् (c. 6. -क्षिपति, -क्षेप्तुं), ह्रस् in caus. (ह्रासयति,<BR>ह्रासयितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=001-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abbreviature
ABBREVIATURE, s. सङ्क्षेपः, -पणं, समसनं, सङ्ग्रहः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abdicate
To ABDICATE, v. a. (To resign an office) राज्यं or अधिकारं or पदं<BR>त्यज् (c. 1. त्यजति, त्यक्तुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abdication
ABDICATION, s. राज्यत्यागः, अधिकारत्यागः, पदत्यागः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abdomen
ABDOMEN, s. वस्तिः m., उदरं, कुक्षिः m.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abdominal
ABDOMINAL, a. वास्तेयः -यी -यं, उदरकः -का -कं, कौक्षः -क्षी -क्षं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aberration
ABERRATION, s. विभ्रमः, भ्रान्तिः, भ्रंशः, च्युतिः f., पथभ्रष्टता, उन्मार्गगमनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abet
To ABET, v. a. (To encourage) प्रोत्सह् in caus. (-साहयति, -साहयितुं),<BR>प्रवृत् in caus. (-वर्त्तयति, -वर्त्तयितुं).<BR>— (To help) उपकृ (c. 8. -करोति,<BR>-कर्त्तुं), उपचर् (c. 1. -चरति, -चरितुं), उपकारं or साहाय्यं कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abettor
ABETTOR, s. प्रोत्साहकः, प्रवर्त्तकः, उपकारकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abeyance
ABEYANCE, s. अपेक्षा, विलम्बः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abhor
To ABHOR, v. a. गर्ह् (c. 1. गर्हते, गर्हितुं), बाध् in des. (बीभत्सते,<BR>बीभत्सितुं), घृणां कृ, द्विष् (c. 2. द्वेष्टि, द्वेष्टुं), प्रद्विष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abhorrence
ABHORRENCE, s. बीभत्सः, -त्सं, गर्हणं, घृणा, अरुचिः f.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abhorrent
ABHORRENT, a. (Struck with abhorrence) बीभत्सान्वितः -ता -तं<BR>—<BR>(Inconsistent with) विरुद्धः -द्धा -द्धं, अयोग्यः -ग्या -ग्यं, असङ्गतः<BR>-ता -तं, असंस्थितः -ता -तं, विपरीतः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abide
To ABIDE, v. n. (To dwell) वस् (c. 1. वसति, वस्तुं).<BR>— (To remain)<BR>स्था (c. 1. तिष्ठति -ते, स्थातुं), वृत् (c. 1. वर्त्तते, वर्त्तितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abide
To ABIDE, v. a. (To wait for, expect) प्रतीक्ष् (c. 1. -ईक्षते, -ईक्षितुं).<BR>उद्दृश् (c. 1. -पश्यति, -द्रष्टुं), प्रतिपाल् (c. 10. -पालयति, -पालयितुं).<BR>—<BR>(To bear, support) सह् (c. 1. सहते, सोढुं), क्षम् (c. 1. क्षमते, क्षन्तुं),<BR>तिज् in des. (तितिक्षते, तितिक्षितुं).<BR>— (To abide by one's promise)<BR>प्रतिज्ञातं पाल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abiding
ABIDING, a. स्थायी -यिनी -यि (न्), वर्त्ती -र्त्तिनी -र्त्ति (न्), वृत्तिमान्<BR>-मती -मत् (त्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ability
ABILITY, s. शक्तिः f., शक्तता, बलं, सामर्थ्यं.<BR>— (Skill) कुशलता, प्रवीणता.<BR>‘To the utmost of one's ability,’ यथाशक्ति ind., यावच्छक्यं,<BR>सर्व्वयत्नैः, यथासामर्थ्यं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abject
ABJECT, a. कृपणः -णा -णं, अधमः -मा -मं, अपकृष्टः -ष्टा -ष्टं, निकृष्टः -ष्टा -ष्टं,<BR>नीचः -चा -चं, अवगर्हितः -ता -तं.<BR>— (Without hope) निराशः -शा -शं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abjectly
ABJECTLY, adv. कृपणं, कार्पण्येन, निकृष्टं, नीचतया, अधमप्रकारेणं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abjectness
ABJECTNESS or ABJECTION, s. कार्पण्यं, अधमत्वं, अपकृष्टता, निकृष्टता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abjuration
ABJURATION, s. (Renouncing with oath) शपथेन त्यागः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abjure
To ABJURE, v. a. (To renounce with oath) शयथेन त्यज् (c. 1. त्यजति,<BR>त्यक्तुं).<BR>— (To renounce) प्रत्याख्या (c. 2. -ख्याति -ख्यातुं), परित्पज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ablative case
ABLATIVE CASE, अपादानं, पञ्चमी विभक्तिः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

able
ABLE, a. (Of power sufficient) समर्थः -र्था -र्थं, क्षमः -मा -मं, शक्तः<BR>-क्ता -क्तं.<BR>— (Powerful) प्रबलः -ला -लं, बलवान् -वती -वत् (त्),<BR>शक्तिमान् -मती -मत् (त्)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

able
To be ABLE, v. n. शक् (c. 5. शक्नोति, c. 4. शक्यति -ते, शक्तुं), क्षम्<BR>(c. 1. क्षमते, क्षन्तुं), उत्सहृ (c. 1. -सहते -सोढुं) with inf.; प्रभू (c. 1.<BR>-भवति -भवितुं) with dat.; as, ‘they are able to destroy the<BR>world,’ प्रभवन्ति क्षयाय जगतः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=001-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

able-bodied
ABLE-BODIED, a. प्रबलशरीरः -रा -रं, प्रबलकायः -या -यं, दृढाङ्गः -ङ्गा -ङ्गं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ablution
ABLUTION, s. स्नानं, मज्जनं, धावनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abnegation
ABNEGATION, s. निह्नवः, अपह्नवः, प्रत्याख्यानं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abode
ABODE, s. (Place of residence) गृहं, वेश्म n. (न्), आयतनं, निवासः,<BR>निलयः, -यनं, आलयः.<BR>— (Continuance in a place) वसतिः, अवस्थानं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abolish
To ABOLISH, v. a. (To annul) लोपं कृ, निरर्थकं -कां -कं कृ.<BR>— (To<BR>destroy) नश् in caus. (नाशयति, नाशयितुं), विनश्; सद् in caus.<BR>(सादयति, सादयितुं), उत्सद्, प्रोत्सद्; उद्धृ (c. 1. -हरति -हर्त्तुं), उच्छिद्<BR>(c. 7. -छिनत्ति, -छेत्तुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abolished
ABOLISHED, p. p. लुप्तः -प्ता -प्तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abolition
ABOLITION, s. (Act of annulling) लोपः.<BR>— (Destruction) विनाशः,<BR>उद्धरणं, उच्छेदः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abominable
ABOMINABLE, a. गर्हणीयः -या -यं, द्वेष्यः -ष्या -ष्यं, घृणार्हः -र्हा -र्हं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abominably
ABOMINABLY, adv. गर्ह्मप्रकारेण, गर्हितं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abominate
To ABOMINATE, v. a. गर्ह् (c. 1. गर्हते, गर्हितुं), बाध् in des. (बीभत्सते,<BR>बीभत्सितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abominated
ABOMINATED, p. p. गर्हितः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abomination
ABOMINATION, s. (Detestation) बीभत्सः, गर्हा, गर्हणं.<BR>— (An abomi-<BR>nated thing, the object of detestation) गर्हितं, अशुद्धद्रव्यं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abortion
ABORTION, s. गर्भस्रावः, अकालप्रसवः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abortive
ABORTIVE, a. (Producing abortion) गर्भस्रावी -विनी -वि (न्).<BR>—<BR>(Brought forth prematurely) गर्भस्रस्तः -स्ता -स्तं, अपूर्णकालः -ला<BR>-लं.<BR>— (That does not succeed) निष्फलः -ला -लं, मोघः -घा -घं,<BR>व्यर्थः -र्था -र्थं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abound
To ABOUND, v. n. (Followed by with or in) सङ्कॄ in pass. (-कीर्य्यते)<BR>with inst. c.; पॄ in pass. (पूर्य्यते), आपॄ with inst. c.<BR>— (To be<BR>in great plenty) बहुलीभू (c. 1. -भवति, -भवितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abounding in
ABOUNDING IN, आढ्यः -ढ्या -ढ्यं, सङ्कीर्णः -र्णा -र्णं, चितः -ता -तं,<BR>निचयी -यिनी -यि (न्), संवलितः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

about
ABOUT, prep. (Encircling) परि prefixed.<BR>— (Near to, in time)<BR>प्रति.<BR>— (In number) देशीय affixed; as, ‘about twelve years<BR>old,’ द्वादशवर्षदेशीयः; न्यूनाधिकं.<BR>— (Concerning, relating to)<BR>प्रति, प्रतीक्ष्य, उद्दिश्य.<BR>— (On account of) हेतोः, हेतौ, अर्थं, अर्थे, कृते,<BR>निमित्ते, कारणात्, with the crude form, or sometimes the<BR>gen. c. of the preceding noun.<BR>— (Engaged in any thing)<BR>व्यापृतः, निष्ठितः, निरतः, with loc. c.<BR>— (Close to one's person)<BR>पार्श्वतस् ind., निकटे, समीपं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

about
ABOUT, adv. (Circularly) परितस् ind., अभितस् ind.<BR>— (Nearly)<BR>प्रायशस् or प्रायस् ind.<BR>— (Here and there) इतस्ततस् ind.,<BR>सर्व्वतस् ind.<BR>— (To be about to do any thing) expressed by<BR>उद्यतः, ‘prepared,’ with the infin.; as, ‘about to kill,’<BR>हन्तुम् उद्यतः; or by the act. part. of the 2d fut.; as, गमिष्यन्,<BR>‘about to go,’ एधिष्यमाणः, ‘about to increase’; or, by<BR>the desid. adj.; as, जिगमिषुः, ‘about to go,’ मुमूर्षुः ‘about<BR>to die.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

above
ABOVE, prep. or adv. (Higher in place) अधि or अभि prefixed;<BR>उपरि, उपरिष्टात्, ऊर्द्ध्वं.<BR>— (More in quantity) अधिकं, उत्तरं.<BR>—<BR>(Higher in rank) उत्तरः -रा -रं, विशिष्टः -ष्टा -ष्टं, श्रेष्ठः -ष्ठा -ष्ठं.<BR>—<BR>(Superior to, beyond) अति; as, ‘above man's power,’ अति-<BR>मानुपं.<BR>— (Above all, especially) विषेशतस् ind., प्राधान्यतस् ind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

above
To be ABOVE, v. n. (To excel) अभिभू (c. 1. -भवति -भवितुं), प्रभू,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=002-b" target="_blank">Page002-b+ 51</a>]<BR>अतिभू; विशिष् in pass. (-शिष्यते).<BR>— (To be higher) ऊर्द्ध्वं स्था<BR>(c. 1. तिष्ठति, स्थातुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=002-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

above-ground
ABOVE-GROUND, a. (Not in the grave, still existing) वर्त्तमानः -ना<BR>-नं, जीवन् -वन्ती -वत् (त्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

above-mentioned
ABOVE-MENTIONED, a. पूर्व्वोक्तः -क्ता -क्तं, पूर्व्वोदितः -ता -तं, प्रागुक्तः -क्ता -क्तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abreast
ABREAST, adv. पार्श्वापार्श्वि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abridge
To ABRIDGE, v. a. संहृ (c. 1. -हरति -ते -हर्त्तुं) उपसंहृ; सङ्क्षिप् (c. 6.<BR>-क्षिपति -क्षेप्तुं).<BR>— (To shorten) ह्रस् in caus. (ह्रासयति, ह्रासयितुं).<BR>—<BR>(To deprive of, cut off) उच्छिद् (c. 7. -छिनत्ति -छेत्तुं), वियुज् in caus.<BR>(-योजयति -योजयितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abridgment
ABRIDGMENT, s. प्रत्याहारः, सङ्क्षेपः, -पणं, समसनं, सङ्ग्रहः, सभाहारः,<BR>समाहृतिः f.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abroad
ABROAD, adv. (In another country) विदेशे loc. c.<BR>— (At large, un-<BR>confined) निर्विघ्नं.<BR>— (Out of the house) वहिस्.<BR>— (In all direc-<BR>tions) सर्व्वत्र, इतस्ततस् ind.<BR>— (Sojourn abroad in a foreign<BR>country) प्रवसनं.<BR>— (A sojourner abroad) प्रवासी (न्), प्रोषितः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abrogate
To ABROGATE, v. a. लोपं कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abrogated
ABROGATED, p. p. लुप्तः -प्ता -प्तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abrogation
ABROGATION, s. लोपः, लोपकरणं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abrupt
ABRUPT, a. (Broken, craggy) भग्नः -ग्ना -ग्नं, भिन्नः -न्ना -न्नं, रुक्षः<BR>-क्षा -क्षं.<BR>— (Sudden) आकस्मिकः -की -कं.<BR>— (Unconnected)<BR>असम्बन्धः -न्धा -न्धं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abruptly
ABRUPTLY, adv. (Hastily) सहसा, अकस्मात्, झटिति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abscess
ABSCESS, s. विद्रधिः m., पूयसम्पूर्णः स्फोटः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abscond
To ABSCOND, v. n. (To hide one's self) आत्मानं गुह् (c. 1. गूहति -ते,<BR>गोढुं), निगुह्; गुप्तः -प्ता -प्तं or प्रच्छन्नः -न्ना -न्नं भू.<BR>— (To disappear)<BR>अन्तर्धा in pass. (-धीयते).<BR>— (To escape privately) पलाय् (c. 1.<BR>पलायते -यितुं), निष्पत् (c. 1. -पतति -पतितुं), व्यपसृप् (c. 1. -सर्पति<BR>-सर्पितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

absence
ABSENCE, s. अभावः, परोक्षं, अनुपस्थितिः f., अनुपस्थानं, अविषयः,<BR>असन्निधिः m.<BR>— (Absence from) विरहः, वियोगः.<BR>— (Of mind)<BR>अमनोयोगः, अन्यमानसत्वं, समाधिः m.<BR>— (In one's absence) परोक्षे.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

absent
ABSENT, a. (Not present) अवर्त्तमानः -ना -नं, अविद्यमानः -ना -नं,<BR>परोक्षः -क्षा -क्षं, स्थानान्तरङ्गतः -ता -तं, अनुपस्थितः -ता -तं, अनुपस्थायी<BR>-यिनी -यि (न्), असमक्षः -क्षा -क्षं, अप्रत्यक्षः -क्षा -क्षं.<BR>— (Abroad)<BR>प्रोषितः -ता -तं.<BR>— (Absorbed in meditation) समाहितः -ता -तं.<BR>—<BR>(Thinking of something else) अन्यमानसः -सी -सं or -मनाः -नाः<BR>-नः (स्), शून्यहृदयः -या -यं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

absent
To be ABSENT, v. n. अन्यत्र, or स्थानान्तरे, or असाक्षात् वृत् (c. 1.<BR>वर्त्तते, वर्त्तितुं) or अस् (c. 2. अस्ति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

absentee
ABSENTEE, s. प्रोषितः, प्रवासी m. (न्), अदेशस्थः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

absolute
ABSOLUTE, a. (Complete) सम्पूर्णः -र्णा -र्णं, समाप्तः -प्ता -प्तं, समग्रः<BR>-ग्रा -ग्रं, पर्य्याप्तः -प्ता -प्तं.<BR>— (Not relative, simple) मात्रकः -का -कं,<BR>केवलः -ला -लं.<BR>— (Sovereign, paramount) परमः -मा -मं, उत्तमः<BR>-मा -मं.<BR>— (An absolute king) अधिराजः, सम्राट् (ज्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

absolutely
ABSOLUTELY, adv. (Entirely) सर्व्वशस्, केवलं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

absolution
ABSOLUTION, s. पापमोचनं, पापक्षमा, निष्कृतिः f., क्षमा, मुक्तिः f.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

absolve
To ABSOLVE, v. a. (To acquit of a crime) पापात् मुच् (c. 6. मुञ्चति -ते,<BR>मोक्तुं), विमुच्, or in caus. (मोचयति -यितुं), पापं क्षम् (c. 1. क्षमते,<BR>क्षन्तुं), अपराधं क्षम्; ‘he is absolved from crime,’ दुष्कृतात् पूयते.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

absolved
ABSOLVED, p. p. पापमुक्तः -क्ता -क्तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=002-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

absorb
To ABSORB, v. a. निपा (c. 1. -पिवति, -पातुं), उत्पा; शुष् in caus.<BR>(शोषयति -यितुं), उच्छुष्, उपशुष्; ग्रस् (c. 1. ग्रसते, ग्रसितुं), उपग्रस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

absorbed
ABSORBED, p. p. (Absorbed in any occupation) निरतः -ता -तं,<BR>निविष्टः -ष्टा -ष्टं, परायणः -णा -णं, आसक्तः -क्ता -क्तं.<BR>— (In medita-<BR>tion) समाहितः -ता -तं, एकाग्रः -ग्रा -ग्रं; (Drunk in) निपीतः<BR>-ता -तं, ग्रस्तः -स्ता -स्तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

absorption
ABSORPTION, निपानं, शोषणं, ग्रसनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abstain
To ABSTAIN, v. n. निवृत् (c. 1. -वर्त्तते -वर्त्तितुं) with abl.; as, ‘he<BR>abstains from eating flesh,’ निवर्त्तते मांसभक्षणात्; वृज् in caus.<BR>(वर्जयति -यितुं), परिवृज्, विवृज् with acc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abstemious
ABSTEMIOUS, a. अल्पाहारी -रिणी -रि (न्), अभोजी -जिनी -जि (न्),<BR>मिताशनः -ना -नं, मितभुक् m. f. n. (ज्), परिमिताहारः -रा -रं, नियता-<BR>हारः -रा -रं, यताहारः -रा -रं, लध्वाशी -शिनी -शि (न्), लध्वाहारः -रा -रं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abstemiousness
ABSTEMIOUSNESS, s. आहारपरित्यागः, अल्पाहारित्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abstinence
ABSTINENCE, s. (Abstaining from food) उपवासः, अभोजनं.<BR>— (Re-<BR>straint of the passions) जितेन्द्रियत्वं, संयमनं, संयामः.<BR>— (Forbear-<BR>ance from any thing) निवृत्तिः f., क्षान्तिः, f.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abstinent
ABSTINENT, a. (Temperate) जितेन्द्रियः -या -यं, निवृत्तरागः -गा -गं,<BR>संयमी -मिनी -मि (न्), संयतात्मा -त्मा -त्म (न्).<BR>— (Fasting) उपवासी<BR>-सिनी -सि (न्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abstract
To ABSTRACT, v. a. अपहृ (c. 1. -हरति -ते -हर्त्तुं), व्यपहृ; अपकृष् (c. 1.<BR>-कर्षति, c. 6. -कृषति -क्रष्टुं), अपाकृष्, अवकृष्, व्यपकृष्; आदा (c. 3. -दत्ते<BR>-दातुं), उपादा, अभ्यादा.<BR>— (To reduce to an epitome) सङ्क्षिप्<BR>(c. 6. -क्षिपति -क्षेप्तुं), संहृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abstract
ABSTRACT, a. विभिन्नः -न्ना -न्नं, वियुक्तः -क्ता -क्तं, विविक्तः -क्ता -क्तं, पृथक्कृतः<BR>-ता -तं, केवलः -ला -लं<BR>— (From material objects) विषयविविक्तः<BR>-क्ता -क्तं, विषयापकृष्टः -ष्टा -ष्टं<BR>— (Metaphysical) आन्वीक्षिकः -की -कं.<BR>— (Abstracted in mind) समाहितः -ता -तं, अनन्यमनाः -नाः -नः (स्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=003-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

abstract
