ACCLIVITY, s. उत्सङ्गः, स्थानं क्रमश उद्गम्यं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accommodate
To ACCOMMODATE, v. a. (To adapt, adjust) युज् in caus. (योजयति<BR>-यितुं), सन्धा (c. 3. -दधाति -धातुं), समाधा.<BR>— (To settle a difference)<BR>सन्धा, समाप् in caus. (-आपयति -यितुं).<BR>— (To supply with con-<BR>veniences) सोपकारद्रव्याणि उपकॢप् (c. 10. -कल्पयति -यितुं), युज्<BR>in caus. समायुज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accommodation
ACCOMMODATION, s. (Supplying of conveniences) सोपकारद्रव्योपक-<BR>ल्पनं.<BR>— (Convenience) उपकरणं.<BR>— (Mutual accommodation)<BR>प्रत्युपकारः.<BR>— (Adaptation) संयोजनं, सन्धानं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accompanied
ACCOMPANIED, p. p. सहितः -ता -तं, संवृतः -ता -तं, सहायवान् -वती<BR>-वत्, परिवारितः -ता -तं, समेतः -ता -तं. As applied to two<BR>persons द्वितीय or सहाय may be used; as, ‘Nakula ac-<BR>companied by Sahadeva,’ नकुलः सहदेवद्वितीयः; ‘accompa-<BR>nied by Umā,’ उमासहायः, Sometimes स is prefixed with<BR>this, sense; as, ‘accompanied by his ministers,’ ससचिवः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accompany
To ACCOMPANY, v. a. (As a companion) अनुया (c. 2. -याति -यातुं),<BR>समनुया, अन्वि (c. 2. -एति -एतुं), परिवृ in caus. (-वारयति -यितुं),<BR>सहायीभू.<BR>— (To join with) युज् (c. 7. युनक्ति, योक्तुं, c. 10. योजयति<BR>-यितुं), संयुज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accomplice
ACCOMPLICE, s. (In crime) पापसहायः, पापसम्मितः, कुसहायः.<BR>— (Co-<BR>adjutor) सहकारी m. (न्).<BR>— (Adherent) अनुपङ्गी m. (न्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accomplish
To ACCOMPLISH, v. a. सिध् or साध् in caus. (साधयति -यितुं) संसाध्;<BR>समाप् in caus. (-आपयति -यितुं), सम्पद् in caus. (-पादयति -यितुं),<BR>समाचर् (c. 1. -चरति -चरितुं), निर्वृत् in caus. (-वर्त्तयति -यितुं), समास्था<BR>(c. 1. तिष्ठति -ते -स्थातुं), अनुष्ठा, आस्था, कृ (c. 8. करोति, कर्त्तुं) सङ्कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accomplishable
ACCOMPLISHABLE, साध्यः -ध्या -ध्यं, साधनीयः -या -यं, सम्पादनीयः -या -यं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accomplished
ACCOMPLISHED, सिद्धः -द्धा -द्धं, निर्वृत्तः -त्ता -त्तं, निष्पन्नः -न्ना -न्नं, सम्पन्नः<BR>-न्ना -न्नं, कृतार्थीभृतः -ता -तं.<BR>— (Clever) गुणवान् -वती -वत् (त्), गुणी<BR>-णिनी -नि (न्), निपुणः -णा -णं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accomplishment
ACCOMPLISHMENT, s. सिद्धिः f., समाप्तिः f., निष्पत्तिः f., आसाधनं, निर्व्वाहः,<BR>राद्धिः f., निर्वृत्तिः f.<BR>— (Of one's object) कृतकृत्पता, कृतार्थता,<BR>स्वार्थसिद्धिः f.<BR>— (The condition of an accomplished man)<BR>गुणिता, सम्पूर्णभावः, निपुणता.<BR>— (Embellishment) परिष्कारः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accord
To ACCORD, v. n. (To agree, suit) युज् in pass. (युज्यते), अनुरूपः -पा<BR>-पं, or सदृशः -शा -शं, or तुल्यः -ल्या -ल्यं अस्.<BR>— (To be of<BR>the same opinion) एकचित्तीभू, सम्मतः -ता -तं भू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accord
ACCORD, s. (Concurrence) सम्मतिः f., ऐकमत्यं, एकचित्तता, समता,<BR>समवाक्यं, स्वीकररां.<BR>— (In music) एकतालः.<BR>— (Of one's own<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=004-b" target="_blank">Page004-b+ 51</a>]<BR>accord) स्वयं, कामतस् ind., कामहैतुकः -की -कं.<BR>— (With one<BR>accord) एकचित्तीभूय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=004-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accordance
ACCORDANCE, s. (Conformity) अनुसारः, अनुरूपता, सादृश्यं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

according
ACCORDING, prep. (According to) यथा, अनुरूपं, अनुसारतस् ind.<BR>अनुरूपेण, अनुसारेण, अनु prefixed; ‘according to seniority,’<BR>अनुज्येष्ठं; ‘according to one's desire,’ यथेष्टं, यथाभिमतं;<BR>‘according to one's power,’ यथाशक्ति ind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accordingly
ACCORDINGLY, adv. तथैव, तदनुसारतस् ind., तदनुरूपेण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accost
To ACCOST. v. a. अभिभाष् (c. 1. -भाषते -भाषितुं), आभाष्, समाभाष्,<BR>अभिधा (c. 3. -दधाति -धातुं), आमन्त्र् (c. 10. -मन्त्रयति -ते -यितुं), समामन्त्र्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accosted
ACCOSTED, p. p. अभिहितः -ता -तं, अभिभाषितः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

account
ACCOUNT, s. (A computation) गणितं, विगणनं, गणना -नं, सङ्ख्यानं,<BR>लेखा.<BR>— (Value, estimation) मूल्यं, अर्घः, सम्मानं.<BR>— (Great value)<BR>बहुमतिः.<BR>— (Narrative, explanation) कथा, कथनं, उपाख्यानं,<BR>यथातथं, यथास्थितं; ‘on this account,’ अतस् ind., अनेन हेतुना,<BR>इति हेतोः; ‘on what account?’ केन हेतुना or केन कार्य्येण;<BR>‘on account of,’ हेतोः, हेतौ, अर्थं or अर्थे, कृते, निमित्ते,<BR>कारणात् with the crude form; or expressed by simply<BR>putting the noun in the abl. c.; as, ‘on account of anger,’<BR>कोपात्; or by the indec. part. of उद्दिश्; as, ‘on which<BR>account,’ यदुद्दिश्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

account
To ACCOUNT, v. a. (To esteem) मन् (c. 4. मन्यते, मन्तुं, or caus.<BR>मानयति -यितुं), मम्मन् in caus.; ज्ञा (c. 9. जानाति, जानीते, ज्ञातुं).<BR>—<BR>(To reckon, compute) गण् (c. 10. गणयति -यितुं), विगण्, सङ्ख्या<BR>(c. 2. -ख्याति -ख्यातुं).<BR>— (To give an account or relation) कथ्<BR>(c. 10. कथयति -यितुं), आख्या, निविद् in caus. (-वेदयति -यितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accountable
ACCOUNTABLE, a. परानुयोगाधीनः -ना -नं, अनुसन्धेयः -या -यं, अनु-<BR>सन्धानायत्तः -त्ता -त्तं, आह्वानाधीनः -ना -नं, यो निक्षेपं or न्यासं<BR>प्रतिपादयितुम् अर्हति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accountant
ACCOUNTANT, s. गणकः, लेखकः, लिपिकारः, मसिपण्यः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

account-book
ACCOUNT-BOOK, s. गणनापुस्तकं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accoutre
To ACCOUTRE, v. a. नह् (c. 4. -नह्यति -ते -नद्धुं), सन्नह्, पिनह्, सज्जीकृ<BR>(c. 8. -करोति -कर्त्तुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accoutred
ACCOUTRED, सन्नद्धः -द्धा -द्धं, पिनद्धः -द्धा -द्धं, सज्जः -ज्जा -ज्जं, सज्जितः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accoutrement
ACCOUTREMENT, s. सन्नाहः, सज्जा, परिधानं, अलङ्कारः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accrue
To ACCRUE, v. n. (To be added) प्रतिवृत् (c. 1. -वर्त्तते -वर्त्तितुं), मिल्<BR>(c. 1. मिलति, मेलितुं), प्राप् in pass. (-आप्यते).<BR>— (To arise as<BR>profit) उत्पद् (c. 4. -पद्यते -पत्तुं), जन् (c. 4. जायते, जनितुं), सञ्जन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accumulate
To ACCUMULATE, v. a. चि (c. 5. चिनोति, चेतुं), सञ्चि, समाचि, प्रचि,<BR>राशीकृ, एकत्र कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accumulate
To ACCUMULATE, v. n. उपचि in pass. (-चीयते), वृध् (c. 1. वर्धते,<BR>वर्धितुं), राशीभू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accumulated
ACCUMULATED, p. p. उपचितः -ता -तं, सञ्चितः -ता -तं, समाचितः -ता -तं,<BR>राशीकृतः -ता -तं, वर्द्धितः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accumulation
ACCUMULATION, s. सञ्चयः, समुदायः, सम्पत्तिः f., सङ्घातः, सन्नयः, ओघः,<BR>राशीकरणं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accuracy
ACCURACY, s. याथार्थ्यं, तथ्यं, याथातथ्यं, सम्यक्त्वं, शुद्धत्वं, सत्यता.<BR>—<BR>(Nicety) मूक्ष्मत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accurate
ACCURATE, a. यथार्थः -र्था -र्थं, सत्यः -त्या -त्यं, तथ्यः -थ्या -थ्यं, ऋतः<BR>-ता -तं, समञ्जसः -सा -सं, याथार्धिकः -की -कं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accurately
ACCURATELY, adv. यथार्थं, सम्यक्, ऋतं, सत्यं, अञ्जसा, सूक्ष्मत्वन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=004-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accursed
ACCURSED, p. p. अभिशप्तः -प्ता -प्तं, शापग्रस्तः -स्ता -स्तं, आक्रुष्टः -ष्टा -ष्टं,<BR>आक्रोशनीयः -या -यं, अवगर्हितः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accusation
ACCUSATION, s. अभियोगः, दोषकल्पनं, अपवादः.<BR>— (False) अभिशंसनं,<BR>अभिशापः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accusative
ACCUSATIVE, a. (Case) कर्म्म n. (न्), द्वितीया विभक्तिः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accuse
To ACCUSE, v. a. अभियुज् (c. 7. -युनक्ति -योक्तुं), अभियोगं कृ, अधिक्षिप्<BR>(c. 6. -क्षिपति -क्षप्तुं), अपवद् (c. 1. -वदति -वदितुं), दोषकल्पनं कृ,<BR>परिशप् (c. 1. -शपति -शप्तुं), अभिशप्.<BR>— (To be accused), अभियुज्<BR>in pass. (-युज्यते).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accused
ACCUSED, अभियुक्तः -क्ता -क्तं, अभिशप्तः -प्ता -प्तं, अभिशस्तः -स्ता -स्तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accuser
ACCUSER, s. अभियोगी m. (न्), अभियोक्ता m. (क्तृ), अपवादकः, परिवादकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accustom
To ACCUSTOM, v. a. अभ्यस् (c. 4. -अस्यति -असितुं), अभ्यासं or व्यवहारं कृ,<BR>शिक्ष् in caus. (शिक्षयति -यितुं).<BR>— (To be accustomed) अभ्यस्तः -स्ता<BR>-स्तं भू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accustomary
ACCUSTOMARY, a. आचारिकः -की -कं, आचरितः -ता -तं, व्यावहारिकः<BR>-की -कं, व्यवहारानुरूपः -पा -पं, स्वाभाविकः -की -कं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

accustomed
ACCUSTOMED, p. p. अभ्यस्तः -स्ता -स्तं, शिक्षितः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ace
ACE, s. (On cards or dice) मुद्राविशेषः.<BR>— (Within an ace, all but)<BR>प्रायस्, यत्किञ्चिन् न्यूनं, ईषदूनं.<BR>— ‘All but dead,’ मृतकल्पः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acerbity
ACERBITY, s. कटुता, अम्लता, शुक्तता.<BR>— (Sharpness of temper)<BR>स्वभावकटुता, अरुन्तुदत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ache
ACHE, s. वेदनं -ना, पीडा, व्यथा.<BR>— (Headache) शिरोवेदना.<BR>— (Tooth-<BR>ache) दन्तवेदना.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ache
To ACHE, v. n. पीड् in pass. (पीड्यते), व्यथ् (c. 1. व्यथते, व्यथितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

achieve
To ACHIEVE, v. a. (To perform, finish) समाप् in caus. (-आपयति<BR>-यितुं), सम्पद् in caus. (-पादयति -यितुं), सिध् in caus. (साधयति<BR>-यितुं).<BR>— (To obtain) प्राप् (c. 5. -आप्नोति -आप्तुं), समाप्, सम्प्राप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

achievement
ACHIEVEMENT, s. (A noble exploit) प्रशंसनीयकर्म्म n. (न्), चेष्टितं,<BR>चरित्रं.<BR>— (In heraldry) पदचिह्नं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acid
ACID, a. अम्लः -म्ला -म्लं, शुक्तः -क्ता -क्तं, शौक्तः -की -क्तं, शौक्तिकः -की -कं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acid
ACID, s. अम्लः, शुक्तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acidity
ACIDITY, s. अम्लता -त्वं, अम्लभावः, शुक्तता.<BR>— (Of stomach) अम्लपित्तः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acidulate
To ACIDULATE, v. a. अम्लीकृ; अम्लय् (nom. अम्लयति -यितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acidulated
ACIDULATED, p. p. अम्लाक्तः -क्ता -क्तं, अम्लीकृतः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acknowledge
To ACKNOWLEDGE, v. a. अभिज्ञा (c. 1. -जानाति -नीते -ज्ञातुं), प्रत्यभिज्ञा,<BR>समभिज्ञा, प्रतिज्ञा; स्वीकृ, अङ्गीकृ, अनुभाप् (c. 1. -भाषते -भाषितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acknowledgment
ACKNOWLEDGMENT, s. स्वीकारः, अङ्गीकारः, प्रत्यभिज्ञानं.<BR>— (Of a fault)<BR>स्वपापस्वीकारः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acorn
ACORN, s. प्रसिद्धवृक्षस्य फलं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acquaint
To ACQUAINT, v. a. ज्ञा in caus. (ज्ञापयति -यितुं), विज्ञा; बुध् in caus.<BR>(बोधयति -यितुं), प्रबुध्, प्रतिबुध्, अवबुध्, निविद् in caus. (-वेदयति -यितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acquaintance
ACQUAINTANCE, s. परिचयः.<BR>— (Knowledge) ज्ञानं, परिज्ञानं.<BR>— (An ac-<BR>quaintance, friend) मित्रं, संसर्गी m. (न्), विभावः.<BR>— (Familiarity)<BR>संसर्गः, संस्तवः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acquainted
ACQUAINTED, परिचितः -ता -तं, संस्तुतः -ता -तं.<BR>— (Known) ज्ञातः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acquiesce
To ACQUIESCE, v. n. तुष् (c. 1. तुष्यति तोष्टुं), सन्तुप् with inst. or loc.<BR>—<BR>(In an opinion) सम्मतिं कृ.<BR>— (To assent) अनुमन् (c. 4. -मन्यते<BR>-मन्तुं), अनुज्ञा (c. 9. -जानाति -ज्ञातुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acquiescence
ACQUIESCENCE, s. तुष्टिः f., परितोषः, सन्तोषः, सम्मतिः f., अनुमतिः f.,<BR>शान्तिः f.<BR>— (Submission) क्षान्तिः f.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acquirable
ACQUIRABLE, a. प्राप्यः -प्या -प्यं, लभ्यः -भ्या -भ्यं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=005-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acquire
To ACQUIRE, v. a. अर्ज् (c. 1. अर्जति अर्जितुं), उपार्ज्, लभ् (c. 1. लभते<BR>लब्धुं), उपलभ्, प्राप् (c. 5. -आप्रोति -आप्तुं), अवाप्; प्रतिपद् (c. 4.<BR>-पद्यते -पत्तुं), अश् (c. 5. अश्नुते, अशितुं), उपाश् समश्; आविश् (c. 6.<BR>-विशति -वेष्टुं), समाविश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acquired
ACQUIRED, p. p. प्राप्तः -प्ता -प्तं, लब्धः -ब्धा -ब्धं, आपन्नः -न्ना -न्नं, अर्ज्जितः<BR>-ता -तं, उपार्ज्जितः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acquisition
ACQUISITION or ACQUIREMENT, s. लाभः, लब्धिः f., अर्ज्जनं, प्राप्तिः f.,<BR>अवाप्तिः f., सम्प्राप्तिः f., प्रतिपत्तिः f., ग्रहणं.<BR>— (The thing gained)<BR>आगमः.<BR>— (Acquirement of knowledge) विद्याप्राप्तिः f., विद्यार्ज्जनं,<BR>विद्यागमः.<BR>— (Acquisition of property) धनार्ज्जनं.<BR>— (Various<BR>acquirement) विप्रतिपत्तिः f.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acquit
To ACQUIT, v. a. पापात् मुच् (c. 6. मुञ्चति, मोक्तुं), विमुच्, or in caus.<BR>(मोचयति -यितुं), शुध in caus. (शोधयति -यितुं), निस्तृ in caus.<BR>(-तारयति -यितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

acquittal
