ACROSTIC, s. श्लोकविशेषः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

act
To ACT, v. n. चेष्ट् (c. 1. चेष्टते, चेष्टितुं), विचेष्ट्, सञ्चेष्ट्, कृ (c. 8. करोति,<BR>कुरुते, कर्त्तुं), विधा (c. 3. -दधाति -धातुं).<BR>— (To conduct one's self)<BR>व्यवहृ (c. 1. -हरति -ते -हर्त्तुं), आचर् (c. 1. -चरति -चरितुं)<BR>— (As a<BR>stage-player) नट् (c. 1. नटति, नटितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

act
To ACT, v. a. (To feign by action) नट् (c. 10. नाटयति -यितुं); as,<BR>‘Acting the sentiment of love,’ शृङ्गारभावं नाटयन्ती; रूप्<BR>(c. 10. रूपयति -यितुं), अभिनयं कृ. The sense of acting a part<BR>may be expressed by nominal verbs; as, ‘he acts the<BR>king,’ राजायते.<BR>— (To assume disguise) छद्मवेशं कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=005-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

act
