ADVISABLE, a. (Prudent) उचितः -ता -तं, योग्यः -ग्या -ग्यं, युक्तः -क्ता<BR>-क्तं.<BR>— (Open to advice) उपदेष्टव्यः -व्या -व्यं, उपदेशग्राही -हिणी<BR>-हि (न्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

advise
To ADVISE, v. a. (To give counsel) उपदिश् (c. 6. -दिशति -देष्टुं),<BR>शिक्ष् in caus. (शिक्षयति -यितुं), अनुशास् (c. 2. -शास्ति -शासितुं).<BR>— (To inform) ज्ञा in caus. (ज्ञापयति -यितुं), निविद् in caus.<BR>(-वेदयति -यितुं), बुध् in caus. (बोधयति -यितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

advise
To ADVISE, v. n. (To consult) मन्त्र् (c. 10. मन्त्रयते -यितुं).<BR>— (To<BR>deliberate) विचर् in caus. (-चारयति -यितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

advised
ADVISED, उपदिष्टः -ष्टा -ष्टं.<BR>— (Informed) ज्ञापितः -ता -तं, निवेदितः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=008-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

advisedly
ADVISEDLY, adv. (Prudently) मन्त्रतस् ind., अवधानतस् ind.,<BR>अवधानपुरःसरं, सावधानं.<BR>— (Purposely) ज्ञानतस् ind., अभिप्रायेण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adviser
ADVISER, s. उपदेशकः, उपदेष्टा m. (ष्टृ), उपदेशी m. (न्), आदेशी m. (न्)<BR>मन्त्री m. (-न्).<BR>— (Counsellor) अमात्यः, सचिवः, मन्ता m. (न्तृ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

advocate
ADVOCATE, s. (A pleader in law) उत्तरवादी m. (न्), परार्थं<BR>प्रतिवादी m. (न्), प्रतिनिधिः m.<BR>— (Any defender) प्रतिपालकः,<BR>रक्षकः, आश्रयः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

advocate
To ADVOCATE, v. a. परार्थं वद् (c. 1. वदति वदितुं); प्रतिनिधिः अस्;<BR>रक्ष् (c. 1. रक्षति रक्षितुं), परिरक्ष्, अभिरक्ष्; प्रतिपाल् (c. 10. -पालयति<BR>-यितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

advowee
ADVOWEE, s. (He that has the right of advowson) धर्म्माध्यापने<BR>योऽन्यं नियोक्तुम् अर्हति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

advowson
ADVOWSON, s. (A right to present to a benefice) धर्म्माध्यापने<BR>नियोजनाधिकारः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

adze
ADZE, s. तक्षणी, कुठारिका, वामिः m. -सी f.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aerial
AERIAL, a. (Belonging to the air) आकाशीयः -या -यं, वायवः -वी<BR>-वं, वैहायसः -सी -सं.<BR>— (Produced in the air) आकाशजः -जा -जं,<BR>वायुजः -जा -जं.<BR>— (Inhabiting the air) वायुगः -गा -गं, आकाशस्थः<BR>-स्था -स्थं, खेचरः -रा -रं, नभःस्थः -स्था -स्थं.<BR>— (Lofty) उच्चः -च्चा -च्चं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aerie
AERIE, s. (A hawk's nest) श्येननीडः, शकुनिनीडः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aerology
AEROLOGY, s. आकाशविद्या, वायुविद्या.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aeronaut
AERONAUT, s. आकाशगामी m. (न्), आकाशचरः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aether
AETHER, s. आकाशः, वायुः m., नभः n. (स्), विहायः n. (स्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

afar
AFAR, adv. (At a great distance) दूरं, दूरे, अतिदूरं, दूरतस् ind.<BR>—<BR>(To a great distance) दूरपर्य्यन्तं.<BR>— (From afar) दूरतस्, दूरात्.<BR>— (Afar off) दूरस्थः -स्था -स्थं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affability
AFFABILITY, a. मृदुशीलत्वं, सुशीलत्वं, अभिगम्यता, चाटूक्तिः f, कोमलत्वं,<BR>मृदुता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affable
AFFABLE, a. मृदुशीलः -ला -लं, कोमलस्वभावः -वा -वं, सुशीलः -ला -लं,<BR>अभिगम्यः -म्या -म्यं, मृदुः -द्वी -दु, चाटुवादी -दिनी -दि (न्), प्रियवादी<BR>-दिनी -दि (न्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affably
AFFABLY, adv. मृदु, मृदुवचनेन, चाटूक्त्या, मृदुतया, मृदुजनवत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affair
AFFAIR, s. कार्य्यं, कर्म्म n. (न्), व्यापारः, विषयः, अर्थः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affect
To AFFECT, v. a. (Aim at) सेव् (c. 1. सेवते सेवितुं), उपसेव् निषेव्;<BR>समाचर् (c. 1. -चरति -चरितुं); भज् (c. 1. भजते, भक्तुं).<BR>— (Operate<BR>upon) विकृ (c. 8. -करोति -कर्त्तुं); उपहन् (c. 2. -हन्ति -हन्तुं); चल्<BR>in caus. (चालयति -यितुं).<BR>— (To move with grief, &c.) शोकोपहतं<BR>-तां -तं कृ; ‘to affect with joy,’ हर्षाकुलं -लां -लं कृ.<BR>— (To<BR>pretend) छद्म or छलं कृ; मिथ्या वद्; ‘to affect to befriend a<BR>person,’ मिथ्योपचारं कृ.<BR>— (To think one's self) मन् (c. 10.<BR>मानयते); ‘one who affects learning,’ पण्डितम्मन्यः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affectation
AFFECTATION, s. अहङ्कारः, वैलक्ष्यं, मानित्वं; महापण्डितो ऽहम् इति<BR>अतिसुन्दरी अहम् इति बुद्धिर् व्यवहारो वा; ‘affectation of learning,’<BR>पण्डितम्मन्यत्वं.<BR>— (A branch of feminine action) अवहित्थं, न्त्था,<BR>विलासः, हावः.<BR>— (False pretence) उपधा, छलं, छद्म n. (न्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affected
AFFECTED, part. a. (Pretended) कृत्रिमः -मा -मं; मिथ्या prefixed,<BR>as, मिथ्योपचारः, ‘affected kindness.’<BR>— (Full of affectation)<BR>सवैलक्ष्यः -क्ष्या -क्ष्यं, अहङ्कारी -रिणी -रि (न्), मानी -निनी -नि (न्),<BR>विलासवान् -वती -वत्.<BR>— (Affected by, disturbed by) उपहतः<BR>-ता -तं, आकुलः -ला -लं, ग्रस्तः -स्ता -स्तं, रञ्जितः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ffectedly
FFECTEDLY, adv. वैलक्ष्येण, साहङ्कारं, अहङ्कारेण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affecting
AFFECTING, a. हृदयङ्गमः -मा -मं, मर्म्मभेदी -दिनी -दि (न्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affection
AFFECTION, s. स्नेहः m., प्रियता f., अनुरक्तिः f., अनुरागः, प्रणयः,<BR>प्रेमा m. or -म n. (-मन्), हार्द्दं, प्रश्रयः.<BR>— (Passion of any kind)<BR>रागः, भावः, रसः.<BR>— (Of the mind) मनसो भावः.<BR>— (Of the body)<BR>शरीरस्य भावः.<BR>— (Parental) वात्सल्यं; ‘I have great affection<BR>for him’ तेन सह मम महान् स्नेहः or तस्मिन्न् अनुरागवान् अस्मि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affectionate
AFFECTIONATE, a. स्नेही -हिनी -हि (न्), स्निग्धः -ग्धा -ग्धं, स्नेहशीलः<BR>-ला -लं, सुहृत्तमः -मा -मं, अनुरागी -गिणी -गि (न्), प्रीतिमान् -मती<BR>-मत् (त्), वत्सलः -ला -लं, हितः -ता -तं, प्रणयी -यिणी -यि (न्),<BR>सप्रणयः -या -यं, जातहार्द्दः -र्द्दा -र्द्दं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affectionately
AFFECTIONATELY, adv. स्नेहेन, प्रीत्या, प्रीतिपूर्व्वं, स्नेहपुरःसरं, सानुरागं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affiance
AFFIANCE, s. (A marriage-contract) वाग्दानं, विवाहसम्बन्धः.<BR>—<BR>(Trust, confidence) विश्वासः, प्रत्ययः, श्रद्धा, आस्था.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affiance
To AFFIANCE, v. a. (To betroth) वादानं कृ, विवाहनियमं कृ.<BR>—<BR>(To confide) विश्वस् (c. 2. -श्वसिति -श्वसितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affianced
AFFIANCED, p. p. वाग्दत्तः -त्ता -त्तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affidavit
AFFIDAVIT, s. शपथपत्रं.<BR>— (To make affidavit) तथेति or नेति शपथेन<BR>ब्रू (c. 2. ब्रवीति वक्तुं), शपथं शप् (c. 1. शपति शप्तुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affiliation
AFFILIATION, s. कृत्रिमपुत्रकरणं, पीष्यपुत्रग्रहणं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affinity
AFFINITY, s. सम्बन्धः, सम्पर्कः, योगः, ज्ञातित्वं, बन्धुता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affirm
To AFFIRM, v. n. (Opposed to deny) तथेति ब्रू (c. 2. ब्रवीति, ब्रूते<BR>वक्तुं).<BR>— (Maintain, declare positively) दार्ढ्येन वद् (c. 1. वदति<BR>वदितुं).<BR>— (Ratify) स्थिरीकृ, दृढीकृ, निश्चितं -तां -तं कृ, संस्तम्भ् (c. 5.<BR>-स्तभ्नोति, c. 9. -स्तभ्नाति -स्तम्भितुं), प्रमाणीकृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affirmation
AFFIRMATION, s. (Declaring positively) दृढोक्तिः f., वचनं, दृढवचनं.<BR>— (Argumentative statement) पक्षः.<BR>— (Confirmation)<BR>प्रमाणीकरणं, निश्चयः, दृढीकरणं, स्थिरीकरणं.<BR>— (False) विप्रलापः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affirmative
AFFIRMATIVE, a. (That which affirms) वादी -दिनी -दि (न्), निश्चा-<BR>यकः -का -कं.<BR>— (Favourable to the argument) पक्षानुकूलः -ला -लं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affix
To AFFIX, v. a. अनुवन्ध् (c. 9. -बध्नाति -बन्द्धुं), निबन्ध्, सम्बन्ध्; संयुज्<BR>(c. 7. -युनक्ति, c. 10. -योजयति -यितुं), आयुज्, उपयुज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affix
AFFIX, s. (Grammatical) अनुबन्धः, प्रयोगः, आप्तोक्तिः f.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

afflict
To AFFLICT, v. a. क्लिश् (c. 9. क्लिश्नाति क्लेशितुं or क्लेष्टुं), पीड् (c. 10.<BR>पीडयति -यितुं), अभिपीड्, उपपीड्, परिपीड्; व्यथ् in caus. (व्यथयति<BR>-यितुं), आयस् in caus. (-यासयति -यितुं).<BR>— (To be afflicted with<BR>disease) रोगेण पीड् in pass. (पीड्यते) or बाध् in pass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

afflicted
AFFLICTED, p. p. व्यसनार्त्तः -र्त्ता -र्त्तं, दुर्गतः -ता -तं, आपद्ग्रस्तः -स्ता -स्तं,<BR>आपन्नः -न्ना -न्नं.<BR>— (Afflicted with) पीडितः -ता -तं, आतुरः -रा -रं,<BR>आर्त्तः in composition; ‘afflicted with disease,’ रोगपीडितः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affliction
AFFLICTION, s. क्लेशः, शोकः, दुःखं, कष्टं, व्यथा, पीडा, विडम्बना.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

afflictive
AFFLICTIVE, a. क्लेशकः -का -कं, क्लेशी -शिनी -शि (न्), दुःखकरः -री -रं,<BR>व्यथाकरः -री -रं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affluence
AFFLUENCE or -ENCY, s. धनबाहुल्यं, धनसम्पत्तिः, धनित्वं, समृद्धिः f.,<BR>समृद्धता.<BR>— (The act of flowing to any one place) एकस्थानं<BR>प्रति प्रवाहः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affluent
AFFLUENT, a. महाधनः -ना -नं, बहुधनः -ना -नं, धनी -निनी -नि (न्), धन-<BR>वान् -वती -वत् (त्), समृद्धः -द्धा -द्धं, वसुमान् -मती -मत् (त्), धनाढ्यः -ढ्या<BR>-ढ्यं.<BR>— (Flowing to any one place) एकस्थानं प्रति प्रवाहकः -का -कं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

afflux
AFFLUX or AFFLUXION, s. एकस्थानं प्रति स्रोतसां प्रवाहः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

afford
To AFFORD v. a. (Give) दा (c. 3. ददाति, c. 1. यच्छति दातुं), प्रादा,<BR>अभिदा, प्रदा; उपपद् in caus. (-पादयति -यितुं).<BR>— (To be able to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-a" target="_blank">Page010-a+ 51</a>]<BR>bear expenses) व्ययं कर्त्तुं समर्थः -र्था -र्थं अस् or शक् (c. 8. शक्नोति<BR>शक्तुं), or व्ययाय उपकॢप् (c. 1. -कल्पते -कल्पितुं or -कल्प्तुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=009-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affranchise
To AFFRANCHISE, v. a. मुच् (c. 10. मोचयति -यितुं, c. 6. मुञ्चति मोक्तुं),<BR>विमुच्; मोक्ष् (c. 10. मोक्षयति -यितुं), विमुक्ष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affray
AFFRAY, s. सङ्गामः, समरः, संयुगः, युद्धं, कलहः, डिम्बः, डमरः, डामरः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affright
To AFFRIGHT, v. a. त्रस् in caus. (त्रासयति -यितुं), वित्रस्; भी in<BR>caus. (भाययति or भीषयति -ते -यितुं), उद्विज् in caus. (-वेजयति -यितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affright
AFFRIGHT, s. त्रासः, सन्त्रासः, साध्वसं, भयं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affrightedly
AFFRIGHTEDLY, adv. सत्रासं, सभयं, सन्त्रासेन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affront
AFFRONT, s. अपमानं, बिप्रियं, क्षेपः, अवज्ञानं, धर्षणं, तिरस्कारः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affront
To AFFRONT, v. a. (Offer open insult) साक्षात्, or सम्मुखं, or<BR>प्रतिमुखं, or मुखामुखि, or प्रत्यक्षं अवमन् (c. 4. -मन्यते -मन्तुं), अवज्ञा<BR>(c. 9. -जानाति -ज्ञातुं), तिरस्कृ (c. 8. -करोति -कर्त्तुं), आक्षर् in caus.<BR>(-क्षारयति -यितुं), अधिक्षिप् (c. 6. -क्षिपति -क्षेप्तुं), अवक्षिप्, परिक्षिप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affronted
AFFRONTED, p. p. अपमानितः -ता -तं, अवज्ञातः -ता -तं, तिरस्कृतः -ता -तं,<BR>अधिक्षिप्तः -प्ता -प्तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affronter
AFFRONTER, s. साक्षात् or प्रतिमुखम् अपमानकः, अवज्ञानकर्त्ता m. (र्त्तृ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affrontive
AFFRONTIVE, a. अपमानकः -का -कं, अपमानोपेतः -ता -तं, अवज्ञानयुक्तः<BR>-क्ता -क्तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affusion
AFFUSION, s. आसेकः, आसेचनं, अभिषेकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

affy
To AFFY, v. a. (Betroth) वाग्दानं कृ, प्रतिज्ञापत्रेण विवाहसम्बन्धं कृ,<BR>नियमपत्रेण विवाहप्रतिज्ञां कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

afloat
AFLOAT, adv. (Floating) प्लवमानः -ना -नं, प्लवः -वा -वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

afoot
AFOOT, adv. (On foot) पादेन, पदेन.<BR>— (Going on foot) पादगः<BR>-गा -गं<BR>— (In action, or use) प्रचलः -ला -लं, प्रचलितः -ता -तं,<BR>प्रचरितः -ता -तं.<BR>— (Set on foot) आरब्धः -ब्धा -ब्धं, उद्यतः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

afore
AFORE, prep. (In front) प्रतिमुखं, अभिमुखं, सम्मुखं, अग्रे, पुरस्, पुरतस्,<BR>साक्षात्.<BR>— (In former time) पूर्व्वकाले, गतकाले, पूर्व्वं, पूर्व्वसमये, पुरा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aforesaid
AFORESAID, p. p. पूर्व्वोक्तः -क्ता -क्तं, पूर्व्वोदितः -ता -तं, प्रागुक्तः -क्ता -क्तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aforetime
AFORETIME, adv. पूर्व्वकाले, गतकाले, पुरा, पूर्व्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

afraid
AFRAID, a. भीतः -ता -तं, भयान्वितः -ता -तं, शङ्कान्वितः -ता -तं; ‘to<BR>be afraid of,’ भी (c. 3. बिभेति भेतुं), with abl. or gen.; as,<BR>‘he is afraid of the dog,’ कुक्कुरात् or कुक्कुरस्य बिभेति. So<BR>also त्रस् (c. 4. त्रस्यति त्रसितुं), उद्विज् (c. 6. -विजते -विजितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

afresh
AFRESH, adv. पुनर्, पुनरपि, नूतनं, अभिनवं, प्रतिनवं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aft
AFT, s. (The part of a ship towards the stern) नावः पश्चिमभागः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aft
AFT, adv. (Towards the stern of a ship) नावः पश्चिमभागं प्रति,<BR>नावः पश्चाद्भागं प्रति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

after
AFTER, prep. अनु or पश्चात् prefixed; as, ‘to go after,’ अनुगन्तुं;<BR>‘to run after,’ पश्चाद् धावितुं.<BR>— (Of time) पश्चात्, परं, अनन्तरं,<BR>ऊर्द्ध्वं, अर्वाक् with abl.<BR>— (According to) अनु, अनुरूपं, अनुसारतस्,<BR>अनुरूपेण, अनुसारेण; ‘after that,’ तदनन्तरे, or तदनन्तरं, or तस्मात्<BR>परं, or अत ऊर्द्ध्वं; ‘after one another,’ अनुपूर्व्वशस्; ‘a century<BR>after,’ वर्षशते गते; ‘after eating,’ भोजनानन्तरं or भोजनात् परं;<BR>‘after the rising of the sun,’ सूर्य्योदयाद् ऊर्द्ध्वं; ‘after a few<BR>days,’ दिनेषु गच्छत्सु. Sometimes ‘after’ is expressed by<BR>the indec. part.; as, ‘after ascending the tree the nests<BR>were destroyed,’ वृक्षम् आरुह्म नीडा भग्नाः, or even by पूर्व्वकं;<BR>as, ‘after laying down a stake,’ पणस्थापनपूर्व्वकं; or by<BR>repeating the word in such phrases as, ‘he waters tree<BR>after tree,’ वृक्षं वृक्षं सिञ्चति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

after
AFTER, adv. (In after time) परं, परकाले, आगामिकाले, उत्तरकाले,<BR>— (Following after another) पश्चात्.<BR>— (Subsequently) परस्तात्,<BR>उत्तरत्र, उत्तरतस् ind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

after-ages
AFTER-AGES, s. उत्तरकालः, परकालः, आगामिकालः, भाविकालः.<BR>—<BR>(Descendants) पुत्रपौत्राः m. pl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

after all
AFTER ALL, अन्ततस् ind., अन्ते, परं, शेषे, अवशेषे.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

after-birth
AFTER-BIRTH, s. गर्भपरिस्रवः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

after-comer
AFTER-COMER, s. उत्तरागामी m. (न्), परम् उपतिष्ठति यः, उत्तरकाले<BR>जीवति यः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

after-crop
AFTER-CROP, s. शस्यस्य द्वितीयसङ्गहः or द्वितीयोत्पत्तिः f., फलस्य<BR>द्वितीयसङ्ग्रहः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

after-dinner
AFTER-DINNER, s. भोजनानन्तरं, भोजनात् परं, भोजनोत्तरं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

after-endeavour
AFTER-ENDEAVOUR, s. उत्तरोद्योगः, द्वितीययत्नः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

after-game
AFTER-GAME, s. उत्तरोपायः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

after-grass
AFTER-GRASS or AFTER-MATH s. द्वितीयतृणं, द्वितीयतृणोत्पत्तिः f.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

after-inquiry
AFTER-INQUIRY, s. उत्तरानुसन्धानं, उत्तरजिज्ञासा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

after-life
AFTER-LIFE, s. जीवनावशेषः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

afternoon
AFTERNOON, s. अपखह्लः, पराह्लं, वैकालः, विकालः.<BR>— (Relating to<BR>the afternoon) आपराह्लिकः -की -कं, वैकालिकः -की -कं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

after-pains
AFTER-PAINS, s. अनुतापः, उत्तरव्यथा.<BR>— (Atchildbirth) प्रसवानन्तरं वेदना.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

after-state
AFTER-STATE, s. परावस्था, उत्तरावस्था, भाव्यवस्था.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

after-taste
AFTER-TASTE, s. उत्तरस्वादः, अनुस्वादः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

after-thought
AFTER-THOUGHT, s. अनुबोधः, उत्तरचिन्ता, कार्य्यानन्तरं विचारणं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

after-times
AFTER-TIMES, s. उत्तरकालः, परकालः, आगामिकालः.<BR>— (Descen-<BR>dants) पुत्रपौत्राः m. pl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

afterwards
AFTERWARDS, s. पश्चात् ind., तत्पश्चात्, तदनन्तरं, अनन्तरं, ततः परं,<BR>परं ind., अपरं, परस्तात्, उत्तरतस्, ततस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

again
AGAIN, adv. पुनर्, पुनरपि, भूयस् ind.<BR>— (Moreover) अन्यच्च, किञ्च,<BR>इतरम् indec.<BR>— (On the other hand) अन्यपक्षे, पुनर्.<BR>— (Repeat-<BR>edly) मुहुस्, पुनःपुनर्, असकृत्, भूयो भूयस्, वारंवारं.<BR>— (Further, in<BR>argument) अङ्गं.<BR>— (As much again) द्विगुणः -णा -णं.<BR>— (Back<BR>again, as re in English or Latin) प्रति.<BR>— (In return for) प्रति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

against
AGAINST, prep. प्रति, अभि.<BR>— (Opposed to) विरुद्धः -द्धा -द्धं, प्रतिकूलः<BR>-ला -लं, विपक्षः -क्षा -क्षं.<BR>— (Over against) अभिमुखं, प्रतिमुखं,<BR>सम्मुखं; ‘against the wind,’ प्रतिवातं, वाताभिमुखं; ‘against the<BR>stream,’ प्रतिसोतस् ind. ‘Against’ may be expressed by<BR>अर्थे or अर्थं, in such phrases as ‘one should store up<BR>money against misfortune,’ आपदर्थे धनं रक्षेत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

agape
AGAPE, adv. जृम्भमाणः -णा -णं, विस्मयोत्फुल्लनयनः -ना -नं, फुल्ललोचनः<BR>-ना -नं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

agaric
AGARIC, s. वृक्षरुहः छत्राकविशेषः, तरुरोही, औषधीयछत्राकविशेषः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

agastya
AGASTYA, s. (A celebrated Saint, son of Mitra and Varuna,<BR>and regent of the star Canopus) अगस्त्यः, मैत्रावारुणिः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

agate
AGATE, s. रत्नविशेषः, नानावर्णः प्रस्तरविशेषः, नानाछायान्वितः प्रस्तरविशेषः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

age
AGE, s. (Period) युगं, कालः, समयः.<BR>— (Life) आयुः n. (स्), जीवितकालः<BR>वयः n. (स्).<BR>— (Age of the world) कल्पः.<BR>— (Old age) वृद्धत्वं,<BR>वार्द्धकं, वृद्धभावः; ‘a youth who has come of age,’ व्यवहारप्राप्तः,<BR>व्यवहारज्ञः; ‘a son twenty years of age,’ विंशतिवर्षीयः पुत्रः;<BR>‘of the same age,’ समानवयस्कः -स्का -स्कं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aged
AGED, a. वृद्धः -द्धा -द्धं, जीर्णः -र्णा -र्णं, प्राचीनः -ना -नं, वयोगतः -ता -तं,<BR>आयुषः -षी -षं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=010-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

agency
AGENCY, s. (State of an agent) कर्त्तृत्वं, कर्त्तृकत्वं.<BR>— (Operation)<BR>कारणत्वं, हेतुता, कारणं; ‘human agency,’ पौरुषेयत्वं.<BR>— (Office<BR>of a deputy) नियोगिपदं, नियोगित्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

agent
AGENT, s. (Doer) कर्त्ता m. (र्त्तृ), कर्त्तृकः, कारः, कारकः, करः in<BR>comp.<BR>— (A deputy) नियोगी m. (न्), प्रतिपुरुषः, कार्य्याधीशः,<BR>प्रतिनिधिः m.<BR>— (That which has the power of operating)<BR>हेतुकः, हेतुः m., कारणं, साधनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=011-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

agglomerate
