and
AND, conj. च placed after the word which it connects with<BR>another. In many cases ‘and’ may be omitted in San-<BR>skrit, and the connection expressed by the use of the<BR>indeclinable participle; as, ‘the beasts assembled and<BR>informed the lion,’ पशुभिर्मिलित्वा सिंहो विज्ञप्तः.<BR>— (Moreover)<BR>अपिच, किञ्च, अपरं, अन्यच्च.<BR>— (And then) अथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

