approaching
APPROACHING, a. (Near at hand) उपस्थितः -ता -तं, समुपस्थितः<BR>-ता -तं, आसन्नः -न्ना -न्नं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

approbation
APPROBATION, s. सम्मतिः f. or -तं, अनुमतिः f. or -तं, प्रशंसा, प्रसादः,<BR>मनःसन्तोषः, ग्रहणं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

appropriate
To APPROPRIATE, v. a. (To consign to some particular use)<BR>प्रयुज् (c. 7. -युनक्ति -युंक्ते -योक्तुं, caus. -योजयति -यितुं), उपयुज्, विनियुज्.<BR>— (To claim to one's self by an exclusive right) स्वीकृ,<BR>स्वीयमिति or ममेति वद् (c. 1. वदति वदितुं), स्वकीयं -यां -यं or<BR>आत्मीयं -यां -यं or स्वाधीनं -नां -नं or आत्माधीनं -नां -नं or आत्नसात्<BR>कृ, स्वस्वत्वं बुध् in caus. (बोधयति -यितुं), or ज्ञा in caus. (ज्ञाप-<BR>यति -यितुं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

appropriate
APPROPRIATE, a. (Suited to the occasion) प्रस्तावसदृशः -शी -शं.<BR>— (Belonging peculiarly) आत्मनीनः -ना -नं, स्वकीयः -या -यं, सम्बन्धी<BR>-न्धिनी -न्धि (न्), सम्बन्धकः -का -कं, विशेषकः -का -कं, जनीनः -ना -नं.<BR>—<BR>(Suitable) युक्तः -क्ता -क्तं, योग्यः -ग्या -ग्यं, सङ्गतः -ता -तं, उपयोगी -गिनी<BR>-गि (न्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

appropriated
APPROPRIATED, p. p. (Made one's own) आत्मसात्कृतः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

appropriately
APPROPRIATELY, adv. युक्तं, यथायोग्यं, यथोचितं, यथातथा, स्थाने.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

