aspect
ASPECT, s. (Appearance, look) रूपं, आकारः, आकृतिः f., आभा,<BR>मूर्त्तिः f.<BR>— (Countenance) वदन्रं.<BR>— (State) अवस्था, दशा.<BR>— (Act<BR>of beholding) आलोकनं, दर्शनं, निरीक्षणं.<BR>— (Relation) सम्पर्कः,<BR>सम्बन्धः.<BR>— (Situation) अवस्थानं.<BR>— (Disposition of a planet) दशा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aspen
ASPEN, s. स्फुरितपत्रशीलो वृक्षविशेषः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aspen
ASPEN, a. (Like the aspen-tree) पूर्व्वोक्तवृक्षोपमः -मा -मं.<BR>— (Made<BR>of the aspen) पूर्व्वोक्तवृक्षनिर्म्मितः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

asperity
ASPERITY, s. (Unevenness of surface) रूक्षता, असमानत्वं, वैषम्यं.<BR>(Of temper) कर्कशत्वं, अरुन्तुदत्वं, स्वभावकटुता.<BR>— (Sharpness)<BR>तैक्ष्ण्यं, तीव्रता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

asperse
To ASPERSE, v. a. (To sprinkle) सिच् (c. 6. सिञ्चति -ते, सेक्तुं), निषिच्,<BR>संसिच्, उक्ष् (c. 1. उक्षति, उक्षितुं), अभ्युक्ष्, प्रोक्ष्, समुक्ष्.<BR>— (To<BR>calumniate) अवक्षिप् (c. 6. -क्षिपति -क्षेप्तुं), अधिक्षिप्; कलङ्क<BR>(nom. कलङ्कयति -यितुं), कलङ्कं कृ, परिवद् (c. 1. -वदति -वदितुं),<BR>अपवद्; अभिशप् (c. 1. -शपति -ते -शप्तुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aspersed
ASPERSED, p. p. (Sprinkled) सिक्तः -क्ता -क्तं, प्रोक्षितः -ता -तं.<BR>— (Ca-<BR>lumniated) अवक्षिप्तः -प्ता -प्तं, कलङ्कितः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

asperser
ASPERSER, s. कलङ्ककरः, परिवादकः, अपवादकः, अवक्षेपकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aspersion
ASPERSION, s. (Sprinkling) सेकः, सेचनं, निषेकः, प्रोक्षणं, श्च्योतः,<BR>प्राधारः.<BR>— (Calumny) अपवादः, कलङ्कः, अवक्षेपः, क्षेपः, गुणनिन्दा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aspirant
ASPIRANT, s. अर्थी m. (न्), प्रार्थयिता m. (तृ), आकाङ्क्षी m. (न्),<BR>कुतूहली m. (न्), अभिलाषुकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aspirate
ASPIRATE, s. महाप्राणः, महाप्राणसूचकं चिह्नं.<BR>— (The soft aspirate)<BR>अभिनिष्ठानं, अल्पप्राणः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aspirate
To ASPIRATE, v. n. महाप्राणेन उच्चर् in caus. (-चारयति -यितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aspirated
ASPIRATED, p. p. महाप्राणेन उच्चारितः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aspiration
ASPIRATION, s. (An ardent wish) आकाङ्क्षा, लालसा, महाकाङ्क्षा<BR>कौतूहलं, स्पृहा, अभिरुचिः f., अभिलाषः.<BR>— (Pronunciation with<BR>a full breath) महाप्राणेन उच्चारणं, महाप्राणः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aspire to
