AVARICIOUSLY, adv. लोभेन, लोभात्, सलोभं, कार्पण्येन, कृपणं, अतिकाङ्क्षया.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

avaunt
AVAUNT, interj. अपैहि, अपसर, दूरम् अपसर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

avenge
To AVENGE, v. a. प्रतिकृ (c. 8. -करोति -कुरुते -कर्त्तुं), परिष्कृ, प्रतिहिंस्<BR>(c. 1. -हिंसति, c. 7. हिनस्ति -हिंसितुं), प्रतीकारं or प्रतिहिंसां कृ.<BR>—<BR>(To punish) दण्ड् (c. 10. दण्डयति -यितुं).<BR>— (To wipe out a<BR>grudge) वैरं शुघ् in caus. (शोधयति -यितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

