AVERMENT, s. दृढवाक्यं, दृढवचनं, दृढोक्तिः f., स्थिरवचनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

averse
AVERSE, a. विरक्तः -क्ता -क्तं, प्रतिकूलः -ला -लं, विपरीतः -ता -तं, विमतः<BR>-ता -तं, विमनीभूतः -ता -तं, द्वेषी -षिणी -षि (न्), वैरी -रिणी -रि<BR>(न्).<BR>— (To be averse) विरञ्ज् in pass. (-रज्यते), अपावृत् (c. 1.<BR>-वर्त्तते -वर्त्तितुं), प्रतीप (nom. प्रतीपायते).<BR>— (Averting the face)<BR>पराङ्मुखः -खी -खं, विमुखः -खी -खं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aversely
AVERSELY, adv. निष्कामं, प्रतिकूलं, विपरीतं, विरक्तं, विरक्त्या.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

averseness
AVERSENESS, AVERSION, s. वैरक्त्यं, विरक्तिः f., निग्रहः, प्रतिकूलता,<BR>विमतिः f., पराङ्मुखता, वैमुख्यं, वैपरीत्यं, अप्रियता, अप्रीतिः f., द्वेष्यताः<BR>‘aversion to business.’ कार्य्यप्रद्वेषः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

avert
To AVERT, v. a. अपवृत् in caus. (-वर्त्तयति -यितुं), व्यावृत्, निवृत्,<BR>विनिवृत्, निवृ in caus. (-वारयति -यितुं), प्रतिवृ, अपानुद् (c. 6.<BR>-नुदति -नोत्तुं), व्यपानुद्, विमुखीकृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

averted
AVERTED, p. p. (Having the face averted) पराङ्मुखः -खी -खं,<BR>विमुखः -खी -खं, विमुखीकृतः -ता -तं, विमुखी -खिनी -खि (न्), पराचीनः<BR>-ना -नं.<BR>— (Kept off) निवारितः -ता -तं, व्यावृत्तः -त्ता -त्तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aviary
AVIARY, s. विटङ्कः, पञ्जरं, पिञ्जरं, वीतंसः, कपोतपालिका, पक्षिशाला,<BR>कुलायिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

avidity
AVIDITY, s. अतिक्षुधा, गृघ्रता, गर्द्धः, अतिस्पृहा, कौतूहलं, लालसा, अतिलोभः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

avocation
AVOCATION, s. (Calling aside, withdrawing) अपकर्षणं, आकर्षः,<BR>अपहरणं.<BR>— (Business that calls aside) कार्य्यं, कर्म्म n. (न्),<BR>विकर्म्म n. (न्), व्यापारः, व्यवसायः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

avoid
To AVOID, v. a. वृज् in caus. (वर्जयति -यितुं), परिवृज्, विवृज्; परिहृ<BR>(c. 1. -हरति -ते -हर्त्तुं); प्रोज्झ् (c. 6. -उज्झति -उज्झितुं); हा (c. 3.<BR>जहाति, हातुं); त्यज् (c. 1. त्यजति, त्यक्तुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

avoidable
AVOIDABLE, a. (To be avoided) परिहरणीयः -या -यं, परिहर्त्तव्यः -व्या<BR>-व्यं, परित्याज्यः -ज्या -ज्यं, हेयः -या -यं, हातव्यः -व्या -व्यं, त्याज्यः -ज्या -ज्यं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

avoidance
AVOIDANCE, s. त्यागः, परित्यागः, परिहारः, परिहरणं, प्रतिहरणं, वर्जनं,<BR>प्रोज्झनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

avoided
AVOIDED, p. p. परिहृतः -ता -तं, त्यक्तः -क्ता -क्तं, परित्यक्तः -क्ता -क्तं, विवर्ज्जितः<BR>-ता -तं, प्रोज्झितः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

avouch
To AVOUCH, v. a. (To affirm) दर्ढ्येन or स्थैर्य्येण or शपथेन वद् (c. 1.<BR>वदति, वदितुं).<BR>— (To vindicate, assert any thing in favour of<BR>another) परार्थं प्रतिवद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

avow
To AVOW, v. a. (To confess) स्वीकृ, अङ्गीकृ, ऊरीकृ, अनुभाष् (c. 1.<BR>-भाषते -भाषितुं).<BR>— (To declare openly) प्रकाशं or व्यक्तं वद् (c. 1.<BR>वदति, वदितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

avowed
AVOWED, p. p. स्वीकृतः -ता -तं, अङ्गीकृतः -ता -तं, व्यक्तोदितः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

avowedly
AVOWEDLY, adv. प्रकाशं, व्यक्तं, प्रकटं, अगूढं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

await
To AWAIT, v. a. अपेक्ष (c. 1. -ईक्षते -ईक्षितुं), उदीक्ष्, प्रतीक्ष्; प्रतिपाल्<BR>(c. 10. -पालयति -यितुं), उद्दृश् (c. 1. -पश्यति -द्रष्टुं), अपेक्षां कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

awake
To AWAKE, AWAKEN, v. a. जागृ in caus. (जागरयति -यितुं), बुध् in<BR>caus. (बोधयति -यितुं), प्रबुध्, प्रतिबुध्, विबुध्; निद्रां भञ्ज् (c. 7. भनक्ति,<BR>भंक्तुं), निद्राभङ्गं कृ.<BR>— (To incite) उत्था in caus. (-थापयति -यितुं),<BR>उत्सह् in caus. (-साहयति -यितुं), प्रोत्सह्; उत्तिज् (c. 10. -तेजयति -यितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

awake
To AWAKE, v. n. जागृ (c. 2. जागर्त्ति, जागरितुं), प्रजागृ; बुध् (c. 4.<BR>बुध्यते, बोद्धुं), अनुबुध्, प्रबुध्, प्रतिबुध्, विबुध्, प्रतिसम्बुध्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

awake
AWAKE, a. जागरः -रा -रं, प्रबुद्धः -द्धा -द्धं, प्रतिबुद्धः -द्धा -द्धं, विप्रबुद्धः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-b" target="_blank">Page034-b+ 51</a>]<BR>-द्धा -द्धं, प्रजागरः -रा -रं, उन्निद्रः -द्रा -द्रं; ‘that which keeps<BR>one awake at night,’ रात्रिजागरदः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

awakened
AWAKENED, p. p. जागरितः -ता -तं, प्रबोधितः -ता -तं, निद्राभङ्गः -ङ्गा -ङ्गं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

awakening
AWAKENING, s. प्रबोधनं, प्रबोधः, निद्राभञ्जनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

award
To AWARD, v. a. दा in caus. (दापयति -यितुं), तीर् (c. 10. तीरयति -यितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

award
AWARD, s. (Judgment, sentence) विचारः, निर्णयः, निष्पत्तिः f.,<BR>तीरणं, समाधानं, दण्डः, आज्ञा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

awarded
AWARDED, p. p. दापितः -ता -तं, तीरितः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

awarder
AWARDER, s. विचारकः, निर्णेता m. (तृ), दापकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aware
AWARE, a. (Excited to consciousness) विज्ञापितः -ता -तं, बोधितः<BR>-ता -तं.<BR>— (Knowing) वेदी -दिनी -दि (न्), ज्ञः -ज्ञा -ज्ञं in comp.<BR>—<BR>(Vigilant, attentive) सावधानः -ना -नं, जागरः -रा -रं, -री -रिणी<BR>-रि (न्); ‘he is aware,’ वेत्ति, जानाति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

away
AWAY, a. and adv., expressed by the preposition अप.<BR>— (Ab-<BR>sent) परोक्षः -क्षा -क्षं, स्थानान्तरङ्गतः -ता -तं, अनुपस्थितः -ता -तं, अवि-<BR>द्यमानः -ना -नं.<BR>— (Far away) दूरस्थः -स्था -स्थं, दूरस्थायी -यिनी -यि (न्).<BR>— (Come along) यातु.<BR>— (Begone!) अपैहि, अपसर, हूम्; ‘away<BR>with this fear,’ अलम् अनया शङ्कया.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

awe
AWE, s. आदरः, सम्भ्रमः, विस्मयः, त्रासः, आतङ्कः, आदरप्रयुक्तं भयं.<BR>—<BR>(To stand in awe of) भी (c. 3. बिभेति, भेतुं), त्रस् (c. 4. त्रस्यति,<BR>त्रसितुं) with abl., आदृ (c. 6. -द्रियते) with acc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

awe
To AWE, v. a. (To strike terror into) भी in caus. (भाययति or<BR>भीषयति -यितुं), त्रस् in caus. (त्रासयति -यितुं), व्याकुलीकृ, आकुलीकृ,<BR>सम्भ्रमेण उपहन् (c. 2. -हन्ति -हन्तुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

awe-struck
AWE-STRUCK, a. सम्भ्रान्तः -न्ता -न्तं, विस्मयाकुलः -ला -लं, भयविप्लुतः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

awful
AWFUL, a. घोरः -रा -रं, दारुणः -णा -णं, भैरवः -वा -वं, भीषणः -णा -णं,<BR>भयङ्करः -रा -रं, भयानकः -का -कं.<BR>— (Worshipful) आदरणीयः -या<BR>-यं, आदृत्यः -त्या -त्यं, पूज्यः -ज्या -ज्यं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

awfully
AWFULLY, adv. दारुणं, घोरं, यथा सम्भ्रम उत्पद्यते तथा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

awfulness
AWFULNESS, s. घोरता, दारुणता, भीषणं, भैरवं, भीष्मं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

awhile
AWHILE, adv. कियत्कालं, किञ्चित्कालं, अल्पकालं, इयत्कालं, मुहूर्त्तं, क्षणं,<BR>यत्किञ्चित्समयं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

awkward
AWKWARD, a. (Clumsy, unskilful) अदक्षः -क्षा -क्षं, अनाप्तः -प्ता -प्तं,<BR>अपटुः -टुः -टु, अक्षिप्रः -प्रा -प्रं, अविज्ञः -ज्ञा -ज्ञं, अकृती -तिनी -ति (न्).<BR>— (Inelegant) विरूपः -पी -पं, स्थूलः -ला -लं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

awkwardly
AWKWARDLY, adv. अपटु, अदक्षं, अक्षिप्रं, अनाप्तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

awkwardness
AWKWARDNESS, s. (Unskilfulness) अपाटवं, अपटुता, अदक्षत्वं, अक्षि-<BR>प्रत्वं.<BR>— (Inelegance) स्थूलता, वैरूप्यं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

