awry
AWRY, adv. तिरस्, साचि, तिर्य्यक्, कुटिलं, जिह्मं, अनृजु.<BR>— (Per-<BR>versely) विपरीतं, प्रतिकूलं, विलोमं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

axe
AXE, s. टङ्कः, कुठारः, परशुः m., परश्वधः, छिदिः f., वृक्षभिद् f., वृक्षभेदी<BR>m. (न्), स्वधितिः m.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

axiom
AXIOM, s. तत्त्वं, सूत्रं, सिद्धान्तः, आदेशः, वचनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

axiomatic
AXIOMATIC, a. सौत्रः -त्री -त्रं, सिद्धान्ती -न्तिनी -न्ति (न्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

axis
AXIS, s. अक्षः, ध्रुवः, मेरुः m.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

axle
AXLE, AXLE-TREE, s. अक्षाग्रं, अक्षदन्तः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ay
AY, adv. तथेति, एवं, हूम्, आम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

aye
AYE, adv. सर्व्वदा, सदा, नित्यं, नित्यदा, शाश्वतं, अजस्रं, शाश्वतीः समाः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

azure
AZURE, a. नीलः -ला -लं, नीलवर्णः, -र्णा -र्णं, आकाशवर्णः -र्णा -र्णं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

baa
To BAA, v. n. उ (c. 1. अवते, ओतुं), मेषवत् or उरभ्रवत् शब्दं कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

babble
To BABBLE, v. n. (To prattle like a child) बालवत् जल्प् (c. 1.<BR>जल्पति, जल्पितुं).<BR>— (To talk idly) जल्प्.<BR>— (To tell secrets) रहस्यं<BR>प्रकाश् in caus. (-काशयति -यितुं) or विख्या, in caus. (-ख्यापयति<BR>-यितुं), रहस्यभेदं कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

babble
BABBLE or BABBLING, s. जल्पः, जल्पनं, वावदूकता, बालवचनं, आख्यायिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

babbler
BABBLER, s. वाचालः, जल्पकः, उपजल्पी m. (न्), वाचाटः, जल्पाकः,<BR>वावदूकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

babe
BABE, BABY, s. बालः -ला, बालकः, शिशुः m., शावकः.<BR>— (At the<BR>breast) स्तनन्धयः, स्तनपाः m. (पा), क्षीरपः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

babel
BABEL, s. (Confusion) सङ्करः, साङ्कर्य्यं, तुमुलं, कोलाहलः, कालकीलः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

baboon
BABOON, s. वानरः, कपिः, मर्कटः, प्लवङ्गः, प्लवगः, शाखामृगः, बलीमुखः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

babyhood
BABYHOOD, s. बाल्यं, बालकत्वं, बालभावः, शैशवं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

babyish
BABYISH, a. बालकीयः -या -यं, बालिशः -शा -शं, बालेयः -यी -यं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bacchanalian
BACCHANALIAN, s. पानरतः, पानप्रसक्तः, मद्यपीतः, मद्यप्रियः, सम्पीतिरतः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bachelor
BACHELOR, s. (A man unmarried) अविवाहितः, अकृतदारः, अकृत-<BR>दारसङ्ग्रहः, अकृतविवाहः.<BR>— (One who takes his first degree)<BR>विद्यालये पूर्व्वपदप्राप्तः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

back
BACK, s. पृष्ठं, विग्रहावरं; ‘to turn the back, avert the face,’<BR>पराङ्मुखः -खी -खं or पराचीनः -ना -नं भू; ‘to turn back, away<BR>from,’ अपवृत् (c. 1. -वर्त्तते -वर्त्तितुं), विनिवृत्, अपावृत्, निवृत्; ‘turned<BR>back,’ विपरिवर्त्तितः -ता -तं; ‘at one's back, behind the back,’<BR>पृष्ठतस्; ‘behind one's back, in one's absence,’ परोक्षे.<BR>— (The hinder part) पृष्ठदेशः, पश्चाद्देशः, पश्चाद्भागः, पृष्ठं, नितम्बः;<BR>‘the back of the hand,’ करपृष्ठं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

back
BACK, adv. (To the place whence one came) commonly ex-<BR>pressed by प्रति prefixed; as, ‘to go back,’ प्रतिगम्; ‘come<BR>back,’ प्रत्यावृत्तः -त्ता -त्तं, पुनरागतः -ता -तं; ‘brought back,’<BR>प्रत्यानीतः -ता -तं.<BR>— (Backward from the present station)<BR>expressed by परा, प्रति, or पश्चात् prefixed; as, ‘to beat<BR>back,’ पराहन्, प्रत्याहन्.<BR>— (Again) expressed by पुनर्, प्रति,<BR>or अनु prefixed; as, ‘to give back,’ प्रतिदा.<BR>— (Kept back)<BR>निगृहीतः -ता -तं, निवारितः -ता -तं; ‘in the back-ground,’ दूरस्थः<BR>-स्था -स्थं, निभृते.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

back
To BACK, v. a. (To mount a horse) आरुह् (c. 1. -रोहति -रोढुं),<BR>अधिरुह्, समारुह्.<BR>— (To support, justify) रक्ष् (c. 1. रक्षति, रक्षितुं),<BR>अभिरक्ष्, संरक्ष्; पक्षपातं कृ, उपकृ, अनुग्रह् (c. 9. -गृह्लाति -ग्रहीतुं).<BR>—<BR>(To impel backwards) पराणुद् (c. 6. -णुदति -णोत्तुं), विपरीतं प्रणुद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

back
To BACK, v. n. (To go backwards) अपक्रम् (c. 1. -क्रामति, c. 4.<BR>-क्राम्यति, -क्रमितुं), व्यपक्रम्, परावृत् (c. 1. -वर्त्तते -वर्त्तितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

backbite
To BACKBITE, v. a. पृष्ठमांसं खाद् (c. 1. खादति, खादितुं).<BR>— (To slan-<BR>der) परिवद् (c. 1. -वदति -ते -वदितुं), अपवद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

backbiter
BACKBITER, s. पृष्ठमांसादः, परोक्षे अपवादकः, परिवादकः, पिशुनः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

backbiting
BACKBITING, s. परिवादः, अपवादः, पिशुनवाक्यं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

backbone
BACKBONE, s. कशेरुका, पृष्ठवंशः, पृष्ठास्थि n., रीढकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

backdoor
BACKDOOR, s. पक्षद्वारं, अन्तर्द्वारं, उपद्वारं, प्रच्छन्नं, पक्षकः, खडक्किका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

backgammon
BACKGAMMON, s. चर्म्मपट्टिकाक्रीडा.<BR>— (Backgammon-board) चर्म्म-<BR>पट्टिका, अष्टापदं, बध्नः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

backroom
BACKROOM, s. अन्तर्गृहं, अन्तःशाला, उपरोधकं, उपशाला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

backside
BACKSIDE, s. (The hinder part of any thing) पृष्ठदेशः, पश्चाद्देशः,<BR>पश्चाद्भागः, अधोदेशः.<BR>— (The hinder part of any animal) नि-<BR>तम्बः, पृष्ठं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

backslide
To BACKSLIDE, v. n. स्वधर्म्मात् परिभ्रंश् (c. 4. -भ्रश्यति -भ्रंशितुं) or च्यु (c. 1.<BR>च्यवते, च्योतुं), स्थधर्म्मं त्यज् (c. 1. त्यजति, त्यक्तुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

backslider
BACKSLIDER, s. धर्म्मच्युतः, धर्म्मभ्रष्टः, स्वधर्म्मत्यागी m. (न्), उन्मार्गगामी m.<BR>(न्), अन्यशाखकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

backstairs
BACKSTAIRS, s. उपसोपानं, अन्तःसोपानं, पक्षसोपानं, प्रच्छन्नसोपानं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

backward
BACKWARD or BACKWARDS, adv. Expressed by परा or प्रति pre-<BR>fixed; पश्चात्, प्रतीपं, विपरीतं, अवकटं; ‘to walk backwards and<BR>forwards,’ गतागतानि or प्रतिगतागतं or गमनागमने or यातायातं कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

backward
BACKWARD, a. (Unwilling) प्रतीपः -पा -पं, अनिच्छः -च्छा -च्छं, अस-<BR>म्मतः -ता -तं, अनिच्छकः -का -कं.<BR>— (Sluggish) मन्दः -न्दा -न्दं, अलसः<BR>-सा -सं, विलम्बी -म्बिनी -म्बि (न्).<BR>— (Dull of apprehension) मन्द-<BR>मतिः -तिः -ति.<BR>— (Late, after its time) अतीतकालः -ला -लं, अति-<BR>क्रान्तकालः -ला -लं, दीर्घकालीनः -ना -नं, दीर्घपक्वः -क्वा -क्वं, दीर्घपक्व-<BR>शीलः -ला -लं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

backwardness
BACKWARDNESS, s. (Unwillingness) अनिच्छा, अस्वीकारः, असम्मतिः f.<BR>— (Sluggishness) आलस्यं, मान्द्यं, विलम्बत्वं.<BR>— (Dulness) मन्दम-<BR>तिता.<BR>— (Lateness) दीर्घकालीनता, अतीतकालत्वं, दीर्घता, दीर्घपक्वता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bacon
BACON, s. वल्लूरं, शूकरस्य शुष्कमांसं,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bad
BAD, a. (Vicious, corrupt) पापः -पा -पं, दुष्टः -ष्टा -ष्टं, अधमः -मा -मं,<BR>नीचः -चा -चं, खलः -ला -लं, कुत्सितः -ता -तं, कदर्य्यः -र्य्या -र्य्यं.<BR>—<BR>(Not good) अभद्रः -द्रा -द्रं, असाधुः -धुः -धु, अधार्म्मिकः -की -कं, असारः<BR>-रा -रं, असन् -सती -सत् (त्).<BR>— (Worthless) निर्गुणः -णा -णं.<BR>—<BR>(Hurtful, unwholesome) हिंस्रः -स्रा -स्रं, अहितः -ता -तं, अपथ्यः<BR>-थ्या -थ्यं, रुजाकरः -रा -रं.<BR>— (Sick) रोगी -गिणी -गि (न्), व्याधितः<BR>-ता -तं.<BR>— (Sick of) आतुरः -रा -रं, आर्त्तः -र्त्ता -र्त्तं in comp.<BR>— (Un-<BR>fortunate) विपन्नः -न्ना -न्नं, दुर्गतः -ता -तं. ‘Bad,’ as a general<BR>word, is often expressed by दुर्, कु, कत्, or sometimes by<BR>वि or अप prefixed; as, ‘a bad road,’ दुरध्वः, कुपथं, कदध्वा<BR>m. (न्), विमार्गः; ‘a bad man,’ दुर्ज्जनः, दुराचारः; ‘bad wea-<BR>ther,’ दुर्द्दिनं; ‘bad food,’ कदन्नं; ‘bad thing,’ अपद्रव्यं; ‘bad<BR>conduct,’ दुर्णयः, कुकर्म्म n. (न्), अपकर्म्म n. (न्); ‘bad policy,’<BR>अनीतिः f.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

badge
BADGE, s. चिह्नं, लिङ्गं, व्यञ्जनं, लक्षणं.<BR>— (Badge of rank) पदचिह्नं,<BR>पदसूचकं चिह्नं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

badger
BADGER, s. गर्त्तवासी जन्तुविशेषः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

badinage
BADINAGE, s. लघुवाक्यं, लघूक्तिः f., हास्यवाक्यं, नर्म्म n. (न्), टट्टरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

badly
BADLY, adv. दुष्ठु, दुष्टं, अभद्रं. Often expressed by दुर्, कु, अप<BR>prefixed; as, ‘badly managed,’ दुर्णीतः -ता -तं; ‘badly<BR>shaped,’ कुरूपः -पी -पं; ‘badly-behaved,’ दुःशीलः, कुशीलः;<BR>‘badly done,’ दुष्कृतः -ता -तं, अपकृतः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

badness
BADNESS, s. दुष्टता, दौष्ठवं, निर्गुणत्वं, नीचता, अभद्रता, कदर्य्यत्वं.<BR>— (Of<BR>character) दुरात्मता, दुराचारत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

baffle
To BAFFLE, v. a. (To make ineffectual) मोधीकृ, निष्फल् (nom.<BR>निष्फलयति -यितुं), खण्ड् (c. 10. खण्डयति -यितुं), व्यर्थीकृ, प्रतिहन्<BR>(c. 2. -हन्ति -हन्तुं), मुधा कृ, वृथा कृ.<BR>— (To defeat) पराभू (c. 1.<BR>-भवति -भवितुं), पराजि (c. 1. -जयति -ते -जेतुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

baffled
BAFFLED, p. p. प्रतिहतः -ता -तं, मोघशः -शा -शं, मनोहतः -ता -तं, प्रति-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=036-a" target="_blank">Page036-a+ 51</a>]<BR>बद्धः -द्धा -द्धं, भग्नोद्यमः -मा -मं, खण्डितः -ता -तं, खण्डिताशंसः -सा -सं,<BR>पराजितः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bag
BAG, s. शाणपुटः -टं, स्यूतः, स्योतः, कोषः, आधारः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bag
To BAG, v. a. (To put into a bag) शाणपुटे or स्यूते or कोषे निधा<BR>(c. 3. -दधाति -धातुं) or निविश् in caus. (-वेशयति -यितुं).<BR>— (To<BR>make tumid) श्वि in caus. (श्वाययति -यितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bag
To BAG, v. n. (To swell out like a bag) स्यूतवत् लम्ब् (c. 1. लम्बते,<BR>लम्बितुं), प्रलम्ब्, or पॄ in pass. (पूर्य्यते), or श्वि (c. 1. श्वयति, श्वयितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bagatelle
BAGATELLE, s. स्वल्पविषयः, अल्पमूल्पद्रव्यं, क्षुद्रद्रव्यं, क्षुद्रविष्रयः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

baggage
BAGGAGE, s. (The furniture of an army) सामग्री -ग्र्यं, भारः, उप-<BR>करणं, परिच्छदः.<BR>— (A worthless woman) पुंश्चली f., वेश्या, बन्धकी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bagnio
BAGNIO, s. (A house for bathing) स्नानागारं, गात्रमार्ज्जनशाला.<BR>—<BR>(A brothel) वेश्यालयः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bail
BAIL, s. (Security for one's appearance) दर्शनप्रतिभूः m., दर्शनप्राति-<BR>भाव्यं, प्रतिनिधिः m., प्रतिभूः m., प्रातिभाव्यं, पारिभाव्यं, लग्नकः, न्यासः,<BR>अन्वाधिः m., बन्धकः, तृणमत्कुणः.<BR>— (The person who gives the<BR>security) प्रतिनिधिः m., प्रतिभूः m., लग्नकदायी m. (न्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bail
