To BEFOOL, v. a. मुह् in caus. (-मोहयति -यितुं), व्यामुह्, विप्रमुह्, भ्रम्<BR>in caus. (भ्रमयति -यितुं), वञ्च् in caus. (वञ्चयति -ते -यितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

before
BEFORE, prep. and adv. प्र, अभि prefixed.<BR>— (In the front of, not<BR>behind) अग्रे, अग्रतस्, पुरस्, पुरतस्, पुरस्तात्, अभितस्, प्रतिमुखं,<BR>अभिमुखं; ‘going before,’ पुरोगः -गा -गं, अग्रेसरः -रा -रं; ‘before<BR>the fire,’ अध्यग्नि.<BR>— (In the presence of) साक्षात्, प्रत्यक्षे, अग्रे,<BR>समक्षं, प्रतिमुखं; ‘he took them before the king,’ तान् राज-<BR>समीपम् आनीतवान्.<BR>— (In the sight of, before the face) समक्षं,<BR>प्रत्यक्षं, प्रत्यक्षतस्, साक्षात्, सम्मुखं; ‘before many persons,’ बहु-<BR>जनसमक्षं.<BR>— (Earlier in time, sooner than) प्राक्, पूर्व्वं, with the<BR>abl. c.; अग्रे; ‘before offering the cakes,’ पिण्डदानात् पूर्व्वं;<BR>‘before the appointed time,’ निरूपितसमयात् पूर्व्वं or प्राग् वि-<BR>हितकालात्; ‘he knows your necessities before you ask,’<BR>यत् तव प्रयोजनं तद् याच्ञातः पूर्व्वं जानाति; ‘before dinner,’ भोज-<BR>नात् पूर्व्वं; ‘before the event,’ प्राग् घटनात्; ‘before me,’<BR>मदग्रे.<BR>— (In time past) पुरा, पूर्व्वं, पूव्वकाले.<BR>— (As yet, hitherto)<BR>अद्य यावत्, अद्यपर्य्यन्तं, एतत् कालं यावत्, अद्यापि.<BR>— (Already)<BR>तत्पूर्व्वं, प्राग् वर्त्तमानकालात्; ‘before mentioned,’ पूर्व्वोक्तः -क्ता -क्तं,<BR>प्रागुक्तः -क्ता -क्तं, पूर्व्वचोदितः -ता -तं; ‘the day before yesterday,’<BR>अपरेद्युस्; ‘before and after,’ पूर्व्वोत्तरं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

before-hand
BEFORE-HAND, adv. पूर्व्वे, अग्रे, पूर्व्वं, अग्रतस्, पूर्व्वतस्; ‘determining<BR>beforehand,’ अग्रनिरूपणं; ‘to taste beforehand,’ पूर्व्वस्वादनं कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

before-time
BEFORE-TIME, adv. पुरा, पूर्व्वं, पूर्व्वकाले, गतकाले.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

befoul
To BEFOUL, v. a. मलिन (nom. मलिनयति -यितुं), दुष् in caus. (दूष-<BR>यति -यितुं), कलुष (nom. कलुपयति -यितुं), आविल (nom. आविल-<BR>यति -यितुं), समलं -लां -लं कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

befriend
To BEFRIEND, v. a. मित्र (nom. मित्रीयते -यितुं), उपकृ (c. 8. -करोति<BR>-कुरुते -कर्त्तुं), अनुग्रह् (c. 9. -गृह्लाति -ग्रहीतुं), साहाय्यं कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

befriended
BEFRIENDED, p. p. कृतोपकारः -रा -रं, उपकृतः -ता -तं, अनुगृहीतः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beg
To BEG, v. a. (To ask) अर्थ् (c. 10. अर्थयते -यितुं), अभ्यर्थ्, प्रार्थ्,<BR>सम्प्रार्थ्, याच् (c. 1. याचति -ते, याचितुं), अभियाच्, प्रयाच्, सम्प्रयाच्,<BR>संयाच्.<BR>— (To ask alms) भिक्ष् (c. 1. भिक्षते, भिक्षितुं).<BR>— (To beg<BR>as a favour) वृ (c. 9. वृणीते, वरितुं, वरीतुं) or in caus. (वारयति<BR>-यितुं) with 2 acc., प्रसद् in caus. (-सादयते -यितुं).<BR>— (To beg<BR>for pardon) क्षम् in caus. (क्षमयति -यितुं) with acc. of the pers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beg
To BEG, v. n. भिक्ष् (c. 1. भिक्षते, भिक्षितुं), भैक्ष्यं चर् (c. 1. चरति,<BR>चरितुं), भिक्षाटनं कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beget
To BEGET, v. a. जन् in caus. (जनयति -यितुं), विजन्, सञ्जन्, प्रसु (c. 2.<BR>-सूते, c. 4. -सूयते -सोतुं).<BR>— (To produce, cause) उत्पद् in caus.<BR>(-पादयति -यितुं).<BR>— (To create) सृज् (c. 6. मृजति, स्रष्टुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

begetter
BEGETTER, s. जनकः, जननः, जनयिता m. (तृ), जनिता m. (तृ), जन्मदः,<BR>सुती m. (न्), उत्पादकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beggar
BEGGAR, s. (One who lives on alms) भिक्षुः m., भिक्षुकः -की f.,<BR>भिक्षोपजीवी m. (न्), भिक्षाचरः, दरिद्रः.<BR>— (A petitioner) प्रार्थकः,<BR>अर्थी m. (न्), -र्थिनी f., प्रार्थयिता m. (तृ), याचकः, याचनकः, मार्गणः<BR>-णकः, वनीयकः.<BR>— (In ragged garments) कर्पटी m. (न्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beggar
To BEGGAR, v. a. दरिद्रीकृ, सर्व्वस्वं हृ (c. 1. हरति, हर्त्तुं), धनाद् भ्रंश् in<BR>caus. (भ्रंशयति -यितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beggared
BEGGARED, a. दरिद्रितः -ता -तं, धनच्युतः -ता -तं, हृतसर्व्वस्वः -स्वा -स्वं,<BR>परिक्षीणः -णा -णं, गतवित्तः -त्ता -त्तं, नष्टार्थः -र्था -र्थं, गतविभवः -वा -वं,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=044-b" target="_blank">Page044-b+ 51</a>]<BR>गतलक्ष्मीकः -का -कं, गतश्रीकः -का -कं; ‘he is beggared,’ श्रमणायते.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beggarly
BEGGARLY, a. (Indigent) दरिद्रः -द्रा -द्रं, निर्धनः -ना -नं, दुर्गतः -ता<BR>-तं, कृपणः -णा -णं, दीनः -ना -नं.<BR>— (Mean) तुच्छः -च्छा -च्छं, नीचः<BR>-चा -चं, अपकृष्टः -ष्टा -ष्टं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beggarly
BEGGARLY, adv. कृपणं, कार्पण्येन, दीनं, नीचप्रकारेण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beggary
BEGGARY, s. (Indigence) दरिद्रता, दारिद्रं -द्र्यं, निर्धनता, परिक्षीणता,<BR>कार्पण्यं, अर्थिता, दीनता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

begged
BEGGED, p. p. प्रार्थितः -ता -तं याचितः -ता -तं भिक्षितः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

begging
BEGGING, (Act of) s. भिक्षा, भिक्षाटनं, भैक्षचर्य्या, अर्थना, अभ्यर्थना,<BR>याचना, याच्ञा, प्रार्थनं -ना, अर्द्दना, अभिशस्तिः f.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

begin
To BEGIN, v. a. and n. आरभ् (c. 1. -रभते -रब्धुं), अभ्यारभ्, प्रारभ्,<BR>समारभ्, प्रक्रम् (c. 1. -क्रमते -क्रमितुं), उपक्रम्, समुपक्रम्, प्रवृत् (c. 1.<BR>-वर्त्तते -वर्त्तितुं); प्रकृ, सम्प्रकृ; प्रस्तु (c. 2. -स्तौति -स्तोतुं); ‘he be-<BR>gan to cut,’ छेत्तुं प्रवृत्तः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beginner
BEGINNER, s. (One who begins) आरब्धा m. (ब्धृ), आरम्भकः, उप-<BR>क्रन्ता m. (न्तृ), उपक्रमिता m. (तृ), उपक्रमकारी m. (न्).<BR>— (A novice)<BR>नवछात्रः, नूतनशिष्पः, प्राथमकल्पिकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beginning
BEGINNING, s. आरम्भः, प्रारम्भः, समारम्भः, प्रारब्धिः f., आदिः m.<BR>उपक्रमः, प्रक्रमः, उद्घातः, उपोद्घातः, अभ्यादानं.<BR>— (Origin, source)<BR>मूलं, योनिः m. f., उद्भवः, प्रभवः, गर्भः, जन्म n. (न्).<BR>— (Rudiments)<BR>आरम्भः.<BR>— (Elementary property) कारणगुणः; ‘without be-<BR>ginning,’ अनाद्यः -द्या -द्यं; ‘from beginning to end,’ आद्यन्तं,<BR>आप्रथमात् शेषं यावत्; ‘beginning, middle, and end,’ आदिम-<BR>ध्यावसानं; ‘beginning with,’ आदि, आद्य affixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

begird
To BEGIRD, v. a. परिवेष्ट् (c. 1. -वेष्टते -वेष्टितुं), अवरुध् (c. 7. -रुणद्धि -रोद्धुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

begirt
BEGIRT, p. p. परिवेष्टितः -ता -तं, परिगतः -ता -तं, वलयितः -ता -तं,<BR>आवृतः -ता -तं; ‘begirt with the sea,’ समुद्रमेखलः -ला -लं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

begone
BEGONE, interj. अपैहि, अपसर, दूरम् अपसर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

begotten
BEGOTTEN, p. p. जनितः -ता -तं, उत्पादितः -ता -तं, प्रसूतः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

begrease
To BEGREASE, v. a. वसया or स्नेहेन or तैलेन or घृतेन लिप् (c. 6.<BR>लिम्पति -लेप्तुं), स्निग्धीकृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

begrime
To BEGRIME, v. a. मलेन दुष् in caus. (दूषयति -यितुं), मलिन (nom<BR>मलिनयति -यितुं), कलुष (nom. कलुषयति -यितुं), कलङ्क (nom. कल<BR>ङ्कयति -यितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

begrimed
BEGRIMED, p. p. मलदूषितः -ता -तं, कलुषितः -ता -तं, कलङ्कितः -ता -तं<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

begrudge
To BEGRUDGE, v. a. स्पृह् (c. 10. स्पृहयति -यितुं), असूय (nom. असूयति<BR>-यितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beguile
To BEGUILE, v. a. मुह् in caus. (मोहयति -यितुं), विप्रमुह्, व्यामुह्,<BR>वञ्च् in caus. (वञ्चयते -यितुं), परिवञ्च्, प्रवञ्च्, भ्रम् in caus. (भ्रमयति<BR>-यितुं), प्रलभ् (c. 1. -लभते -लब्धुं), विप्रलभ्, आकृष् (c. 1. -कर्षति<BR>-क्रष्टुं -कर्षितुं).<BR>— (To beguile the time) विनुद् in caus. (-नोद-<BR>यति -यितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beguiled
BEGUILED, p. p. मोहितः -ता -तं, विमोहितः -ता -तं, वञ्चितः -ता -तं,<BR>विप्रलब्धः -ब्धा -ब्धं, विमूढः -ढा -ढं, प्रपञ्चितः -ता -तं, प्रलोभितः -ता -तं,<BR>विलोभितः -ता -तं, प्रतारितः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

begun
BEGUN, p. p. आरब्धः -ब्धा -ब्धं, प्रारब्धः -ब्धा -ब्धं, उपक्रान्तः -न्ता -न्तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

behalf
BEHALF, s. (In behalf of) अर्थं, अर्थे, हेतोः, हेतौ, कारणात्, निमित्ते,<BR>कृते, generally affixed to the crude of a noun; ‘on my<BR>behalf,’ मत्कृते or मदर्थे; ‘on behalf of (his) son,’ पुत्रहेतोः.<BR>— (Favour) अनुग्रहः, प्रसादः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

behave
To BEHAVE, v. n. चर् (c. 1. चरति, चरितुं), आचर्, समाचर्, वृत् (c. 1.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-a" target="_blank">Page045-a+ 51</a>]<BR>वर्त्तते, वर्त्तितुं); sometimes वृत्तिं is added; as, ‘in whatever<BR>way you behave towards them,’ यां वृत्तिं तेषु वर्त्तसे। वृत्तिम्<BR>अनुष्ठा (c. 1. -तिष्ठति -स्थातुं), व्यवहृ (c. 1. -हरति -हर्त्तुं).<BR>— (Well-be-<BR>haved) सदाचारयुक्तः -क्ता -क्तं, सदाचारवान् -वती -वत् (त्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

behaviour
BEHAVIOUR, s. वृत्तिः f., वृत्तं, आचारः, रीतिः f., व्यवहारः, चरित्रं,<BR>चरितं, आचरणं, गतिः f., चेष्टितं, स्थितिः f.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

behead
To BEHEAD, v. a. शिरः or मस्तकं छिद् (c. 7. छिनत्ति, छेत्तुं), विमस्तक<BR>(nom. विमस्तकयति -यितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beheaded
BEHEADED, p. p. विमस्तकितः -ता -तं, छिन्नमस्तः -स्ता -स्तं, -स्तकः -का -कं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beheading
BEHEADING (act of) s. शीर्षछेदः.<BR>— (Worthy of) शीर्षछेद्यः -द्या -द्यं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beheld
BEHELD, p. p. आलोकितः -ता -तं, दृष्टः -ष्टा -ष्टं, आलोचितः -ता -तं,<BR>ईक्षितः -ता -तं, ईक्ष्यमाणः -णा -णं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

behest
BEHEST, s. आज्ञा, आदेशः, निर्द्देशः, निदेशः, शासनं, वशं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

behind
BEHIND, prep. or adv. पश्चात्, अनु prefixed.<BR>— (Behind the back,<BR>at the back of) पृष्ठतस्; ‘following behind,’ अनुगामी -मिनी<BR>-मि (न्).<BR>— (Below, inferior) अधस्तात्, अधरस्तात्.<BR>— (Posterior)<BR>अवरतस्, अवरम्नात्.<BR>— (At a distance) दूरतस्, दूरे.<BR>— (The<BR>hinder part) पृष्ठदेशः, पश्चाद्देशः, पृष्ठं, नितम्बः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

behindhand
BEHINDHAND, adv. अतीतकालः -ला -लं, विलम्बी -म्बिनी -म्बि (न्),<BR>दीर्घकालीनः -ना -नं.<BR>— (Surpassed by another) अतिक्रान्तः -न्ता -न्तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

behold
To BEHOLD, v. a. दृश् (c. 1. पश्यति, द्रष्टुं), अभिदृश्, विदृश्, सन्दृश्; ईक्ष्<BR>(c. 1. ईक्षते, ईक्षितुं), समीक्ष्, वीक्ष्, अभिवीक्ष्, प्रेक्ष्, अभिप्रेक्ष्, सम्प्रेक्ष्,<BR>उदीक्ष्, अवेक्ष्, अन्वीक्ष्, अवलोक् (c. 10. -लोकयति -यितुं, c. 1. -लोकते<BR>-लोकितुं), आलोक्, समालोक्, विलोक्, लक्ष् (c. 10. लक्षयति -ते -यितुं),<BR>आलक्ष्, समालक्ष्, उपलक्ष्, संलक्ष्; आलोच् (c. 10. -लोचयति -यितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

behold
BEHOLD, interj. पश्य, प्रेक्षस्व<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beholden
To be BEHOLDEN, v. n. कृतोपकारस्मरणेन पराधीनः -ना -नं or परायत्तः<BR>-त्ता -त्तं भू, प्राप्तोपकारहेतोर् बद्धः -द्धा -द्धं or निबद्धः -द्धा -द्धं भू or<BR>अस्, कृतोपकारं ज्ञा (c. 9. जानाति, ज्ञातुं), प्रत्युपकारः करणीय इति<BR>ज्ञा, आप्राप्तोपकारमोक्षात् परवशं ज्ञा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beholder
BEHOLDER, s. प्रेक्षकः, द्रष्टा m. (ष्टृ), प्रेक्षमाणः, दर्शी m. (न्), पश्यन् m. (त्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

behoof
BEHOOF, s. अर्थः, फलं, लाभः, वृद्धिः f., विवृद्धिः f., फलोदयः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

behoveful
BEHOVEFUL, a. यथोचितः -ता -तं, योग्यः -ग्या -ग्यं, अर्थकरः -री -रं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

behoves
It BEHOVES, v. imp. Expressed by the future passive parti-<BR>ciple; as, ‘it behoves you to marry the damsel,’ त्वया कन्या<BR>वोढव्या; or by the potential mood, as, त्वं कन्यां वहेः; or<BR>by the use of the verb अर्ह् (c. 1. अर्हति), as त्वं कन्यां वोढुम्<BR>अर्हसि; ‘to act as it behoves one,’ यथोचितं कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

being
BEING, s. (A being) भूतं, सत्त्वः.<BR>— (A sentient being) प्राणी m.<BR>(न्), प्राणभृत् m. f. n., शरीरी m. (न्), देही m. (न्), जन्तुः m., जन्युः m.,<BR>चेतनः, जन्मी m. (न्).<BR>— (Existence) प्राणधारणं, असुधारणं, निश्व-<BR>सनप्रश्वसनं, सम्भवः, अस्ति ind., वृत्तिः f., सत्त्वं.<BR>— (Particular state)<BR>भावः, अवस्था, दशा, वृत्तिः f.<BR>— (Supreme Being) परमेश्वरः.<BR>—<BR>(Pres. part.) सन् सती सत् (त्), वर्त्तमानः -ना -नं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

being that
BEING THAT, conj. (Since) यतस्, यस्मात्, येन, इति हेतोः, यतोहेतोः.<BR>‘Being,’ is often expressed by the loc. c. of सत्, as, ‘the<BR>man being gone,’ पुरुषे गते सति; ‘it being so,’ एवं सति,<BR>तथात्वे, एवम्भूत्वा. ‘Being’ may also be expressed by the<BR>abl. c. of the abstract noun in such phrases as ‘he being<BR>a good man,’ सज्जनत्वात्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beitso
BEITSO, एवमस्तु, तथास्तु, भवतु, अस्त्वेवं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

belabour
To BELABOUR, v. a. तड् (c. 10. ताडयति -यितुं), हन् (c. 2. हन्ति, हन्तुं),<BR>अभिहन् अभ्याहन्, समाहन्; प्रहृ (c. 1. -हरति -हर्त्तुं).<BR>— (With a<BR>stick) वेत्राघातं कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

belay
To BELAY, v. a. (Block up) प्रतिरुघ् (c. 7. -रुणद्धि -रोद्धुं), उपरुध्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

belch
To BELCH, v. a. उद्वम् (c. 1. -वमति -वमितुं), उद्गॄ (c. 6. -गिरति -गरितुं -गरीतुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

belch
BELCH, BELCHING, s. उद्वमः, उद्वमनं, उद्गारः, उद्गिरणं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beldam
BELDAM, s. वृद्धा स्त्री, जरिणी, जरापरिणता स्त्री, कुट्टिनी, कुरूपी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beleaguer
To BELEAGUER, v. a. (To besiege) रुध् (c. 7. रुणद्धि, रोद्धुं), अवरुध्,<BR>उपरुध्; परिवेष्ट् (c. 1. -वेष्टते -वेष्टितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

beleaguered
BELEAGUERED, p. p. परिवेष्टितः -ता -तं, उपरुद्धः -द्धा -द्धं, बाधितः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

belfounder
BELFOUNDER, s. घण्टाकारी m. (न्), घण्टानिर्म्माणकर्त्ता m. (र्त्तृ), कांस्यकारः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

belfry
BELFRY, s. घण्टाताडनयोग्यं प्रासादशृङ्गं, घण्टास्थानं, घण्टाशाला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

belie
To BELIE, v. a. (To counterfeit, imitate) छल् (c. 10. छलयति -यितुं),<BR>छद्म or छद्मवेशं कृ, अनुकृ (c. 8. -करोति -कर्त्तुं).<BR>— (To charge any<BR>one with falsehood, to argue) अनृतं or असत्यं or मिथ्यावादं<BR>कस्मैचिद् आरुह् in caus. (-रोपयति -यितुं), पिशुन (nom. पिशुनयति<BR>-यितुं).<BR>— (To calumniate) परिवद् (c. 1. -वदति -वदितुं), अपवद्,<BR>कलङ्कं कृ, मिथ्याभियोगं कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

belief
BELIEF, s. (Credence) प्रत्ययः, विश्वासः, विश्रम्भः, प्रमाणं.<BR>— (Religious<BR>belief) श्रद्धं -द्धा, भक्तिः f., विश्वासः.<BR>— (Opinion) मतिः f., बुद्धिः f.,<BR>बोधः<BR>— (The thing believed in, tenet) मतं; ‘my belief is,’ मन्ये.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

believable
BELIEVABLE, a. विश्वास्यः -स्या -स्यं, श्रद्धेयः -या -यं, विश्वासयोग्यः -ग्या -ग्यं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

believe
To BELIEVE, v. a. (To give credit to) प्रती (c. 2. प्रत्येति, प्रत्येतुं),<BR>प्रत्ययीकृ.<BR>— (To have religious belief in) विश्वस् (c. 2. -श्वसिति<BR>-श्वसितुं) with loc. c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

believe
To BELIEVE, v. n. (To exercise religious faith) श्रद्धा (c. 3. -दधाति<BR>-धातुं), विश्वासं कृ, प्रत्ययं कृ.<BR>— (To believe in, hold as an object<BR>of faith) विश्वस् (c. 2. -श्वसिति -श्वसितुं) with loc. c.<BR>— (To think)<BR>मन् (c. 4. मन्यते, मन्तुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

believed
BELIEVED, p. p. विश्वसितः -ता -तं, विश्वस्तः -स्ता -स्तं, प्रतीतः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

believer
BELIEVER, s. श्रद्धान्वितः, आस्तिकः, प्रत्ययी m. (न्), विश्वासी m. (न्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

believing
BELIEVING, a. श्रद्दधानः -ना -नं, श्रद्धालुः -लुः -लु, श्राद्धः -द्धा -द्धं, श्रद्धा-<BR>-वान् -वती -वत् (त्), जातविश्वासः -सा -सं, विश्वासी -सिनी -सि (न्),<BR>प्रत्ययी -यिनी -यि (न्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

belike
BELIKE, adv. अपिनाम, किंस्वित्, किल, स्यात्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bell
BELL, s. घण्टा, घण्टिका, घनं.<BR>— (Tinkling ornaments) किङ्किणी;<BR>‘to ring a bell,’ घण्टां हन् (c. 2. हन्ति, हन्तुं) or तड् (c. 10. ताडयति<BR>यितुं) or वद् in caus. (वादयति -यितुं); ‘bell-shaped,’ घण्टाकारः -रा -रं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bell-clapper
BELL-CLAPPER, s. घण्टावादकः, घण्टाकोणः, घण्टाभ्यन्तरे लम्बमान इतस्ततो<BR>दोलायमानस् तद्वादनयोग्यो लवङ्गाकारः कोणः; घण्टाभ्यन्तरे लग्नः स्थूल-<BR>शिरस्को मुसलाकार आयसकीलो येन इतस्ततो लोलमाना घण्टा वाद्यते<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

belle
BELLE, s. सुन्दरी f., सुरूपी f., रूपवती f., सुवेशिनी f., प्रमदा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

belles-lettres
BELLES-LETTRES, s. अलङ्कारविद्या, रसविद्या, रसिका विद्या, वाङ्मयं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

belligerent
BELLIGERENT, a. युध्यमानः -ना -नं, रणशीलः -ला -लं, युयुत्सुः -त्सुः -त्सु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bellipotent
BELLIPOTENT, a. रणवीरः -रा -रं, विक्रमी -मिणी -मि (न्), महावीर्य्यः<BR>-र्य्या -र्य्यं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bell-metal
BELL-METAL, s. कांस्यं, घण्टाशब्दं, घोषः, ताम्बार्द्धं, घोरपुष्पः, पीतलोहं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bellow
To BELLOW, v. n. गर्ज् (c. 1. गर्जति, गर्जितुं), नर्द् (c. 1. नर्दति, नर्दितुं),<BR>विनर्द्, रस् (c. 1. रसति, रसितुं), रु (c. 2. रौति, रवितुं), विरु, संरु;<BR>रट् (c. 1. रटति, रटितुं), गज् (c. 1. गजति, गजितुं), हम्भ (nom.<BR>हम्भायते -यितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bellowed
BELLOWED, p. p. गर्ज्जितः -ता -तं, नर्द्दितः -ता -तं, प्रणर्द्दितः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bellowing
