blush
BLUSH, s. कपोलरागः.<BR>— (Colour in the face resulting from<BR>shame) लज्जाप्रयुक्तं वदनरक्तत्वं, व्रीडाजनितो मुखारुसिमा m. (न्).<BR>—<BR>(Bashfulness) लज्जा, ह्रीः f., व्रीडा, त्रपा; ‘full of blushes,’<BR>ह्रीपरिगतः -ता -तं.<BR>— (To put to the blush) ह्री in caus. (ह्रेपयति<BR>-यितुं); ‘put to the blush,’ ह्रेपितः -ता -तं.<BR>— (At the first<BR>blush or aspect) प्रथमदर्शने, आदावेव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bluster
To BLUSTER, v. n. (To roar) गर्ज् (c. 1. गर्जति, गर्जितुं).<BR>— (To be<BR>tumultuous) तुमुलं कृ, मुखरीभू, शब्द (nom. शब्दायते).<BR>— (To<BR>brag) विकत्थ् (c. 1. -कत्थते -कत्थितुं).<BR>— (To be violent) भृश (nom.<BR>भृशायते).<BR>— (To bully) तर्ज् (c. 1. तर्जति, तर्जितुं), मुखरीकृ, भर्त्स् (c. 10.<BR>भर्त्सयते -यितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

