border
BORDER, s. (Of a river, &c.) तीरं, कूलं, तटं, कच्छः, कच्छान्तः<BR>—<BR>(Edge of any thing) प्रान्तः, अन्तः -न्तं, उपान्तं, समन्तः, पर्य्यन्तं,<BR>सीमा, उत्सङ्गः, धारः.<BR>— (Frontier) समन्तः, सामन्तं, पर्य्यन्तं, सीमा;<BR>‘dwelling on the border,’ सामन्तवासी -सिनी -सि (न्), पर्य्यन्तस्थः<BR>-स्था -स्थं; ‘the border of a wood,’ वनान्तं; ‘of a city,’<BR>नगरोपान्तं; ‘along the border,’ प्रान्ततस्.<BR>— (Of a garment)<BR>अञ्चलः, वस्त्राञ्चलं.<BR>— (A garden-bed) स्थलं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

border
To BORDER, v. a. (To surround with a border) प्रान्त (nom.<BR>प्रान्तयति -यितुं), समन्त (nom. समन्तयति -यितुं), पर्य्यन्तं कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

border
To BORDER, UPON, v. n. प्रान्ततस् or पर्य्यन्ते or निकटे or समीपं स्था<BR>(c. 1. तिष्ठति, स्थातुं) or वृत् (c. 1. वर्त्तते, वर्त्तितुं) or वस् (c. 1. वसति,<BR>वस्तुं), स्पृश् (c. 6. स्पृशति, स्प्रष्टुं).<BR>— (To approach nearly to, re-<BR>semble) कल्पः -ल्पा -ल्पं अस् in comp., सदृशः -शी -शं अस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bordered
BORDERED, p. p. प्रान्तितः -ता -तं, समर्य्यादः -दा -दं, वलयितः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

borderer
BORDERER, s. सामन्तवासी m. (न्), सीमावासी m. (न्), निकटवर्त्ती m.<BR>(न्), समीपवासी m. (न्), प्रतिवासी -सिनी -सि (न्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bordering
BORDERING, a. प्रत्यन्तः -न्ता -न्तं, सामन्तः -न्ता -न्तं, पर्य्यन्तस्थः -स्था -स्थं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bore
BORE, s. (Hole made by boring) छिद्रं, रन्ध्रं.<BR>— (The instrument<BR>of boring) वेधनी, वेधनिका.<BR>— (Diameter of a hole) सुषिरं,<BR>शुषिरं, छिद्रं, व्यासं, छिद्रव्यासं.<BR>— (A swelling tide) वानं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bore
To BORE, v. a. व्यध् (c. 4. विध्यति, व्यद्धुं), छिद्र् (c. 10. छिद्रयति -यितुं),<BR>शुषिरीकृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boreal
BOREAL, a. उत्तरः -रा -रं, उदङ् -दीची -दक् (च्), उदीचीनः -ना -नं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boreas
BOREAS, s. उत्तरवायुः m., उदीचीनवातः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bored
BORED, p. p. (Pierced) विद्धः -द्धा -द्धं, छिद्रितः -ता -तं, शुषिरः -रा -रं;<BR>‘having the ears bored,’ छिद्रकर्णः -र्णा -र्णं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

borer
BORER, s. वेधकः, छिद्रकर्त्ता.<BR>— (An instrument) वेधनी, वेधनिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

born
To be BORN, v. pass. जन् (c. 4. जायते, जनितुं), अभिजन्, सञ्जन्,<BR>उत्पद् (c. 4. -पद्यते -पत्तुं), प्रसु in pass. (-सूयते), सम्भू (c. 1. -भवति<BR>-भवितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

born
BORN, p. p. जातः -ता -तं, जनितः -ता -तं, उपजातः -ता -तं, उत्पन्नः -न्ना -न्नं,<BR>उत्पादितः -ता -तं, सम्भूतः -ता -तं, प्रसूतः -ता -तं, प्रभवः -वा -वं, कृतजन्मा<BR>-न्मा -न्म (न्), उत्पतितः -ता -तं; ‘born blind,’ जात्यन्धः; ‘a born<BR>slave,’ गर्भदासः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

borne
BORNE, p. p. सोढः -ढा -ढं, ऊढः -ढा -ढं, क्षान्तः -न्ता -न्तं; ‘easy to<BR>be borne,’ सुसहः -हा -हं, सुवहः -हा -हं; ‘grass borne along<BR>by the wind,’ वात्याप्रेरिततृणं; ‘it is borne on the shoulder,’<BR>स्कन्धेन समुह्यते<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

borough
BOROUGH, s. नगरं -री, पुरं -री, प्रजाप्रतिनिधिसभायां सामाजिकजनप्रेर-<BR>णाधिकारयुक्ता नगरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

borrow
To BORROW, v. a. ऋणं ग्रह् (c. 9. गृह्लाति, ग्रहीतुं), ऋणं प्रार्थ् (c. 10.<BR>-अर्थयते -ति -यितुं), याच् (c. 1. याचति, याचितुं), ऋणं परियाच्<BR>निरूपितकालपर्य्यन्तं परद्रव्यप्रयोगं प्रार्थ्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

borrow
BORROW, s. (The thing borrowed) याचितकं, प्रतिदेयं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

borrower
BORROWER, s. ऋणग्राही m. (न्), ऋणग्रहः, ऋणप्रार्थकः, ऋणप्रार्थयिता<BR>m. (तृ), याचकः, ऋणयाचकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

borrowing
BORROWING, s. ऋणग्रहः -हणं, ऋणयाचना, याचना, ऋणप्रार्थनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bosky
BOSKY, a. तरुगुल्मावृतः -ता -तं, वार्क्षः -र्क्षी -र्क्षं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bosom
BOSOM, s. उरः n. (स्), क्रोडं -डा, अङ्कः, वत्सं, वक्षः n. (स्), वक्षस्स्थलं,<BR>भुजान्तरं.<BR>— (Female breast) स्तनः, स्तनौ m. du., कुचः, कुचतटं,<BR>वक्षोरुहः, वक्षोजं, उरसिजः, उरसिरुहः, स्तनकुट्मलं.<BR>— (The heart)<BR>हृदयं, अन्तःकरणं, चित्तं, मनः n. (स्), मर्म्म n. (न्).<BR>— (A secret<BR>receptacle) गर्भः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boss
BOSS, s. गण्डः, उच्चैःप्रकारेण खचित अलङ्कारः, पिण्डः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bossed
BOSSED or BOSSY, a. गण्डखचितः -ता -तं, गण्डानुविद्धः -द्धा -द्धं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

botanic
BOTANIC, BOTANICAL, a. उद्भिद्विद्याविषयः -या -यं, वृक्षादिविद्यासम्बन्धकः<BR>-का -कं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

botanist
BOTANIST, s. उद्भिद्विद्याज्ञः, वृक्षादिविद्यातत्त्वज्ञः, वृक्षादिशास्त्रपण्डितः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

botany
