botcher
BOTCHER, s. जीर्णवस्त्रसूचिकः, चीरवस्त्रभेदकः, कर्पटवस्त्रभेदी m. (न्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

botchy
BOTCHY, a. पामनः -ना -नं, दद्रुणः -णा -णं, कच्छुरः -रा -रं, सिध्मलः -ला -लं।<BR>व्रणमयः -यी -यं, मली -लिनी -लि (न्), सदोषः -षा -षं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

both
BOTH, a. उभौ m. du., उभयः -या -यं, द्वयं; ‘on both sides,’ उभयतस्,<BR>उभयत्र; ‘in both ways,’ उभयथा; ‘for both objects,’ उभयार्थं;<BR>‘both hands,’ हस्तद्वयं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

both
BOTH, conj. (And) च -च.<BR>— (As well as) तथा. ‘Both’ may be<BR>expressed by the use of the indeclinable participle; as,<BR>‘he both labours and suffers reproach,’ परिअम्य निन्दां भुंक्ते.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bother
