bowstring
BOWSTRING, s. ज्या, गुणः, धनुर्गुणः, मौर्व्वी, भारवं, शिञ्जिनी, तावरं,<BR>पतञ्चिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bow-window
BOW-WINDOW, s. धनुराकृति वातायनं, धनुराकारो गवाक्षः, प्रग्रीवः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bowyer
BOWYER, s. धनुर्धरः, धनुर्भृत् m., धन्वी m. (न्), धनुष्मान् m. (त्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

box
BOX, s. (A kind of tree) अतिदृढो वृक्षप्रभेदः.<BR>— (A case to hold<BR>any thing) भाण्डं, सम्पुटः, सम्पुटकः, मुद्राधारः, आधारः, पात्रं,<BR>भाजनं, समुद्गः, पेटिका, वासनं.<BR>— (For spectators) प्रेक्षागारं.<BR>— (A<BR>blow) मुष्ट्याघातः, मुष्टिप्रहारः, मुष्टिपातः, पाणिघातः, कराघातः, कीला,<BR>आघातः, प्रहारः, बाहुप्रहरणं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

box
To BOX, v. n. (To fight with the fist) मल्लयुद्धं कृ, मुष्ट्या युध् (c. 4.<BR>युध्यते, योद्धुं), मुष्टीमुष्टि or बाहूबाहवि युध्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

box
To BOX, v. a. (To strike with the fist) मुष्ट्या अभिहन् (c. 2. -हन्ति<BR>-हन्तुं), निहन्, or तड् (c. 10. ताडयति -यितुं) or प्रहृ (c. 1. -हरति<BR>-हर्त्तुं).<BR>— (To enclose in a box) सम्पुटके or भाण्डे निविश् in caus.<BR>(-वेशयति -यितुं) or निधा (c. 3. -दधाति -धातुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boxen
BOXEN, a. पूर्व्वोक्तवृक्षकाष्ठनिर्म्मितः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boxer
BOXER, s. मल्लयोधः, झल्लः, मल्लः, पाणिघातः, बाहुप्रहरणः, बाहुयोधी m.<BR>(न्), रङ्गावतारी m. (न्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boxing
BOXING, s. मौष्टा, मल्लयुद्धं, मुष्टिपातः, पाणिघातः, बाहुयुद्धं, बाहुप्रहरणं.<BR>— (Boxing-match) मल्लयात्रा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boy
BOY, s. कुमारः -रकः, बालः, बालकः, पुत्रः, पुत्रकः, अप्राप्तव्यवहारः.<BR>—<BR>(A word of contempt for a young man) माणवः, माणवकः;<BR>‘multitude of boys,’ माणव्यं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boyhood
BOYHOOD, s. बालकत्वं, बाल्यं, शैशवं, शिशुत्वं, कौमारं, कैशोरं, माणव्यं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boyish
BOYISH, a. वालिशः -शा -शं, बालेयः -या -यं, बालकीयः -या -यं, बालक-<BR>शीलः -ला -लं, कौमारः -री -रं, शिशुयोग्यः -ग्या -ग्यं, माणवीणः -णा -णं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boyishly
BOYISHLY, adv. बालरूपेण, बालकवत्, शिशुवत्, कुमारवत्, बालिशप्रकारेण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

boyishness
BOYISHNESS, s. बालिश्यं, बालेयत्वं, बालकत्वं, कुमारशीलत्वं, शिशुशीलता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brabble
BRABBLE, s. कलहः, व्यवक्रोशनं, विवादः, वाग्युद्धं, विप्रलापः, द्वन्द्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brabble
To BRABBLE, v. n. कलह (nom. कलहायते -यितुं), व्यवक्रुश् (c. 1.<BR>-क्रोशति -क्रोष्टुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brace
To BRACE, v. a. बन्ध् (c. 9. बध्नाति, बन्द्धुं), योक्त्र (nom. योक्त्रयति -यितुं).<BR>— (To strain up, tighten) सन्निबन्ध्, संस्तम्भ् (c. 9. -स्तभ्नाति<BR>-स्तम्भितुं), द्रढ् (nom. द्रढयति -यितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brace
BRACE, s. (A pair) युगं, युग्मं, युगलं, द्वयं, यमलं, यामलं.<BR>— (Bandage)<BR>बन्धनं, बन्धः.<BR>— (Strap) चर्म्मबन्धः -न्धनं.<BR>— (Of a coach) रथालम्बि<BR>चर्म्मबन्धादि.<BR>— (Of a ship) नौकासम्बन्धी रज्जुविशेषः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bracelet
BRACELET, s. वलयः -यं, कङ्कणं, करभूषणं, अङ्गदं, हस्तसूत्रं, वालकः,<BR>कम्बुः m., आवापकः, पारिहार्य्यः, कटकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brachial
BRACHIAL, a. बाहुसम्बन्धी -न्धिनी -न्धि (न्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brachygraphy
BRACHYGRAPHY, s. सङ्क्षिप्तलिखनविद्या, सङ्क्षिप्ताक्षरलिखनं, सङ्केतलेखनविद्या.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bracket
BRACKET, s. नागदन्तः -न्तकः, नागः, हस्तिदन्तः, गजदन्तः, सालेयः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brackish
BRACKISH, a. क्षाररसयुक्तः -क्ता -क्तं, ईषल्लवणः -णा -णं, क्षारसंसृष्टः -ष्टा -ष्टं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brackishness
BRACKISHNESS, s. क्षारः, क्षारत्वं, क्षाररसः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brad
BRAD, s. लोहमयः कीलविशेषः, क्षुद्रशङ्कुः m.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brag
To BRAG, v. n. कत्थ् (c. 1. कत्थते, कत्थितुं), विकत्थ्, श्लाघ् (c. 1. श्लाघते,<BR>श्लाघितुं), with inst. of the thing, आत्मानं श्लाघ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brag
BRAG, s. अहङ्कारोक्तिः f., विकत्था -त्थनं, दम्भः, आहोपुरुषिका अहमह-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=061-b" target="_blank">Page061-b+ 51</a>]<BR>मिका, आत्मश्लाघा, गर्व्वितवाक्यं, शूरमानं, परिकीर्त्तनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

braggart
BRAGGART, BRAGGADOCIO, BRAGGER, s. शूरम्प्तन्यः, शूरमानी m. (न्),<BR>पिण्डीशूरः, उपजल्पी m. (न्), विकत्थी m. (न्), अवलिप्तः, अहङ्कारी<BR>m. (न्), अहङ्कारपूर्णः, आत्मश्लाघी m. (न्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

braggingly
BRAGGINGLY, adv. अहङ्कारेण, साहङ्कारं, विकत्थया, आत्मश्लाघापूर्व्वं, दम्भात्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brahma
BRAHMĀ, s. (The first deity of the Hindu triad, the Creator<BR>of the world, Providence) ब्रह्मा m. (न्), वेधाः m. (स्), विधिः m.,<BR>विरिञ्चिः m., द्रुहिणः.<BR>— (As creator of the world) स्रष्टा m. (ष्टृ),<BR>विश्वसृक् -ट् (ज्).<BR>— (Born in the lotus which sprung from the<BR>navel of Viṣṇu) नाभिजः, नाभिभूः m., अञ्जजः, अञ्जयोनिः,<BR>पद्मगर्भः, पद्मभूः m., पद्मासनः, कमलासनः.<BR>— (The self-existent)<BR>स्वयम्भूः m., आत्मभूः m.<BR>— (Born from the golden egg) हिरण्यगर्भः.<BR>— (As elder of the deities) सुरज्येष्ठः.<BR>— (The four-faced one)<BR>चतुर्म्मुखः, चतुराननः.<BR>— (The great father and lord of all)<BR>पितामहः, प्रजापतिः m., लोकेशः.<BR>— (Supporter of all) धाता m. (तृ),<BR>विधाता m. (तृ).<BR>— (Exalted in heaven) परमेष्ठः -ष्ठी m. (न्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brahmin
BRAHMIN or BRĀHMAN, s. ब्राह्मणः, विप्रः, बाडवः.<BR>— (As the first-<BR>born among mortals) अग्रजन्मा m. (न्).<BR>— (As receiving second<BR>birth at his investiture with the sacred thread) द्विजः,<BR>द्विजातिः m., द्विजन्मा m. (न्).<BR>— (As learned in the Vedas)<BR>श्रोत्रियः.<BR>— (As a deity upon earth) भूदेवः, भूमिदेवः.<BR>— (As born<BR>from the mouth of Brahmā) मुखजः.<BR>— (A Brahmin by birth<BR>but not by duties) ब्राह्मणब्रुवः.<BR>— (The wife of a Brahmin)<BR>ब्राह्मणी.<BR>— (The condition of a Brahmin) ब्राह्मण्यं, ब्राह्मणता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brahminical
BRAHMINICAL, a. ब्राह्मः -ह्मी -ह्मं, ब्राह्मणजातीयः -या -यं; ‘the brah-<BR>minical caste,’ ब्राह्मणजातिः f.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brahminicide
BRAHMINICIDE, s. ब्रह्महत्या, ब्राह्मणबधः.<BR>— (One who kills a Brah-<BR>min) ब्रह्महा m. (न्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

braid
To BRAID, v. a. वेणीकृ, वेणिरूपेण केशान् रच् (c. 10. रचयति -यितुं)<BR>or ग्रन्थ् (c. 9. ग्रथ्नाति, c. 1. ग्रन्थति, ग्रन्थितुं) or केशसंस्कारं कृ.<BR>—<BR>(Weave, interweave) वे (c. 1. वयति, वातुं), ग्रन्थ्, उत्खच् (c. 10.<BR>-खचयति -यितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

braid
BRAID, s. (Of hair) वेणिः -णी f., प्रवेणिः, कवरः -री, धम्मिल्लः, केशवेशः,<BR>केशगर्भः.<BR>— (A knot) ग्रन्थिः m., बन्धः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

braided
BRAIDED, p. p. वेणीभूतः -ता -तं, ग्रथितः -ता -तं, कवरः -री -रं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brain
BRAIN, s. मस्तिष्कं or -स्कः, गोर्द्दं, मस्तकस्नेहः.<BR>— (Intellect) बुद्धिः f.,<BR>मतिः f., धीः f.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brain
To BRAIN, v. a. मस्तकं निष्पिष्प मस्तिष्कं वहिःकृत्य हन् (c. 2. हन्ति, हन्तुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brainish
BRAINISH, a. मदोन्मत्तः -त्ता -त्तं, मदोत्तप्तः -प्ता -प्तं, उत्तप्तः -प्ता -प्तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

brainless
