BURROW, s. (Hole) गर्त्तः, विवरं, विलं, खातं, श्वभ्रं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

burrow
To BURROW, v. n. गर्त्तं or विवरं कृ, गर्त्ते वस् (c. 1. वसति, वस्तुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

burrowing
BURROWING, a. विलवासी -सिनी -सि (न्), गर्त्तवासी -सिनी -सि (न्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bursar
BURSAR, s. विद्यालये धनाधिकारी m. (न्), धनाध्यक्षः, कोषाध्यक्षः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bursarship
BURSARSHIP, s. अर्थाधिकारः, धनाधिकारः, धनाध्यक्षाधिकारः, कोषाध्यक्षपदं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bursary
BURSARY, s. विद्यालये धनगृहं, धनागारः, कोषः, धनकोष्ठकं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

burse
BURSE, s. बणिक्समागमचत्वरं, श्रेष्ठिचत्वरं, पणायाशाला, निगमस्थानं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

burst
To BURST, v. a. भिद् (c. 7. भिनत्ति, भेत्तुं or caus. भेदयति -यितुं), विभिद्,<BR>निर्भिद्, भञ्ज् (c. 7. भनक्ति, भंक्तुं), प्रभञ्ज्, विभञ्ज्, खण्ड् (c. 10. खण्डयति<BR>-यितुं), स्फुट् (c. 10. स्फोटयति -यितुं), दॄ in caus. (दारयति -यितुं), विदॄ,<BR>अवदॄ, शकलीकृ, खण्डशः कृ, विदल् in caus. (-दलयति -यितुं), लुप्<BR>(c. 6. लुम्पति, लोप्तुं), अवलुप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

burst
To BURST, v. n. भिद् in pass. (भिद्यते), विभिद्, निर्भिद्; भञ्ज् in<BR>pass. (भज्यते), प्रभञ्ज्, विभञ्ज्, स्फुट् (c. 6. स्फुटति, स्फुटितुं, c. 1.<BR>स्फोटते, स्फोटितुं), विदॄ in pass. (-दीर्य्यते), अवदॄ, विदल् (c. 1. -दलति<BR>-दलितुं), विशॄ in pass. (-शीर्य्यते), परिशॄ.<BR>— (To burst in pieces)<BR>शकलीभू, खण्डशो भिद् in pass. or भञ्ज् in pass.<BR>— (To burst<BR>forth, break out) प्रपत् (c. 1. -पतति -पतितुं).<BR>— (As seeds) प्रोद्भिद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

burst
BURST, s. (Sudden rending) स्फोटनं, स्फुटनं, अकस्माद् भञ्जनं, भङ्गः,<BR>विभङ्गः, भेदनं, भेदः.<BR>— (Of laughter) प्रहसनं, प्रहसितं, अतिहसित,<BR>अट्टहासः.<BR>— (Of light) ज्वाला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

burst
BURST, p. p. स्फुटः -टा -टं, स्फुटितः -ता -तं, विदीर्णः -र्णा -र्णं, विभग्नः<BR>-ग्ना -ग्नं, विघटितः -ता -तं, विदलितः -ता -तं, भिन्नः -न्ना -न्नं, विभिन्नः<BR>-न्ना -न्नं.<BR>— (Diseased with hernia) अन्त्रवृद्धिपीडितः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

burthen
BURTHEN, s. भारः, धुरा. See BURDEN.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bury
To BURY, v. a. श्मशाने or भूमौ स्था in caus. (स्थापयति -यितुं) or<BR>निधा (c. 3. -दधाति -धातुं) or निखन् (c. 1. -खनति -खनितुं or<BR>-खातुं), निर्हृ (c. 1. -हरति -ते -हर्त्तुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

burying
BURYING, s. भूमिखननं, निखननं, श्मशाने स्थापनं, भूमिसमर्प्पणं, प्रेतनिर्हारः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

burying-ground
BURYING-GROUND, s. श्मशानं, प्रेतवनं, प्रेतगृहं, पितृवनं, मृतशरीरस्थानं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bush
BUSH, s. गुल्मः, क्षुपः, स्तम्बः, छुपः, झुण्टः, झटिः m.<BR>— (A bough of<BR>a tree fixed at the door of a tavern) अत्र सुरादि विक्रीयते इति<BR>घोषणार्थं द्वारोपरि स्थापिता तरुशाखा; सुराध्वजः.<BR>— (Tail of a fox)<BR>लोमशापुच्छं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bushel
BUSHEL, s. (A measure) द्रोणः -णं, आढकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bushy
BUSHY, a. (Full of bushes) गुल्मी -ल्मिनी -ल्मि (न्), तरुगुल्मावृतः<BR>-ता -तं.<BR>— (Thick) घनः -ना -नं, निविडः -डा -डं, अविरलः -ला -लं.<BR>— (Formed like a bush) गुल्माकारः -रा -रं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

busiless
BUSILESS, s. कार्य्यरहितः -ता -तं, शून्यः -न्या -न्यं, निष्कर्म्मा -र्म्मा -र्म्म (न्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

busily
BUSILY, adv. अनलसं, अतन्द्रितं, मनःप्रवेशेन, अभिनिवेशेन, औत्सुक्येन.<BR>— (Inquisitively) चर्च्चया.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

business
BUSINESS, s. (Affair) कर्म्म n. (न्), कार्य्यं, अर्थः.<BR>— (Employment) व्यापारः,<BR>व्यवसायः, व्यवहारः, कार्य्योद्योगः, नियोगः, प्रवृत्तिः f., प्रवर्त्तनं, चरितं,<BR>सम्बन्धः.<BR>— (Something to be done) कृत्यं, कर्त्तव्यं, कार्य्यं.<BR>—<BR>(Object) विषयः, अर्थः, प्रयोजनं.<BR>— (A point, case) अर्थः, पदं.<BR>—<BR>(Means of livelihood, profession) वृत्तिः f., वर्त्तनं, जीविका,<BR>आजीवनार्थं.<BR>— (Point, matter of discussion) स्थलं; ‘a man<BR>of business, one who knows the proper ways of acting,’<BR>क्रियाविधिज्ञः, कार्य्ये कुशलः, दृष्टकर्म्मा m. (न्); ‘what business<BR>have I with that?’ कोऽर्थो मे तेन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

busk
BUSK, s. चेलिकास्तब्धीकरणे स्त्रीजनैः प्रयुक्तः शृङ्गलोहादिनिर्म्मितः फलक-<BR>विशेषः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

buskin
BUSKIN, s. (A half-boot) अर्द्धजङ्घापरिमाणः पादुकाविशेषः, पन्नद्धा,<BR>अनुपदीना, उपानत् f. (ह्).<BR>— (A high-heeled shoe worn by<BR>ancient actors) उच्चपार्ष्णियुक्तो गौरवसूचकः पूर्व्वकालीननटैर् भृतः<BR>पादुकाविशेषः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

buskined
BUSKINED, p. p. पूर्व्वोक्तपादुकारूढः -ढा -ढं, सपादुकः -का -कं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

buss
BUSS, s. चुम्बनं, परिणिंसा, निमित्तकं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

buss
To BUSS, v. a. चुम्ब् (c. 1. चुम्बति, चुम्बितुं), निंस् (c. 2. निंस्ते, निंसितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bust
BUST, s. मस्तकाग्रात्प्रभृति वक्षस्स्थलपर्य्यन्तम् अर्द्धशरीरप्रतिमा, ऊर्द्ध्वकायप्रतिमा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bustard
BUSTARD, s. आरण्यपक्षिप्रभेदः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bustle
To BUSTLE, v. n. चेष्ट् (c. 1. चेष्टते, चेष्टितुं), आत्मानं चेष्ट् in caus.<BR>(चेष्टयति -यितुं), व्यवसो (c. 4. -स्यति -सातुं), कार्य्यव्यग्रत्वाद् इतस्ततो<BR>धाव् (c. 1. धावति, धावितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bustle
BUSTLE, s. (Hurry, confusion) सम्भ्रमः, वैक्लव्यं, विप्लवः, त्वरा, व्यग्रता,<BR>आकुलत्वं, व्यस्तता.<BR>— (Tumult) तुमुलं, कोलाहलः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

bustler
BUSTLER, s. व्यवसायी m. (न्), चेष्टाशीलः, सचेष्टः, तीक्ष्णकर्म्मा m. (न्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

busy
BUSY, a. व्यापारी -रिणी -रि (न्), व्यापृतः -ता -तं, व्यवसायी -यिनी -यि<BR>(न्), कर्म्मी -र्म्मिणी -र्म्मि (न्), कर्म्मोद्युक्तः -क्ता -क्तं, कार्य्योद्युक्तः -क्ता -क्तं,<BR>कार्य्यनिविष्टः -ष्टा -ष्टं, कर्म्मिष्ठः -ष्ठा -ष्ठं, कार्य्यी -र्य्यिणी -र्य्यि (न्), कार्य्य-<BR>वान् -वती -वत् (त्), सचेष्टः -ष्टा -ष्टं, प्रयत्नवान् -वती -वत् (त्), सोत्साहः<BR>-हा -हं, सोद्योगः -गा -गं, प्रवृत्तः -त्ता -त्तं, अतन्द्रितः -ता -तं, अनलसः -सा<BR>-सं, कार्य्यनिमग्नः -ग्ना -ग्नं.<BR>— (Meddling) परकार्य्यचर्च्चाशीलः -ला -लं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

busy
To BUSY, v. a. (To employ) व्यापृ in caus. (व्यापारयति -यितुं), कार्य्ये<BR>नियुज् in caus. (-योजयति -यितुं, c. 7. -युनक्ति -योक्तुं) or अधिकृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

busybody
BUSYBODY, s. परकार्य्यचर्च्चकः, पराधिकारचर्च्चकः, छिद्रान्वेषी m. (न्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

but
BUT, conj. (As an adversative) किन्तु, तु, परन्तु, पुनर्, अथवा.<BR>—<BR>(Except) ऋते with abl., विना with acc. or inst., अन्यः with<BR>abl.; as, ‘any one but the father,’ पितुर् अन्यः.<BR>— (But for,<BR>without) व्यतिरेकेण, अन्तरेण, विना; as, ‘but for sin every<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=071-b" target="_blank">Page071-b+ 51</a>]<BR>thing flourishes,’ पापं विना सर्व्वं फलति.<BR>— (But yet, howbeit)<BR>तथापि.<BR>— (Only) केवलं, मात्रं.<BR>— (All but) अल्पोनः -ना -नं, ईषदूनः<BR>-ना -नं; ‘next but one,’ एकान्तरः -रा -रं.<BR>— (If it were not,<BR>unless) यदि न.<BR>— (Moreover) किञ्च, अपरञ्च, अधिकन्तु.<BR>— (On<BR>the other hand) पुनर्.<BR>— (Otherwise than) अन्यथा with abl.<BR>‘But’ may often be omitted in Sanskrit, or expressed by<BR>another form of sentence; as, ‘he will not gain his end<BR>but by doing that,’ तद् अकृत्वा प्राप्तार्थो न भविष्यति; ‘I do not<BR>doubt but I am to blame,’ सापराधोऽस्मि इति न संशयः; ‘but<BR>a short time since,’ न चिरात्; ‘there is none but fears<BR>him,’ सर्व्वे तस्माद् बिभ्यति; ‘she does nothing but grieve,’<BR>सा निरन्तरं शोचति; “who but a child weeps,” को रोदित्य्<BR>अबालिशः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

butcher
BUTCHER, s. (Seller of meat) मांसविक्रयी m. (न्), मांसिकः, शौनिकः,<BR>सौनिकः, शूनावान् m. (त्), सूनी m. (न्), पशुमारणपूर्व्वकं मांसविक्र-<BR>यजीवी m. (न्), प्राणिहिंसापरः.<BR>— (Butcher's meat) सौनं, घात-<BR>स्थानभवं मांसं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

butcher
To BUTCHER, v. a. हन् (c. 2. हन्ति, हन्तुं), निहन्, or in caus. (घातयति<BR>-यितुं), मृ in caus. (मारयति -यितुं), बध् (defective, usually found<BR>in the 3d pret. अबधीत् and fut. बधिष्यति -ते), विशस् (c. 1.<BR>-शसति -शसितुं), निसूद् in caus. (-सूदयति -यितुं), अभिसूद्, विनिसूद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

butchery
BUTCHERY, s. बधः, हननं, निहननं, घातनं, निषूदनं, विशसनं.<BR>— (The<BR>place where animals are killed) शूना, सूना, बधस्थानं, बधस्थली,<BR>बध्यभूमिः f., घातस्थानं, पशुमारणस्थानं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

butea
BUTEA, s. (A plant) किंशुकः, पलाशः, वातपोथः, पर्णः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

but-end
BUT-END, s. घनाग्रं, स्थूलाग्रं, अतीक्ष्णाग्रं.<BR>— (Hilt) त्सरुः m.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

butler
BUTLER, s. पानपात्रवाहकः, मद्यरक्षकः, मद्यागाराधिकृतः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

butment
BUTMENT, s. उभयतस् तोरणमूलोत्तम्भकः सेतुहर्म्यादिभागः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

butt
BUTT, s. (For shooting at) लक्षं, लक्ष्यं, शरव्यं, वेध्यं, व्यध्यः, प्रतिकायः,<BR>दृष्टिगुणः.<BR>— (Aim, end) अभिप्रायः, आशयः, उद्देशः, चिकीर्षितं.<BR>—<BR>(Object of jest) उपहासस्थानं, परिहासास्पदं, हास्यभूमिः f.<BR>— (A<BR>cask) पात्रं, भाण्डं, सुराभाजनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

butt
To BUTT, v. n. (To strike with the head like horned animals)<BR>शृङ्गिणवत् or मेषादिवत् शिरसा आहन् (c. 2. -हन्ति -हन्तुं)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

butter
BUTTER, s. नवनीतं, क्षीरसारः, दधिजं, दधिसारः, किलाटः -टं, मन्थजं,<BR>नवोद्धृतं.<BR>— (Clarified butter or ghee) घृतं, हविः n. (स्), सर्पिः n.<BR>(स्), पुरोडाशः, आज्यं.<BR>— (Of yesterday's milk) हैयङ्गवीनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

butter
To BUTTER, v. a. नवनीतेन लिप् (c. 6. लिम्पति, लेप्तुं) or अञ्ज् (c. 7.<BR>अनक्ति, अंक्तुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

butter-bump
BUTTER-BUMP, s. क्रौञ्चजातीयः पक्षिभेदः, क्रौञ्चः, वकप्रभेदः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

butter-cup
BUTTER-CUP, BUTTER-FLOWER, s. पीतपुष्पप्रभेदः स च वसन्तसमये यवसमध्ये<BR>प्ररोहति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

buttered
BUTTERED, p. p. नवनीताक्तः -क्ता -क्तं, घृताक्तः -क्ता -क्तं, घृताभ्यक्तः -क्ता -क्तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

butterfly
BUTTERFLY, s. चित्रपतङ्गः, चित्राङ्गः पतङ्गभेदः, आपन्नपक्षः कीटभेदः,<BR>कीटोद्भवश् चित्रपतङ्गः, सपक्षः कीटः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

butteris
BUTTERIS, s. (An instrument for paring the hoof of a horse)<BR>अश्वखुरतक्षणयोग्या कर्त्तरिका, तुरगशफकर्त्तनार्थं यन्त्रविशेषः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

butter-knife
BUTTER-KNIFE, s. कुन्तलिका, घृतकुन्तलिका, नवनीतकर्त्तरिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

butter-man
BUTTER-MAN, s. नवनीतविक्रयी m. (न्), नवनीतविक्रयजीवी m. (न्),<BR>घृतविक्रेता m. (तृ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

butter-milk
BUTTER-MILK, s. दण्डाहतं, तक्रं, प्रमथितं, अरिष्टं, कालशेयं, गोरसः, कटुरं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

butter-print
BUTTER-PRINT, s. नवनीताङ्कनयोग्या काष्ठमयी मुद्रा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

butter-teeth
BUTTER-TEETH, s. मुखाग्रभागे वृहद्दन्तद्वयं, सम्मुखस्थौ छेदकदन्तौ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

buttery
BUTTERY, a. नवनीतगुणविशिष्टः -ष्टा -ष्टं, घृतमयः -यी -यं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

buttery
BUTTERY, s. (The room where provisions are laid up) खाद्य-<BR>द्रव्यागारं, विद्यालये पूपनवनीतयवसुरादिकोष्ठकं, कुशूलः, अन्नकोष्ठकं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

buttock
BUTTOCK, s. स्फिचौ f. du. (स्फिच्), नितम्बः, कटिप्रोथः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

button
BUTTON, s. (Catch by which clothes are fastened) गण्डः, पुंसो<BR>वस्त्राञ्चलद्वयसङ्ग्रहणार्थं गुलिका.<BR>— (Bud) मुकुलं, कुट्मलं, पल्लवः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

button
To BUTTON, v. a. (To dress) संव्ये (c. 1. -व्ययति -व्यातुं), वेष्ट् (c. 1.<BR>वेष्टते, वेष्टितुं).<BR>— (To fasten with buttons) पूर्व्वोक्तगण्डेन सङ्ग्रह् (c. 9.<BR>-गृह्लाति -ग्रहीतुं) or संलग्नीकृ or बन्ध् (c. 9. बध्नाति, बन्द्धुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

button
To BUTTON, v. n. (To bud) गण्डाकारमुकुलवत् स्फुट् (c. 6. स्फुटति, स्फुटितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

button-hole
BUTTON-HOLE, s. गण्डाधारः, गण्डछिद्रं, गुलिकाग्रहणयोग्यं छिद्रं, शिक्यं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

button-maker
BUTTON-MAKER, s. गण्डकृत्, गण्डकारी m. (न्), गुलिकाकारः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

buttress
BUTTRESS, s. वप्रः, भवनस्य वहिरालम्बः, भित्त्युम्भनार्थं वप्रः or प्राकारः.<BR>— (Prop, support) उपस्तम्भः, आलम्बः, उपघ्नः, आश्रयः, आधारः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

buttress
To BUTTRESS, v. a. (To prop) पूर्व्वोक्तवप्रेण उत्तम्भ् (c. 9. उत्तभ्नाति, उत्तम्भितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

buxom
BUXOM, a. (Gay, lively) हृष्टः -ष्टा -ष्टं, प्रहसितवदनः -ना -नं, प्रहासी<BR>-सिनी -सि (न्), प्रफुल्लवदनः -ना -नं, आनन्दी -न्दिनी -न्दि (न्), सरसः<BR>-सा -सं.<BR>— (Wanton) ललितः -ता -तं, विलासी -सिनी -सि (न्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

buxomly
BUXOMLY, adv. सानन्दं, सहर्षं, सललितं, सविलासं, सरसं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

buxomness
BUXOMNESS, s. (Wantonness) लालित्यं, सविलासता, सरम्रता, लीला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

buy
To BUY, v. a. क्री (c. 9. क्रीणाति -णीते, क्रेतुं), उपक्री, सङ्क्री, मूल्यं दत्त्वा<BR>लभ् (c. 1. लभते, लब्धुं) or प्राप् (c. 5. -आप्नोति, -आप्तुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

buyer
BUYER, s. क्रेता m. (तृ), क्रयी m. (न्), क्रायकः, क्रयिकः.<BR>— (Buyer and<BR>seller) क्रयविक्रयी m. (न्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

buying
BUYING, s. क्रयः.<BR>— (Buying and selling) क्रयविक्रयः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

buzz
To BUZZ, v. n. रु (c. 2. रौति, रवितुं), गुञ्ज् (c. 1. गुञ्जति, गुञ्जितुं), रण्<BR>(c. 1. रणति, रणितुं), रणरणं कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

buzz
BUZZ, BUZZING, s. गुञ्जनं, गुञ्जितं, कलः, कलकलः, मर्म्मरः, रणत्कारः,<BR>कलरवः, कलस्वरं; part. गुञ्जन् -ञ्जन्ती -ञ्जत् (त्), रणन् -णन्ती -णत् (त्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

buzzard
BUZZARD, s. अपकृष्टजातिः श्येनभेदः, श्येनकः.<BR>— (A blockhead) स्थूलधीः<BR>m., मन्दमतिः m., मूर्खः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

by
BY, prep. (By the side of) expressed by उप prefixed; as,<BR>‘he sits by me,’ माम् उपास्ते; ‘a tank by a well,’ उपकूपजलाशयः.<BR>— (Beside, denoting passage) expressed by अति prefixed;<BR>as, ‘he passes by me,’ माम् अत्येति.<BR>— (Denoting the agent,<BR>instrument, cause, means or manner) expressed by the<BR>instr. case; as, ‘by him,’ ‘by that,’ ‘on that account,’<BR>‘by that means,’ ‘in that manner,’ may all be expressed<BR>by तेन. In modern Sanskrit the instrument and agent<BR>are often expressed by द्वारा or द्वारेण and कर्त्तृक; as, ‘to<BR>hit with a stick,’ काष्ठद्वारा or काष्ठद्वारेण तड्; ‘sacrifices by<BR>sages,’ ऋषिकर्त्तृकयज्ञाः. ‘By,’ in some of these senses, may<BR>often be expressed by the indec. part.; ‘a man may be<BR>happy by doing penance,’ तपस् तप्त्वा सुखी भवेत्.<BR>— (According<BR>to) अनुरूपं, अनुसारेण; ‘by rule,’ विधिवत्, विधितस्, यथाविधि.<BR>— (As soon as, not later than) मध्ये; as, ‘by next year,’<BR>आगामिवत्सरमध्ये.<BR>— (The quantity at one time) expressed by<BR>the affix शस्; as, ‘by thousands,’ सहस्रशस्; ‘by twos and<BR>threes,’ द्विशस् त्रिशस्; ‘by companies,’ पंक्तिभिः.<BR>— (Successive<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=072-b" target="_blank">Page072-b+ 50</a>]<BR>action) expressed by प्रति or अनु, or by repeating the<BR>word; as, ‘man by man,’ प्रतिपुरुषं; ‘day by day,’ प्रतिदिवणं<BR>or अनुदिवसं or दिवसे दिवसे.<BR>— (By himself, alone) एकान्ततस्,<BR>निभृतं, रहसि, रहीभूतः -ता -तं.<BR>— (In swearing or adjuring)<BR>expressed by the instr. c.; as, ‘swear not at all, neither<BR>by heaven, nor by earth,’ कमपि शपथं मा ऽकार्ष्ट स्वर्गेण न पृथिव्या<BR>न; ‘by name,’ नाम्ना, नामतस्, नामधेयतस्; ‘by force,’ बलात्,<BR>बलात्कारेण, प्रसह्म; ‘by chance,’ दैवात्; ‘by day,’ दिवा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

by
BY, adv. (Near) निकटे, समीपे, अन्तिके, अभितस्, आरात्.<BR>— (By the<BR>side) पार्श्वतस्, पार्श्वे.<BR>— (Passing by) expressed by the prep.<BR>अति; as, ‘he passes by,’ अतिक्रामति.<BR>— (In presence) सन्निधाने,<BR>साक्षात्, अग्रे, समक्षं, सम्मुखे.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

by
BY, s. (Something not the direct object of regard) expressed,<BR>when in composition, by उप; as, ‘a duty by the by,’ i. e.<BR>‘a secondary duty,’ उपधर्म्मः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

by and by
BY AND BY, adv. अनन्तरं, क्षणान्तरे, न चिरेण, अचिरेण, अचिरात्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

by the by
BY THE BY, or BY THE WAY, adv. (Exclusively of the subject<BR>in hand) प्रस्तुतम्, अन्तरेण, प्रस्तुतविषयव्यतिरेकेण.<BR>— (Besides, more-<BR>over) किञ्च, अपरञ्च, अन्यच्च.<BR>— (In reference to that) तदुद्दिश्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

by-degrees
