CAPTIVITY, s. बन्धनं, वन्दिभावः, कारागोपनं, वशित्वं, वश्यता, शत्रुवशिता.<BR>— (Servitude) दासत्वं, दास्यं, दासभावः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

captor
CAPTOR, s. वन्दीकर्त्ता m. (र्त्तृ), ग्राहकः, जेता m. (तृ), लोप्त्रकृत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

capture
CAPTURE, s. (The act of taking) ग्रहणं; ‘capture of a fort,’<BR>दुर्गलङ्घनं, दुर्गभङ्गः.<BR>— (The prize taken) लोप्त्रं, लोत्रं; ‘capture<BR>of cattle,’ गोग्रहः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

capture
