chap
CHAP, s. (Cleft, chink) त्रुटितं, त्रुटिः f. -टी, छिद्रं, रन्ध्रं, गर्त्तः, भित्तिः f.;<BR>‘in the feet,’ पाददारी, अलसः.<BR>— (A person, a fellow, con-<BR>-temptuously) माणवः -वकः, मनुष्यकः, नागरः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

chape
CHAPE, s. (The catch of any thing by which it is held) बन्धनी,<BR>बन्धनकीलकः, सङ्गहणार्थं दन्तकः, ग्रहणी, रक्षणी, आलानं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

chapel
CHAPEL, s. (Shrine) देवागारः, देवतागारः, देवायतनं, देवालयं.<BR>— (A<BR>small place of worship subject to a church) महामन्दिराधीना<BR>क्षुद्रपूजाशाला, अप्रधानमन्दिरं.<BR>— (Of ease) दूरस्थैः सेवितं क्षुद्रभजनभवनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

