currier
CURRIER, s. चर्म्मकारः -री m. (न्), चर्म्मछेदनकारी m., चर्म्मावकर्त्ती<BR>m. (न्), कुरटः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

currish
CURRISH, a. कुक्कुराचारः -रा -रं, श्वशीलः -ला -लं, शौवः -वी -वं, दुःशीलः<BR>-ला -लं, शौवापदः -दी -दं; ‘a currish man,’ श्वनरः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curry
To CURRY, v. a. (Dress leather) चर्म्म परिष्कृ.<BR>— (Beat) तड् (c. 10.<BR>ताडयति -यितुं), प्रहृ (c. 1. -हरति -हर्त्तुं).<BR>— (Rub a horse with a<BR>curry-comb) अश्वलोम लोहकङ्कतेन मृज् (c. 2. मार्ष्टि, मार्ष्टुं).<BR>—<BR>(Curry favour) आराध् in caus. (-राधयति -यितुं), सान्त्व् (c. 10.<BR>सान्त्वयति -यितुं), लल् in caus. (लालयति -यितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

curry
