estuate
To ESTUATE, v. n. फेन (nom. फेनायते), उत्सेचनंकृ, वेला (nom. वेलायते).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=238-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

et-caetera
ET-CAETERA. Expressed by आदिः -दि in the m. or n. gender<BR>and in the plur. or sing. numb.; as, ‘parrots, starlings,<BR>&c.,’ शुकसारिकादयः; ‘Indra, Kuvera, &c.,’ इन्द्रकुवेरादयः; ‘Of<BR>Agni, Pavana, &c.,’ अग्निपवनादीनां; ‘the nose, eyes, &c.,’<BR>नासचक्षुरादीनि; ‘peace, war, &c.’ सन्धिविग्रहादि; ‘by libe-<BR>-rality, &c.,’ दात्नादिना; ‘from liberality, &c.,’ दानादेः (for<BR>दानादिनः). Sometimes इति is prefixed to आदि; as, ‘the<BR>word chitralig, &c.,’ चित्रलिगित्यादि. Sometimes आदिकः<BR>-का -कं, आद्यः -द्या -द्यं and प्रभृति are used for आदि; as, ‘gifts,<BR>&c.,’ दानादिकं; ‘Indra, &c.,’ इन्द्राद्याः, or इन्द्रप्रभृतयः pl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=238-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

etch
