To GAMMON, v. a. शूकरमांसं शुष्कीकृ or लवणीकृ, वल्लूरं कृ.<BR>— (Hoax)<BR>प्रलभ् (c. 1. -लभते -लब्धुं), अभिसन्धा (c. 3. -दधाति -धातुं), वञ्च् (c. 10.<BR>वञ्चयति -यितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=300-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gamut
GAMUT, s. (Musical scale) ग्रामः. The seven musical notes<BR>of the Hindū gamut are called निपादः, ऋषभः, गान्धारः,<BR>पड्जः, मध्यमः, धैवतः, पञ्चमः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=300-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gander
GANDER, s. वरटः, हंसः, राजहंसः, कलहंसः, चक्रः, चक्रवाकः, चक्राङ्गः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=300-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gandharba
GANDHARBA, s. (A celestial musician. These are demigods<BR>who inhabit heaven, and form the orchestra at the<BR>banquets of the gods) गन्धर्ब्बः, हाहाः (स्), हुहुः m., हुहूः m., हहाः m.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=300-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ganesha
GANESHA, s. (Son of Siva and Pārvatī, the god of wisdom,<BR>and remover of difficulties and obstacles, addressed at<BR>the commencement of all undertakings, and at the open-<BR>ing of all compositions. He is called ‘Ganesha,’ as<BR>presiding over the troop of deities attendant on Siva)<BR>गणेशः, गणनाथः, गणाधिपः, गणनायकः, गणपतिः m., गणाग्रणीः m.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=301-a" target="_blank">Page301-a+ 51</a>]<BR>गणः, हेमाङ्गः, हेरम्बः, हस्तिमल्लः,<BR>— (As remover of obstacles)<BR>विघ्नेशः, विघ्नराजः, विघ्ननाशकः -शनः, विघ्नविनायकः, विनायकः,<BR>विघ्नहारी m. (न्).<BR>— (Elephant-faced) गजाननः, गजवदनः, गजास्यः.<BR>— (Elephant-toothed) गजदन्तः.<BR>— (One-toothed) एकदन्तः.<BR>—<BR>(Big-bellied) लम्बोदरः.<BR>— (Two-bodied) द्विदेहः.<BR>— (Having two<BR>mothers) द्वैमातुरः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=300-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gang
GANG, s. (Company of persons) गणः, जनसमूहः, जनसंसर्गः, जननिवहः,<BR>सङ्घः, सङ्गः; ‘of thieves,’ चौरगणः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gang-board
GANG-BOARD, s. नौकारोहणावरोहणार्थं दीर्घकाष्ठफलकं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gang-days
GANG-DAYS, s. भ्रमणदिवसाः m. pl., परिक्रमदिवसाः, पर्य्यटनकालः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ganges
GANGES, s. (The River) गङ्गा, गङ्गाका, गङ्गिका. The name<BR>Gangā is derived from the root gam, ‘to go,’ i. e. ‘that<BR>which goes or flows on the earth,’ whence also the name<BR>भवायना, ‘going in the world.’ (Daughter of Jahnu.<BR>The Ganges in its course from heaven disturbed the de-<BR>votions of this saint, upon which he drank up its waters,<BR>but released them again at the intercession of the sage<BR>Bhagīratha. Hence the following names) जाह्नवी, जह्नुतनया,<BR>जह्नुसुता, भागीरथी (Crest of Siva. The Ganges, in its descent<BR>from heaven, alighted on the head of Siva, where it<BR>wandered for a time in the tresses of his hair) हरशेखरा.<BR>(River of heaven) स्वर्णदी, सुरनदी, सुरनिम्नगा, स्वरापगा, स्वर्गगङ्गा,<BR>स्वर्वापी, खापगा, सिद्धापगा.<BR>— (Flowing in heaven, earth, and<BR>hell) त्रिपथगा, त्रिस्रोताः f. (स्).<BR>— (Flowing from the foot of<BR>Viṣṇu) विष्णुपदी.<BR>— (Mother of Bhīṣma) भीष्मसूः f.<BR>— (The<BR>very auspicious one) महाभद्रा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ganglion
GANGLION, s. स्नायुस्फोटः -टकः, शिरास्फोटकः, नाडीविस्फोटः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gangrene
GANGRENE, s. कोथः, पूतिमांसं, विद्रधिः m., क्षतं, नालीव्रणः, मांसपाकः,<BR>रक्तविद्रधिः m., मांसपूतिः, शरीरस्य परभागे स्वस्थे सति एकभागस्य पूतीभावः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gangrene
To GANGRENE, v. n. मांसैकदेशे पूतीभू, पूतमांसीभू, कोथीभू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gangrenous
GANGRENOUS, a. कोथवान् -वती -वत् (त्), कोथीयः -या -यं, पूतिमांसवान् &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gangway
GANGWAY, s. नौकायां गमनागमनपथः or आरोहणावरोहणपथः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gantlet
GANTLET, GANTLOPE, s. सेनायां दण्डार्हस्य दण्डविशेषः; ‘to run the<BR>gantlet,’ महापातकिवत् सैन्यानां यष्टिपाणीनां द्विपंक्तिमध्ये धाव् (c. 1.<BR>धावति -ते -वितुं) यावद् एकैकेन यष्ट्याघातः क्रियते.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gaol
GAOL, s. कारा, कारागारं, कारावेश्म n. (न्), बन्धनागारं, बन्धनालयः,<BR>बन्धनगुहं, बन्धनस्थानं, गुप्तिः f.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gaol
To GAOL, v. a. कारायां बन्ध् (c. 9. बघ्नाति, बन्धुं) or निरुध् (c. 7.<BR>-रुणद्धि -रोद्धुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

gaol-delivery
