multiplication
MULTIPLICATION, s. (In Arithmetic, &c.) गुणनं, हननं, घातः, बधः,<BR>पूरणं, गुणत्वं -ता, अङ्कपूरणं, हतं, अभ्यासः, अङ्कवृद्धिः f., संख्यावृद्धिः f.,<BR>प्रत्युत्पन्नं, गुणाकारः -रं. The Hindus have different methods<BR>of multiplication; as, ‘cross multiplication,’ वज्राभ्यासः,<BR>वज्रबधः, वज्रघातः; ‘duodecimal multiplication,’ गोमूत्रिका;<BR>‘multiplication by a figure divided into squares,’ कपाट-<BR>सन्धिः m.; ‘multiplication according to the places,’ स्थान-<BR>गुणनं; ‘by sub-multiples of the multiplier,’ विभागगुणनं;<BR>‘by dividing the multiplier into parts, and taking the<BR>sums of the products of the multiplier.’ खण्डगुणनं; ‘by the<BR>whole multiplier at once,’ स्वरूपगुणनं.<BR>— (Act of increasing)<BR>बहुलीकरणं, प्रचुरीकरणं, वर्धनं, वृद्धिः f.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=520-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

