must
MUST, v. n. (Be necessitated). Expressed by the fut. pass.<BR>part.; as, ‘anger must be restrained,’ कोपो नियन्तव्यः;<BR>‘I must go, or it is to be gone by me.’ मया गन्तव्यं; ‘I<BR>must do that,’ तन् मया कर्त्तव्यं or करणीयं or कार्य्यं. The<BR>adverb अवश्यं may be added; as, तन् मया अवश्यं कर्त्तव्यं.<BR>Sometimes the verb अर्ह् (c. 1. अर्हति -र्हितुं) has the sense<BR>of ‘must;’ as, ‘he must not receive that,’ न तत् प्राप्तुम् अर्हति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=522-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

must
MUST s. (Wine just pressed from the grape) नवमद्यं, नूतनमद्यं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=522-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

must
