observance
OBSERVANCE, s. (Act of keeping or performing) पालनं, रक्षणं,<BR>सेवनं, निषेवनं, धारणं, आचरणं, अनुष्ठानं.<BR>— (Practising) आचरणं,<BR>अनुष्ठानं, करणं, विधानं, अभ्यासः, निषेवनं.<BR>— (Following) अनुसारः,<BR>अनुसरणं.<BR>— (Custom, practice) व्यवहारः, आचारः, चर्य्या, चरितं,<BR>रीतिः f.<BR>— (Religious observance) व्रतं, नियमः, यमः, नियामः,<BR>विधिः m., विधानं.<BR>— (Respect) आदरः, सत्कारः, मानं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=543-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

observant
OBSERVANT, a. (Taking notice) निरीक्षकः -का -कं, प्रेक्षकः -का -कं.<BR>— (Keeping, practising, following) पालकः -का -कं, निषेवकः<BR>-का -कं, अनुष्ठायी -यिनी -यि (न्), धारी &c., अनुसारी &c., आस्थितः<BR>-ता -तं, निष्ठितः -ता -तं, आश्रितः -ता -तं.<BR>— (Of orders) आज्ञापालकः.<BR>— (Of benefits received) कृतवेदी &c., कृतज्ञः -ज्ञा -ज्ञं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=543-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

observation
OBSERVATION, s. (Act of looking at or taking notice) निरीक्षणं,<BR>निरीक्षा, अवेक्षणं, अवेक्षा, अवलोकनं, आलोकनं, आलोचनं, निरूपणं,<BR>सन्दर्शनं, दृष्टिः f., लक्ष्यं, लक्षं.<BR>— (Result of taking notice)<BR>लिखितं, चर्चा. See NOTE, NOTICE; ‘in one's observation,’<BR>प्रत्यक्षे -क्षतस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=543-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

