OLDEST, a. ज्येष्ठः -ष्ठा -ष्ठं, वयोज्येष्ठः &c., वर्षिष्ठः &c., श्रेष्ठः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

old-fashioned
OLD-FASHIONED, a. पुराणरीत्यनुसारी -रिणी -रि (न्), प्राचीनव्यवहा-<BR>रानुरूपः -पा -पं, प्राक्तनमतानुयायी &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oldish
OLDISH, a. ईषद्वृद्धः -द्धा -द्धं, ईषज्जीर्णः -र्णा -र्णं, ईषत्पुराणः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oldness
OLDNESS, s. (Old age). See the word. (Antiquity, state of<BR>being of long standing) पुराणता -त्वं, प्राचीनता -त्वं, प्राक्तनता,<BR>पुरातनत्वं, प्रत्नता, प्राक्कालिकत्वं, प्राक्कालीनता, चिरकालीनता, चिरता.<BR>— (As of clothes, &c.) जीर्णता, जर्जरता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oleaginous
OLEAGINOUS, a. स्निग्धः -ग्धा -ग्धं, स्नेही -हिनी -हि (न्), चिक्कणः -णा<BR>-णं, मेदुरः -रा -रं, स्नेहवान् &c. See OILY.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

