oracle
ORACLE, s. (Answer of a god to an inquiry made) शकुनं -नः,<BR>प्रश्नः, प्रसादः; ‘through a voice,’ देववाणी, आकाशवाणी.<BR>— (The<BR>deity who gives the answer) प्रश्नदेवता, प्रसाददेवता, प्रश्नदेवः,<BR>शकुनदेवः.<BR>— (The place where the answer is given) प्रश्नस्थानं,<BR>शकुनस्थानं, प्रसादस्थानं.<BR>— (A person whose opinion is of great<BR>authority) प्रमाणं, आप्तः.<BR>— (A wise or authoritative sentence)<BR>आप्तवचनं, आप्तोक्तिः f.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

oracular
