pair
PAIR, s. मिथुनं, द्वयं, द्वन्द्वं, युगं, युग्मं, युगलं, यमलं, यामलं, यमः, यमकं,<BR>युतकं; ‘a pair of doves,’ पारावतमिथुनं; ‘a pair of oxen,’<BR>गोमिथुनं, गोयुगं; ‘a pair of birds,’ पक्षिणोर् मिथुनं, पक्षिमिथुनं,<BR>पक्षिद्वयं; ‘a married pair,’ दम्पती m. du., भार्य्यापती m. du.,<BR>स्त्रीपुरुषौ. The word द्वन्द्वः is used to denote that form of<BR>grammatical combination which unites two or more<BR>words of similar or opposite signification; thus, ‘hand<BR>and foot,’ पाणिपादं; ‘affection and hatred,’ रागद्वेषौ m. du.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

