plant
PLANT, s. उद्भिद् m. f. n., ओषधिः -धी f., औषधिः -धी f., उद्भिज्जं, उद्भिदं,<BR>पल्लवः -वं, अङ्कुरः, प्ररोहः, रोहः, शाकः; ‘gramineous,’ तृणं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plant
To PLANT, v. a. (Put in the ground for growth) रुह् in caus.<BR>(रोपयति -यितुं), निरुह्, निखन् (c. 1. -खनति -नितुं), रोपणं कृ.<BR>—<BR>(Fix, set, place) स्था in caus., प्रतिष्ठा, न्यस्, विन्यस्, धा, निधा,<BR>निविश्, रुह् or आरुह् in caus.; ‘to plant the foot,’ पादं न्यस्.<BR>(Plant a colony) वस् in caus. (वासयति -यितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plantain
PLANTAIN, s. (Tree) कदली -लः, कदलकः, रम्भा, तृणसारा, गुच्छफला,<BR>ततपत्री, मोचा, मोचकः, अंशुमत्फला, काष्ठीला, वारणबुषा, वारणबुसा,<BR>वारणवल्लभा, वारबुषा; ‘the fruit,’ कदलीफलं, मोचं, मोचाटः, रम्भा;<BR>‘wild plantain tree,’ काष्ठकदली; ‘mixture of sugar and<BR>milk with plantains and spices,’ शिखरिणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plantation
PLANTATION, s. (Act of planting) रोपणं, आरोपणं, आरोपः.<BR>— (Place<BR>planted) वृक्षवाटिका, वृक्षवाटी, वाटः -टी -टिका, कृत्रिमवनं, उपवनं,<BR>वनं, कर्म्मान्तः, शाकटं or शाकिनं in comp.; as, ‘a plantation<BR>of sugar canes,’ इक्षुशाकटं, इक्षुशाकिनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

