plume
PLUME, s. (Feather) पक्षः, पर्णः, पिच्छं.<BR>— (Feather worn as<BR>ornament, crest) शेखरः, चूडा, शिखा, किरीटः^1, मुकुटं, मौलिः m. f.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by sanaatani on 20230112. note: There is no word as kirAwa. Synonyms match kirIwa..<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

plume
To PLUME, v. a. (Adjust feathers) पक्षान् or पर्णान् रच् (c. 10.<BR>रचयति -यितुं) or विरच्.<BR>— (Strip of feathers) पक्षान् or पर्णान्<BR>उत्कृष् or निष्कृष् or हृ or उत्पट्, निष्पक्षीकृ. See To PLUCK.<BR>—<BR>(Pride one's self) अभिमन् (c. 4. -मन्यते -मन्तुं), आत्मानं श्लाघ् (c. 1.<BR>श्लाघते -घितुं); ‘to plume one's self on one's learning,’<BR>पण्डितम्मन्यः -न्या -न्यं भू or अस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

