ragout
RAGOUT, s. मिष्टान्नं, सव्यञ्जनाहारः, व्यञ्जनं, उपस्करः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rahu
RĀHU, s. (The ascending node, fabled as a demon, the son<BR>of Singhikā, with the tail of a dragon. His head was<BR>cut off by Viṣṇu, at the churning of the ocean; but<BR>being immortal, by having tasted the amrit, the head<BR>and tail retained their separate existence, and were<BR>transferred to the stellar sphere. The head, or Rāhu,<BR>became the cause of eclipses, by endeavouring at various<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=653-a" target="_blank">Page653-a+ 51</a>]<BR>times to swallow the sun and moon. The tail was<BR>called Ketu, or the descending node, see PLANET) राहुः,<BR>सिंहिकासूनुः m., सैंहिकः, सैंहिकेयः, ग्रहः, ग्रहकल्लोलः, खेटः, विधुन्तुदः,<BR>सूर्य्यग्रहः. An eclipse is called राहुग्राहः, राहुग्रासः, राहुसंस्पर्शः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rail
