rally
To RALLY, v. a. (Restore to order troops thrown into confusion)<BR>पिञ्जलसैन्यान् or विद्रुतसैन्यान् or भग्नव्यूहसैन्यान् पुनर् व्यूहीकृ or<BR>व्यूह् (c. 1. -ऊहते -हितुं) or पुनः समूहीकृ or पुनर् व्यूहक्रमेण रच्,<BR>पुनः संग्रह्.<BR>— (Jest, banter) अवहस्, अपहस्, अवहासभूमिं कृ, अव-<BR>क्षिप्, मुखरीकृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=654-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rally
To RALLY, v. n. (Recover order) पुनर् व्यूहीभू or समूहीभू.<BR>— (Re-<BR>cover strength) पुनर् बलं लभ् (c. 1. लभते, लब्धुं), समुत्था (c. 1.<BR>-तिष्ठति -थातुं, rt. स्था), प्रत्याश्चस् (c. 2. -श्वसिति -तुं), पुनः स्वस्थः<BR>-स्था -स्थं भू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=654-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ram
RAM, s. (Male sheep) मेषः, उरभ्रः, मेढ्रः, मेण्डः, मेण्ढः -ण्ढकः, मेठः,<BR>अविः m., एडकः, ऊर्णायुः m., उरणः -णकः, रोमशः, लोमशः, वृष्णिः m.,<BR>भेडः, हुडुः m., सम्फालः, संस्फालः.<BR>— (Battering ram), see the<BR>word.<BR>— (The sign aries) मेषः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=654-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ram
To RAM, v. a. बलात् or बलेन निविश् (c. 10. -वेशयति -यितुं) or प्रविश्,<BR>अतिबलेन निविश्, अतिबलेन प्रणुद् (c. 6. -णुदति -णोत्तुं), अतिबलेन<BR>ताडयित्वा निविश् or अन्तः प्रविश् or सम्बाध् (c. 1. -बाधते -धितुं) or<BR>सम्पीड् (c. 10. -पीडयति -यितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=654-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rama
RĀMA, s. The name common to three incarnations of Viṣṇu,<BR>viz. 1. Paraśu Rāma, or Rāma with the axe, the sixth<BR>avatār or incarnation of Viṣṇu. He was a Brahman,<BR>the son of the holy sage Jamadagni, and born at the begin-<BR>ning of the second or Treta age, for the purpose of<BR>repressing the tyranny, and punishing the violence of<BR>the Kshatriya or military tribe. He appears to typefy<BR>the class of Brahmans, and their contest with the Ksha-<BR>triyas. Some of his names are परशुरामः -मकः, परशुधरः, पर्शुरामः,<BR>जमदग्निसुतः, जामदग्न्यः. 2. Rāmachandra or the moon-like<BR>Rāma, the seventh incarnation of Viṣṇu. He was<BR>born into the world as the son of Daśaratha, king of<BR>Oude, and great grandson of Raghu, at the close of the<BR>second or Treta age, for the purpose of destroying the<BR>demons who infested the earth, and especially Rāvana, the<BR>Daitya sovereign of Ceylon. His names are रामचन्द्रः,<BR>रघुनन्दनः, रघूद्वहः, रघुवरः, रघुनाथः, राघवः, रावणारिः m., रावण-<BR>जित् m., दशास्यजित् m., मखत्राता m. (तृ), रामभद्रः. 3. Balarāma,<BR>or the strong Rāma, according to some the eighth incar-<BR>nation of Viṣṇu. He was born at the end of the Dvā-<BR>para, or third age, as the seventh son of Vasudeva and<BR>Devakī, and therefore elder brother of Krishna, but was<BR>transferred from the womb of Devakī to that of Rohinī<BR>the other wife of Vasudeva. Hence one of his names<BR>सङ्कर्षणः. He is sometimes regarded as an incarnation<BR>of the serpent Ananta or Śeṣa, and hence called, अनन्तः,<BR>शेषः. His other names are बलरामः, बलदेवः, बलभद्रः, बलः,<BR>बललः, हलायुधः, हलभृत् m., हली m. (न्), सीरपाणिः m., कृष्णा-<BR>ग्रजः, अच्युताग्रजः, प्रियमधुः m., मधुप्रियः, मुष्टिकान्तकः, गुप्नचरः, रेवती-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=654-b" target="_blank">Page654-b+ 51</a>]<BR>रमणः, रेवतीशः. See BALARĀMA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=654-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ramble
To RAMBLE, v. n. इतस्ततो भ्रम् (c. 4. भ्राम्यति, भ्रमितुं) or परिभ्रम् or<BR>विहृ (c. 1. -हरति -हर्त्तुं) or पर्यट् (c. 1. -अटति -टितुं), इतस्ततो भ्रमणं<BR>कृ or परिभ्रमणं कृ, विहारं कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ramble
RAMBLE, s. भ्रमणं, परिभ्रमणं, विहारः, विहरणं, पर्यटनं, इतस्ततो विहारः,<BR>इतस्ततोगमनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rambler
