rivet
To RIVET, v. a. (Fasten with a rivet) कील् (c. 10. कीलयति<BR>-यितुं), कीलकेन बन्ध् (c. 9. बध्नाति, बन्द्धुं), कीलकबद्धं -द्धां कृ.<BR>—<BR>(Fix or fasten firmly) दृढं बन्ध्, दृढीकृ; ‘to rivet the at-<BR>tention,’ चित्ताभिनिवेशं कृ or जन्, अभिनिविष्टचित्तं -त्तां कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=695-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

riveted
RIVETED, p. p. कीलकबद्धः -द्धा -द्धं, कीलितः -ता -तं, दृढीकृतः -ता -तं;<BR>‘having the attention riveted,’ अभिनिविष्टचित्तः -त्ता -त्तं; ‘by<BR>sound,’ नादलुब्धः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=695-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

rivulet
