root
ROOT s. (That part of a plant or tree which enters the earth)<BR>मूलं, अंघ्रिः m., अंह्रिः m., ब्रध्नः, व्रघ्नः, पादः, चरणः -णं, पदं, वृक्षमूलं,<BR>वृक्षांघ्रिः m.; ‘firm roots,’ दृढमूलं, धरणमूलं; ‘having firm<BR>roots,’ दृढमूलः -ला -लं, बद्धमूलः &c.; ‘to the roots, by the<BR>roots,’ आमूलं, समूलं, मूलतस्; ‘to pluck up by the roots,’<BR>उन्मूल् (c. 10. -मूलयति -यितुं), समूलं or आमूलम् उत्पट्; ‘from root<BR>to top,’ आमूलशिखरं, आमूलचूडं; ‘to take root,’ मूलं बन्ध्;<BR>‘fibrous root,’ शिफा, जटा; ‘from a radicant branch,’ अव-<BR>रोहः; ‘bulbous root,’ कन्दः -न्दं; ‘root-digger,’ मूलोत्पाटजीवी m.<BR>— (Lower part of any thing) अधोभागः, अधमभागः, जाहः;<BR>the latter is only applied to parts of the body of animals;<BR>as, ‘the root of the tail,’ पुच्छजाहः; ‘of the hair,’ केशजाहः.<BR>— (Original, source, first cause) मूलं, वीजं, योनिः m. f.,<BR>आदिः m., हेतुः m., मूलहेतुः m., प्रथमहेतुः m., निदानं, कारणं, मूल-<BR>कारणं, आदिकारणं, आदिहेतुः m., गर्भः; ‘having for its root,’<BR>मूल or मूलक in comp.; as, ‘happiness, having its root<BR>in contentment,’ सन्तोषमूलकं सुखं; ‘strife having its root<BR>in avarice,’ लोभमूलः कलहः.<BR>— (Root of a word, radical word)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=697-b" target="_blank">Page697-b+ 51</a>]<BR>शब्दयोनिः f., प्रकृतिः f.; ‘relation of a root to its ramifica-<BR>tion,’ प्रकृतिविकृतिभावः.<BR>— (Of a number) मूलं.<BR>— (Of a square<BR>or cube) पदं, मूलं; ‘square root,’ वर्गमूलं, वर्गपदं; ‘cube-<BR>root,’ घनमूलं, घनपदं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=697-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

root
