said
SAID, p. p. उक्तः -क्ता -क्तं, प्रोक्तः -क्ता -क्तं, भाषितः -ता -तं, भणितः -ता<BR>-तं, गदितः &c., निगदितः &c., उदितः &c., अभिहितः &c., उदाहृतः<BR>&c., उदीरितः &c., जल्पितः &c., लपितः &c., आख्यातः &c.,<BR>व्याख्यातः &c.; ‘well said,’ साध्वभिहितः -ता -तं; ‘having said,’ उक्त्वा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sail
SAIL, s. (Of a ship) वातवसनं, वायुवसनं, नौकावसनं, नौवसनं, नौवस्त्रं,<BR>वातवस्त्रं, वायुवस्त्रं, नौकापटः, वायुपटः.<BR>— (Ship) नौः f., नौका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sail
To SAIL, v. n. (Move in a ship or by water) नौकया वह् in pass.<BR>(उह्यते) or गम् (c. 1. गच्छति, गन्तुं) or चल् (c. 1. चलति -लितुं) or<BR>संचर् (c. 1. -चरति -रितुं) or या (c. 2. याति -तुं) or प्लु (c. 1. प्लवते,<BR>प्लोतुं), समुद्रेण गम् or या, जलपथेन गम्; ‘he sailed over the<BR>ocean in a ship,’ नौकया समुद्रं पुप्लुवे; ‘he sails in the Ganges,’<BR>गङ्गायाम् प्लवते; ‘he sails on the ocean,’ समुद्रेण गच्छति.<BR>— (Set<BR>sail, impel a ship) नौकां or नावं चल् (c. 10. चालयति -यितुं) or<BR>सञ्चल् or वह् (c. 10. वाहयति -यितुं), नौचालनं कृ.<BR>— (Pass over<BR>in a ship) नौकया तॄ (c. 1. तरति -रितुं -रीतुं) or समुद्रपारं गम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sailing
SAILING, s. समुद्रयानं, समुद्रगमनं, नौकाचालनं, नौकावाहनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sailing
SAILING, part. समुद्रयायी -यिनी -यि (न्), उह्यमानः -ना -नं, प्लवमानः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sailor
SAILOR, s. नाविकः, समुद्रगः, समुद्रयायी m. (न्), समुद्रगामी m., निर्यामः<BR>-मकः, पोतवाहः -हकः, नौकावाहकः, नौवाहकः, नौचालकः. See<BR>MARINER.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

saint
SAINT, s. सिद्धः, सिद्धजनः, सिद्धपुरुषः, पवित्रलोकः, पुण्यलोकः, पवि-<BR>त्रजनः, ऋषिः m., रिषिः m., मुनिः m., साधुः m., यतेन्द्रियः, नियते-<BR>न्द्रियः, जितेन्द्रियः, पूतात्मा m. (न्), पुण्यात्मा m., परमार्थविद् m.,<BR>आत्मज्ञः, परपुरुषः, महापुरुषः, मौनी m. (न्), मुमुक्षुः m., यती m.,<BR>महातपाः m. (स्), पावकः, सत्पवचाः m. (स्), निर्ग्रन्थः; ‘patron-<BR>saint,’ इष्टदेवता; ‘a company of saints,’ सिद्धसंघः; ‘a suc-<BR>cession of saints,’ सिद्धपरम्परा; ‘the seven great saints<BR>forming the Great Bear constellation,’ सप्तर्षयः m. pl. These<BR>are sometimes called Prajāpatis, and, as created by<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=706-a" target="_blank">Page706-a+ 51</a>]<BR>Brahma, Brahmarshis or Brahmādikas. Their names<BR>are मरीचिः, अत्रिः, अङ्गिरस्, पुलस्त्यः or पुलस्तिः, पुलहः, क्रतुः,<BR>वशिष्ठः. Some authorities add the names of भृगुः, दक्षः,<BR>कश्यपः नारदः and प्रचेतस् to the list of Brahmarshis or<BR>Prajāpatis. According to the Viṣṇu Purāna there are<BR>three kinds of Rishis or saints. 1. Brahmarshis, ब्रह्मर्षयः m. pl.,<BR>or saints who are the sons of Brahmā, or Brahmans, such<BR>as Marīchi, Atri, Vaśiṣtha, &c., dwelling in the sphere<BR>of Brahma 2. Devarshis, देवर्षयः m. pl., or saints who<BR>are also demigods, as Nārada, Nara, Nārāyana, Kardama,<BR>&c., dwelling in the region of the gods. 3. Rājarṣis,<BR>राजर्षयः m. pl., royal saints or holy personages who are<BR>also kings or men of the military class, and who have<BR>attained^1 to the rank of Rajarshi from the practice of re-<BR>ligious austerities. Such were Ikṣvāku, Viśvamitra,<BR>son of Gadhi, Purūravas, Dushmanta, &c. Their sphere<BR>is the heaven of Indra. Four other classes of Rishis<BR>are enumerated in the Amara Kosha, viz. 1. Maharshis,<BR>नहवयः m. pl., or great saints, such as Vyāsa, the arranger<BR>of the Vedas. &c. 2. Paramarshis, परमर्षयः m. pl., or most<BR>excellent saints, such as the Muni Bhela, the author of<BR>some medical works. 3. Kāndarṣis, काण्डर्षयः m. pl., or<BR>saints and sages who teach a particular kānda or section<BR>of the Vedas, as Jaimini, founder of the Pūrva Mīmānsa<BR>system, &c. 4. Śrutarṣis, श्रुतर्षयः m. pl., or inspired<BR>saints, as the author of the medical work called suśruta, &c.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210422. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

saint-anthonys fire
SAINT-ANTHONY'S FIRE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sainted
SAINTED, p. p. सिद्धलोकारोपितः -ता -तं, अतिपुण्यः -ण्या -ण्यं, अतिपवित्रः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

saint-like
SAINT-LIKE, SAINTLY, a. साधुसदृशः -शी -शं, सिद्धसदृशः &c., पुण्यात्मा<BR>-त्मा -त्म (न्), पूदात्मा &c., अतिपुण्यः -ण्या -ण्यं, अतिपवित्रः -त्रा -त्रं,<BR>अतिधार्म्मिकः -की -कं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

