SĀNKHYA, s. (A system of philosophy ascribed to the Muni<BR>Kapila. It asserts duality द्वैतं, or the co-existence of<BR>two principles in the universe, viz. spirit and matter.<BR>Its doctrines being opposed to the oneness of the Vedas<BR>led to the formation of another school called the Ve-<BR>dānta or Uttara-Mīmānasā system, asserting the opposite<BR>idea of unity एकत्वं or अद्वैतं, and shewing that the end or<BR>aim of the Vedas was to inculcate the oneness of Spirit or<BR>God) सांख्यः, सांख्यदर्शनं; ‘with the commentary,’ सांख्यकारिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sanskrit
SANSKRIT, s. (The classical and sacred language of the Hindūs,<BR>from which are formed all their modern dialects. The<BR>word means highly polished and artificially constructed)<BR>संस्कृतं, संस्कृतोक्तिः f., संस्कृतभाषा, ब्राह्मणभाषा, देवभाषा, दैवभाषा, आदिभाषा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sap
SAP, s. (Of plants) सारः, रसः, द्रवः, मज्जा, मज्जा m. (न्), निर्यासः,<BR>निकरः, सत्त्वं, वृक्षसारः, वृक्षरसः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sap
To SAP, v. a. (Undermine) अधस् or अधस्तात् खन् (c. 1. खनति<BR>-नितुं), अधोभागे गूढखातं कृ, अधो खात्वा पर्यस् (c. 4. -अस्यति -सितुं)<BR>or निपत् (c. 10. -पातयति -यितुं) or नश् (c. 10. नाशयति -यितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

