shastra
SHĀSTRA, SHĀSTER, s. A term applied to scientific or philo-<BR>sophical treatises and books of law. There are properly<BR>only six Ṣāstras, comprising the five philosophical sys-<BR>tems (see SCHOOL), and the code of legal institutes; viz.<BR>1. मीमांसाशास्त्रं or पूर्व्वमीमांसाशास्त्रं, 2. सांख्यशास्त्रं, 3. वेदान्तशास्त्रं,<BR>4. न्यायशास्त्रं, including under it the वैशेषिकशास्त्रं, 5. योगशास्त्रं,<BR>6. धर्म्मशास्त्रं. The last includes the celebrated code of<BR>Manu or मानवधर्म्मशास्त्रं. The term Ṣāstra is also applied<BR>to less important branches of literature, and when used in<BR>the singular number denotes the body of all that has<BR>been written on each subject; as, ‘Treatises on rhetoric,’<BR>अलङ्कारशास्त्रं; ‘poetical works,’ काव्यशास्त्रं; ‘Treatises on<BR>the mechanical arts,’ शिल्पिशास्त्रं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=735-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shatter
To SHATTER, v. a. (Break into many pieces) शतखण्डशः कृ or<BR>भिद् or भञ्ज्, सहस्रखण्डशः कृ, बहुखण्डशः कृ or भञ्ज्, शतखण्डीकृ,<BR>शतचूर्णीकृ, खण्डविखण्डीकृ, बहुशकलीकृ, खण्डं खण्डं कृ, छिन्नभिन्नीकृ,<BR>छेदविच्छेदं कृ, खण्ड्, मृद्, निष्पिष्, परिभञ्ज्, प्रभञ्ज्, विदॄ, चूर्ण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=735-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

