shiver
To SHIVER, v. a. शतखण्डशः कृ or भिद्, सूक्ष्मखण्डशो भिद्, शतखण्डीकृ,<BR>सहस्रखण्डशो भञ्ज्, शतचूर्णीकृ, चूर्णीकृ, चूर्ण, निष्पिष्. See To<BR>SHATTER, v. a.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shiver
To SHIVER, v. n. (Fall or be broken into many small pieces)<BR>सहस्रखण्डशो भिद् in pass. or पत्, शतखण्डशो भिद् in pass.,<BR>शतचूर्णीभू.<BR>— (Quake or shake with cold, &c.) शीतार्त्तत्वात्<BR>कम्प् (c. 1. कम्पते -म्पितुं) or विकम्प् or प्रकम्प्, हिमार्त्तत्वाद् वेप्<BR>(c. 1. वेपते -पितुं) or प्रवेप्, सीत्कारं कृ, शीत्कारं कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shiver
SHIVER, s. (Small fragment) सूक्ष्मखण्डः -ण्डकः, भित्तिः f., शकलः<BR>-लं, छेदः, दलं, छिन्नं, भिन्नं; ‘into shivers,’ सहस्रखण्डशः, सूक्ष्म-<BR>खण्डशः.<BR>— (Shaking) कम्पः, सीत्कारः, see SHIVERING, s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

shivered
