sitting
SITTING, part. आसीनः -ना -नं, अध्यासीनः &c., उपविष्टः -ष्टा -ष्ट,<BR>निषीदन् -दन्ती -दत् (त्); ‘on a seat,’ आसनोपविष्टः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=746-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

situated
SITUATED, SITUATE, a. (Placed or standing with regard to any<BR>other object) स्थः स्था स्थं, स्थितः -ता -तं, अवस्थितः &c., संस्थः<BR>-स्था -स्थं, संस्थितः -ता -तं, दिश्यः -श्या -श्यं; ‘situated near,’<BR>समीपस्थः &c., समीपस्थितः &c.; ‘situated to the south,’ दक्षि-<BR>णस्थः -स्था -स्थं, दक्षिणदिश्यः &c.; ‘towards the east,’ पूर्व्वस्थः<BR>&c., पूर्व्वदिश्यः &c.; ‘well situated,’ सुस्थितः -ता -तं, सुसंस्थितः<BR>&c.; ‘pleasantly situated,’ सौवास्तवः -वी -वं.<BR>— (With regard<BR>to men or things) स्थः स्था -स्थं, स्थितः -ता -तं, अवस्थ in comp.,<BR>अवस्थाप्राप्तः -प्ता -प्तं, अवस्थापन्नः -न्ना -न्नं; ‘well situated,’ सुस्थः<BR>&c., सुस्थितः &c.; ‘so situated,’ तदवस्थः -स्था -स्थं; ‘how<BR>situated?’ किमवस्थः -स्था -स्थं; ‘badly situated,’ दुःस्थितः -ता<BR>-तं, दुःस्थः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=746-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

situation
SITUATION, s. (Place, position) स्थानं, स्थितिः f., अवस्थितिः f., अव-<BR>स्थानं, आस्पदं, पदं, पदविः -वी f.<BR>— (State, circumstances) अवस्था,<BR>दशा, स्थितिः f., संस्थितिः f., भावः, वृत्तिः f., आस्पदं, पदं; ‘dis-<BR>graceful situation,’ परिभवास्पदं, परिभवपदं.<BR>— (Office, post) पदं,<BR>पदविः -वी, अधिकारः, स्थानं, स्थलं, नियोगः, व्यापारः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=746-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

siva
ŚIVA, s. A celebrated Hindū God, the Destroyer of Creation,<BR>and therefore the most formidable of the Hindū Triad.<BR>He also personifies reproduction, since the Hindū philo-<BR>sophy excludes the idea of total annihilation without<BR>subsequent regeneration. Hence he is sometimes con-<BR>founded with Brahmā, the Creator, or first person of the<BR>Triad. He is the particular god of the Tāntṛkas, or<BR>followers of the books called Tantras. His worshippers<BR>are termed Śaivas, and although not so numerous as<BR>the Vaishnavas, exalt their god to the highest place in<BR>the heavens, and combine in him many of the attributes<BR>which properly belong to the other deities. According<BR>to them Śiva is Time, Justice, Fire, Water, the Sun, the<BR>Destroyer and Creator. As presiding over generation,<BR>his type is the Linga, or Phallus, the origin probably of<BR>the Phallic emblem of Egypt and Greece. As the god<BR>of generation and of justice, which latter character he<BR>shares with the god Yama, he is represented riding<BR>a white bull. His own colour, as well as that of the<BR>bull, is generally white, referring probably to the un-<BR>sullied purity of Justice. His throat is dark blue; his<BR>hair of a light reddish colour, and thickly matted together,<BR>and gathered above his head like the hair of an ascetic.<BR>He is sometimes seen with two hands, sometimes with<BR>four, eight, or ten, and with five faces. He has three<BR>eyes, one being in the centre of his forehead, pointing<BR>up and down. These are said to denote his view of the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=747-a" target="_blank">Page747-a+ 51</a>]<BR>three divisions of time, past, present, and future. He<BR>holds a trident in his hand to denote, as some say, his<BR>relationship to water, or according to others, to show<BR>that the three great attributes of Creator, Destroyer,<BR>and Regenerator are combined in him. His loins are<BR>enveloped in a tiger's skin. In his character of Time,<BR>he not only presides over its extinction, but also its as-<BR>tronomical regulation. A crescent or half-moon on his<BR>forehead indicates the measure of time by the phases<BR>of the moon; a serpent forms one of his necklaces to<BR>denote the measure of time by years, and a second neck-<BR>lace of human skulls marks the lapse and revolution of<BR>ages, and the extinction and succession of the generations<BR>of mankind. He is often represented as entirely<BR>covered with serpents, which are the emblems of immor-<BR>tality. They are bound in his hair, round his neck,<BR>wrists, waist, arms, and legs; they serve as rings for<BR>his fingers, and earrings for his ears, and are his con-<BR>stant companions. Śiva has more than a thousand<BR>names, which are detailed at length in the sixty-ninth<BR>chapter of the Śiva Purāna. The following list of the<BR>principal of these will give the best idea of his character<BR>and attributes. (The Auspicious one) शिवः, शम्भुः m.,<BR>शङ्करः, सदाशिवः, श्रीमान् m. (त्), भद्रः, भगः.<BR>— (The great god or<BR>lord) महादेवः, ईश्वरः, महेश्वरः, महेशः, ईशः, ईशानः, नाथः, देवः.<BR>— (Lord of the universe, as worshipped at Benares) वि-<BR>श्वेश्वरः, विश्वेशः, विश्वनाथः, सर्व्वेश्वरः.<BR>— (Lord of the earth) धर-<BR>णीश्वरः.<BR>— (The seizer) हरः, हरकः, हरिः m.<BR>— (The Destroyer,<BR>a personification of Time that destroys all things) कालः,<BR>महाकालः, जगद्घाती m. (न्), जगद्भक्षकः, कालञ्जरः.<BR>— (The Repro-<BR>ducer, the Conqueror of Death and cause of life and<BR>being) भवः, मृत्युञ्जयः, मृत्युवञ्चनः, जगद्योनिः m., भूतात्मा m. (न्),<BR>जः, भरुः m.<BR>— (Disperser of the tears of mortals) रुद्रः.<BR>—<BR>(The terrific or tremendous one) भैरवः, घोरः, भीषणः, भीष्मः,<BR>भीमः.<BR>— (The fierce one) उग्रः, चण्डः.<BR>— (Blue-throat, having<BR>a dark blue and beautiful throat, so stained by the acri-<BR>mony of the poison, which he swallowed on its produc-<BR>tion at the churning of the ocean; see OCEAN) नीलकण्ठः,<BR>श्यामकण्ठः, नीलग्रीवः, शितिकण्ठः, कालकण्ठः, श्रीकण्ठः, नीललो-<BR>हितः.<BR>— (Tri-ocular, having three eyes) त्रिलोचनः, त्रिनेत्रः,<BR>त्रिदृक् m. (श्), त्रिनयनः, त्र्यक्षः.<BR>— (Having deformed or un-<BR>natural eyes) विरूपाक्षः.<BR>— (Moon-crested, having a crescent<BR>on his brow) चन्द्रमौलिः m., चन्द्रशेखरः, शशिशेखरः, इन्दुभृत्,<BR>चन्द्रापीडः, शशीशः, चन्द्रिलः, सोमः.<BR>— (Borne on, or accom-<BR>panied by the Bull which personifies Justice) वृषवाहनः,<BR>वृषभवाहनः, वृषध्वजः, वृषभध्वजः, धर्म्मवाहनः, वृषपतिः m., वृषभगतिः m.,<BR>वृषपर्व्वा m. (न्), वृषाङ्कः, वृषाञ्चनः, वृषाणकः.<BR>— (Having matted<BR>or braided hair) धूर्जटिः m., जटाधरः, जटाधारी m. (न्), जटिलः,<BR>जटाटङ्कः, जटाटीरः कपर्दी m. (न्), कर्पदः.<BR>— (Having sky-coloured<BR>hair) व्योमकेशी m. (न्), व्योमकेशः.<BR>— (Trident-bearer) शूली m.<BR>(न्), त्रिशूली m., शूलधरुः, पिनाकी m.<BR>— (Lord of animals or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=747-b" target="_blank">Page747-b+ 51</a>]<BR>cattle) पशुपतिः m., गोपतिः, गोरक्षः, गोपालकः.<BR>— (Lord of spirits)<BR>भूतेशः, भूतनाथः, भूतः.<BR>— Bearer of the Ganges, this river<BR>having on its descent from heaven alighted on his head,<BR>and thence descended upon earth, through a chasm in the<BR>Himālaya mountains called Gomukha) गङ्गाधरः.<BR>— (Clothed<BR>with a tiger's skin) कृत्तिवासाः m. (स्), कृत्तिवासः.<BR>— (Bound<BR>or covered with snakes) अहिब्रध्नः.<BR>— (Having a necklace<BR>of human skulls) कपालभृत्, कपाली m. (न्), अस्थिमाली m.,<BR>पुरुषास्थिमाली m., अस्थिधन्वा m. (न्), भगाली m.<BR>— (The white<BR>one or yellowish white) शुचिः, गौरः, हरिणः.<BR>— (Conqueror<BR>and Destroyer of the district and king of Tripura) त्रिपु-<BR>रजित्, त्रिपुरसूदनः, त्रिपुरदहनः, त्रिपुरान्तकः.<BR>— (Presiding over<BR>the three Vedas, or the three letters of the mystical syl-<BR>lable om) त्र्यम्बकः.<BR>— (He of whom one form is water) जल-<BR>मूर्त्तिः m.<BR>— (The Steadfast) स्थाणुः m.<BR>— (The Universal) सर्व्वः.<BR>— (The Omnipresent) सर्व्वगः.<BR>— (The Omniscient) सर्व्वज्ञः.<BR>—<BR>(The Imperishable) अक्षरः.<BR>— (The Five-faced) पञ्चमुखः,<BR>पञ्चाननः, पञ्चवक्त्रः, सर्व्वतोमुखः.<BR>— (Scorcher of Cupid, see KĀMA-<BR>DEVA) स्मरहरः, कामध्वंसी m. (न्), अनङ्गासुहृद्, भर्गः.<BR>— (Restorer of<BR>his body) पराङ्गदः.<BR>— (Lord of Kailāsa, in the Himālayas, the<BR>favourite haunt of both Śiva and Kuvera) गिरीशः, गिरिशः,<BR>कैलासौकाः m. (स्), कैलासनिकेतनः.<BR>— (Lord of Benares) काशी-<BR>नाथः, काशीशः; hence one of the names of Benares is<BR>रुद्रावासः, शिवपुरी.<BR>— (Having three residences) त्रिधामा m.<BR>—<BR>(Destroyer of Daksha's sacrifice. That sage having on<BR>one occasion made a sacrifice, to which he invited all<BR>the gods, excepting his son-in-law Śiva and his daughter<BR>Durgā, the latter went unbid, and being received coldly,<BR>threw herself into the fire, whence emanated a form of<BR>Śiva, who decapitated the sage) दक्षाध्वरध्वंसकृत्, दक्षयज्ञवि-<BR>नाशी m. (न्), क्रतुध्वंसी m.<BR>— (He of whom the seed was cast<BR>into Fire) वह्निरेताः m. (स्), कृशानुरेताः m.<BR>— (Teacher of the<BR>gṛhya, or book of domestic rites) गृह्यगुरुः.<BR>— (Possessor<BR>of the head of Brahmā, having in a dispute cut off one<BR>of the heads of that deity) ब्रह्ममूर्द्धभृत्.<BR>— (Enemy of the<BR>demon Pura) पुरारिः m., पुरासुहृद्.<BR>— (Enemy of the demon<BR>Andhaka) अन्धकरिपुः m.<BR>— (He who cuts to pieces with<BR>his axe) खण्डपरशुः m., खण्डपर्शुः m.<BR>— (Armed with the<BR>Khatvānga or Pānśula) खट्वाङ्गी m., खट्वाङ्गभृत् m., पांशुली m.<BR>— (Armed with a rope) पाशी m.<BR>— (Lord of devotion or<BR>devotees) योगेशः.<BR>— (Lord of gold) हेमकेशः.<BR>— (Fond of danc-<BR>ing) नाट्यप्रियः.<BR>— (The naked one) दिगम्बरः, दिग्वासाः m. (स्),<BR>नग्नः.<BR>— (Covered with sandal powder) पांशुचन्दनः, पांशुलः.<BR>— (Mounted on a dog in his terrific form) श्वाश्वः.<BR>— (The<BR>perverse) वामः, वामदेवः.<BR>— (Husband of Pārvatī) पार्व्वतीनाथः.<BR>— (Of Durga) दुर्गापतिः, दक्षजापतिः.<BR>— (Of Gaurī) गौरीपतिः.<BR>—<BR>(Of Umā) उमापतिः.<BR>— (Of Bhavānī) भवानीपतिः.<BR>— (Lord of<BR>the Pramathas, his attendants) प्रमथाधिपः.<BR>— (Lord of Nandi,<BR>one of his chief attendants) नन्दीशः, नन्दीश्वरः, नन्दिवर्धनः.<BR>— (Lord of Bhṛngi, one of his chamberlains) भृङ्गीशः.<BR>—<BR>(Loved of Viṣṇu) हरिप्रियः.<BR>— (Having Viṣṇu as his dart.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=748-a" target="_blank">Page748-a+ 51</a>]<BR>that deity having served him for a shaft which set the<BR>city of Tripura on fire) हरिशरः. Some of his other names,<BR>the derivation of which is not very apparent, are the fol-<BR>lowing: नकुलः, अध्यूढः, शिपिविष्टः, शिविपिष्ठः, श्रीरङ्गः, नात्रः,<BR>मृडः, कुष्करः, वारः, उः m.<BR>— (Under the emblem of the Phallus)<BR>लिङ्गं; ‘a worshipper of him under that type,’ लिङ्गी m.<BR>—<BR>(A form of Śiva, half male and half female) अर्द्धनारीशः,<BR>अर्द्धनारीनटेश्वरः.<BR>— (Inferior manifestations of him, called<BR>Bhairavas) असिताङ्गः, रुरुः m., चण्डः, क्रोधः, उन्मत्तः, कुपतिः,<BR>भीषणः, संहरः, नकुलः.<BR>— (His wife) पार्व्वती, दुर्गा, गौरी, उमा,<BR>सती, भवानी, see PARVATĪ; as the symbol of created nature<BR>his wife is called प्रकृतिः.<BR>— (His sons) कार्त्तिकेयः, गणेशः, see<BR>KĀRTIKEYA, GANESHA.<BR>— (His attendants) प्रमथः, शिवकीर्त्तनः.<BR>— (Some of the names of his attendants are) नन्दी m.,<BR>नन्दिः m., भृङ्गी m., नाडीदेहः, नाडीविग्रहः, नाडीस्नेहः, भृङ्गरिटः,<BR>तण्डुः, पशुः.<BR>— (His vehicle or bull) वृषः, नन्दी m.<BR>— (Tem-<BR>ple consecrated to his bull) गोपुटिकः.<BR>— (His trident)<BR>त्रिशूलं, पिनाकः, महितं, पाशुपतास्त्रं.<BR>— (His bow) पिनाकः, अजगवं.<BR>— (One of his weapons, a staff with transverse pieces,<BR>representing the breast-bone and ribs, surmounted by a<BR>skull) खट्वाङ्गं, पांशुलः.<BR>— (His rope for binding incorrigible<BR>offenders) पाशः.<BR>— (His musical instrument, a kind of rattle,<BR>shaped like an hour-glass, and held in one hand) डमरुः m.<BR>— (His serpent earrings) नागकुण्डलं.<BR>— (His necklace of<BR>skulls) अस्थिमाला, मुण्डमाला.<BR>— (His matted hair) जटा, जटा-<BR>जूटः, कपर्दः.<BR>— (His superhuman power) विभूतिः f., भूतिः f., see<BR>SUPERHUMAN, a.<BR>— (Daitya flayed by him) रुरुः.<BR>— (Worship-<BR>per of Śiva) शैवः, शैव्यः, शिवज्ञः, पाञ्चार्थिकः. Many plants<BR>are sacred to Śiva, as the aśoka, vilva, mango, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=746-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

six
SIX, a. षट् m. f. n. pl. (षष्), षट्संख्यकः -का -कं, षट्कः -ट्का -ट्कं;<BR>‘six months,’ षण्मासाः m. pl., षण्मासं; ‘the six seasons,’<BR>षडृतवः m. pl.; ‘of six months standing,’ षाण्मासिकः -की -कं,<BR>षण्मास्यः -स्या -स्यं; ‘six-fingered,’ षडङ्गुलिः -लिः -लि; ‘six-<BR>angled,’ षट्कोणः -णा -णं; ‘six-limbed,’ षडङ्गः -ङ्गा -ङ्गं; ‘six-<BR>armed,’ षड्भुजः -जा -जं; ‘six-faced,’ षण्मुखः -खा -खं; ‘a yoke<BR>of six oxen,’ षङ्गवं; ‘having six feet,’ षट्पदः -दा -दं; ‘in<BR>six ways,’ षड्धा; ‘the aggregate of six,’ षट्कं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

six-fold
SIX-FOLD, a. षङ्गुणः -णा -णं, षड्विधः -धा -धं, षट्कः -ट्का -ट्कं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sixteen
SIXTEEN, a. षोडशः m. f. n. pl. (न्), षोडशकः -का -कं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sixteenth
SIXTEENTH, a. षोडशः -शी -शं; ‘a sixteenth part,’ षोडशांशः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sixth
SIXTH, a. षष्ठः -ष्ठी -ष्ठं, षष्ठकः -का -कं; ‘a sixth part,’ षड्भागः,<BR>षडंशः; ‘a sixth meal,’ षष्ठान्नं; ‘being or having a sixth,’<BR>षष्ठी -ष्ठिनी -ष्ठि (न्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sixthly
SIXTHLY, adv. षष्ठतर्, षष्ठस्थाने, षष्ठपदे.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sixtieth
SIXTIETH, a. पष्टितमः -मी -मं, षष्टः -ष्टी -ष्टं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

sixty
SIXTY, a. षष्टिः f., षष्टिसंख्यकः -का -कं; ‘he reigned sixty years,’<BR>षष्टिम् अब्दान् राज्यं चकार; ‘sixth-one,’ एकषष्टिः; ‘sixty-two,’<BR>द्वापष्टिः; ‘sixty-three,’ त्रयःपष्टिः; ‘sixty-four,’ चतुःषष्टिः;<BR>‘sixty-five,’ पञ्चपष्टिः; ‘sixty-six,’ षट्पष्ठिः; ‘sixty-seven,’<BR>सप्तषष्टिः; ‘sixty-eight,’ अष्टाषष्टिः; ‘sixty-nine,’ नवषष्टिः, एको-<BR>नसप्ततिः, ऊनसप्ततिः; ‘aggregate of sixty,’ षष्टिकं; ‘bought<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=748-b" target="_blank">Page748-b+ 51</a>]<BR>with sixty,’ षष्टिकः -का -कं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

size
SIZE, s. (Bulk) परिमाणं, मानं, परिमितिः f., प्रमाणं, मात्रं, आकारः,<BR>आकारमानं, आकृतिः f., आकृतिमानं, महत्त्वमानं, महत्त्वपरिमाणं,<BR>आकारपरिमाणं, आकृतिपरिमाणं; ‘of the same size,’ समपरिमाणः<BR>-णा -णं, सममात्रः -त्रा -त्रं; ‘of the size of an egg,’ अण्डपरिमाणः<BR>-णा -णं; ‘of the size of a grain of mustard,’ सर्षपपरिमाणः<BR>-णा -णं; ‘of unequal size,’ विषमपरिमाणः &c., असमपरिमाणः<BR>&c.; of all sizes,’ उत्तमाधममध्यमाः m. pl.; ‘having ascer-<BR>tained the size and distance of the moon,’ चन्द्रस्य मानं<BR>दूरत्वं च ज्ञात्वा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

skain
SKAIN, SKEIN, s. पञ्जिका, पिञ्जिका, पञ्जिः -ञ्जी f., पिञ्जिः -ञ्जी f.; ‘of<BR>silk,’ कौशिकसूत्रपञ्जी, कौशिकसूत्रग्रन्थिः m.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

skate
SKATE, s. (For moving on the ice) हिमसंहतजलोपरि विसर्पणयोग्या<BR>लोहयुक्तपादुका or स्खलनयोग्यपादुका, स्खलनपादुका.<BR>— (The fish),<BR>see SCATE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

skate
