To TAINT, v. a. दुष् (c. 10. दूषयति -यितुं), लिप् (c. 6. लिम्पति, लेप्तुं),<BR>दोषयुक्तं -क्तां कृ, दूषणं कृ. See To CORRUPT, INSPECT, STAIN.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=794-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

taint
TAINT, s. दूषणं, दोषः, कलङ्कः, मलं, लेपः -पनं. See STAIN.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=794-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tainted
TAINTED, p. p. दूषितः -ता -तं, लिप्तः -प्ता -प्तं, कलङ्कितः -ता -तं, सक-<BR>लङ्कः -ङ्का -ङ्कं; ‘as meat,’ पूतिगन्धिकः -का -कं, दुर्गन्धी -न्धिनी &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=794-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

take
To TAKE, v. a. ग्रह् (c. 9. गृह्लाति -ह्लीते, ग्रहीतुं), प्रतिग्रह्, अभिग्रह्,<BR>परिग्रह्, सम्प्रग्रह्, उपसम्प्रग्रह्, आदा (c. 3. -ददाति -दत्ते -दातुं), उपादा,<BR>लभ् (c. 1. लभते, लब्धुं), उपलभ्, धा (c. 3. धत्ते, धातुं), प्रताष् (c. 6.<BR>-इच्छति -एपितुं), ग्रहणं कृ, आदानं कृ.<BR>— (Seize) हृ (c. 1. हरति,<BR>हर्त्तुं), धृ (c. 1. धरति, धर्त्तुं), हरणं कृ.<BR>— (Captivate), see the word.<BR>— (Apprehend) ग्रह्, उपलभ्, अवगम्.<BR>— (Feel, experience, be<BR>affected by) उपहतः -ता -तं भू, अनुभू, उपगम्, उपागम्, विद्.<BR>—<BR>(Swallow) गॄ, निगॄ, ग्रस्, खाद्, पा.<BR>— (Admit) ग्रह्, स्वीकृ, अङ्गीकृ.<BR>— (Gain possession of) आप्, प्राप्, अर्ज्, उपार्ज्, लभ्, आसद्,<BR>अधिगम्, see To GAIN.<BR>— (Take possession of) आक्रम् (c. 1.<BR>-क्रामति -क्रमितुं), आविश्, समाविश्.<BR>— (Require) आकांक्ष्, see To<BR>REQUIRE.<BR>— (Take away) अपनी (c. 1. -नयति -नेतुं), नी, अपहृ,<BR>हृ, see To REMOVE, v. a.<BR>— (Take back) प्रत्यादा; ‘lead back,’<BR>प्रतिनी.<BR>— (Take down), see To PULL DOWN, DEPRESS, WRITE.<BR>— (Take in), see To COMPREHEND, CHEAT.<BR>— (Take off) अपनी,<BR>अवतॄ or उत्तॄ in caus., उत्कृष्, see To STRIP, DIVEST, IMITATE.<BR>—<BR>(Take up), see To LIFT, UNDERTAKE, OCCUPY, ENGROSS, COM-<BR>PRISE.<BR>— (Take upon one's self) स्वीकृ, see To UNDERTAKE.<BR>Obs. The word ‘take’ in English has often no equivalent<BR>in Sanskrit, but must be rendered by some other form<BR>of expression. It may often be expressed by the roots<BR>कृ or भू in conjunction with a noun, and is not unfre-<BR>quently inherent in the verb without being expressed at<BR>all, as in the following examples.<BR>— (Take aim) बद्धानुशयः<BR>-या -यं भू, लक्षीकृ, अनुसन्धा.<BR>— (Take an airing) वायुहेतोः परि-<BR>क्रम् or विहृ.<BR>— (Take breath), see To PAUSE, REST.<BR>— (Take<BR>care, take heed), see To HEED.<BR>— (Take care of) रक्ष, see under<BR>CARE.<BR>— (Take a course), see To RESORT.<BR>— (Take effect) प्रभू,<BR>सप्रभावः -वा -वं भू, प्रबलीभू, सफलीभू, see EFFICACIOUS.<BR>— (Take<BR>hold), see To SEIZE, HOLD.<BR>— (Take in hand), see To UNDER-<BR>TAKE.<BR>— (Take leave) आमन्त्र्, आमन्त्रणं कृ, see FAREWELL.<BR>—<BR>(Take notice), see To OBSERVE, NOTICE.<BR>— (Take pains), see<BR>under PAIN.<BR>— (Take part), see To SHARE.<BR>— (Take place),<BR>see To HAPPEN.<BR>— (Take root), see To ROOT, v. n.<BR>— (Take to<BR>task) निर्भर्त्स्, see To REPROVE.<BR>— (Take the name) नाम ग्रह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

take
To TAKE, v. n. (Betake one's self) आश्रि, see RECOURSE, RESORT.<BR>—<BR>(Gain reception, succeed) सिध् (c. 4. सिध्यति, सेद्धुं), सम्पद् (c. 4.<BR>-पद्यते -पत्तुं), प्रसिद्धिं प्राप्, प्रसिद्धीभू, लोकप्रसिद्धः -द्धा -द्धं भू.<BR>— (Have<BR>effect) प्रभू.<BR>— (Take after) अनुकृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

taken
TAKEN, p. p. गृहीतः -ता -तं, आदत्तः -त्ता -त्तं, आत्तः &c., उपात्तः &c.<BR>— (Gained) प्राप्तः -प्ता -प्तं, आप्तः &c., लब्धः -ब्धा -ब्धं.<BR>— (Taken<BR>away) अपनीतः -ता -तं, अपहृतः -ता -तं, हृतः &c., see REMOVED.<BR>— (Taken down) अवपातितः -ता -तं, पातितः -ता -तं, see LOWERED,<BR>HUMBLED.<BR>— (Taken off, as clothes, &c.) अवतारितः -ता -तं, see<BR>STRIPPED.<BR>— (Captivated) मोहितः -ता -तं, हृतचित्तः -त्ता -त्तं, वशी-<BR>कृतः &c.; ‘let it be taken,’ गृह्यतां; ‘proper to be taken,’<BR>ग्रहणीयः -या -यं, आदेयः -या -यं; ‘having taken,’ गृहीत्वा, आदाय;<BR>‘having taken his bow and arrow,’ गृहीतेषुकार्म्मुकः, आत्तेषु-<BR>कार्म्मुकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

taker
TAKER, s. ग्राही m. -हिणी f. (न्), ग्राहकः -हिका, ग्रहीता m. -त्री f.<BR>(तृ), आदायी m. -यिनी f., प्रतिग्रहीता m., हर्त्ता m., हारी m.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

taking
TAKING, s. (The act) ग्रहणं, ग्रहः, ग्राहः, प्रतिग्रहणं, प्रतिग्राहः, आदानं,<BR>उपादानं, स्वीकरणं, स्वीकारः; ‘taking away,’ अपनयनं, हरणं,<BR>अपहरणं, see REMOVAL.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

taking
TAKING, a. मनोहारी -रिणी &c., हृदयग्राही &c. See CAPTIVATING.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

talc
TALC, s. अभ्रकं, अभं, अमलं, निर्मलं, गिरिजं, गिरिजामलं, मेघजालं,<BR>मेघनालं, शुभ्रं, स्वच्छपत्रं, अम्बरं, अन्तरीक्षं, भृङ्गं; ‘calx of it,’ अभ्र-<BR>कभस्म m. (न्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tale
TALE, s. कथा, उपाख्यानं, आख्यानं, परिकथा, उदन्तः. See STORY.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tale-bearer
TALE-BEARER, s. कर्णेजपः, कर्णजपः, उपजापकः, पिशुनः, भेदजनकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tale-bearing
TALE-BEARING, s. पैशुन्यं पिशुनता, उजापः, कर्णेजापः, दोषानुवादः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

talent
TALENT, s. (Endowment) गुणः.<BR>— (Great abilities) बुद्धिवैभवं, बुद्धि-<BR>कौशलं, बुद्धिशक्तिः f., बुद्धिप्रभावः, दाक्षिण्यं, see GENIUS.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

talented
TALENTED, a. गुणी -णिनी -णि (न्), गुणवान् &c. See under GENIUS.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

talisman
TALISMAN, s. कवचः -चं, संवदनं -ना, यन्त्रं. See AMULET.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

talk
To TALK, v. n. भाष् (c. 1. भाषते -षितुं), सम्भाष्, वद् (c. 1. वदति -दितुं),<BR>संवद्, आलप्, मन्त्र्, कथोषकथनं कृ. See To CONVERSE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

talk
TALK, s. कथोपथनं, संवादः, सम्भाषा -षणं, आलापः, कथा, कथाप्रसङ्गः,<BR>see CONVERSATION; ‘small talk,’ लघुभाषणं; ‘fine talk,’ शब्द-<BR>पाण्डित्यं; ‘mere talk,’ वाङ्मात्रं.<BR>— (Report) वदन्तिः -न्ती f.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

talkative
TALKATIVE, a. वावदूकः -का -कं, कथनः &c. See LOQUACIOUS.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

talkativeness
TALKATIVENESS, s. वावदूकता, वाचालता. See LOQUACIOUSNESS.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

talker
TALKER, s. वक्ता m. (क्तृ), कथकः, भाषी m. (न्), आलाषी m., वादी m.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tall
TALL, a. तुङ्गः -ङ्गा -ङ्गं, उत्तुङ्गः &c., प्रांशुः -शुः -शु, उच्चः -च्चा -च्चं, see<BR>HIGH; ‘in stature,’ उच्चदेहः -हा -हं, उच्चमूर्त्तिः -र्त्तिः -र्त्ति, दीर्घदेहः<BR>-हा -हं, दीर्घमूर्त्तिः &c., दीर्घतनुः -नुः -नु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tallness
TALLNESS, s. उच्चता, तुङ्गता, प्रांशुता, उन्नतिः f.; ‘of stature,’ देहदी-<BR>र्घता, दीर्घदेहत्वं, शरीरदीर्घता, शरीरोच्चता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tallow
TALLOW, s. मेषवपा, मेषवसा, गोवपा, गोवसा, गोमेदस् n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tallow-candle
TALLOW-CANDLE, s. गोवपामयदीपकः, गोवसानिर्म्मितदीपिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tallow-chandler
TALLOW-CHANDLER, s. गोवपाविक्रयी m. (न्), मेषादिवपाव्यापारी m.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tally
TALLY, To TALLY. See MATCH, To MATCH, v. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

talon
TALON, s. नखः, नखरः, कररुहः, करजः. See CLAW.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tamarind
TAMARIND, s. (The tree) अम्लिका, अम्लीका, आम्लिका, आम्लीका, अम्ल-<BR>फलः, तिन्तिडी, तिन्तिली, तिन्तिडीकः -का -कं, तिन्तिडिका, चिञ्चा,<BR>चुक्रा -क्री, गुरुपत्रा, चारित्रा, चरित्रा, गुरुपत्रा, चण्डः.<BR>— (The fruit)<BR>अम्लफलं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tamarisk
TAMARISK, TAMARIX, s. (Tree) पिचुलः, पिच्छिलः, झावुः m., झावुकः,<BR>बहुग्रन्थिः m., यमदूतका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tambour
TAMBOUR, TAMBOURINE, s. मृदङ्गः, पटहः. See DRUM.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tame
TAME, a. (Not wild) गृह्यः -ह्या -ह्यं, गृह्यकः -का -कं, ग्राम्यः -म्या -म्यं,<BR>गृहपुष्टः -ष्टा -ष्टं, छेकः -का -कं, अहिंस्रः -स्रा -स्रं, गृह or ग्राम in<BR>comp.; ‘a tame pigeon,’ गृहकपोतकः; ‘tame hog,’ ग्राम्य-<BR>शूकरः, ग्रामशूकरः, विड्वराहः.<BR>— (Subdued, trained) दान्तः -न्ता -न्तं,<BR>दमितः -ता -तं, वशः -शा -शं, अधीनः -ना -नं, शिक्षितः -ता -तं, उप-<BR>शान्तः &c.<BR>— (Flat, spiritless), see the words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tame
To TAME, v. a. दम् (c. 10. दमयति -यितुं), प्रदम्, क्रूरतां शम् (c. 10. शम-<BR>यति -यितुं), क्रूरताशान्तिं कृ, क्रूरतानाशं कृ, क्रूरताभङ्गं कृ, वशीकृ,<BR>निग्रह् (c. 9. -गृह्लाति -ग्रहीतुं), सन्निग्रह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tameable
TAMEABLE, a. दमनीयः -या -यं, दम्यः -म्या -म्यं, सुदमः -मा -मं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tamed
TAMED, p. p. दमितः -ता -तं, दान्तः -न्ता -न्तं, वशीकृतः -ता -तं, वशीभूतः<BR>&c., वशङ्गतः &c., शान्तः &c., शान्तक्रौर्य्यः -र्य्या -र्य्यं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tamely
TAMELY, adv. कापुरुषवत्, क्लीववत्, कातरवत्, सकातर्य्यं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tameness
TAMENESS, s. गृह्यता, वशता, वश्यता, अहिंस्रता, वशीभूतता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tamer
TAMER, s. दमकः, दमी m. (न्), दमनकारी m. See SUBDUER.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

taming
TAMING, s. दमनं, दमः, दमथः -थं, दमथुः m. See SUBJUGATION.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tamper
