tea-pot
TEA-POT, s. चहापात्रं, चहाधारः, चहाभाजनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

teach
To TEACH, v. a. उपदिश् (c. 6. -दिशति -देष्टुं), शिक्ष् (c. 10. शिक्षयति<BR>-यितुं), अनुशिक्ष्, अभिशिक्ष्, अधी in caus. (अध्यापयति -यितुं, rt.<BR>इ), पठ् in caus., शास् &c., see To INSTRUCT. Sometimes the<BR>causal expresses the sense of ‘teach;’ as, ‘he teaches<BR>to dance,’ नर्त्तयति; ‘he teaches to read,’ पाठयति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

teachable
TEACHABLE, a. शिक्षणीयः -या -यं, शिक्ष्यः -क्ष्या -क्ष्यं. See DOCILE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

teachableness
TEACHABLENESS, s. शिक्षणीयता, शिक्ष्यता, सुशिक्ष्यता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

teacher
TEACHER, s. उपदेशकः, शिक्षकः, अध्यापकः, बोधकः, अवबोधकः, see<BR>INSTRUCTOR; ‘of children,’ बालाध्यापकः, see PEDAGOGUE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

teaching
TEACHING, s. उपदेशः, शिक्षा, अध्यापनं. See INSTRUCTION.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

teak
TEAK, s. (Tree) अर्णः, शाकः, शाकाख्यः, करच्छदः, खरपत्रः, अर्जुनो-<BR>पमः, हलीनः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

