TEARFUL, a. साश्रुः -श्रुः -श्रु, सास्रुः &c., साश्रः -श्रा -श्रं, सास्रः &c.,<BR>सवाष्पः -ष्पा -ष्पं, अश्रुपूर्णः -र्णा -र्णं, वाष्प्यपूर्णः &c., अश्रुमयः -यी -यं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tearfully
TEARFULLY, adv. सवाष्पं, साश्रं, सास्रं, वाष्पाकुलवाचा, साश्रुपातं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tearing
TEARING, s. दारणं, विदारणं, विदारः, विभेदः -दनं, पाटनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tease
To TEASE, v. a. बाध् (c. 1. बाधते -धितुं). See To ANNOY, TORMENT.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

