TEETHING, s. दन्तोद्भेदः, दन्तोद्भवः, दन्तस्फोटः, दन्तोत्पत्तिः f., दन्तजननं;<BR>‘time of teething,’ दन्तोद्भेदनकालः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tegument
TEGUMENT, s. आवेष्टनं, कवचः -चं, पुटः -टी. See INTEGUMENT.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

telescope
TELESCOPE, s. दूरदर्शकयन्त्रं, महादूरदर्शकयन्त्रं, दूरदर्शनयन्त्रं, चाक्षुषयन्त्रं,<BR>दृष्टिसाधकयन्त्रं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

telingana
TELINGANA, s. (The country) अन्ध्रः, आन्ध्रः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tell
To TELL, v. a. कथ् (c. 10. कथयति -यितुं). See To RELATE, NARRATE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tell
To TELL, v. n. (Take effect) सबलीभू, सफलीभू, सप्रभावः -वा -वं भू,<BR>सिध्.<BR>— (Hit the mark), see under MARK.<BR>— (Tell of) सूच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

teller
TELLER, s. कथकः, कथिकः, आख्यायकः. See RELATER.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

telling
TELLING, s. कथनं, उपकथनं, आख्यानं, see RELATION, NARRATION.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tell-tale
TELL-TALE, s. सूचकः, सूची m. See TALE-BEARER, INFORMER.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

temerity
TEMERITY, s. साहसं, दुःसाहसं, विषमसाहसं. See RASHNESS.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

temper
To TEMPER, v. a. शम् (c. 10. शमयति -यितुं). See To MODERATE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

temper
TEMPER, s. (Of mind) शीलः, प्रकृतिः f., भावः, स्वभावः, संवेदनं;<BR>‘good temper,’ सद्भावः, see GOOD-HUMOUR; ‘bad temper,’<BR>असद्भावः.<BR>— (Calmness, moderation) शान्तिः f., शान्तता, समता,<BR>संयमः, रोषाभावः.<BR>— (Anger) रोषः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

temperament
TEMPERAMENT, s. प्रकृतिः f., स्वभावः, भावः, देहप्रकृतिः f., देहस्वभावः,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=797-b" target="_blank">Page797-b+ 51</a>]<BR>शरीरप्रकृतिः f., जन्मप्रकृतिः f.; ‘bilious,’ पित्तप्रकृतिः f.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

temperance
TEMPERANCE, s. (Moderation) संयमः, यमः, परिमितता, अप्रसक्तिः f.<BR>—<BR>(In eating) मिताशनं, अल्पाशनं, मिताहारः -रित्वं, मितभोजनं, अल्पा-<BR>हारः -रित्वं, परिमिताहारः, परिमितभोजनं -जित्वं.<BR>— (In drinking)<BR>परिमितपानं, मितपानं, अल्यपानं, मात्रापानं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

temperate
TEMPERATE, a. (Moderate) संयमी -मिनी &c., संयतः -ता -तं, संयत-<BR>वृत्तिः -त्तिः -त्ति, संयमशीलः -ला -लं, see MODERATE.<BR>— (In de-<BR>sires) अल्पाकांक्षी -क्षिणी &c., अप्रसक्तः -क्ता -क्तं, जितेन्द्रियः -या<BR>-यं.<BR>— (In eating) मिताशनः -ना -नं, परिमिताहारः -रा -रं, मिता-<BR>हारः &c., मिताहारी -रिणी &c., यताहारः &c., अल्पाहारः &c.,<BR>अल्पाहारी &c., स्वल्पाहारः &c., मितभोजी &c., नियताहारी &c.,<BR>लघ्वाहारः -रा -रं, लघ्वाहारी &c., अल्पाशी &c., मिताशी &c.<BR>—<BR>(In drinking) मितपायी &c., परिमितपायी &c., अल्पपायी &c.,<BR>मितपानी &c., पानाप्रसक्तः -क्ता -क्तं.<BR>— (Not excessive) परिमितः<BR>-ता -तं, अतीव्रः -व्रा -व्रं.<BR>— (Moderately warm) ईषदुष्णः -ष्णा<BR>-ष्णं, मन्दोष्णः &c., अचण्डः -ण्डा -ण्डं, अग्रीष्मः -ष्मा -ष्मं.<BR>— (Calm,<BR>not violent) शान्तः -न्ता -न्तं, अरोषणः -णा -णं, शान्तिप्रयुक्तः -क्ता<BR>-क्तं, अचण्डः -ण्डा -ण्डं, धीरः -रा -रं, धैर्य्यशाली &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

temperately
TEMPERATELY, adv. अरोषेण, अक्रोधेन, अतीव्रं, अचण्डं, शान्त्या.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

temperature
TEMPERATURE, s. उष्णानुष्णमानं, उष्णानुष्णप्रमाणं, उष्णशीतमानं, उष्णा-<BR>नुष्णता, उष्णमानं, उष्णप्रमाणं, ग्रीप्माग्रीप्मता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tempered
TEMPERED, p. p. शमितः -ता -तं, उपशमितः &c., नियमितः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tempest
TEMPEST, TEMPESTUOUS. See STORM, STORMY, HURRICANE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tempest-tost
TEMPEST-TOST, TEMPEST-BEATEN, a. पवनाहतः -ता -तं, पवनक्षिप्तः -प्ता<BR>-प्तं, पवनाघातप्रेरितः &c., वात्यावेगप्रेरितः &c., अनिलसंक्षुब्धः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

temple
TEMPLE, s. (Building dedicated to a deity) मन्दिरं, प्रासादः, देव-<BR>मन्दिरं, देवालयं, देवगृहं, देवभवनं, मण्डपः -पं, देवागारः -रं, देववेश्म n.<BR>(न्), देवतामन्दिरं, भजनालयं, देवतागारः -रं, देवतायतनं, देवावासः,<BR>महालयः -यं, सुरस्थानं, सुरमन्दिरं, सुरगृहं, देवकुलं, यज्ञियशाला,<BR>वीहारः, वयुनं, विच्छर्दकः, विच्छन्दकः, स्वस्तिकः, सर्वतोभद्रः, नन्द्यावर्त्तः,<BR>रुचकः; ‘temple dedicated to Siva,’ शिवालयं, शिवमन्दिरं;<BR>‘open temple,’ मण्डपः; ‘endowments of a temple,’ देवस्वं;<BR>‘worship at the entrance of a temple,’ द्वारपूजा.<BR>— (Of the<BR>head) कपोलः, केनारः, शङ्खः, शङ्खकः -कं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

temporal
TEMPORAL, a. ऐहिकः -की -कं, ऐहलौकिकः -की -कं, लौकिकः &c.,<BR>सांसारिकः &c., दृष्टार्थः -र्था -र्थं. See SECULAR.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

temporarily
TEMPORARILY, adv. अल्पकालमात्रं, क्षणमात्रं, अचिरेण, अशाश्वतं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

