tend
To TEND, v. n. (Aim at, be directed or incline towards) अभि-<BR>सन्धा (c. 3. -दधाति -धातुं), उद्दिश् (c. 6. -दिशति -देष्टुं), अभिप्रे (c. 2.<BR>अभिप्रैति -तुं, rt. इ), प्रवणः -णा -णं भू; ‘act which tends to a<BR>main object,’ प्रत्युत्क्रमः, प्रत्युत्क्रान्तिः f., प्रयोगार्थः.<BR>— (Conduce,<BR>contribute), see the words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tendency
TENDENCY, s. प्रावण्यं, प्रवणता, प्रवृत्तिः f., प्रवाहः, शीलता or आलुता<BR>in comp., see INCLINATION; ‘to descend,’ अधोगतिशीलता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tender
TENDER, a. (Soft) कोमलः -ला -लं, मृदुः -द्वी -दु, आर्द्रः -र्द्रा -र्द्रं.<BR>—<BR>(Sensible of pain) सुलभदुःखः -खा -खं, सुदुःखितः -ता -तं, see<BR>SORE.<BR>— (Delicate) सुकुमारः -रा -रं, कौमारः -री -रं, पेलवः -वा -वं,<BR>मृदुः &c.; ‘having a tender frame,’ प्रकृतिपेलवः -वा -वं, मृद्वङ्गः<BR>-ङ्गी -ङ्गं.<BR>— (Young) बालः -ला -लं, कौमारः -री -रं.<BR>— (Compas-<BR>sionate) दयालुः -लुः -लु, कारुणिकः -की -कं, आर्द्रः -र्द्रा -र्द्रं, दयार्द्रः<BR>&c., सहार्दः &c., see PITIFUL.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tender
TENDER, To TENDER. See OFFER, To OFFER.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tender-hearted
