tenderness
TENDERNESS, s. (Softness) कोमलता -त्वं, मृदुता, मार्दवं, सौकुमार्य्यं,<BR>कौमारं, आर्द्रता.<BR>— (Compassion, kindness) कारुण्यं, करुणा, कृपा,<BR>दया, अनुकम्पा, दयालुता, वात्सल्यं, see PITY.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tendinous
TENDINOUS, a. शिरालः -ला -लं, शिरामयः -यी -यं, स्नायुमयः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tendon
TENDON, s. स्नायुः m., स्नासा, शिरा, सिरा, स्नावः, सन्धिबन्धनं, ग्रन्थि-<BR>बन्धनं, नाडी, see MUSCLE; ‘of the neck,’ मन्या.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

