THOU, pron. त्वं (युष्पत्); ‘to thou and thee,’ त्वङ्कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

though
THOUGH, conj. यद्यपि, अपि, तथापि, यदि. See ALTHOUGH.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thought
THOUGHT, s. (Operation of the mind, act of thinking) चिन्ता<BR>-न्तनं, विचारणं -णा, विचारः, ध्यानं, अभिध्यानं, आध्यानं, भावना,<BR>चर्चा, मननं, मनोव्यापारः, अन्तःकरणव्यापारः, चित्तव्यापारः, चित्तचेष्टा,<BR>मनश्चेष्टा, अन्तःकरणचेष्टा, see REFLECTION, MEDITATION.<BR>— (That<BR>which is formed in the mind) बुद्धिः f., मतिः f., मतं, मनस् n.,<BR>बोधः, मनोगतं, कल्पना, मनःकल्पना, मनःकल्पितं, सङ्कल्पः, मनोगुप्तं,<BR>मनसिजं, मनोवृत्तिः f., चित्तवृत्तिः f., हृद्गतं, भावना, तर्कः; ‘inmost<BR>thoughts,’ अन्तर्गतं मनस्; ‘evil thoughts,’ कुकल्पना, कुतर्कः,<BR>अपध्यानं; ‘speed of thought,’ मनोवेगः, मनोजवं; ‘swift as<BR>thought,’ मनोजवः -वा -वं, मनोयायी -यिनी &c.; ‘beyond<BR>thought,’ अचिन्त्यः -न्त्या -न्त्यं, अचिन्तनीयः -या -यं; ‘in thought,<BR>word, or deed,’ मनोवचनकर्म्मभिः inst. pl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thought
THOUGHT, p. p. चिन्तितः -ता -तं, मतः &c., भावितः &c., कल्पितः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thoughtful
THOUGHTFUL, a. (Contemplative) चिन्तापरः -रा -रं, see MEDITA-<BR>TIVE.<BR>— (Considerate, attentive) विचारशीलः -ला -लं, विचारवान्<BR>वती &c., सविचारः -रा -रं, सचिन्तः -न्ता -न्तं, चिन्तावान् &c.,<BR>चिन्तायुक्तः -क्ता -क्तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thoughtfulness
THOUGHTFULNESS, s. विचारशीलता, सविचारता, सचिन्तता, मानसत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thoughtless
THOUGHTLESS, a. निश्चिन्तः -न्ता -न्तं, विवेकहीनः -ना -नं, विचारहीनः<BR>&c., अविचारशीलः -ला -लं, अनूहः -हा -हं. See HEEDLESS,<BR>NEGLIGENT.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thoughtlessly
THOUGHTLESSLY, adv. अचिन्तया, निश्चिन्तं, अविचारेण, अविवेकेन;<BR>‘thoughtlessly done,’ अविचारकृतः -ता -तं, अविवेककृतः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thoughtlessness
THOUGHTLESSNESS, s. अविचारः -रता, अविवेकता, अविवेकः, विचार-<BR>हीनता, विवेकहीनता, प्रमादः. See HEEDLESSNESS.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thousand
THOUSAND, a. सहस्रं n. sing., दशशतं. The word सहस्रं may be<BR>used with the nom. pl. or gen. pl.; as, ‘a thousand an-<BR>cestors,’ सहस्रं पितरः or सहस्रं पितॄणां; ‘ten thousand,’ अयुतः<BR>-तं; ‘one hundred thousand,’ लक्षं -क्षा; ‘a thousand times,’<BR>सहस्रकृत्वस्; ‘in a thousand ways,’ सहस्रधा; ‘thousand eyed,’<BR>सहस्रनयनः -ना -नं; ‘a regiment of a thousand men,’ सहस्री m.<BR>(न्), साहस्रः; ‘the aggregate of a thousand,’ साहस्रं; ‘thou-<BR>sand-fold,’ सहस्रगुणः -णा -णं; ‘by thousands,’ सहस्रशस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thousandth
THOUSANDTH, a. सहस्रतमः -मी -मं, साहस्रः -स्री -स्रं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thralldom
THRALLDOM, s. दास्यं, वशता, पारतन्त्र्यं, see SERVITUDE, SLAVERY.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thrash
To THRASH, v. a. निस्तुपीकृ, कण्डनं कृ, पू, तड्. See To THRESH.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thread
THREAD, s. सूत्रं, तन्तुः m., तन्त्रं, गुणः, सूत्रतन्तुः m., सरत् n., सरित् f.,<BR>कुब्रं, चीनः, खात्रं; ‘point of a thread,’ पक्ष्म n. (न्), सूत्राग्रं;<BR>‘thread of a story or subject,’ प्रबन्धार्थः, अर्थप्रबन्धः, अन्वयः,<BR>अर्थान्वयः, अर्थसन्दर्भः, कथासन्दर्भः, कथाप्रबन्धः, सन्धानं, अनुसन्धानं;<BR>‘thread of hope,’ आशातन्तुः m.; ‘sacrificial thread,’ see<BR>under SACRIFICIAL.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thread
To THREAD, v. a. सूत्र (Nom. सूत्रयति -यितुं), गुम्फ्, see To STRING.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

threadbare
THREADBARE, a. जर्जरीकः -का -कं, जर्जरः -रा -रं, सूत्रदरिद्रः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

threaded
THREADED, p. p. सूत्रितः -ता -तं, गुम्फितः &c., ग्रन्थितः &c., ग्रथितः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

threat
THREAT, s. भर्त्सनं, निर्भर्त्सनं, तर्जनं, दण्डमूचनं. See MENACE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

threaten
To THREATEN, v. a. भर्त्स् (c. 10. भर्त्सयति -ते -यितुं), निर्भर्त्म्, तर्ज्, see<BR>To MENACE.<BR>— (Declare purpose of punishing) दण्डसूचनं कृं,<BR>दण्डप्रदर्शनं कृ, दण्डसङ्कल्पप्रदर्शनं कृ.<BR>— (Exhibit the appearance<BR>of something evil approaching) अनिष्टसूचनं कृ, अनिष्टावेदनं कृ,<BR>see To PREBODE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

threatened
THREATENED, p. p. भर्त्सितः -ता -तं, निर्भर्त्सितः &c., तर्जितः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

threatening
THREATENING, part. भर्त्सनकारी -रिणी &c., अनिष्टावेदी -दिनी &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

three
THREE, a. त्रयः m. pl., तिस्रः f. pl., त्रीणि n. pl. (त्रि); ‘the three<BR>worlds,’ त्रिभुवनं; ‘the aggregate of three,’ त्रयं, त्रयी, त्रिकं,<BR>त्रितयं. The word त्रयं is often used at the end of a com-<BR>pound to express ‘three;’ as, ‘three months,’ मासत्रयं;<BR>‘three years,’ वर्षत्रयं; ‘three steps,’ पदत्रयं; ‘the three<BR>properties,’ गुणचयं; ‘he was seen by three rogues,’ स धूर्त्त-<BR>त्रयेण दृष्ठः; ‘two or three,’ द्वित्राः -त्राः -त्राणि (त्र being here<BR>put for वि); two or three or any number,’ द्वित्रादिसंख्या,<BR>द्वित्राद्याः m. pl.; ‘three or four,’ त्रिचतुराः -राः -राणि; ‘rule<BR>of three,’ त्रैराशिकगणितं, see under RULE, s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

three-fold
THREE-FOLD, a. त्रिगुणः -णा -णं, त्रिविधः -धा -धं, त्रिवृत् m. f. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

three-fourths
THREE-FOURTHS, s. pl. त्रयश् चतुर्थांशाः m. pl., त्रिपादाः, त्र्यंशाः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

threnody
THRENODY, s. यमगाथा, यमगीतं, यमगानं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thresh
To THRESH, v. a. (Corn) धान्यादि मृद् (c. 9. मृद्नाति, मर्दितुं) or पू or<BR>परिपू or निस्तुनीकृ, धान्यादिमर्दनं कृ, धान्यादिकण्डनं कृ, अवघातं कृ.<BR>— (Beat) तड् (c. 10. ताडयति -यितुं), ताडनं कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

threshed
THRESHED, p.p. मर्दितः -ता -तं, मृदितः &c., निस्तुषितः &c., निस्तुपाकृतः<BR>&c., पूतः &c., परिपूतः &c., अपहतः &c., बहुलीकृतः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

threshing
THRESHING, s. धान्यादिमर्दनं, धान्यादिकण्डनं, कण्डनं, निस्तुपीकरणं, अव-<BR>घातः, पावनं, ताडनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

threshing-floor
THRESHING-FLOOR, s. धान्यादिमर्दनस्थानं, धान्यादिकण्डनस्थानं, धान्यमर्दन-<BR>भूमिः f., खलः, शस्यमर्दनस्थानं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

threshold
THRESHOLD s. देहली, गृहावग्रहणी, गृहतटी, शिला -ली, द्वारपिण्डी,<BR>रुण्डिका, अम्बुरः, उडुम्बरः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thrice
THRICE, adv. त्रिवारं, वारत्रयं, त्रिः, त्रिकृत्वम्, त्रिगुणः -णा -णी -णं,<BR>त्रि in comp.; ‘thrice ploughed,’ त्रिसीत्यः -त्या -त्यं, त्रिहल्यः<BR>-ल्या -ल्यं, त्रिगुणाकृतः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thrift
THRIFT, THRIFTINESS, THRIFTY, &c., See FRUGALITY, FRUGAL, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thrill
THRILL, s. स्फुरणं, स्फूर्त्तिः f., स्फुरितं, हर्षः; ‘of joy,’ रोमहर्षः -र्षणं,<BR>रोमोद्धर्षणं, रोमोद्गमः, रोमोद्भेदः, रोमाञ्चः, पुलकः, पुलकोद्गमः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thrill
To THRILL, v. n. स्फुर् (c. 6. स्फुरति -रितुं), हृष् (c. 4. हृष्यति, हर्षितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thrilling
THRILLING, part. स्फुरन् -रन्ती -रत् (त्), स्फुरितः -ता -तं; ‘with<BR>joy,’ हृष्टः -ष्टा -ष्टं, हर्षी -र्षिणी -र्षि (न्), पुलकितः -ता -तं, रोमा-<BR>ञ्चितः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thrive
To THRIVE, v. n. See To FLOURISH, PROSPER, v. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thriving
THRIVING, v. n. समृद्धः -द्धा -द्धं. See PROSPEROUS, FLOURISIHNG.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

throat
THROAT, s. कण्ठः, गलः, ग्रीवा, कन्धरः -रा, कुहरं, कृकः, निगरणः,<BR>see NECK; ‘relating to it,’ कण्ठ्यः -ण्ठ्या -ण्ठ्यं; ‘seated in<BR>it,’ कण्ठस्थः -स्था -स्थं, कण्ठगतः -ता -तं; ‘up to the throat,’<BR>आकण्ठात्; ‘dryness of it,’ कण्ठशोपः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

throb
To THROB, v. n. स्फुर् (c. 6. स्फुरति -रितुं), विस्फुर्, स्पन्द् (c. 1. स्पन्दते<BR>न्दितुं), प्रतिस्पन्द्, परिस्पन्द्, कम्प्, विकम्प्, वेप्. See To PALPI-<BR>TATE, BEAT.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

throb
THROB, THROBBING, s. स्फुरणं -णा, स्फुरितं, स्पन्दनं, स्पन्दितं, विष्पन्दः,<BR>स्पन्दः, कम्पः, स्फोरणं, स्फुरः, स्फरणं, स्फारणं, स्फुलनं; ‘of the<BR>eye,’ चक्षुःस्पन्दः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

throe
THROE, s. (Of child-birth) प्रसववेदना, गर्भवेदना, वेधना.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

throne
THRONE, s. सिंहासनं, नृपासनं, राजासनं, उच्चासनं, भद्रासनं, राजशय्या,<BR>महाशय्या, मञ्चः, राजासनमञ्चः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

throng
THRONG, To THRONG. See CROWD, To CROWD.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thronged
THRONGED, p. p. सङ्कीर्णः -र्णा -र्णं, समाकीर्णः &c., बाधितः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

throttle
To THROTTLE, v. a. गलग्रहं कृ, गलहस्त. See To CHOKE, SUFFOCATE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

through
THROUGH, prep. (From one end or side to the other) पारं,<BR>आपार्श्वान्तरात्, पार्श्वान्तरपर्य्यन्तं, पार्श्वान्तरं यावत्, तीरान्तरं.<BR>— (Denot-<BR>ing passage) मध्येन, अन्तरेण or expressed by the inflection<BR>of the noun; ‘he goes through a fissure in the rock,’<BR>गिरिरन्ध्रमध्येन गच्छति; ‘through the branches,’ विटपान्तरेण.<BR>—<BR>(By means of, through the agency or influence of) ex-<BR>pressed by the abl. or instr. case; as, ‘through ambition,’<BR>लोभात्, लोभेन; ‘through anger,’ कोपात्, रोषणतया; ‘through<BR>him,’ तेन, see under BY, prep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

through
THROUGH, adv. (From the beginning to the end) साद्यन्तं, आद्यन्तं.<BR>— (To the end) शेपपर्य्यन्तं, शेषं याषत्, समाप्तिपर्य्यन्तं, अवसानपर्य्यन्तं,<BR>आसमाप्तेः, आशेपात्, see THROUGHOUT; ‘to carry through, get<BR>through,’ पार् (c. 10. पारयति -यितुं), तीर् (c. 10. तीरयति -यितुं),<BR>see To FINISH, v. a.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

throughout
THROUGHOUT, adv. (From the beginning to the end) साद्यन्तं,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-a" target="_blank">Page803-a+ 51</a>]<BR>आद्यन्तं, शेषपर्य्यन्तं.<BR>— (Of time) expressed by पर्य्यन्तं, यावत् or<BR>आ in comp.; thus, ‘throughout the month,’ मासपर्य्यन्तं;<BR>‘throughout the year,’ वर्षपर्य्यन्तं; ‘throughout the whole<BR>year,’ आवर्षान्तात् or वर्षान्तं यावत् (i. e. to the end of the<BR>year); ‘throughout life,’ यावज्जीवं, जीवनपर्य्यन्तं, आजीवनान्तात्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

throw
To THROW, v. a. क्षिप् (c. 6. क्षिपति, क्षेप्तुं), प्रक्षिप्, अस् (c. 4. अस्यति<BR>-सितुं), प्रास्, मुच् (c. 6. मुञ्चति, मोक्तुं), प्रमुच्, ईर् (c. 10. ईरयति<BR>-यितुं), समीर्, उदीर्, पत् (c. 10. पातयति -यितुं), सृज्, प्रहृ, प्रेष् in<BR>caus.<BR>— (Throw away) अपास्, व्युदस्, अपव्यध्, त्यज्, अपहा,<BR>विहा, नश् in caus., see To LOSE, REJECT; ‘one's time,’ कालं<BR>क्षिप्, कालक्षेपं कृ.<BR>— (Throw about) विक्षिप्, इतस्ततः क्षिप्.<BR>—<BR>(Throw behind one's back) पृष्ठतः कृ or क्षिप्.<BR>— (Throw down)<BR>पत् in caus., अवपत्, अधःपत्, अधः क्षिप्, अधः कृ, भ्रंश् in caus.,<BR>प्रभ्रंश्, च्यु in caus., प्रच्यु.<BR>— (Throw into disorder) व्यूहान् भञ्ज्<BR>or भिद्, पिञ्जलीकृ.<BR>— (Throw off) अवधू, निर्धू, विधू, निरस्,<BR>निराकृ, अपव्यध्.<BR>— (Throw out) निरस्, निराकृ; ‘as hints,<BR>&c.,’ सूच्, सूचनां कृ.<BR>— (Throw up) उत्क्षिप्, उत्क्षेपं कृ, see To<BR>VOMIT.<BR>— (Throw up), see To RESIGN.<BR>— (Throw one's self<BR>down) स्वदेहावपातं कृ; ‘from a cliff,’ गिरिशिखराद् अवपातं कृ<BR>or प्रपतनं कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

throw
THROW, s. क्षेपः -पणं, प्रक्षेपः, आक्षेपः, असनं, पातः -तनं, क्षिप्तिः f.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thrower
THROWER, s. क्षेपकः, प्रक्षेपकः, क्षेप्ता m. (मृ), प्रासकः, क्षेपणकृत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thrown
THROWN, p. p. क्षिप्तः -प्ता -प्तं, प्रक्षिप्तः &c., अस्तः -स्ता -स्तं, प्रास्तः<BR>&c., ईरितः -ता -तं, पातितः -ता -तं; ‘away,’ अपास्तः &c., व्युदस्तः<BR>&c., अपविद्धः -द्धा -द्धं, अपसारितः -ता -तं, त्यक्तः -क्ता -क्तं, नष्टः -ष्टा<BR>-ष्टं; ‘a kindness is thrown away on bad men,’ सुकृतम्<BR>असत्सु नष्टं; ‘thrown down,’ पातितः -ता -तं, निपातितः &c.,<BR>अधःपातितः &c., अधःक्षिप्तः -प्ता -प्तं, अधःकृतः -ता -तं, भ्रंशितः -ता<BR>-तं; ‘thrown into disorder,’ भग्नव्यूहः -हा -हं, भिन्नव्यूहः &c.,<BR>पिञ्जलः -ला -लं, समुत्पिञ्जलः &c.; ‘thrown off,’ निर्धूतः -ता -तं,<BR>अवधूतः &c., अपविद्धः &c.; ‘as from a horse, &c.,’ निरस्तः -स्ता -स्तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thrum
THRUM, s. (Ends of threads) दशाः f. pl., वस्तयः f. pl. (वस्ति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thrush
THRUSH, s. (Bird) सारिका, शारिका, मदनसारिका, शलाका, शरारिः f.,<BR>शरालिः f., सरातिः f., आटिः f., आडिः f., आतिः f.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thrust
To THRUST, v. a. तड् (c. 10. ताडयति -यितुं), प्रमृ (c. 10. -सारयति<BR>-यितुं), प्रसारणं कृ; ‘aside,’ अपसृ, see To PUSH.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thrust
THRUST, s. ताडनं, आघातः, अभिघातः, प्रसारणं, प्रहारः, see PUSH.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thumb
THUMB, s. अङ्गुष्ठः, अङ्गुलः, वृद्धाङ्गुलिः f.; ‘thumb and forefinger,’<BR>सन्तोषः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thumb
To THUMB, v. a. अङ्गुलीभिर् अङ्क् (c. 10. अङ्कयति -यितुं) or परामृश् or<BR>स्पृश्, अङ्गुल्यङ्कितं -तां कृ. See To FINGER, v. a.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thump
THUMP, s. आघातः, प्रहारः, करघातः, मुष्टिपातः. See BLOW.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thump
To THUMP, v. a. तड् (c. 10. ताडयति -यितुं), प्रहृ, आहन्. See To BEAT.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thunder
THUNDER, s. गर्जनं -ना, गर्जितं, मेघगर्जितं, मेघनादः, मेघशब्दः, मेघनि-<BR>र्घोषः, स्फूर्जः, स्फूर्जनं, स्फूर्जथुः m., विस्फूर्जथुः m., विस्फूर्जितं, मेघवि-<BR>स्फूर्जितं, स्तनितं, मेघस्तनितं, स्तननं, मेघस्तननं, स्तनयित्नुः m., घनशब्दः,<BR>घनस्वनः, घनरवः, मेघध्वनिः m., परिघोषः, गम्भीरनादः, गर्जिः m.,<BR>गर्मं, रसितः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thunder
To THUNDER, v. n. गर्ज् (c. 1. गर्जति -र्मितुं), परिगर्ज्, स्फुर्ज् (c. 1. स्फूर्जति<BR>-र्मितुं), विस्फुर्न्, स्तन् (c. 1. स्तनति -नितुं), गर्जनं कृ, स्फूर्जनं कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thunderbolt
THUNDERBOLT, s. वज्रः -ज्रं, वज्राघातः, कुलिशः -शं, भिदुरं, भिदिः m.,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-b" target="_blank">Page803-b+ 51</a>]<BR>भिदिरं, भिदुः m., अशनिः m. f., वज्राशनिः m., छिदक, मृदाकरः,<BR>शतधारं, शतारं, बहुधारः, शतकोटिः m., षट्कोणं, अभ्रोत्थं, त्रिदशाङ्कुशं,<BR>गिरिज्वरः, गिरिध्वजः, गिरिकण्टकः, इन्द्रप्रहरणं, स्वरुः m., दम्भोलिः m.,<BR>ह्रादिनी, पविः m., शम्बः, शम्भः, पेशिः m., जसुरिः m., व्याधानः,<BR>मेघभूतिः f., दृम्भूः m., दधीच्यस्थि n., वैद्युतो -ग्निः; ‘fall of a thun-<BR>derbolt,’ वज्रपातः; ‘like a thunderbolt,’ वज्रप्रायः -या -यं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thunder-clap
THUNDER-CLAP, s. स्फूर्जथुः m., वज्रनिर्घोषः, वज्रनिष्पेषः, वज्राघातः,<BR>वज्रज्राला, वज्रपातशब्दः, वज्रस्तनितं, वज्रनिस्वनः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thunder-cloud
THUNDER-CLOUD, s. घनः, वज्रघनः, मेघः, वज्रमेघः, वज्राभ्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thunderer
THUNDERER, s. वज्री m. (न्), वज्रपाणिः m., वज्रधरः, कुलिशभृत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thundering
THUNDERING, s. स्फूर्जनं, गर्जनं, मेघगर्जनं. See THUNDER.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thundering
THUNDERING, part. गर्जन् -र्जन्ती -र्जत् (त्), स्फूर्जावान् -वती -वत् (त्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thunder-storm
THUNDER-STORM, s. वज्रवर्षः, अशनिवर्षः, कुलिशवर्षः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thunderstruck
THUNDERSTRUCK, a. वज्राहतः -ता -तं, वज्रहतः &c., वज्रप्रहतः &c., वज्र-<BR>ताडितः -ता -तं, विद्युद्धतः &c. See ASTOUNDED.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thursday
THURSDAY, s. वृहस्पतिवारः, गुरुवारः, गुरुवासरः, लक्ष्मीवारः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thus
THUS, adv. (In this manner) एवं, इत्थं, अनेन प्रकारेण, एवम्प्रकारेण,<BR>उक्तेन प्रकारेण, उक्तप्रकारेण, अनया रीत्या, अनयर्त्या, अतएव.<BR>— (So)<BR>तथा, तथाहि, इति, एतादृशं.<BR>— (Thus much) इयान् -यती -यत् (त्),<BR>एतावान् &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thwart
To THWART, v. a. खण्ड्, प्रतिहन्, प्रतिरुध्, see To FRUSTRATE, HINDER.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thwarted
THWARTED, p. p. संरुद्धचेष्टः -ष्टा -ष्टं, प्रतिबद्धः &c. See FRUSTRATED.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thy
THY, pron. तव gen. c. (युष्मत्), त्वदीयः -या -यं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

thyself
THYSELF, pron. स त्वं, आत्मा m. (न्). See MYSELF.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tiara
TIARA, s. मुकुटं, किरीटः, मौलिः m. f., अवतंसः, ललाटपट्टं, चूडा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tibia
TIBIA, s. जङ्घायाः पूर्व्वास्थि n. or अग्रास्थि n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tick
TICK, s. (Credit), see CREDIT.<BR>— (Louse) यूकः, लोमकीटः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tick
To TICK, v. n. (As a clock) कालमापकवत् किटकिटशब्दं कृ or पटप-<BR>टशब्दं कृ, पटपट (nom. पटपटायते -ति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ticket
TICKET, s. पत्रकं, पत्रं, सूचकपत्रं, निदर्शनपत्रं, अङ्कपत्रं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ticket
To TICKET, v. a. अङ्कपत्रयुक्तं -क्तां कृ, अङ्कपत्रविशिष्टं -ष्टां कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tickle
To TICKLE, v. a. कण्डू (nom. कण्डूयति), कण्डूयनं कृ, कण्डूयां कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tickler
TICKLER, s. कण्डूयनकः, कण्डूतिकारी m. (न्), कण्डूयाकृत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ticklish
TICKLISH, a. कण्डूयनासहनः -ना -नं, कण्डूयासहः -हा -हं, कण्डूत्यसहः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tid-bit
TID-BIT, s. सुग्रासः, विशिष्टग्रासः, आहारविशेषः, भोजनविशेषः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tide
TIDE, s. वेला, स्रोतस् n., प्रवाहः, रयः; ‘of the sea,’ समुद्रवेला;<BR>‘against the tide,’ प्रतिस्रोतस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tidings
TIDINGS, s. वार्त्ता, सन्देशः, समाचारः. See NEWS, INTELLIGENCE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tidy
TIDY, TIDINESS, TIDILY. See NEAT, NEATNESS, NEATLY.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tie
To TIE, v. a. बन्ध् (c. 9. बध्नाति, बन्द्धुं), निबन्ध्, पिनह्; ‘together,’<BR>सम्बन्ध्, योक्त्र (nom. योक्त्रयति -यितुं), संयुज्, संश्लिष् in caus., सन्धा,<BR>संलग्नीकृ, संहृ, ग्रन्थ्, गुम्फ्, see To FASTEN, KNIT, &c.; ‘with<BR>a fetter,’ पाशीकृ, पाश (nom. पाशयति -यितुं); ‘to tie up a<BR>young deer,’ मृगपोतकं संयोजयितुं; ‘to tie up in a bag,’ वस्त्र-<BR>वद्धं -द्धां कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tie
TIE, s. (A fastening, knot) बन्धः -न्धनं -नी, ग्रन्थिः m., बन्धनग्रन्थिः m.;<BR>‘of a yoke,’ आबन्धः, योक्त्रं, योत्रं; ‘of a letter or parcel,’<BR>तालिकः.<BR>— (A fetter) पाशः, बन्धनं.<BR>— (String) गुणः, दाम -मा, see<BR>STRING.<BR>— (Attachment, tie of affection, &c.) सङ्गः; ‘free<BR>from ties,’ निःसङ्गः -ङ्गा -ङ्गं, सङ्गवर्जितः -ता -तं, असज्जितात्मा -त्मा<BR>-त्म (न्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tied
TIED, p. p. बद्धः -द्धा -द्धं, निबद्धः &c., सन्निबद्धः &c., निबन्धितः -ता -तं,<BR>आबद्धः &c., पिनद्धः -द्धा -द्धं, आनद्धः &c., दृब्धः &c., गुणवान् -वती<BR>&c.; ‘together,’ सम्बद्धः -द्धा -द्धं, आबद्धः &c., संयोजितः -ता -तं,<BR>संसक्तः -क्ता -क्तं, संलग्नीकृतः -ता -तं, सन्धानितः &c., सन्धितः &c.,<BR>सन्दितः &c.; ‘tied with a fetter,’ पाशितः -ता -तं, पाशीकृतः<BR>&c.; ‘tied up in,’ निबद्धः -द्धा -द्धं; ‘a quantity of money<BR>tied up in a bag,’ वस्त्रबद्धो मुद्रासञ्चयः; ‘a man with his arms<BR>tied behind him,’ पश्चाद्बद्धबाहुः पुरुषः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tier
TIER, s. पंक्तिः f., श्रेणिः -णी f., राजिः -नी f. See ROW, LINE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tiger
TIGER, s. व्याघ्रः, शार्दूलः, द्वीपी m. (न्), विचित्राङ्गः, गुहाशयः, मृगारिः m.,<BR>मृगाद् m., हिंसारुः m., भयानकः; ‘state of one,’ व्याघ्रता; ‘re-<BR>lating to one,’ वैयाघ्रः &c.; ‘its skin,’ व्याघ्रचर्म्म n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tight
TIGHT, a. (Close, firm) दृढः -ढा -ढं, घनः -ना -नं, संहतः -ता -तं,<BR>अशिथिलः -ला -लं, गाढः -ढा -ढं, प्रगाढः &c.<BR>— (Tied tight) दृढ-<BR>बद्धः -द्धा -द्धं, सन्निबद्धः &c., दृढसन्धिः -न्धिः -न्धि.<BR>— (Tight-drawn)<BR>आततः -ता -तं, दृढः &c., see STRETCHED.<BR>— (Pinching) सम्बाधकः<BR>-का -कं, सम्बाधः -धा -धं, सङ्कोचकः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tighten
To TIGHTEN, v. a. दृढीकृ, द्रढ (nom. द्रढयति -यितुं), दृढतरीकृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tightly
TIGHTLY, adv. दृढं, गाढं, प्रगाढं; ‘tied tightly,’ दृढबद्धः -द्धा -द्धं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tightness
TIGHTNESS, s. दृढता, दार्ढ्यं, घनता, संहतत्वं, सम्बाधता -धकता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tigress
TIGRESS, s. व्याघ्री, शार्दूली, द्वीपिनी, विचित्राङ्गी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tigrine
TIGRINE, TIGRISH, a. वैयाघ्रः -घ्री -घ्रं, व्याघ्रोपमः -मा -मं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tile
