TITULAR, a. नामधारी -रिणी -रि (न्). See NOMINAL.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

to
TO, prep. Many of the meanings of ‘to’ are expressed by<BR>prepositions or affixes, or by the infin. mood, or are in-<BR>herent in the inflections of the Sanskrit noun; thus, (Mo-<BR>tion to or toward any place) expressed by the acc. case<BR>alone, or with प्रति &c. added; as, ‘he went to the city,’<BR>नगरं or नगरं प्रति जगाम, or by the gen. c., with अन्तिकं &c.;<BR>as, ‘he sent me to you,’ मां तवान्तिकं or तव सकाशम् अप्रैबीत्.<BR>— (Motion to any state) by the acc. c.; as, ‘he attains<BR>to fame,’ ख्यातिं याति.<BR>— (Adaptation) by the dat. c. or crude<BR>form; as, ‘that husband was not to her taste,’ स पतिस्<BR>तस्याः सन्तोषाय नाभवत्; ‘suited to royalty,’ राजयोग्यः -ग्या<BR>-ग्यं, राजार्हः &c.; ‘that is pleasing to me,’ तन् मह्यं रोचते.<BR>—<BR>(Address, declaration, compellation) by the acc. c. or dat.<BR>c.; as, ‘he addressed a speech to the king,’ राजानं वचनम्<BR>अब्रवीत्; ‘speak to me,’ मां ब्रूहि; ‘I will declare this to<BR>my pupils,’ शिष्येभ्यः प्रवक्ष्यामि तत्; ‘he made it known to<BR>the king,’ तद् राज्ञे विज्ञापयति.<BR>— (Giving) by the dat., gen.,<BR>or loc. c.; ‘he gives sweetmeats to his son,’ पुत्राय or पुत्रस्य<BR>मोदकान् ददाति.<BR>— (Up to, as far as, denoting extent, degree,<BR>&c.) आ prefixed to the abl. or acc. c., पर्य्यन्त or अन्त in<BR>comp.; as, ‘to the ocean,’ आसमुद्रात् or समुद्रपर्य्यन्तं; ‘to the<BR>throat,’ आकण्ठात्; ‘to the knee,’ आजानु; ‘the numbers<BR>from one up to ten thousand,’ एकाद्ययुतान्तसंख्याः.<BR>— (Posses-<BR>sion, appertainment) by the gen. c.; as, ‘money belongs<BR>to me,’ मम धनं भवति.<BR>— (Purpose, intention, object) by the<BR>dat. c. or infin. mood, or by अर्थं &c. affixed; as, ‘the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=806-a" target="_blank">Page806-a+ 51</a>]<BR>sat down to consult,’ मन्त्रणाय or मन्त्रयितुं or मन्त्रणार्थम् उपविष्टाः;<BR>‘the barber came to shave his master,’ भर्त्तृक्षौरकरणाय नापित<BR>आगच्छत्; ‘he came to make peace,’ सन्धिं कर्त्तुम् आगच्छत्;<BR>‘give me something to eat,’ आहारार्थं किञ्चिन् मम देहि.<BR>—<BR>(As a sign of the infinitive) expressed by the infinitive,<BR>or by यथा &c.; as, ‘unable to move,’ चलितुम् असमर्थः; ‘I<BR>desire to hear,’ श्रोतुम् इच्छामि; ‘I did not expect to see you<BR>again,’ न म आसीद् आशंसा यथा पुनरपि त्वां प्रेक्षिप्ये. There<BR>may be other ways of expressing ‘to’ in Sanskrit, as in<BR>the following examples: ‘the peacock dances to the songs<BR>of the bees,’ शिखी नृत्यति मधुकरगीतैः; ‘he performed penance<BR>to the deity,’ देवम् उद्दिश्य तपस् तेपे; ‘the town was speedily<BR>reduced to ashes,’ नगरी सहसा भस्मसाद् अक्रियत; ‘compared<BR>to that,’ तदपेक्ष्य or तदपेक्षया; ‘to the east of the village,’<BR>प्राग् ग्रामात्; ‘he goes to and fro,’ गमनागमनं करोति, see<BR>FRO; ‘to one's face,’ प्रत्यक्षं -क्षतस्, समक्षं; ‘to a man,’ अशे-<BR>षतस्, अशेषेण; ‘I have a debt to pay,’ मया ऋणं दातव्यं; ‘ready<BR>to go,’ गन्तुम् उद्यतः, गमनोन्मुखः; ‘he causes her to enter<BR>the house,’ तां गृहं प्रवेशयति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

toad
TOAD, s. स्थूलमण्डूकः, स्थूलभेकः, वर्षाभूः m.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

toadstool
TOADSTOOL, s. गोमयछत्रं, विड्जं, विड्जछत्रं. See FUNGUS.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

toast
To TOAST, v. a. उपाग्नि धृत्वा शुष्कीकृ, अग्निशुष्कं -ष्कां कृ, अग्निना<BR>तप् (c. 10. तापयति -यितुं), भृज्, भ्रज्ज्. See To FRY, v. a.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

toast
TOAST, s. दग्धापूपः, दग्धपिष्टकः, अग्निशुष्कापूपः, भृष्टापूपः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

toasted
TOASTED, p. p. भृष्टः -ष्टा -ष्टं, भर्जितः -ता -तं, अग्निशुष्कः -ष्का -ष्कं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tobacco
TOBACCO, s. ताम्रकुट्टः -ट्टकः, ताम्रकूटः, ताम्रपत्रिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tobacconist
TOBACCONIST, s. ताम्रकुट्टविक्रयी m. (न्), ताम्रकुट्टकव्यापारी m.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tocsin
TOCSIN, s. आसन्नभयसूचकघण्टा, भयज्ञापकघण्टा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

to-day
TO-DAY, s. or adv. अद्य; ‘of to-day,’ अद्यतनः -नी -नं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

toddle
To TODDLE, v. n. बालकवत् स्खलद्गत्या क्रम् or चर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

toddy
TODDY, s. (Of the palm) ताली, तालकी, ताडी -डिः f.<BR>— (Of the<BR>cocoa-nut) नारिकेलासवः, नारिकेरासवः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

toe
TOE, s. पादाङ्गुली -लिः f., पादाङ्गुरिः f., पदाङ्गुली -लिः f., पादशाखा,<BR>अङ्गुरिः f.; ‘the great toe,’ पादाङ्गुष्ठः; ‘the little toe,’ पादस्य<BR>कनिष्ठाङ्गुली; ‘toe-nail,’ पादनखः, चरणनखः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

together
TOGETHER, adv. (In company) सह in comp., समं, सहितं, एक in<BR>comp., एकत्र; ‘going together,’ सहगामी -मिनी &c.; ‘danc-<BR>ing together,’ सहनर्त्तनं; ‘drinking together,’ सहपानं; ‘eat-<BR>ing together,’ सहभोजनं, एकभोजनं, एकत्र भोजनं; ‘fighting<BR>together,’ सहयुध्वा m. (न्); ‘all together, in a body,’ सङ्घ-<BR>शस्, एकसङ्घे -ङ्घतस्, साकल्येन.<BR>— (Into union or junction) सम्<BR>prefixed; as, ‘to bind together,’ सम्बन्ध्; ‘to meet together,’<BR>सङ्गम्, सम्मिल्; ‘having the feet together,’ सम्पदं; ‘two<BR>letters placed together,’ सन्निहितवर्णौ m. du.<BR>— (In the same<BR>place) एकत्र, एकस्थाने, एकदेशे.<BR>— (At the same time) एककाले,<BR>समकाले, युगपत्, सह in comp.; ‘born at the same time,’<BR>एककालजः -जा -जं, समकालजः &c., सहजः &c.<BR>— (With one<BR>another) परस्परं, अन्योन्यं; ‘quarelling together,’ परस्परकलहः,<BR>अन्योन्यकलहः.<BR>— (Together with) सह, समं, सार्द्धं, सहितं, साकं,<BR>all with instr. c.; ‘together with him,’ तेन सह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

toil
To TOIL, v. n. आयस्, श्रम्, क्लिश्. See To LABOUR, DRUDGE, FAG.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

toil
TOIL, s. आयासः, क्लेशः, श्रमः, कष्ट. See LABOR, DRUDGERY.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

toilet
TOILET, s. (Act or mode of dressing) वस्त्रमाल्यादिविन्यासः, वस्त्र-<BR>माल्यादिरचना, अङ्गसंस्कारः, मण्डनं, नेपथ्यं, भूषणं; ‘he makes his<BR>toilet,’ नेपथ्यं धारयति, वस्त्रविन्यासं करोति; ‘one who has finished<BR>her toilet,’ अवसितमण्डना; ‘toilet-table,’ भूषणाधारः; ‘cover,’<BR>भूषणाधाराच्छादनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

toilsome
TOILSOME, a. कष्टसाध्यः -ध्या -ध्यं, श्रमसाध्यः &c. See LABORIOUS.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

token
TOKEN, s. लक्षणं, चिह्नं, अभिज्ञानं, सङ्केतः, see SIGN, MEMENTO.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tola
TOLA, s. (Indian weight for gold and silver) तोलः -लं, तोलकः -कं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

told
TOLD, p. p. कथितः -ता -तं, आख्यातः &c., समाख्यातः &c., उक्तः -क्ता<BR>-क्तं, भणितः -ता -तं, आवेदितः &c., निवेदितः &c., ज्ञापितः -ता -तं,<BR>ज्ञपितः &c., ख्यापितः &c., ज्ञप्तः -प्ता -प्तं, सन्दिष्टः -ष्टा -ष्टं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tolerable
TOLERABLE, a. (Bearable) सहनीयः -या -यं, सह्यः -ह्या -ह्यं, सोढव्य<BR>-व्या -व्यं.<BR>— (Moderately good) विगुणः -णा -णं, मध्यमगुणः -ण<BR>-णं, मध्यमः -मा -मं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tolerably
TOLERABLY, adv. विगुणं, यावत्तावत्, कल्प or देशीय or देश्य in comp.;<BR>‘tolerably clever,’ पटुकल्पः -ल्पा -ल्पं, पटुदेशीयः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tolerance
TOLERANCE, s. सहनं, सहिष्णुता, क्षमा. See TOLERATION.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tolerant
TOLERANT, a. सहनः -ना -नं, सहिष्णुः -ष्णुः -ष्णु, अनिषेधकारी -रिणी<BR>-रि (न्), अप्रतिबन्धकारी &c. See PATIENT, INDULGENT.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tolerate
To TOLERATE, v. a. सह्, विषह्, क्षम्, मृष्, तिज् in des., उपेक्ष्,<BR>अनिषेधं कृ, अप्रतिबन्धं कृ, अनिवारणं कृ. See To SUFFER, PERMIT.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tolerated
TOLERATED, p. p. अनिषिद्धः -द्धा -द्धं, अनिवारितः -ता -तं, उपेक्षितः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

toleration
TOLERATION, s. क्षमा, क्षान्तिः f., तितिक्षा, सहिष्णुता, अनिषेधः, अनि-<BR>वारणं, अप्रतिबन्धः, उपेक्षा, अप्रतिरोधः, अनिरोधः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

toll
TOLL, s. शुल्कः -ल्कं, तारिकं, तार्य्यं, घट्टादिदेयं, करः. See TAX.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

toll
To TOLL, v. a. (A bell) शनैः शनैः or वारं वारं घण्टां वद् in caus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

toll
To TOLL, v. n. (As a bell) शनैः शनैः or वारं वारं क्वणितं कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

toll-booth
TOLL-BOOTH, TOLL-HOUSE, s. शुल्कस्थानं, शुल्कग्रहणस्थानं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

toll-gatherer
TOLL-GATHERER, s. शौल्किकः, शुल्कग्राही m. (न्), करग्राही m.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tomato
TOMATO, s. हिण्डीरः, हिङ्गुली, वङ्गनः. See EGG-PLANT.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tomb
TOMB, s. समाधिः m., श्मशानं, स्तूपः, प्रेतकुण्डं. See GRAVE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tomb-stone
TOMB-STONE, s. चित्यं, चैत्यं, चिताचूडकं. See GRAVE-STONE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

to-morrow
TO-MORROW, s. or adv. श्वस्, परेद्यस्, परदिनं, see MORROW; ‘day<BR>after,’ परश्वस्; ‘belonging to to-morrow,’ श्वस्तनः -नी -नं,<BR>श्वस्त्यः &c.,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tom-tom
TOM-TOM, s. मृदङ्गः, पटहः, दुन्दुभिः m., डिण्डिमः. See DRUM.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ton
TON, s. सभ्याचारः, सभ्यरीतिः f., सभ्यसम्प्रदायः, शिष्टाचारः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tone
TONE, s. (Sound, note) स्वरः, नादः, ध्वनिः m., विरावः, विरिब्धः, see<BR>SOUND; ‘having a good tone,’ सुस्वरः -रा -रं.<BR>— (Musical<BR>sound) स्वरः, क्वणः, क्वाणः, क्वणनं, निक्वणः, निक्वाणः; ‘of a lute,’<BR>प्रक्वणः, प्रक्वाणः.<BR>— (Seventh part of a scale) मूर्च्छनं -ना; ‘half<BR>tone,’ स्वरांशः; ‘quarter tone,’ श्रुतिः f.<BR>— (In medicine) सुभा-<BR>वना, सद्भावना, सद्भावः, तेजस् n., अग्निः m.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tongs
TONGS, s. pl. सन्दंशः, सन्दंशकं -का, कङ्कमुखः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tongue
TONGUE, s. जिह्वा, रसना, रसज्ञा, रशना, रसिका, रसाला, रसनं,<BR>ललना, लोला, जिह्वः, विस्वासा, मुखचीरी; ‘root of the tongue,’<BR>जिह्वामूलं; ‘tip of it,’ जिह्वाग्रं; ‘that is on the tip of it,’<BR>जिह्वारूढः -ढा -ढं; ‘hold your tongue,’ वाचं नियच्छ, तूष्णीम्भवः<BR>‘tongue-scraper,’ see SCRAPER; ‘one of the seven tongues<BR>of fire,’ स्फुलिङ्गिनी; ‘tongue of a bell,’ लोला; ‘of a bolt,’<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=807-a" target="_blank">Page807-a+ 51</a>]<BR>कण्टकः.<BR>— (Speech) भाषा; ‘mother-tongue,’ जन्मभाषा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tongue-less
TONGUE-LESS, a. अजिह्वः -ह्वा -ह्वं, जिह्वाहीनः -ना -नं, निर्जिह्वः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tongue-tied
TONGUE-TIED, a. बद्धजिह्वः -ह्वा -ह्वं, संयन्त्रितजिह्वः &c., यतजिह्वः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tonic
TONIC, a. रुचकः -का -कं, रोचकः &c., तेजस्करः -रा -रं, दीपकः &c.,<BR>अग्निवर्धकः &c., अग्निदः -दा -दं, पाचकः -का -कं, दीपनः -ना -नं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tonic
TONIC, s. रुचकं, रोचकः, अग्निवर्धनः -नं, पाचकं, दीपनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

to-night
TO-NIGHT, adv. अद्य रात्रौ, अद्य निशि, अद्य नक्तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tonsil
TONSIL, s. कण्ठान्तर्वर्त्ती श्रेप्माद्याशयो मृदुमांसपिण्डः; ‘enlargement of<BR>them,’ अधिमांसकः, शतघ्नी, गण्डमाला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tonsure
TONSURE, s. (Shaving the head) क्षौरं, क्षोरकर्म्म n. (न्), केशवपनं,<BR>शिरोवपनं, मुण्डनं, शिरोमुण्डनं, केशछेदः.<BR>— (As a sacred rite)<BR>चूडाकर्म्म n. (न्), चूडाकरणं, चूडा, चौडं, चौलं, चौलकर्म्म n., चूडालक्षणं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

too
TOO, adv. (Over much) अति or सु prefixed, अतीव, अत्यन्तं, एका-<BR>न्ततस्, एकान्त in comp., see EXCESSIVELY; ‘too great a load,’<BR>अतिभारः; ‘he approaches too near the fire,’ अग्नेर् अतिस-<BR>मीपम् उपसर्पति; ‘too compassionate,’ अतिकरुणः -णा -णं,<BR>एकान्तकरुणः &c.; ‘too early,’ अतिप्रगे, अतिकल्यं; ‘too late<BR>in the evening,’ अतिसायं -ये; ‘too long,’ सुदीर्घः -र्घा -र्घं.<BR>—<BR>(Also) चैव, च, अपि, तथा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tool
TOOL, s. उपकरणं, यन्त्रं, साधनं, शस्त्रं, see INSTRUMENT; ‘a mere<BR>tool,’ निमित्तमात्रं, कारणमात्रं, उपकरणमात्रं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tooth
TOOTH, s. दन्तः, दशनः -नं, रदः, रदनः, दंशः, दंष्ट्रा, स्वादनः, दाढा,<BR>द्विजः, द्विजन्मा m. (न्), मुखजः, छद्वरः, दन्दशः, जम्भः, हालुः m.,<BR>स्वरुः m., वक्त्रखुरः, रुचकः, मल्लकः, फटः; ‘a row of teeth,’ दन्त-<BR>पंक्तिः f., दन्तावली, see TEETH; ‘two middle fore teeth,’ राज-<BR>दन्तौ m. du.; ‘double tooth,’ माढिः f.; ‘decay of a tooth,’<BR>द्विजव्रणः.<BR>— (Of a saw, comb, wheel, &c.) दन्तः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tooth-ache
TOOTH-ACHE, s. दन्तवेदना, दन्तव्यथा, दन्तशूलः, दालनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

