treasonable
TREASONABLE, a. राजद्रोही -हिणी -हि (न्), राजाभिद्रोही &c., राजा-<BR>पकारी &c., राजद्रोहसम्बन्धी &c., राजविरोधी &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

treasure
TREASURE, s. (Store of valuables) निधिः m., निधानं, कोषः.<BR>—<BR>(Accumulation of money, &c.) धनसञ्चयः, द्रव्यसञ्चयः, वित्तनि-<BR>चयः, धनराशिः m., धनसङ्ग्रहः, सञ्चितधनं.<BR>— (Money, &c.) धनं,<BR>वित्तं, वसु n.<BR>— (A treasure) निधिः m., कुलाभिः m.<BR>— (Divine<BR>treasure) निधिः m., सेवधिः m., see under KUVERA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

treasure
To TREASURE, v. a. निधिं कृ, निधा, संचि, कोषीकृ. See To HOARD.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

treasured
TREASURED, p. p. सञ्चितः -ता -तं, कोषीकृतः &c., कोषभूतः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

treasurer
TREASURER, s. कोषाध्यक्षः, कोशाध्यक्षः, कोशाधीशः, कोशनायकः, धना-<BR>धिकारी m. (न्), भाण्डागाराध्यक्षः, धनाध्यक्षः, अर्थाधिकारी m., कन-<BR>काध्यक्षः, कोष्ठपालः, गञ्जाधिकारी m., गञ्जाधिपः, धनाधिपः, भाण्डा-<BR>गारी m., भौरिकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

treasurership
TREASURERSHIP, s. कोषाधिकारः, अर्थाधिकारः, गञ्जाधिकारित्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

treasury
TREASURY, s. कोषः, कोशः, धनागारं, भाण्डागारं, धनशाला, धनगृहं,<BR>कोष्ठः -ष्ठकं, गञ्जः -ञ्जं, अर्थसंस्थानं, निधिः m.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

treat
To TREAT, v. a. (Act or behave towards) आचर् (c. 1. -चरति<BR>-रितुं), समाचर्, व्यवहृ (c. 1. -हरति -हर्त्तुं), सेव् (c. 1. सेवते -वितुं),<BR>विधा (c. 3. -दधाति -धातुं), प्रणी (c. 1. -णयति -णेतुं), विनी; ‘one<BR>should treat one's son like a friend,’ पुत्रं मित्रवद् आचरेत्;<BR>‘to treat ill,’ अपकृ, कुव्यवहारं कृ; ‘to treat with respect,’<BR>पूज्, सत्कृ, see To HONOUR; ‘with hospitality,’ सत्कृ, सत्कारं कृ,<BR>आतिथ्यं कृ.<BR>— (Give food, &c.) उत्तमान्नेन तृप् (c. 10. तर्पयति -यितुं)<BR>or सन्तृप्.<BR>— (A disease) उपचारं कृ, प्रयोगं कृ, चिकित्सां कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

treat
To TREAT, v. n. (Treat of any subject) विषयप्रसङ्गं कृ, प्रसक्तिं कृ,<BR>प्रस्तावं कृ, प्रस्तुतं -तां कृ, मथ् (c. 1. मथति -थितुं), मथनं कृ, विचर्<BR>(c. 10. -चारयति -यितुं), निरूप् (c. 10. -रूपयति -यितुं); ‘to treat<BR>at length,’ प्रपञ्चनं कृ.<BR>— (Negotiate) पण्, see the word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

treat
TREAT, s. उत्तमान्नतर्पणं, परमान्नभोजनं, see FEAST, ENTERTAINMENT.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

treated
