trustworthy
TRUSTWORTHY, TRUSTY, a. विश्वासार्हः -र्हा -र्हं, विश्वासयोग्यः -ग्या -ग्यं,<BR>विश्वास्यः -स्या -स्यं, आप्तः -प्ता -प्तं, विश्वासपात्रं, विश्वासभूमिः f.,<BR>विश्रब्धः -ब्धा -ब्धं, विश्रम्भार्हः -र्हा -र्हं, श्रद्धार्हः &c., अहार्य्यः -र्य्या -र्य्यं,<BR>अभेद्यः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

truth
TRUTH, s. सत्यं, तथ्यं, ऋतं, सम्यक्, अवितथं, तत्त्वं, तत्त्वार्थः, यथार्थवचनं,<BR>याथार्थ्यं, सत्त्वं, सत्ता, परमार्थः, पूतं.<BR>— (Trueness) सत्यता -त्वं, तथ्यता,<BR>यथार्थता, याथार्थ्यं, सम्यक्त्वं, वास्तवत्वं, याथातथ्यं; ‘one who speaks<BR>the truth,’ सत्यवादी m., see VERACIOUS; ‘speaking the truth,’<BR>see VERACITY; ‘one who knows the truth,’ तत्त्वविद्, सत्य-<BR>विद्; ‘investigation of truth,’ मीमांसा; ‘true state of the<BR>case,’ सत्यवृत्तं, सत्यवृत्तान्तः.<BR>— (In truth) सत्यमेव, वस्तुतस्, see TRULY.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

truthful
TRUTHFUL, TRUTHFULNESS. See TRUE, VERACIOUS, VERACITY.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

try
To TRY, v. a. (Test) परीक्ष् (c. 1. -ईक्षते -क्षितुं), परीक्षां कृ, अनुभू,<BR>ज्ञा in des., see To TEST, PROVE, EXAMINE, INVESTIGATE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

try
To TRY, v. n. (Endeavour) यत् (c. 1. यतते -तितुं), प्रयत्, यत्नं कृ।<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=814-a" target="_blank">Page814-a+ 51</a>]<BR>प्रयत्नं कृ, चेष्ट्, व्यवसो, उद्यम्, घट्, उपक्रम्, उद्यनं कृ, उद्योगं कृ;<BR>‘they tried to kill me,’ ते मां हन्तुम् उद्यताः or व्यवसिताः; ‘he<BR>tries to drink the water,’ जलं पातुं व्यवस्यति. Sometimes<BR>expressed by the desid. form; as, ‘he tries to recollect,’<BR>सुस्मूर्षते.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

trying
TRYING, part. or a. परीक्षकः -का -कं, परीक्षाकारी -रिणी -रि (न्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tub
TUB, s. द्रोणी -णिः f., द्रुणी -णिः f.; ‘bathing tub,’ स्नानद्रोणी -णिः f.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tube
TUBE, s. नलिका, नालः -ली -लिः -ला -लं, नाडी -डिः f., प्रणालः -ली<BR>-लिका, नलः, सुषिः f., सुषिरं; ‘glass tube,’ काचनालः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tuber
TUBER, s. (Bulbous root) कन्दः -न्दं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tubercle
TUBERCLE, s. सूक्ष्मव्रणः, सूक्ष्मगुल्मः, ग्रन्थिः m. See PIMPLE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tuberous
TUBEROUS, a. ग्रन्थिलः -ला -लं, कन्दी -न्दिनी &c. See KNOBBY.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tubular
TUBULAR, a. नलिकाकारः -रा -रं, नालाकृतिः -तिः -ति, नलिकाकृतिः<BR>&c.; ‘vessel of the body,’ नालः -ली, नाडिः -डी f., तन्त्री, धमनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tuck
