TUMULTUOUS, a. अनवस्थितः -ता -तं, अव्यवस्थितः -ता -तं, अव्यवस्थः<BR>-स्था -स्थं, क्षुब्धः -ब्धा -ब्धं, तुमुली &c. See DISORDERLY.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tun
TUN, s. (Large cask) वृहद्भाण्डं, वृहद्भाजनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tune
TUNE, s. (Combination of notes) तानः, तालः, कलः, स्वरः, रागिणी,<BR>रागभेदः; ‘time and tune,’ तानमानं.<BR>— (Harmony of sound)<BR>तालैक्यं, स्वरैक्यं, see HARMONY; ‘out of tune,’ अपस्वरः -रा -रं,<BR>कुस्वरः &c., वैतालिकः -की -कं; ‘in tune,’ सुस्वरः &c., युक्तस्वरः<BR>&c., एकस्वरः &c., तुल्यस्वरः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tune
To TUNE, v. a. तानीकृ, युक्तस्वरीकृ, स्वरैक्यं कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tuneful
TUNEFUL, a. सुस्वरः -रा -रं. See HARMONIOUS, MELODIOUS.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tunnel
