To TWIT, v. a. निन्द, उपालभ्, तिरस्कृ, परिवद्. See To REPROACH.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

twitch
To TWITCH, v. a. अकस्माद् आकृष् (c. 1. -कर्षति -कर्ष्टुं) or आक्षिप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

twitch
To TWITCH, v. n. स्फुर् (c. 6. स्फुरति -रितुं), विस्फुर्, कम्प्, स्पन्द्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

twitch
TWITCH, s. स्फुरणं, स्फुरितं, विस्फुरणं, प्रस्फुरणं, स्फूर्त्तिः f., स्पन्दनं, कम्पनं,<BR>आकस्मिकाकर्षः, आकस्मिकाक्षेपः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

twitter
To TWITTER, TWITTER. See To CHATTER, CHATTERING.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

two
TWO, a. द्वौ m. f. du., द्वे n. du. (द्वि), द्वयं affixed, द्वि prefixed;<BR>‘two men,’ द्वौ पुरुषौ or पुरुषद्वयं or expressed simply by<BR>the dual, पुरुषौ; ‘of two men,’ द्वयोः पुरुषयोः, or simply<BR>पुरुषयोः; ‘two months,’ द्विमासं, मासद्वयं; ‘two hundred,’ द्वे<BR>शते n. du., शतद्वयं, or simply शते; ‘two thousand,’ द्वे सहस्रे,<BR>सहस्रद्वयं, or simply सहस्रे. The crude form द्वि is chiefly<BR>used in Bahuvrīhi compounds; as, ‘two-armed,’ द्विभुजः<BR>-जा -जं; ‘two-footed,’ द्विपादः -दा -दं, द्विपदः &c.; ‘two-<BR>handed,’ द्विहस्तः -स्ता -स्तं; ‘two-headed,’ द्विमूर्द्धः -र्द्धा -र्द्धं; ‘two-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=816-a" target="_blank">Page816-a+ 50</a>]<BR>formed,’ द्विरूपः -पा -पं; ‘two-edged,’ द्विधारः -रा -रं, उभयत-<BR>स्तीक्ष्णः -क्ष्णा -क्ष्णं; ‘consisting of two,’ द्विमयः -यी -यं; ‘two-<BR>year-old,’ द्विवार्षिकः -की -कं; ‘in two ways,’ द्विधा, द्वैधं;<BR>‘two or three,’ द्वित्राः -त्राः -त्राणि (त्र).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

two-fold
TWO-FOLD, a. द्विगुणः -णा -णं, द्विगुणितः -ता -तं, द्विगुणीकृतः &c.,<BR>द्विकः -का -कं, द्विविधः -धा -धं, द्वैधः -धी -धं, द्विप्रकारः -रा -रं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tympanites
TYMPANITES, s. अलसकः, गुल्मोदरं, गुल्मः. See FLATULENCE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

type
TYPE, s. (Emblem) लक्षणं, व्यञ्जनं, व्यञ्जकः, चिह्नं, see SYMBOL, SIGN,<BR>MARK; ‘of birth,’ उत्पत्तिव्यञ्जकः.<BR>— (Figure of something to<BR>come) प्रतिरूपं -पकं, प्रतिविम्बं, दर्शकचिह्नं.<BR>— (Printing letter)<BR>मुद्राक्षरं.<BR>— (In medicine) भावना, स्वरूपं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

typical
TYPICAL, a. लाक्षणिकः -की -कं, उद्बोधकः -का -कं, बोधकः &c., प्रति-<BR>रूपकः &c., प्रतिविम्बकः &c. See PREFIGURATIVE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

typefy
To TYPEFY, TYPEFIED. See To PREFIGURE, PREFIGURED.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

typographical
TYPOGRAPHICAL, s. मुद्राङ्कनमम्बन्धी &c., मुद्राक्षरसम्बन्धी &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

typography
TYPOGRAPHY, s. मुद्राङ्कनं, मुद्राक्षरप्रयोगः. See PRINTING.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tyrannic
TYRANNIC, TYRANNICAL, a. प्रजापीडकः -का -कं, प्रजोपद्रवी -विणी &c.,<BR>प्रजाबाधकः -का -कं, प्रजोपप्लवी &c. See OPPRESSIVE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tyrannically
TYRANNICALLY, adv. सनैष्ठुर्य्यं, सक्रौर्य्यं, प्रजापीडकवत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tyrannicide
TYRANNICIDE, s. (The act) प्रजापीडकहत्या.<BR>— (The agent) प्रजापीड-<BR>कहन्ता m. (न्तृ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tyrannize
To TYRANNIZE, v. n. कुशासनं कृ, अनीतिशासनं कृ, असम्यक्शासनं कृ,<BR>असम्यक्पालनं कृ, प्रजापीडनं कृ, प्रजोपद्रवं कृ, प्रजोपप्लवं कृ, अन्याय-<BR>शासनं कृ; ‘tyrannized over,’ उपद्रुतः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tyranny
TYRANNY, s. (Absolute monarchy) स्वतन्त्रराज्यं, अनिर्बन्धराज्यं.<BR>—<BR>(Oppressive rule) कुशासनं, प्रजापीडनं, प्रजोपद्रवः, प्रजोपप्लवः,<BR>निष्ठुरता, नैष्ठुर्य्यं, परिप्लवः, see OPPRESSION, To TYRANNIZE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tyrant
TYRANT, s. प्रजापीडकः, उपद्रवी m., निष्ठुरः, see OPPRESSOR.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

tyro
TYRO, s. नवछात्रः, छात्रः, नवशिष्यः, नूतनशिष्यः, नूतनाभ्यासी m. (न्),<BR>विद्यारम्भकः, क्रियाकारः, किञ्चिज्ज्ञः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ubiquitous
UBIQUITOUS, UBIQUITY. See OMNIPRESENT, OMNIPRESENCE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

udder
UDDER, s. ऊधस् n., उधस् n., ओधस् n., ओधः, ऊधसं, उधसं, आपीनं,<BR>वाणः, वामः; ‘of a cow,’ गोस्तनः; ‘of a bitch,’ शुनीस्तनः,<BR>सुनारः. Obs. ऊधस् becomes ऊपन् in comp.; as, ‘a cow<BR>with a full udder,’ पीनोध्नी, पीवरस्तनी; ‘with an udder like<BR>a well,’ कुण्डोध्नी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ugliness
UGLINESS, s. कुरूपता, विरूपता, वैरूप्यं, अपरूपता, असौन्दर्य्यं, आलावण्यं,<BR>असौम्यता, कुत्सिताकारता, असौष्ठवं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ugly
UGLY, a. कुरूपः -पा -पी -पं, अपरूपः &c., विरूपः &c., रूपहीनः -ना<BR>-नं, कदाकारः -रा -रं, कुत्सिताकारः &c., कुत्सितः -ता -तं, कुत्सि-<BR>ताकृतिः -तिः -ति, असुन्दरः -रा -री -रं, असौम्यः -म्या -म्यं, दुर्दर्शनः<BR>-ना -नं, विकृताकारः &c.; ‘an ugly woman,’ कुस्त्री.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ulcer
ULCER, s. व्रणः, क्षतं, नाढीक्षणः, सपूयक्षतं, पूतिव्रणः, रक्तविद्रधिः m.,<BR>उत्सङ्गी m. (न्); ‘bottom of one,’ उत्सङ्गः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ulcerate
To ULCERATE, v. n. सव्रणीभू, सव्रटीभू, व्रणितः -ता -तं भू, व्रणं बन्ध्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ulcerate
To ULCERATE, v. a. व्रणं कृ, सव्रणीकृ, क्षतं कृ, प्रणम् उत्पद् in caus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ulcerated
ULCERATED, ULCEROUS, a. सव्रणी -णिनी -णि (न्), व्रणिता -ता -तं,<BR>सव्रणः -ण -णं, राक्षतः -ता -तं, जातव्रणः -णा -णं, व्रणमयः -यी -यं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ulceration
ULCERATION, s. व्रणित्वं -ता, सव्रण वः, सक्षतभावः, व्रणबन्धनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ulterior
ULTERIOR, a. उत्तरः -रा -रं, अपरः &c., पाश्चात्यः -त्या -त्यं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ultimate
ULTIMATE, a. अन्तिमः -मा -मं, चरमः &c. See LAST, FINAL.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ultimately
ULTIMATELY, adv. अन्ततस्, अन्ते, शेषे, शेषतस्. See LASTLY.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ultimatum
ULTIMATUM, s. अन्त्यप्रतिज्ञा, अन्त्यवाक्यं, निदानवाक्यं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ultra
ULTRA, s. अत्यन्तः -न्ता -न्तं, एकान्तः &c. See EXCESSIVE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uma
UMĀ, s. (Wife of Śiva) उमा, सती, see DURGĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

umbilical
UMBILICAL, a. नाभ्यः -भ्या -भ्यं, नाभिसम्बन्धी &c.; ‘umbilical cord,<BR>नाभिः f., नालः, नाभिनाडी, नाभिनाला, गर्भनाडी; ‘section of it,’<BR>नाभिच्छेदनं; ‘region,’ नाभिमण्डलं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

umbrage
UMBRAGE, s. असन्तोषः, अतुष्टिः f., अप्रीतिः f.; ‘to take umbrage,’<BR>असन्तुष्टः -ष्टा -ष्टं भू, प्रकुप् (c. 4. -कुप्यति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

umbrella
UMBRELLA, s. छत्रं, जलत्रा, वारित्रा, आतपत्रं, आतपवारणं, वस्त्रकुट्टिमं,<BR>कावारी; ‘state-umbrella,’ छत्रं; ‘bearer of it,’ छत्रधारी m. (न्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

umpire
UMPIRE, s. मध्यस्थः, स्थेयः, प्रमाणपुरुषः, शठः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

un
UN. This prefix is expressed in Sanskrit by अ, अन्, निर्,<BR>वि, अप, दुर् &c., prefixed, or by हीन, रहित, शून्य &c., affixed.<BR>In cases where the English word formed with ‘un’ is<BR>not given in this Dictionary, the student must take the<BR>simple noun and use one of the above prefixes or affixes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unable
UNABLE, a. अशक्तः -क्ता -क्तं, असमर्थः -र्था -र्थं, अक्षमः -मा -मं, अनीशः<BR>-शा -शं, अकल्पः -ल्पा -ल्पं, अपारकः -का -कं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unaccented
UNACCENTED, a. अनुदात्तः -त्ता -त्तं, अस्वरितः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unacceptable
UNACCEPTABLE, a. अप्रतिग्राह्यः -ह्या -ह्यं, अग्राह्यः &c., अग्रहणीयः &c.,<BR>अनादेयः -या -यं, अस्वीकार्य्यः -र्य्या -र्य्यं, अलीकः -का -कं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unaccompanied
UNACCOMPANIED, a. असहायः -या -यं, असहायवान् -वती -वत् (त्),<BR>असहायी -यिनी -यि (न्), असङ्गः -ङ्गा -ङ्गं, एकाकी &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unaccomplished
UNACCOMPLISHED, a. असाधितः -ता -तं, असिद्धः -द्धा -द्धं, असंसिद्धः &c.,<BR>असम्पन्नः -न्ना -न्नं, अनिष्पन्नः &c., अनुपपन्नः &c., असमाप्तः -प्ता -प्तं,<BR>अनधिगतः -ता -तं, अकृतः &c., अनागतवान् &c., असम्पूर्णः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unaccountable
UNACCOUNTABLE, See INEXPLICABLE, IRRESPONSIBLE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unaccustomed
UNACCUSTOMED, a. अनभ्यस्तः -स्ता -स्तं, अनभ्यासी &c., अकृताभ्यासः<BR>-सा -सं; ‘to ornament,’ अननुभूतभूषणः -णा -णं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unacknowledged
