UNWROUGHT, a. अकृतः -ता -तं, असंस्कृतः &c.; ‘silver,’ अकृतरूप्यं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unyielding
UNYIELDING, a. अनायम्यः -म्या -म्यं, अशिथिलः -ला -लं. See FIRM.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

unyoke
To UNYOKE, v. a. वियुज् (c. 7. -युनक्ति -योक्तुं, c. 10. -योजयति -यितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

up
UP, prep. or adv. उत् prefixed, ऊर्द्ध्वं, उच्चैः, उच्चकैः; ‘looking up,’<BR>उन्मुखः -खा -खं, ऊर्द्ध्वदृष्टिः -ष्टिः -ष्टि; ‘to look up,’ ऊर्द्ध्वं दृश्;<BR>‘to rise up,’ उत्था; ‘to go up,’ उद्गम्; ‘to lift up,’ उत्तुल्;<BR>‘having the feet up,’ ऊर्द्ध्वपादः -दा -दं, ऊर्द्ध्वचरणः &c.<BR>— (Up and<BR>down) उन्नतानतः -ता -तं, निम्नोन्नतः &c., उच्चावचः -चा -चं; ‘ups<BR>and downs,’ पातोत्पाताः m. pl.; ‘moving up and down,’ समु-<BR>द्वहन् -हन्ती &c., see UNDULATING.<BR>— (Up to) पर्य्यन्तं, यावत्, आ,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=824-a" target="_blank">Page824-a+ 51</a>]<BR>see under To.<BR>— (To an equal height with) दघ्नः -घ्नी -घ्नं,<BR>द्वयसः -सी -सं, मात्रः -त्री -त्रं; ‘water up to the knees,’ जानु-<BR>दघ्नं जलं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

upanishad
UPANISHAD, s. उपनिषद् f. See under SCRIPTURE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

upapurana
UPAPURĀNA, s. उपपुराणं. See under PURĀNA, SCRIPTURE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

upas-tree
