urethra
URETHRA, s. (In anatomy) मूत्रमार्गः, मूत्रपथः, मूत्रद्वारं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

urge
To URGE, v. a. प्रेर्, प्रणुद्, चुद्, प्रचुद्, संचुद्, बाध्, प्रबाध्, आक्रम्,<BR>उत्तिज्, निर्बन्धं कृ. See To PRESS, INSTIGATE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

urged
URGED, p. p. प्रेरितः -ता -तं, चोदितः &c., प्रचोदितः &c., बाधितः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

urgency
URGENCY, s. (Importunacy) निर्बन्धः, अतिनिर्बन्धः, आग्रहः.<BR>— (Pres-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=824-b" target="_blank">Page824-b+ 51</a>]<BR>sure) प्रेरणा, बाधः -धनं, प्रणोदः, भारः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

urgent
URGENT, a. बाधकः -का -कं, प्रबाधकः &c., निर्बन्धी -न्धिनी &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

urgently
URGENTLY, adv. निर्बन्धेन, अतिनिर्बन्धेन, आग्रहेण, सबाधं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

urinal
URINAL, s. मूत्रपात्रं, मूत्राधारः, मूत्रभाजनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

urinary
URINARY, a. मूत्रलः -ला -लं, मेही -हिनी -हि (न्), मूत्रसम्बन्धी &c.,<BR>मूत्र in comp.; ‘urinary affection,’ मूत्रदोषः, मूत्रकृच्छ्रं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

urine
URINE, s. मूत्रं, प्रस्रावः, मेहः -हनं, वस्तिमलं, गुह्यनिष्यन्दः; ‘milky<BR>urine,’ मूत्रशुक्रं; ‘passing blood in urine,’ रक्तप्रमेहः; ‘passing<BR>mucus,’ लालामेहः; ‘suppression of urine,’ मूत्ररोधः, मूत्राव-<BR>रोधः, मूत्रस्तम्भः, मूत्राघातः; ‘affection of the urine,’ मेहः, प्रमेहः,<BR>मेहनशूलः -लं. Of these, twenty-one varieties are enu-<BR>merated, see DIABETES, GONORRHŒA, &c.; ‘one suffering<BR>from this affection,’ मेही m., प्रमेही m.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

urine
To URINE, v. n. मूत्र् (c. 10. मूत्रयति -यितुं), मिह्. See To PISS.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

urn
URN, s. जलकुम्भः, जलपात्रं, जलभाजनं, कुम्भः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

uroscopy
