vantage
VANTAGE, VANTAGE-GROUND. See SUPERIORITY.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vapid
VAPID, a. विरसः -सा -सं, नीरसः &c., निस्सारः &c. See FLAT.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vaporous
VAPOROUS, VAPORY, a. वाष्परूपः -पा -पं, वाष्पमयः -यी -यं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vapour
VAPOUR, s. वाष्पः, स्वेदः, धूमः -मिका, फेनः -नता, खवाष्पः; ‘hot<BR>vapour,’ उष्णवाष्पः; ‘sultry vapour,’ मृगतृष्णा, see MIRAGE;<BR>‘vapour-bath,’ उप्मस्वेदः, उष्णस्वेदः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vapour
