varuna
VARUNA, s. (God of the waters, the Hindū Neptune, Regent<BR>of the West. He is also Lord of punishment, in which<BR>capacity he resembles Yama and Śiva) वरुणः, प्रचेताः m. (स्),<BR>वारुणीवल्लभः.<BR>— (As lord of the waters) अपाम्पतिः m., अप्पतिः m.,<BR>जलपतिः m., केशः, केशगर्भः.<BR>— (As lord of aquatic animals)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=827-a" target="_blank">Page827-a+ 51</a>]<BR>यादसाम्पतिः m., यादःपतिः m., यादसान्नाथः.<BR>— (As holding the<BR>cord, with which he binds incorrigible offenders under<BR>the water) पाशी m. (न्), पाशभृत् m., पाशपाणिः m. His con-<BR>sort is called वरुणानी, वरुणी. His son अगस्तिः m., अगस्त्यः,<BR>वारुणिः m. His vāhana or vehicle is a fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vary
