VASSAL, VASSALAGE. See DEPENDANT, DEPENDANCE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=827-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vast
VAST, a. सुमहान् -हती -हत् (त्), अतिमहान् &c., अतिवृहन् -हती &c.,<BR>अपरिमितः -ता -तं, पुलः -ला -लं. See HUGE, IMMENSE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=827-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vasudeva
VASUDEVA, s. (Father of Krishna, and son of Śūra, called<BR>Ānakadundubhi, because at his birth the gods sounded<BR>with joy the drums of heaven, as foreseeing that Viṣṇu<BR>would take a human form in one of his family) वसुदेवः,<BR>आनकदुन्दुभिः m., दुन्दुः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=827-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

