VESPERTINE, a. सायङ्कालिकः -की -कं, सायन्तनः &c. See EVENING, a.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vessel
VESSEL, s. (Utensil for holding, as a pot, cup, &c.) पात्रं, भाजनं,<BR>भाण्डं, अमत्रं, आधारः, धारकः; ‘drinking vessel,’ पानपात्रं;<BR>‘for holding water,’ उदकपात्रं, जलपात्रं, घटः, कलशः.<BR>— (Vessel<BR>of the body, as a vein, &c.) शिरा, नाडिः -डी f., नालिः -ली,<BR>धमनी, वाहिनी, see TUBE.<BR>— (Boat, ship) नौः f., नौका, पोतः,<BR>वहिनी, वहित्रं, तरणी, जलयानं, वोहित्थं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vest
