villa
VILLA, s. नगरोपान्ते खेलिगृहं or विनोदगृहं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

village
VILLAGE, s. ग्रामः, निवसथः, अवसथः, उपवसथः, संवसथः, प्रतिवसथः,<BR>सद्वसथः, पल्लिः -ल्ली f., कटकः, खेटकः, पद्रः, ग्रामस्थः; ‘number<BR>of villages,’ ग्रामता, ग्रामसङ्घः; ‘a hundred villages,’ ग्रामशतं;<BR>‘chief or head-man of a village. ग्रामाधिपतिः m., ग्रामाध्यक्षः,<BR>ग्रामाधिकृतः, ग्रामशः, ग्रामनायकः, ग्रामणीः m.; ‘space near a<BR>village,’ ग्रामान्तं, उपशल्यं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

village
VILLAGE, a. ग्राम्यः -म्या -म्यं, ग्रामीयः -या -यं, ग्रामीणः -णा -णं, ग्रामिकः<BR>-की -कं, ग्राम in comp.; ‘village divinity,’ ग्रामदेवता; ‘vil-<BR>lage officer,’ ग्रामाधिकारी m.; ‘village priest,’ ग्रामयाजकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=830-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

villager
