vitreous
VITREOUS, a. काचमयः -यो -यं, काचगुणकः -का -कं, काचसगुणः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vitrefy
To VITREFY, v. a. काचसात्कृ, काचवत्कृ, काचपरिणामं कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vitriol
VITRIOL, s. (Blue) तुत्थं -त्थकं, तुत्थाञ्जनं, ताम्रगर्भः, मूपातुत्थं, तूतकं,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=832-b" target="_blank">Page832-b+ 51</a>]<BR>शिखिग्रीवं, मयूरकं, नीलाञ्जनं, नीलं, वितुन्नकं, हेमतारं.<BR>— (Green)<BR>कासीसं, काशीशं, मलीमसः -सं, धातुशेखरः, विषदं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vituperate
To VITUPERATE, VITUPERATION. See To BLAME, CENSURE, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vivacious
VIVACIOUS, a. तेजोवान् -वती -वत् (त्), उल्लासी &c. See LIVELY.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

vivacity
