WAKING, s. जागरणं, प्रजागरः, जागरः, प्रबोधः -धनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

walk
To WALK, v. n. (Go on the feet) पादाभ्यां गम् (c. 1. गच्छति, गन्तुं)<BR>or या (c. 2. याति -तुं), पादाभ्यां क्रम् (c. 1. क्रामति, c. 4. क्राम्यति,<BR>क्रमितुं), पादाभ्यां चल् or चर्; ‘backwards and forwards,’ गम-<BR>नागमनं कृ.<BR>— (Walk about, as for pleasure, &c.) परिक्रम्, विहृ<BR>(c. 1. -हरति -हर्त्तुं), परिक्रमं कृ.<BR>— (Walk off), see To DECAMP.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

walk
WALK, WALKING, s. पादगमनं, पादचारः, पादव्रजनं, पादक्रमणं, क्रमणं,<BR>पादाभ्यां गमनं; ‘walking about,’ परिक्रमः; ‘for pleasure,’<BR>विहारः, विहरणं.<BR>— (Place for walking) विहारस्थानं, गमनागमन-<BR>मार्गः, पदगमार्गः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

walker
WALKER, s. पादचारी m. (न्), पादयायी m., पादगः, पदगः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wall
WALL, s. (Of a house, &c.) भित्तिः f., भित्तिका, कुड्यं, कुड्यकं.<BR>—<BR>(A surrounding or inclosing wall) प्राकारः, प्राचीरं, परिसरः,<BR>सालः.<BR>— (Wall of bones, rubbish, &c.) एडुकं, ऐडुकं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

walled
WALLED, a. प्राकारीयः -या -यं, प्राकारावृतः &c., प्राचीरावृतः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wallet
WALLET, s. सोपकारद्रव्यकोषः, सोपकारद्रव्याधारः, क्षुद्रकोषः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wallow
To WALLOW, v. n. पङ्के लुठ् (c. 6. लुठति -ठितुं) or प्रलुठ् or क्रीड् (c. 1.<BR>क्रीडति -डितुं); ‘a pig that wallows in mire,’ पङ्कक्रीडः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

walnut
WALNUT, s. (Tree) अक्षोटः, आक्षोटः, अक्षोडः, पीलुः m., कन्दरालः<BR>-लकः, कर्परालः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

waltz
WALTZ, s. विवर्त्तनृत्यं, विवर्त्तननृत्यं, परिवर्त्तननृत्यं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wan
WAN, a. पाण्डुः -ण्डुः -ण्डु, विवर्णः -र्णा -र्णं, पाण्डुवर्णः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wand
WAND, s. दण्डः, वेत्रं, यष्टिः m. f., वेत्रयष्टिः; ‘of death,’ कालदण्डः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wander
To WANDER, v. n. भ्रम् (c. 4. भ्राम्यति, भ्रमितुं), परिभ्रम्, अट् (c. 1. अटति<BR>-ते -टितुं), पर्यट्, विहृ, विचर्, परिक्रम्, प्रव्रज्, परिगम्, भ्रमणं कृ,<BR>see To ROVE, RAMBLE; ‘to wander from,’ see To STRAY.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wanderer
WANDERER, s. भ्रमणकारी m. (न्), भ्रमी m., परिभ्रमी m., विहारी m.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wandering
WANDERING, s. भ्रमणं, परिभ्रमणं, प्रव्रज्या. See ROAMING.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wane
To WANE, v. n. क्षि in pass. (क्षीयते), परिक्षि, प्रक्षि, संक्षि, ह्रस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wane
WANE, s. क्षयः, क्षितिः f., परिक्षयः, अपक्षयः, ह्रासः, तेजःक्षयः, तेजो-<BR>ह्रासः; ‘of the moon,’ इन्दुक्षयः, कृष्णपक्षः, अपरपक्षः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

waned
WANED, p. p. क्षीणः -णा -णं, क्षीणकलः -ला -लं, कलाक्षीणः &c.,<BR>अपक्षीणः &c., निष्कलः -ला -लं, प्राप्तक्षयः -या -यं, जातक्षयः &c.,<BR>जातह्रासः -सा -सं; ‘a waned moon,’ कलाशेषः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wanness
WANNESS, s. पाण्डुता, विवर्णता, वैवर्ण्यं, कालिमा m. (न्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

want
To WANT, v. a. or n. (Be without) हीनः -ना -नं भू or अस्, see<BR>To LACK; ‘he wants wisdom,’ बुद्धिहीनः or निर्बुद्धिर् अस्ति.<BR>— (Have need of) आकांक्ष् (c. 1. -कांक्षति -क्षितुं), अपेक्ष् (c. 1.<BR>-ईक्षते -क्षितुं), see To NEED.<BR>— (Desire, wish) इष् (c. 6. इच्छति,<BR>एषितुं), आकांक्ष्, कांक्ष्, see To DESIRE.<BR>— (Be deficient) न्यूनीभू.<BR>— (Be in poverty) दरिद्रा (c. 2. दरिद्राति -द्रितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

want
WANT, s. (Absence of any thing) अभावः, असम्भवः, अविषयः,<BR>विरहः, अप्राप्तिः f., राहित्यं, रहितत्वं, शून्यत्वं, अदर्शनं; ‘from want<BR>of rain,’ वृष्टेरभावात्; ‘from want of food,’ आहारविरहात्; ‘want<BR>of money,’ धनाभावः.<BR>— (Occasion for) प्रयोजनं, see NEED.<BR>—<BR>(Deficiency) न्यूनता.<BR>— (Indigence) दारिद्र्यं, धनाभावः, द्रव्याभावः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wanting
WANTING, a. न्यूनः -ना -नं, अविद्यमानः &c. See DEFICIENT.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wanton
WANTON, a. (Frolicsome) विलासी -सिनी -सि (न्), विलासवान्<BR>-वती -वत् (त्), see PLAYFUL.<BR>— (Lascivious) कामुकः -का -कं,<BR>कामी &c., लाली &c., see LUSTFUL; ‘a wanton woman,’<BR>पुंश्चली, बन्धकी, लालिनी.<BR>— (Self-willed, unrestrained) स्वैरः<BR>-री -रं, स्वैरी &c., कामचारी &c., स्वेच्छः -च्छा -च्छं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wanton
To WANTON, v. n. विलस् (c. 1. -लसति -सितुं), क्रीड्. See To PLAY.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wantonly
WANTONLY, adv. कामुकवत्, विलासेन, स्वेच्छया, यथेच्छं, यथेष्टं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wantonness
WANTONNESS, s. कामुकत्वं, लीला, विलासः, लालित्यं, स्वैरिता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

war
WAR, s. विग्रहः, युद्धं, प्रयुद्धं, सङ्ग्रामः, रणं, संयुगः, सम्परायः यकं,<BR>भीमरः, राटिः f., see BATTLE; ‘one skilled in it,’ सांयुगीनः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

war
To WAR, v. n. (Make war) विग्रहं कृ, विग्रह् (c. 9. -गृह्लाति -ग्रहीतुं),<BR>युद्धं कृ, युध् (c. 4. युध्यते, योद्धुं), संग्राम् (c. 10. -ग्रामयते -यितुं),<BR>संग्रामं कृ; ‘wishing to make war,’ सिसंग्रामयिषुः -षुः -षु;<BR>‘war-chariot,’ स्यन्दनः; ‘war-cry,’ सिंहनादः; ‘war-horse,’<BR>योधहरः, see CHARGER; ‘war-dance,’ वीरजयन्तिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warble
To WARBLE, WARBLING. See To QUAVER, SING, SINGING.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ward
To WARD, v. a. (Off) प्रतिवृ (c. 10. -वारयति -यितुं), निवृ, प्रतिहन्<BR>(c. 2. -हन्ति -न्तुं), प्रतिकृ, निरुध्, अपसिध्, प्रतिषिध्, व्यपोह्; ‘a<BR>blow,’ प्रतिघातं कृ, परित्राणं कृ, हस्तवारणं कृ, हस्तधारणं कृ, पर्य्याप्तिं कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ward
WARD, s. (Of a town) पुरार्द्धविस्तरः.<BR>— (Custody) रक्षा.<BR>— (One<BR>under a guardian) नाथाधीनः, बालः, शिशुः m., किशोरः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warden
WARDEN, s. रक्षकः, नाथः, अध्यक्षः, अधिकारी m. (न्), पालः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warder
WARDER, s. दौवारिकः, द्वाराध्यक्षः, रक्षकः, दर्शकः, see DOOR-KEEPER.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ward-robe
WARD-ROBE, s. वस्त्राधारः, वस्त्रभाण्डं.<BR>— (Clothes) वस्त्रसमूहः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ware
WARE, WARES, s. पण्यं, विट्पण्यं, द्रव्यं. See COMMODITY.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warehouse
WAREHOUSE, s. पण्यशाला, पण्यद्रव्यशाला, विक्रेयद्रव्यशाला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warfare
WARFARE, s. युद्धं, सङ्ग्रामः, विग्रहः. See WAR, BATTLE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warily
WARILY, WARINESS. See CAUTIOUSLY, CAUTION, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warlike
WARLIKE, a. (Pertaining to war) साङ्ग्रामिकः -की -कं, सामरिकः<BR>&c., साम्परायिकः &c.<BR>— (Disposed for war) रणप्रियः -या -यं,<BR>रणकामी -मिनी &c., रणासक्तः -क्ता -क्तं, रणोत्सुकः -का -कं, रणशूरः<BR>-रा -रं, रणवीरः &c., युयुत्सुः -त्सुः -त्सु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warm
WARM, a. उष्णः -ष्णा -ष्णं, ईषदुष्णः &c., चण्डः -ण्डा -ण्डं, उच्चण्डः &c.,<BR>ईषच्चण्डः &c., तप्तः -प्ता -प्तं, ईषत्तप्तः &c., घर्म्म in comp., see HOT;<BR>‘water,’ घर्म्मपयस् n.<BR>— (Suffering from heat) घर्म्मार्त्तः -र्त्ता -र्त्तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warm
To WARM, v. a. ईषत् तप् (c. 10. तापयति -यितुं) or सन्तप् or प्रतप्,<BR>किञ्चित् तप्, ईषदुष्णीकृ; ‘the feet,’ पादौ प्रतप्; ‘to warm one's<BR>self at the fire,’ अग्नितापं सेव्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warmed
WARMED, p. p. ईषत्तप्तः -प्ता -प्तं, किञ्चित्तप्तः &c., ईषदुष्णीकृतः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warm-hearted
WARM-HEARTED, a. हृदयी -यिणी &c., हृदयालुः -लुः -लु, स्नेही &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warmly
WARMLY, adv. उष्णं, सोप्मं, चण्डं, प्रचण्डं, सस्नेहं, स्नेहेन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warmth
WARMTH, WARMNESS, s. उष्णता, उष्णः, चण्डता, उष्मः, कोष्णता, कोष्णं,<BR>तापः, ईषत्तापः, उत्तापः, रौद्रः -द्रं. See HEAT, HOTNESS.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warn
To WARN, v. a. (Caution, admonish) प्रत्यादिश् (c. 6. -दिशति -देष्टुं),<BR>सन्दिश्, प्रदिश्, उपदिश्, पूर्व्वे प्रबुध् in caus., चित् in caus. (चेत-<BR>यति -यितुं), see To CAUTION, &c.<BR>— (Apprise) विज्ञा in caus.<BR>(-ज्ञापयति -यितुं), सूच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warned
WARNED, p. p. प्रत्यादिष्टः -ष्टा -ष्टं, प्रबोधितः &c., विज्ञापितः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warning
WARNING, s. प्रत्यादेशः, प्रबोधः -धनं, पूर्व्वबोधः -धनं, सन्देशः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warp
To WARP, v. a. साचीकृ, वक्रीकृ, कुञ्च् (c. 10. कुञ्चयति -यितुं), आकुञ्च्,<BR>संकुच् (c. 1. -कोचति -चितुं), आकृष्, संहृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warp
To WARP, v. n. संकुच् or कुञ्च् in pass., तूण्. See To SHRINK, v. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warrant
To WARRANT, v. a. प्रमाणं दा, अधिकारं or अधिकारित्वं दा, सप्रमाणं -णां<BR>कृ, सप्रमाणीकृ, प्रमाणीकृ. See To SANCTION, AUTHORISE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warrant
WARRANT, s. (Authority, sanction) अधिकारित्वं, प्रमाणं, अनुज्ञा,<BR>आश्रयः.<BR>— (Writ) आज्ञापत्रं, शासनपत्रं, अनुज्ञापत्रं, अधिकारपत्रं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

warranted
WARRANTED, p. p. सप्रमाणः -णा -णं, साश्रयः -या -यं, साधारः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

