WE, pron. वयं nom. pl. (अस्मद्); ‘we two,’ आवां nom. du.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weak
WEAK, a. दुर्बलः -ला -लं, निर्बलः &c., अबलः &c., अल्पबलः &c., अल्प-<BR>शक्तिः -क्तिः -क्ति, अकल्पः -ल्पा -ल्पं, निःसत्त्वः -त्त्वा -त्त्वं, निस्तेजाः -जाः<BR>-जः (स्), see FEEBLE, INFIRM.<BR>— (In mind) अल्पबुद्धिः -द्धिः -द्धि,<BR>अल्पधीः -धीः -धि, विकलबुद्धिः &c., विकलान्तःकरणः -णा -णं.<BR>—<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=837-a" target="_blank">Page837-a+ 51</a>]<BR>(Weak point or side) छिद्रं, मर्म्मस्थानं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weaken
To WEAKEN, v. a. दुर्बलीकृ, बलं हृ (c. 1. हरति, हर्त्तुं), बलक्षयं कृ,<BR>शक्तिक्षयं कृ, शक्तिभङ्गं कृ, शक्तिह्रासं कृ. See To DEBILITATE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weakened
WEAKENED, p. p. क्षीणबलः -ला -लं, हृतबलः &c., दुर्बलीकृतः -ता -तं,<BR>हृतौजाः -जाः -जः (स्), क्षीणसत्त्वः -त्त्वा -त्त्वं. See ENFEEBLED.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weakening
WEAKENING, a. बलक्षयकारी -रिणी -रि (न्), सत्त्वक्षयकारी &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weakness
WEAKNESS, s. दुर्बलता, दौर्बल्यं, निर्बलता, अबलं, अशक्तिः f., बलहीनता,<BR>बलक्षयः, शक्तिक्षयः, बलक्षीणता, बलहानिः f., शक्तिभङ्गः, see DE-<BR>BILITY.<BR>— (Foible) छिद्रं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weal
WEAL, s. क्षेमं, कल्याणं, शुभं, श्रेयस्, भद्रं, कुशलं, see WELFARE;<BR>‘weal and woe,’ शुभाशुभं, भद्राभद्रं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wealth
WEALTH, s. धनं, वसु n., वित्तं, विभवः, वैभवं, सम्पत्तिः f., द्रविणं, द्रव्यं,<BR>राः m. (रै), रिक्थं, ऋक्थं, हिरण्यं, द्युम्नं, स्वापतेयं, भोग्यं, see RICHES;<BR>‘in grain,’ धान्यधनं, धान्यार्थः; ‘in cattle,’ गोधनं, चर्म्मधनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wealthiness
WEALTHINESS, s. महाधनता, सधनत्वं. See RICHNESS, OPULENCE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wealthy
WEALTHY, a. धनी -निनी -नि (न्). See RICH, OPULENT.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wean
To WEAN, v. a. त्यक्तस्तन्यं -न्यां कृ, स्तन्यवियुक्तं -क्तां कृ, स्तन्यं -त्यज् in<BR>caus. (त्याजयति -यितुं), स्तन्यत्यागं कृ.<BR>— (From the world) सङ्ग-<BR>विमुखं -खां कृ, विषयविमुखं -खां कृ, त्यक्तसङ्गं -ङ्गां कृ, विरक्तं -क्तां कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weaned
WEANED, p. p. त्यक्तस्तन्यः -न्या -न्यं, त्यक्तस्तनः -ना -नं. See To WEAN.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weaning
WEANING, WEANEDNESS, s. स्तन्यत्यागः; ‘from the world,’ सङ्गत्यागः,<BR>वैराग्यं, विषयासङ्गः, इन्द्रियासङ्गः, विषयविमुखता, प्रत्याहारः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weapon
WEAPON, s. शस्त्रं, आयुधं, अस्त्रं, प्रहरणं, हेतिः f., परिघातः, बधत्रं, शस्त्रास्त्रं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wear
To WEAR, v. a. (Impair, consume by attrition, &c.) क्षि in caus.<BR>(क्षपयति, क्षययति -यितुं), क्षयं कृ, घृष् (c. 1. घर्षति -र्षितुं), घर्षणेन<BR>नश्.<BR>— (Carry on the body, as clothes, &c.) धृ (c. 10. धार-<BR>यति -यितुं, c. 1. धरति, धर्त्तुं), भृ (c. 3. बिभर्त्ति, c. 1. भरति, भर्त्तुं),<BR>धा (c. 3. धत्ते, धातुं), परिधा, आछद् (c. 10. -छादयति -यितुं), वस्<BR>(c. 2. वस्ते -सितुं); ‘he wears clothes,’ वासांसि बिभर्त्ति.<BR>— (Wear<BR>out by use, &c.) जीर्णं -र्णां कृ, जीर्णीकृ, जर्ज्जरीकृ, जर्ज्जरं -रां कृ.<BR>— (Wear out, consume by fatigue, &c.) सद् (c. 10. सादयति<BR>-यितुं), अवसद्, खिद् (c. 10. खेदयति -यितुं), ग्लै in caus. (ग्लपयति<BR>-यितुं), see To FATIGUE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wear
To WEAR, v. n. (Waste away) क्षि in pass. (क्षीयते), सद्, see To<BR>WASTE, v. n.<BR>— (Wear out by use) जॄ (c. 4. जीर्य्यति), परिजॄ,<BR>जीर्णः -र्णा -र्णं भू, जीर्णीभू, जर्ज्जरः -रा -रं भू, जर्ज्जरीभू.<BR>— (Wear off),<BR>see To PASS AWAY.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wear
WEAR, s. (Waste through use) क्षयः, परिक्षयः, अवक्षयः, उपभोगः,<BR>भोगः.<BR>— (Friction) घर्षणं, आघर्षणं.<BR>— (Dam in a river) सेतुः m.,<BR>जलप्रवाहबन्धः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wearer
WEARER, s. धारी m. (न्), धरः, वसिता m. (तृ), भृत् m.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wearied
WEARIED, p. p. श्रान्तः -न्ता -न्तं, क्लान्तः &c. See FATIGUED.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weariness
WEARINESS, s. श्रमः, श्रान्तिः f., क्लान्तिः f., खेदः. See FATIGUE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wearing
WEARING, part. or a. (Carrying) धारी -रिणी -रि (न्), धरः -रा<BR>-रं, उद्वहन् -हन्ती &c.<BR>— (Consuming) क्षयकारी &c.<BR>— (Fit to<BR>wear) परिधानोपयोगी -गिनी &c., परिधानयोग्यः -ग्या -ग्यं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wearisome
WEARISOME, a. श्रमजनकः -का -कं, खेदजनकः &c., आयासजनकः &c.,<BR>श्रान्तिकरः -री -रं, श्रमकरः &c., श्रमकारकः -का -कं, आयासजनकः<BR>&c., कष्टजनकः &c., कष्टप्रदः -दा -दं. See TEDIOUS.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weary
To WEARY, v. a. आयस् (c. 10. -यासयति -यितुं). See To FATIGUE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weary
To WEARY, v. n. खिद् (c. 4. खिद्यते), श्रम् (c. 4. श्राम्यति), आयस् (c. 4. -यस्यति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weary
WEARY, a. श्रान्तः -न्ता -न्तं, क्लान्तः &c., खिन्नः -न्ना -न्नं, ग्लानः -ना -नं,<BR>म्लानः &c., तन्द्रालुः -ला -लु, जातखेदः -दा -दं. See FATIGUED.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weasel
WEASEL, s. नकुलः, अङ्गूषः, बभ्रुः m., सूचिवदनः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weather
WEATHER, s. कालः, समयः, दिनं; ‘fine weather,’ सुदिनं, सुदिनाहः<BR>-हं, उत्तमाहः; ‘bad weather,’ दुर्दिनं, वार्दलं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weather
To WEATHER, v. a. दुःखेन पार् (c. 10. पारयति -यितुं) or तीर् (c. 10.<BR>तीरयति -यितुं), कष्टेन तीरं or पारं गम्, दुःखेन तॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weather-beaten
WEATHER-BEATEN, a. वाताहतः -ता -तं, वातवृष्ट्याहतः ता -तं, अभ्रावका-<BR>शिकः -का -कं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weather-cock
WEATHER-COCK, s. प्रासादशृङ्गाग्रे स्थापितं कुक्कुटाकारं वायुलक्षणं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weather-glass
WEATHER-GLASS. s. वायुमापकयन्त्रं, वायुगुरुत्वज्ञापकयन्त्रं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weather-proof
WEATHER-PROOF, a. वातवृष्ट्यभेद्यः -द्या -द्यं, वृष्ट्यभेद्यः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weather-wise
WEATHER-WISE, a. कालदर्शनकुशलः -ला -लं, कालविद् m. f. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weave
