WELL-WISHER, s. हितैषी -षिणी m. f., प्रियैषी -षिणी m. f., हितेप्सुः m. f.,<BR>हितप्रेप्सुः m. f., श्रेयोर्थी -र्थिनी, हितकामः -मा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

welter
To WELTER, v. n. लुठ् (c. 6. लुठति -ठितुं), प्रलुठ्. See To WALLOW.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

weltering
WELTERING, part. लुठन् -ठन्ती -ठत् (त्). See ROLLING, part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wen
WEN, s. मांसवृद्धिः f., मेदोर्बुदं, गलगण्डः. See TUMOUR.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wench
WENCH, s. जोषा, योषिता, तरुणी, कन्या, बन्धकी, गणिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wench
To WENCH, WENCHING. See To FORNICATE, FORNICATION.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wend
To WEND, v. n. गम्, या, इ, सृ, आवृत्, अभिवृत्, see To GO; ‘hither<BR>he wends his way,’ इत एवाभिवर्त्तते.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

west
WEST, s. (The quarter of the sky) पश्चिमा, पश्चिमदिशा, पश्चि-<BR>मदिक् f. (श्), पश्चिमाशा, प्रतीची, अपरा, चरमा, वारुणी, मध्यः -ध्यं.<BR>The god Varuna is fabled as the Regent of the West.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

west
WEST, WESTERLY, WESTERN, a. पश्चिमः -मा -मं, प्रत्यङ् -तीची -त्यक्<BR>(ञ्च्), प्रतीच्यः -च्या -च्यं, प्रतीचीनः -ना -नं, चरमः -मा -मं, अपरः -रा<BR>-रं, पाश्चात्यः -त्या -त्यं. ‘Madyadesha is west of Prayāga,’<BR>मध्यदेशः प्रयागात् पश्चिमः; ‘as far as the western ocean,’ आप-<BR>श्चिमसमुद्रात्.<BR>— (Facing the west) प्रत्यङ्मुखः -खी -खं, पश्चिमाभि-<BR>मुखः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

westward
WESTWARD, adv. पश्चात्, प्रत्यक्, पश्चिमदिशि, पश्चिमतस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wet
WET, a. आर्द्रः -र्द्रा -र्द्रं, जलार्द्रः &c., क्लिन्नः -न्ना -न्नं, सिक्तः -क्ता -क्तं,<BR>जलसिक्तः &c., समुक्षितः -ता -तं, अनूपः -पा -पं. See MOIST.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wet
WET, s. आर्द्रता, क्लेदः -दं, तेमः, स्तेमः, जलं. See MOISTURE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wet
To WET, v. a. क्लिद् (c. 10. क्लेदयति -यितुं). See To MOISTEN.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wether
WETHER, s. छिन्नवृषणो मेषः, मुष्कशून्यो मेषः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wetness
WETNESS, s. आर्द्रता, क्लिन्नता, जलार्द्रता, सिक्तता -त्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wet-nurse
WET-NURSE, s. धात्रेयी, उपमाता, उपमात्री, पयःप्रस्रविणी, स्तन्यदानेन<BR>पोषयित्री or पालयित्री.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whack
To WHACK, WHACK. See To STRIKE, BEAT, BLOW.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whale
WHALE, s. तिमिः m., तिमिङ्गिलः, तिमिङ्गिलगिलः, मीनरः, समुद्रारुः m.,<BR>मकरः, राघवः, वृहन्मीनः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wharf
WHARF, s. घठ्ठः, उमः, तरस्थानं, तरणस्थानं, गुल्मः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

what
WHAT, pron. rel. (That which) यद्.<BR>— (What kind, what like,<BR>which) यादृशः -शी -शं, यादृक्षः -क्षा -क्षं, यः या यद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

what
WHAT, pron. inter. कः का किं, कौ m. du., के f. n. du., के m. pl., काः f. pl.,<BR>कानि n. pl.; ‘what?’ किं, किन्नु, किमुत, किंस्वित्; ‘what kind?’<BR>कीदृशः -शी -शं, कीदृक्षः -क्षा -क्षं, कीदृक् m. f. n. (श्), किम्भूतः<BR>-ता -तं; ‘on what account?’ किमर्थं; ‘what then?’ किं तर्हि,<BR>किमु; ‘what else?’ अथ किं; ‘what do you wish to say?’<BR>किम् असि वक्तुकामः; ‘what is he doing?’ किंव्यापारः सः; ‘what<BR>is his name?’ किन्नामधेयः सः; ‘to what degree?’ किम्पर्य्यन्तं;<BR>‘what is that to me?’ किं मम तेन; ‘what though?’ यद्यपि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

what
WHAT, interj. कथं, किं, किमुत, उत, उत्, ननु, स्वित्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whatever
WHATEVER, WHATSOEVER, pron. यत्किञ्चित्, यद्यद्, यद्, यावत्; ‘what-<BR>ever wealth is in the world,’ यत्किञ्चिद् or यावद् जगद्वर्त्ति धनम् अस्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wheat
WHEAT, s. गोधूमः, सुमनाः m. (स्), सुमनः, धान्यं, प्रवटः, रसालः, अपूपः,<BR>गन्धविह्वलः, भूजम्बूः f., गोरक्षजम्बूः f., शितसूकः, म्लेच्छभोजनः, सितशि-<BR>म्बिकः, निस्तुषक्षीरः, बहुदुग्धः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wheaten
WHEATEN, a. गोधूममयः -यी -यं, गोधूमात्मकः -का -कं, गोधूम in comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wheedle
To WHEEDLE, WHEEDLER, WHEEDLING. See To COAX, FLATTER, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wheel
WHEEL, s. चक्रं, रथाङ्गं, रथपादः, रथ्यं, मण्डलं, उपधिः m., औपधेयं,<BR>नभिः m., दृम्भूः f.; ‘its circumference,’ नेमिः -मी, प्रधिः m.,<BR>चक्रपरिधिः m.; ‘potter's wheel,’ कुलालचक्रं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wheel
To WHEEL, v. a. परिवृत् (c. 10. -वर्त्तयति -यितुं), विवृत्, आवृत्, व्यावृत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wheel
To WHEEL, v. n. परिवृत् (c. 1. -वर्त्तते -र्त्तितुं), विवृत्, व्यावृत्, सम्परिवृत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wheelbarrow
WHEELBARROW, s. हस्तसञ्चालितम् एकचक्रयुक्तं वाहनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wheeled
WHEELED, a. चक्रवान् -वती -वत् (त्), चक्री -क्रिणी -क्रि (न्), चक्रयुक्तः<BR>-क्ता -क्तं; ‘two-wheeled carriage,’ द्विचक्रयुक्तो रथः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wheel-wright
WHEEL-WRIGHT, s. रथकारः, रथकृत्, रथकरः, चक्रकारः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wheeze
To WHEEZE, v. n. कासश्वासं कृ, कृच्छ्रेण श्वासं कृ, प्रतिक्षुतं कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whelp
WHELP, s. शावः -वकः, शिशुः m., वत्सः; ‘of a lion,’ सिंहशावकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

when
WHEN, adv. (At the time that) यदा, यर्हि, or expressed by<BR>काले, समये, &c. in comp.; as, ‘when he was dying,’<BR>मरणकाले.<BR>— (At what time?) कदा, कर्हि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whence
WHENCE, adv. (Interrog.) कुतस्, कस्माद् देशात् &c., कस्मात् स्था-<BR>नात् &c.; ‘whence have you come?’ कुतः समागतोऽसि.<BR>—<BR>(Indef.) यतस्, यस्माद् देशात् &c.; ‘to return whence one<BR>came,’ प्रतिगन्तुं यथागतं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whenever
WHENEVER, WHENSOEVER, adv. यदा यदा, यर्हि यर्हि, यदाकदाचित्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

where
WHERE, adv. (In which place) यत्र.<BR>— (In what place?) कुत्र, क्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whereas
WHEREAS, adv. यस्मात्, येन, यतस्। यत्. See SINCE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whereby
WHEREBY, adv. (By which) येन.<BR>— (By what?) केन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wherefore
WHEREFORE, adv. (For which reason) यतस्, येन, यत्, यदर्थं, तथात्वे.<BR>— (For what reason?) किमर्थं, किम्, केन हेतुना, कस्य हेतोः,<BR>किन्निमित्तं, केन निमित्तेन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wherein
WHEREIN, adv. (In which) यस्मिन्, यत्र.<BR>— (In what?) कस्मिन्, कुत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whereof
WHEREOF, adv. (Of which) यस्य.<BR>— (Of what?) कस्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wherever
WHEREVER, WHERESOEVER, adv. यत्र कुत्रिचित्, यत्र कुत्रापि, यत्र यत्र,<BR>कुत्रापि, कुत्रचित्, यत्र क्वचित्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whereupon
WHEREUPON, adv. यदनन्तरं, यत्रान्तरे, तदनन्तरं, अत्रान्तरे.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wherry
WHERRY, s. दण्डसञ्चालिता or क्षेपणिसञ्चालिता लघुनौका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whet
To WHET, v. a. निशो, निशि, क्ष्णु, तिज्. See To SHARPEN.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whether
WHETHER, adv. किं, किंवा, वा, उत. The particle वा, either<BR>with or without किं, usually expresses the sense of<BR>‘whether,’ as in the following examples; ‘whether you<BR>kill me or whether you release me,’ मां मारयत वा मुञ्चत वा;<BR>‘do you know whether he is virtuous or not?’ वेत्सि किं<BR>धार्म्मिको न वा; ‘whether or not he does that,’ तत् करोतु न<BR>करोतु वा.<BR>— (Whether of twain, which of two) कतरः -रा -रत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whet-stone
WHET-STONE, s. शाणः -णी, शानः, शाणाश्म n. (न्), भ्रमः, झामरः,<BR>वागरः, सामकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whey
WHEY, s. मस्तु n., दधिमण्डः -ण्डं, दुग्धमण्डं, दध्युत्तरं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

which
WHICH, pron. (Relat.) यः या, यद्, यौ m. du., ये f. n. du., ये m. pl.,<BR>याः f. pl., यानि n. pl., see WHO.<BR>— (Interrog.) कः का किं,<BR>कौ m. du., के f. n. du., के m. pl., काः f. pl., कानि n. pl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whichever
WHICHEVER, pron. Expressed by doubling the relative, thus<BR>यद् यद् &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whiff
WHIFF, s. फुत्कृतं, फुत्कारः, फूत्कृतं, फूत् indec. See PUFF.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

while
WHILE, WHILST, adv. यावत्, यावत्कालं, यत्कालं, यस्मिन् काले, यत्पर्य्यन्तं,<BR>यदा; ‘whilst he thought on this the messenger arrived,’<BR>यावत् तच् चिन्तयति दूतः समागच्छति. The sense of whilst<BR>may sometimes be expressed by मध्ये, see DURING, or by<BR>the locative absolute, or some similar form of expression;<BR>as, स तदेव चिन्तयति दूतश्च समागच्छति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

while
WHILE, s. कालः, समयः; ‘a long while,’ बहुकालः; ‘for a long<BR>while,’ बहुकालं, चिरकालं, चिरं; ‘after a long while,’ चिरात्;<BR>‘a little while,’ अल्पकालः; ‘for a little while,’ अल्पकालं,<BR>किञ्चित्कालं; ‘in a little while,’ अचिरेण -रात्, क्षणान्तरे, कियता<BR>कालेन; ‘for a while,’ कियत्कालं, आपाततस्; ‘a long while<BR>ago,’ पुरा, पूर्व्वकाले; ‘one while,’ कदाचित्.<BR>— (Worth while)<BR>सफलः -ला -लं, फलवान् -वती -वत् (त्), उपयोगी -गिनी &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

while
To WHILE, v. a. विनोदेन कालं गम् (c. 10. गमयति -यितुं) or नी<BR>(c. 1. नयति, नेतुं), विनुद् in caus. (नोदयति -यितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whim
WHIM, s. मनोलौल्यं, चापलं, चापल्यं. See FREAK, CAPRICE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whimper
To WHIMPER, v. a. बालकवत् क्रन्द् or रुद् or रु or कूज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whimsical
WHIMSICAL, a. चपलः -ला -लं, लोलः &c., see CAPRICIOUS, FREAKISH.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whine
To WHINE, v. n. कूज् (c. 1. कूजति -जितुं), अनुकूज्. See To MURMUR.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whine
WHINE, s. कूजनं, कूजितं, विलपनं, कलरुतं, काकुः f., काकूक्तिः f.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whip
To WHIP, v. a. कषया or चर्म्मरज्वा or रज्वा तड् (c. 10. ताडयति -यितुं)<BR>or दण्ड् or शास् (c. 2. शास्ति -सितुं). See To LASH.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whip
WHIP, s. कशा, कषा, चर्म्मयष्टिः f., प्रतिष्कषः, भीमा. See SCOURGE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whipped
WHIPPED, p. p. कशाहतः -ता -तं, दण्डितः &c.; ‘whipped horse,’<BR>प्रतिकशाश्वः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whipping
WHIPPING, s. कशाघातः, कपाघातः, कशाताडनं, ताडनं; ‘worthy of<BR>it,’ कश्यः -श्या -श्यं, कशार्हः -र्हा -र्हं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whirl
To WHIRL, v. a. भ्रम् (c. 10. भ्रमयति -यितुं). See To TURN, TWIRL.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whirl
To WHIRL, v. n. भ्रम् (c. 4. भ्राम्यति, c. 1, भ्रमति -मितुं), अतिशीघ्रं परि-<BR>वृत् (c. 1. -वर्त्तते -र्त्तितुं) or घूर्ण्. See To REVOLVE, v. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whirled
WHIRLED, p. p. भ्रान्तः -न्ता -न्तं, उद्भ्रान्तः &c., शीघ्रं परिवर्त्तितः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whirl
WHIRL, WHIRLING, s. भ्रमः -मणं, भ्रान्तिः f., भ्रमिः f., विभ्रमः, आवृत्तिः f.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whirlpool
WHIRLPOOL, s. जलावर्त्तः, जलभ्रमः, जलगुल्मः, आवर्त्तः -र्त्तका, आवर्त्तिनी,<BR>भृमिः m., भ्रमः, भ्रमरकः, अवघूर्णः. See EDDY.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whirlwind
WHIRLWIND, s. चक्रवातः, वातावर्त्तः, वातमण्डली, वायुगुल्मः, वात्या,<BR>भृमिः m., वातभ्रमः, आवर्त्तः, निर्घातः, ध्राजिः f., कुनाभिः m., पवाका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whisk
To WHISK, v. a. अतिक्षिप्रं चल् (c. 10. चालयति -यितुं), अतिलाघवेन<BR>चल्; ‘he whisks his tail,’ परिपुच्छयति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whisk
WHISK, s. लघुक्षेपः, आकस्मिकक्षेपः.<BR>— (For flies, &c.) चामरं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whisker
WHISKER, s. पक्ष्म n. (न्), गुम्फः, गण्डलोम n. (न्), मुखजलोम n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whisper
To WHISPER, v. n. जप् (c. 1. जपति -पितुं), प्रजप्, नीचस्वरेण or नीच-<BR>वाचा वद् (c. 1. वदति -दितुं), नीचैर् वद्, उपांशु वद्; ‘to whisper<BR>into the ear,’ कर्णम् उपजप्, कर्णे कथ्, कर्णे जप् or वद्; ‘to<BR>whisper to one's neighbour,’ जनान्तिकं वद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whisper
WHISPER, WHISPERING, s. जपः -पनं, जापः, कर्णेजपनं, कर्णेकथनं,<BR>कर्णेवादः, उपांशुवादः, उपांशुकथनं, नीचैर्वादः; ‘in a whisper,’<BR>उपांशु, जनान्तिकं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whisperer
WHISPERER, s. कर्णेजपः, कर्णजपः, कर्णेकथकः, कर्णोपजापकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whistle
To WHISTLE, v. n. ओष्ठाधरसङ्कोचपूर्व्वं श्वासोत्क्षेपं कृत्वा शीश्शब्दं कृ or<BR>सीस्शब्दं कृ or कीचकवत् पटुशब्दंकृ, वेणुवत् कर्कशशब्दं कृ, ओष्ठशब्दं कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whistle
WHISTLE, s. (The sound) शीश्शब्दः, सीस्शब्दः, ओष्ठशब्दः, कीचक-<BR>शब्दः.<BR>— (Instrument for whistling) वंशः -शी, ध्वनिनालः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whit
WHIT, s. लेशः, लवः, लवलेशः; ‘not a whit,’ न मनागपि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

white
WHITE, a. शुक्लः -क्ला -क्लं, श्वेतः -ता -तं, धवलः -ला -लं, सितः -ता -तं,<BR>श्येतः -ता -नी -तं, शुभ्रः -भ्रा -भ्रं, शुचिः -चिः -चि, अवदातः -ता -तं,<BR>विशदः -दा -दं, गौरः -री -रं, धौतः -ता -तं, पाण्डुरः -रा -रं, अमलः<BR>-ला -लं, विमलः &c., रजतः -ता -तं, कर्कः -र्का -र्कं, खरुः -रुः -रु,<BR>अर्जुनः -नी -नं, शितिः -ती -ति, अर्जुनछविः -विः -वि, वलक्षः -क्षा<BR>-क्षं; ‘yellowish white,’ हरिणः -णा -णं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

white
WHITE, s. (The colour) शुक्लः, धवलः, श्वेतः, सितः, वलक्षः.<BR>— (Of<BR>the eye) शुक्लमण्डलं, विञ्जमरं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whiten
To WHITEN, v. a. शुक्ल (nom. शुक्लयति -यितुं), धवल (nom. धवलयति<BR>-यितुं), शुक्लीकृ, धवलीकृ, आदीप् (c. 10. -दीपयति -यितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whiten
To WHITEN, v. n. शुक्लीभू, धवलीभू, श्वेतीभू, विशदीभू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whitened
WHITENED, p. p. धवलितः -ता -तं, धवलीकृतः &c., शुक्लीकृतः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whiteness
WHITENESS, s. शुक्लता -त्वं, शुक्लिमा m. (न्), शौक्ल्यं, धवलत्वं -ता, धावल्यं,<BR>शुभ्रता, श्वेतता, सितत्वं, सितिमा m. (न्), वैशद्यं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whites
WHITES, s. (Fluor albus) प्रदरः, प्रदरामयः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whitewash
WHITEWASH, s. सुधा, शुक्ललेपः, धवललेपः, धवलसुधा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whitewash
To WHITEWASH, v. a. सुधया लिप् (c. 6. लिम्पति, लेप्तुं) or आलिप्,<BR>सुधया धवलीकृ or धवल (nom. धवलयति -यितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whitewashed
WHITEWASHED, p. p. सुधाधवलितः -ता -तं, सुधालिप्तः &c.; ‘house,’<BR>सुधाभवनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whither
WHITHER, adv. (Interrog.) कुत्र, क्व; ‘whither shall I go?’ क्व<BR>गच्छामि.<BR>— (Relat.) यत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whithersoever
WHITHERSOEVER, adv. यत्र कुत्रचित्, यत्र कुत्रापि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whitish
WHITISH, a. ईषच्छुक्लः -क्ला -क्लं, ईषत्पाण्डुः -ण्डुः -ण्डु, धूसरः -रा -रं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whitlow
WHITLOW, s. नखम्पचः, चिप्यं, कुणिः m., नखशूलः -लं, नखव्रणः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whiz
To WHIZ, v. n. शीश्शब्दं कृ, सीस्शब्दं कृ, रणरणशब्दं कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

who
WHO, pron. (Relat.) यः या यद्, यौ m. du., ये f. n. du., ये m. pl.,<BR>यः f. pl., यानि n. pl. The relative pronoun is not much<BR>used in Sanskrit excepting at the beginning of a sentence;<BR>as, ‘he who desires great riches is not wise,’ यो बहुधनम्<BR>आकांक्षति स बुद्धिहीनः. In other cases it is more usually<BR>expressed by स च or is inherent in a compound word or<BR>indecl. part.; thus, ‘in that city there dwelt a king who<BR>was beloved by his subjects,’ तस्मिन् नगरे वसति राजा स च<BR>प्रजावल्लभः; ‘a saint who has subdued his organs of sense,’<BR>जितेन्द्रियो मुनिः; ‘by all the birds who had assembled,’ सर्व्वैः<BR>पक्षिभिर् मिलित्वा.<BR>— (Interrog.) कः का किं, कौ m. du., के f. n. du.,<BR>के m. pl., काः f. pl., कानि n. pl.; ‘who are you?’ कस् त्वं;<BR>‘who's there,’ कोऽत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whoever
WHOEVER, WHOSOEVER, WHOSO, pron. यः कश्चित् m., या काचित् f.,<BR>यत्किञ्चत् n., यः कोपि m., या कापि f., यत्किमपि m., यो यः m., या<BR>या f., यद्यद् n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whole
WHOLE, a. सर्व्वः -र्व्वा -र्व्वं, सकलः -ला -लं, समग्रः -ग्रा -ग्रं, विश्वः -श्वा<BR>-श्वं, कृत्स्नः -त्स्ना -त्स्नं; ‘the whole earth,’ सर्व्वमही; ‘the whole<BR>world,’ सर्व्वलोकः; ‘the whole night,’ सर्व्वरात्रः; ‘the whole<BR>day,’ सर्व्वाह्लः; ‘the whole business from beginning to end,’<BR>साद्यन्तं कर्म्म, आगमनिर्गमौ m. du.; ‘for the whole month,’<BR>मासपर्य्यन्तं; ‘whole number,’ अभिन्नसंख्या.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whole
WHOLE, s. साकल्यं, समुदायः, कार्त्स्न्यं, कार्त्स्नं, सामग्र्यं, आखिल्यं, मात्रं,<BR>समासः, समस्तः -स्तिः f., व्यस्तिः f.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wholeness
WHOLENESS, s. सामग्र्यं, सम्पूर्णता, अभिन्नता. See ENTIRENESS.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wholesale
WHOLESALE, s. or a. समस्तविक्रयः, महाविक्रयः, अखण्डविक्रयः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wholesome
WHOLESOME, a. पथ्यः -थ्या -थ्यं, हितः -ता -तं. See SALUBRIOUS.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wholly
WHOLLY, adv. सर्व्वतस्, सर्व्वशस्, सर्व्वथा, साकल्येन, सम्यक्, अशेषतस्,<BR>अत्यन्तं, सर्व्वभावेन, सर्व्वतोभावेन. See ENTIRELY.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whoop
WHOOP, s. (The cry) हूप्; ‘war-whoop,’ सिंहनादः, क्ष्वेडा -डितं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whoop
To WHOOP, v. n. हूप्शब्दं कृ, उच्चैःस्वरेण क्रुश्. See To SHOUT.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whore
WHORE, s. वेश्या, गणिका, पुंश्चली, बन्धकी. See HARLOT.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whoredom
WHOREDOM, WHOREMONGER. See FORNICATION, HARLOTRY, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whoreson
WHORESON, s. वेश्यापुत्रः, गणिकापुत्रः, पुंश्चलीजः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

whose
WHOSE, pron. (Relat.) यस्य m., यस्याः f. The relative ‘whose’<BR>is not often expressed in Sanskrit, but is frequently in-<BR>herent in a compound, or rendered by तस्य च &c., see WHO;<BR>as, ‘a wife whose husband is abroad,’ प्रोषितभर्त्तृका स्त्री.<BR>—<BR>(Interrog.) कस्य m., कस्याः f.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

why
WHY, adv. किमर्थं, किं, केन हेतुना, किन्निमित्तं, कस्य हेतोः, see WHERE-<BR>FORE; ‘why inquire into my story?’ किं ते मम वृत्तान्तप्रश्नेन;<BR>‘why conceal it?’ संवरणे किं कारणं; ‘why do you do this?’<BR>किमर्थं तत् करोषि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wick
WICK, s. (Of a lamp, &c.) तूला -ली, वर्त्तिः f., वर्त्तिका, तैलिनी,<BR>तैलमाली, दशा, दशाकर्पः, पिञ्जूलं, दीपकूपी, दीपखोरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wicked
WICKED, a. (Said of persons) दुष्टः -ष्टा -ष्टं, पापी -पिनी -पि (न्),<BR>दुर्वृत्तः -त्ता -त्तं, दुरात्मा -त्मा -त्म (न्), पापात्मा &c., अपुण्यः -ण्या<BR>-ण्यं, शठः -ठा -ठं, पामरः -रा -रं, खलः -ला -लं, नैकृतिकः -की -कं,<BR>नैष्कृतिकः &c., अधार्म्मिकः -की -कं, दुष्टमानसः -सा -सं, दुश्चरित्रः<BR>-त्रा -त्रं, विकर्म्मिकः &c., see SINFUL; ‘a wicked man,’ दुर्जनः,<BR>असज्जनः.<BR>— (Of actions) दुष्टः -ष्टा -ष्टं, पाप in comp., see SINFUL;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=841-a" target="_blank">Page841-a+ 51</a>]<BR>‘a wicked act,’ पापकर्म्म n. (न्); ‘very wicked,’ पापिष्ठः -ष्ठा<BR>-ष्ठं, दुरिष्ठः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=840-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wickedly
WICKEDLY, adv. दुष्टं, दुष्टवत्, सपापं, दुर्जनवत्, दुर्वृत्तवत्, खलवत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wickedness
WICKEDNESS, s. पापं, दुष्कृतं, दुष्कृतिः f., कुकर्म्म n. (न्), दुष्कर्म्म n.,<BR>कुकृत्यं, कुसृतिः f., निकृतिः f., निकारः, दुष्टता, दौष्ठवं, दौरात्म्यं,<BR>दौर्जन्यं, दुर्जनत्वं, असाधुता, विप्रकारः, कौकृत्यं, असत्कर्म्म n., see SIN-<BR>FULNESS; ‘great wickedness,’ पापिष्ठता, पापीयस्त्वं, दुरिष्ठं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wicker
WICKER, a. वैदलः -ली -लं, वैणवः -वी -वं, वैणुकेयः -यी -यं, वैत्रकः<BR>-की -कं, वंशादिदलनिर्म्मितः -ता -तं; ‘wicker-work,’ वैदलं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wicket
WICKET, s. क्षुद्रद्वारं, उपद्वारं, द्वारकं, खडक्किका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wide
WIDE, a. विशालः -ला -लं, पृथुः -थुः -थु, विस्तीर्णः -र्णा -र्णं, विपुलः<BR>-ला -लं, विप्रकृष्टः -ष्टा -ष्टं; ‘wide-spread,’ बहुविस्तीर्णः -र्णा -र्णं,<BR>सन्ततः -ता -तं, बहुप्रतानी &c.; ‘wide-awake,’ प्रबुद्धः -द्धा -द्धं;<BR>‘wide-mouthed,’ गुहामुखः -खा -खं; ‘wide-open,’ उत्फुल्लः -ल्ला -ल्लं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wide
WIDE, WIDELY, adv. विस्तीर्णं, विस्तरेण, विपुलं, प्रचुरं, अत्यन्तं, बहु or<BR>अति or सु prefixed, see EXTENSIVELY.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

widen
To WIDEN, v. a. प्रथ् (c. 10. प्रथयति -यितुं), पृथूकृ, विशालीकृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wideness
WIDENESS, s. विशालता, पृथुता, विस्तृतिः f. See BROADNESS.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

widow
WIDOW, s. विधवा, रण्डा, विश्वस्ता, विश्वस्था, गतभर्त्तृका, मृतपतिका,<BR>अभर्त्तृका, निर्नाथा, अनाथा, अवीरा, यतिनी, वृपभी, कात्यायनी,<BR>वितन्तुः f.; ‘widow before puberty,’ वालविधवा, बालरण्डा;<BR>‘widow that burns with the body of her husband,’ सती;<BR>‘the act of doing so,’ अग्निप्रवेशः, सहमरणं, सहगमनं, अनुगमनं,<BR>अन्वारोहणं; ‘stone by which she ascends the pyre,’ धर्म्मशिला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

widowed
WIDOWED, a. हृतभर्त्तृका, हृतपतिका.<BR>— (Stripped) हृतः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

widower
WIDOWER, s. मृतभार्य्यः, मृतपत्नीकः, विधुरः, अयोगः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

widowhood
WIDOWHOOD, s. वैधव्यं, वैधव्यदशा, विधवात्वं, निर्नाथता, रण्डावस्था, छत्रभङ्गः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

width
WIDTH, s. विशालता, परिणाहः, व्यासः, परिसरः. See BREADTH.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wield
To WIELD, v. a. हस्तेन धृ (c. 1. धरति, c. 10. धारयति -यितुं) or धा<BR>(c. 3. दधाति, धातुं) or विधा, हस्तेन भृ (c. 1. भरति, c. 3. बिभर्त्ति,<BR>भर्त्तुं), हस्तेन प्रयुज् or उपयुज् or प्रणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wife
WIFE, s. भार्य्या, स्त्री, पत्नी, जाया, दाराः m. pl., दारा, वधूः f., बधूः f.,<BR>कलत्रं, गृहिणी, गेहिनी, पाणिगृहीता, सहधर्म्मिणी, सधर्म्मिणी, दयिता,<BR>कान्ता, वल्लभा, प्रिया, प्रियतमा, रमणी, नायिका, प्राणेशा, प्राणसमा,<BR>प्रेयसी, प्रेष्ठा, वनिता, द्वितीया, महिला, क्षेत्रं, परिग्रहः, गृहं, गृहाः m. pl.,<BR>धूता, अर्द्धाङ्गं, वामाङ्गं, दम् indec.; ‘virtuous and faithful wife,’<BR>पतिव्रता, सती, साध्वी, सुव्रता, धर्म्मदाराः m. pl., पतिप्राणा, सुचरित्रा;<BR>‘one who has a family,’ कुटुम्बिनी, पुरन्ध्रिः -न्ध्री; ‘a super-<BR>seded wife,’ अध्यूढा, अधिविन्ना, कृतसापत्निका -त्नीका, कृतसापत्नी,<BR>कृतसापत्नका, कृतसपत्निका; ‘wife of one husband,’ एकभर्त्तृका;<BR>‘rival wife,’ सपत्नी; ‘one's own wife,’ स्वकीया, स्वीया; ‘wife<BR>of another,’ परकीया, परस्त्री, परदाराः m. pl.; ‘well-born<BR>wife,’ कुलस्त्री; ‘wife of one's bosom,’ वक्षःसम्मर्दिनी; ‘un-<BR>faithful wife,’ अपतिव्रता, असती; ‘taking a wife,’ दारपरिग्रहः,<BR>दारसंग्रहः, दारक्रिया; ‘along with one's wife, or having a<BR>wife,’ सवधूकः, सपत्नीकः, सभार्य्यः; ‘condition of a wife,’<BR>भार्य्यात्वं, पत्नीत्वं; ‘one whose husband is abroad,’ प्रोषितभर्त्तृका;<BR>‘wife's property,’ स्त्रीधनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wig
WIG, s. उपकेशः, कृत्रिमकेशः, केशमयमस्तकाभरणं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wight
WIGHT, s. जनः, माणवकः, नागरः; ‘unlucky wight,’ तपस्वी m. (न्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wild
WILD, a. (Pertaining to or inhabiting a forest or wilderness,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=841-b" target="_blank">Page841-b+ 51</a>]<BR>not tame) आरण्यः -ण्यी -ण्यं, आरण्यकः -का -कं, वन्यः -न्या -न्यं,<BR>अरण्यजः -जा -जं, वनजः &c., आरणीयः -या -यं, जङ्गलः -ला -लं,<BR>जाङ्गलः -ली -लं, वनेचरः -रा -रं, वनचारी -रिणी -रि (न्), वन in<BR>comp., अरण्य in comp., see DESERT, a.; ‘wild-animal, wild-<BR>beast,’ अरण्यपशुः m., वनपशुः m., आरण्यपशुः m.; ‘wild hog,’<BR>अरण्यशूकरः, आरण्यशूकरः, वनशूकरः; ‘wild goat,’ वनछागः; ‘wild<BR>elephant,’ वनगजः; ‘wild fowl,’ वनकुक्कुटः, वृक्षकुक्कुटः, रज्जुदा-<BR>लकः; ‘wild duck,’ कामिकः; ‘wild stag,’ अरण्यमृगः, व्यालमृगः.<BR>— (Growing without culture) अरण्य in comp., वन in comp.;<BR>‘wild flower,’ वनपुष्पं; ‘wild fruit,’ वनफलं; ‘wild rice,’<BR>अरण्यधान्यं, तृणधान्यं, नीहारः.<BR>— (Irregular, disorderly) विषमः<BR>-मा -मं, उच्छृङ्खलः -ला -लं, प्रकीर्णः -र्णा -र्णं, see IRREGULAR.<BR>—<BR>(Absurd) अयुक्तिकः -का -कं, अनर्थकः -का -कं.<BR>— (Mad) उन्मत्तः<BR>-त्ता -त्तं.<BR>— (Savage, desert), see the words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=841-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wilderness
WILDERNESS, WILD, s. अरण्यं, वनं, जङ्गलं, शून्यारण्यं, मरुदेशः, मरुस्थलं,<BR>मरुः m., जाङ्गलभूमिः f., प्रान्तरं. See DESERT, s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wild-goose-chase
WILD-GOOSE-CHASE, s. मृगतृष्णा, हेममृगानुगमनं, हेममृगानुधावनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wildly
WILDLY, adv. विषमं, उच्छृङ्खलं, उन्मत्तवत्, सोन्मादं, व्याकुलं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wildness
WILDNESS, s. (Uncultivated state) वन्यता, आरण्यता, जङ्गलत्वं.-<BR>(Savageness) रौद्रता, दारुणता, अशिष्टता.<BR>— (Irregularity) विष-<BR>मता, उच्छृङ्खलता.<BR>— (Madness) उन्मत्तता, विक्षिप्तता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wile
WILE, s. माया, छलं, छद्म n. (न्), कपटः -टं, उपायः, व्यपदेशः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wilful
WILFUL, a. स्वैरी -रिणी -रि (न्). See WILLFUL.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

will
WILL, s. (Faculty which is exercised in deciding) इच्छा, सङ्कल्प-<BR>शक्तिः f., निश्चयशक्तिः f.<BR>— (Inclination, choice, liking) इच्छा,<BR>सङ्कल्पः, वशः -शं, अभिप्रायः, अभिलाषः, आकांक्षा, अभिप्रेतं, अभिमतं,<BR>इष्टं, छन्दस् n.; ‘the will of God,’ परमेश्वरेच्छा; ‘of one's own<BR>will, at will,’ इच्छातस्, स्वेच्छातस्, स्वेच्छानुसारेण, यथाकामं, कामतस्;<BR>‘ill-will,’ दुष्टभावः, दुष्टबुद्धिः f.; ‘good will,’ हितेच्छा, हितकाम्या;<BR>‘subject to the will of another,’ परवशः -शा -शं; ‘following<BR>one's own will,’ स्वेच्छाचारी -रिणी -रि (न्), see WILFUL;<BR>‘against the will of,’ अनिच्छया, अनिच्छातस्, अनभिप्रेतेन.<BR>—<BR>(Testament) मृतपत्रं, मृत्युपत्रं, मृतलेखः, मृत्युलेखः.<BR>— (Will-with-a<BR>wisp), see IGNIS FATUUS.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

will
To WILL, v. a. (Determine, decide in the mind) सङ्कल्पं कृ, नि-<BR>श्चयं कृ, निश्चि, निर्णी, संकॢप् (c. 10. -कल्पयति -यितुं), मनसा निश्चि<BR>or निर्णयं कृ.<BR>— (Wish, desire) इष् (c. 6. इच्छति, एषितुं), अभिलष्,<BR>आकांक्ष्.<BR>— (Command), see To COMMAND.<BR>— (Dispose of by<BR>testament) मृतपत्रेण दा or प्रदा or ऋ in caus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

willed
WILLED, p. p. सङ्कल्पितः -ता -तं, साङ्कल्पिकः -की -कं, इष्टः -ष्टा -ष्टं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

willful
WILLFUL, a. स्वैरी -रिणी -रि (न्), यथेष्टचारी &c., यथाकामी &c., स्वैरः<BR>-री -रं, स्वैरवृत्तः -त्ता -त्तं, स्वैरगतिः -तिः -ति, स्वैरगामी -मिनी &c.,<BR>यादृच्छिकः -की -कं, छान्दसः -सी -सं. See SELF-WILLED.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wilfully
WILFULLY, adv. यथाकामं, यथेष्टं, स्वैरवत्, यदृच्छया, इच्छातस्, कामं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wilfulness
WILFULNESS, s. स्वैरिता, स्वैरता, स्वैरं, स्वेच्छा, स्वेच्छाचारः, यथेष्टचारः,<BR>स्वातन्त्र्यं, स्वतन्त्रता, यदृच्छा, प्राकाम्यं. See SELF-WILL.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=841-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

