WINNOWED, p. p. पूतः -ता -तं, परिपूतः &c., बहुलीकृतः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=842-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

winnower
WINNOWER, s. पावकः, निष्पावकः, प्रस्फोटनकारी m. (न्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=842-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

winnowing
WINNOWING, s. निष्पावः, पवनं, पवः, प्रस्फोटनं, बहुलीकरणं, उत्कारः,<BR>निकारः; ‘winnowing-fan or basket,’ सूर्प्पः -र्प्पं, शूर्प्पः -र्प्पं, प्रस्फोटनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=842-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

winter
WINTER, s. हेमन्तः -न्तं, हैमन्तं, हेमन्तकालः, हिमकालः, शीतकालः,<BR>शिशिरः -रं, हिमर्त्तुः m., शीतर्त्तुः, हिमागमः, हैमलं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=842-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

winter
To WINTER, v. n. हेमन्तकालं गम् (c. 10. गमयति -यितुं) or नी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=842-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wintery
WINTERY, a. हैमन्तः -न्ती -न्तं, हैमन्तिकः -की -कं, हैमः -मी -मं, हैमनः<BR>-नी -नं, हिमकालसम्बन्धी &c.; ‘weather,’ हिमदुर्दिनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=842-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wipe
To WIPE, v. a. मृज् (c. 2. मार्ष्टि -र्ष्टुं, c. 1. मार्जति -र्जितुं), प्रमृज्, आमृज्,<BR>परिमृज्, सम्मृज्, प्रक्षल् (c. 10. -क्षालयति -यितुं), मृद्, see To RUB;<BR>‘the mouth,’ मुखं प्रमृज्; ‘the eyes,’ नेत्रे परिमृज्; ‘tears from<BR>the eyes,’ नेत्राभ्याम् अश्रूणि प्रमृज्.<BR>— (Wipe away, wipe off)<BR>अपमृज्, अवमृज्, निःक्षिप्; ‘dirt or defilement,’ मलम् अपमृज्,<BR>निर्लेपं कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=842-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wipe
WIPE, s. मार्जः -र्जनं, प्रक्षालनं.<BR>— (Blow) प्रहारः, आघातः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=842-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wiped
WIPED, p. p. मार्जितः -ता -तं, प्रमार्जितः &c.; ‘with the hand,’<BR>समुद्धस्तः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=842-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wiper
WIPER, s. मार्जनी, मार्जनवस्त्रं, प्रक्षालनी, वरकं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=842-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wire
WIRE, s. तारः -रा, लोहतारा, लोहतन्तुः m., लोहसूत्रं, लोहतन्त्री, शलाका,<BR>धातुसूत्रं, तन्तुः m., सूत्रं, तन्त्री -न्त्रं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=842-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wiredraw
To WIREDRAW, v. a. लोहोद्वर्त्तनं कृ, लोहतारोद्वर्त्तनं कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=842-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wiry
WIRY, a. तन्तुमयः -यी -यं, तन्तुसगुणः -णा -णं, तन्तुप्रायः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=842-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wisdom
WISDOM, s. ज्ञानं, विज्ञानं, प्रज्ञा, बुद्धिः f., प्राज्ञता, विज्ञता, मेधा, वैदुष्यं,<BR>विद्वत्ता, पाण्डित्यं, मनीषा, मतिः f., विवेकः, हिताहितविवेकः, धीः f.;<BR>‘god of wisdom,’ गणेशः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=842-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wise
WISE, a. (Having wisdom) विद्वान् -दुषी -द्वत् (त्), ज्ञानी -निनी -नि<BR>(न्), ज्ञानवान् -वती -वत् (त्), प्राज्ञः -ज्ञा -ज्ञं, प्रज्ञः &c., बुद्धिमान्<BR>-मती &c., मतिमान् &c., धीमान् &c., प्रज्ञावान् &c., पण्डितः -ता -तं,<BR>विज्ञः -ज्ञा -ज्ञं, विवेकी -किनी &c., प्रज्ञी &c., मेधावी -विनी &c.,<BR>सविवेकः -का -कं, कोविदः -दा -दं, -सुधीः -धीः -धि, सुबोधः -धा -धं,<BR>कृतधीः &c., धीरः -रा -रं, विशेषज्ञः -ज्ञा -ज्ञं, कृत्यज्ञः &c., निपुण-<BR>दृक् m. f. n. (श्), प्रेक्षावान् &c., मर्म्मज्ञः &c.; ‘a wise man,’<BR>विद्वज्जनः, बुधः, see LEARNED.<BR>— (Dictated by wisdom) ज्ञान-<BR>प्रयुक्तः -क्ता -क्तं, बुद्धिप्रयुक्तः &c., ज्ञानमूलकः -का -कं, बुद्धिमूलकः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=842-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wise
WISE, s. See MANNER, WAY; ‘in no wise,’ न कथञ्चन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=842-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wiseacre
WISEACRE, s. पण्डितम्मन्यः, ज्ञम्मन्यः, अल्पबुद्धिः m.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=843-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wisely
WISELY, adv. विद्वज्जनवत्, प्राज्ञवत्, विज्ञवत्, सज्ञानं, सविवेकं, विवेक-<BR>पूर्व्वं, सम्यक्, सुष्ठु, युक्तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=843-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wish
To WISH, v. n. इष् (c. 6. इच्छति, एषितुं), अभिलष् (c. 1. -लषति -षितुं),<BR>वाञ्छ् (c. 1. वाञ्छति -ञ्छितुं), कांक्ष् (c. 1. कांक्षति -क्षितुं), आकांक्ष्,<BR>see To DESIRE. Often expressed by the desid. form of a<BR>root; as, ‘to wish to obtain,’ आप् in des. (ईप्सति -प्सितुं), लभ्<BR>in des. (लिप्सते -प्सितुं); ‘to wish to go,’ गम् in des. (जिगमि-<BR>षति -षितुं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=843-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wish
To WISH, v. a. (Well to one) इष्टं or मङ्गलम् or कल्याणम् आशंस्<BR>(c. 1. -शंसते -सितुं) or आशास् (c. 2. शास्ते -सितुं) or प्रार्थ्.<BR>— (Wish<BR>one ill) अनिष्टं or अमङ्गलम् आशंस् or प्रार्थ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=843-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wish
WISH, s. इच्छा, अभिलाषः, आकांक्षा, इष्टं, स्पृहा, मनोरथः, ईप्सितं, see<BR>DESIRE; ‘according to one's wish,’ यथाभिमतं; ‘earnest<BR>wish,’ कौतूहलं, कुतूहलं, see LONGING.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=843-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wished
WISHED, p. p. इष्टः -ष्टा -ष्टं, अभीष्टः -ष्टा -ष्टं. See DESIRED.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=843-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wishing
WISHING, part. or a. इच्छुः -च्छुः -च्छु, आकांक्षी &c. See DESIROUS.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=843-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wisp
WISP, s. (Of straw) शुष्कतृणकूर्च्चकः, शुष्कनालगुच्छकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=843-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wistfull
WISTFULL, WISTFULLY. See EARNEST, EAGER, EAGERLY.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=843-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wit
WIT, s. (Understanding) बुद्धिः f., मतिः f., धीः f.; ‘one who has<BR>lost his wits,’ नष्टबुद्धिः -द्धिः -द्धि.<BR>— (Quickness of fancy) बुद्धि-<BR>पाटवं, बुद्धिचातुर्य्यं, बुद्धिविलासः, बुद्धिकौशलं, बुद्धितीक्ष्णता, वैदग्ध्यं,<BR>विदग्धता.<BR>— (Humour) रसः, रसिकवाक्यं, रसिकोक्तिः f., नर्म्मोक्तिः f.,<BR>नर्म्म n. (न्), मर्म्म n.<BR>— (A wit, man of wit) रसज्ञः, नर्म्मज्ञः, नर्म्म-<BR>वेदी m. (न्), परिहासवेदी m., नर्म्मभापी m.<BR>— (To wit) वस्तुतस्, अर्थतस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=843-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

witch
WITCH, s. मायिनी, पूतना, डाकिनी. See SORCERESS.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=843-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

witchcraft
WITCHCRAFT, s. माया, अभिचारः, पूतनात्वं. See SORCERY.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=843-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

with
WITH, prep. (Denoting cause, means, instrument) usually<BR>expressed by the instrumental case; as, ‘with a sword,’<BR>खङ्गेन; ‘with grief,’ शोकेन.<BR>— (In opposition to, against)<BR>instr. c., with or without सह; as, ‘to fight with one's<BR>enemies,’ शत्रुभिः or शत्रुभिः सह युध् or expressed by उपरि or<BR>by the dat. or gen. c., in such phrases as, ‘he is angry<BR>with his son,’ पुत्रस्योपरि or पुत्राय or पुत्रस्य क्रुध्यति.<BR>— (In com-<BR>pany, together with, along with) सह, सार्द्धं, समं, साकं, सहितं,<BR>सत्रं -त्रा, अमा all with the instrum. c.: ‘along with me,’<BR>मया सह; ‘along with him,’ तेन सह. The preposition सम्,<BR>prefixed to roots, gives this sense of ‘with;’ as, ‘to live<BR>in company with,’ संवस्.<BR>— (Associated, attended^1, connected<BR>with) सहितः -ता -तं in comp. or expressed by the instr. c.,<BR>with or without सह, or by पूर्व्व or षुरःसर in comp.; as,<BR>‘associated with enemies,’ शत्रुसहितः -ता -तं or शत्रुभिः सहितः<BR>&c.<BR>— (Denoting manner) expressed by instr. c., or by स<BR>in comp. with the accus. n., or by पूर्व्वं or पूर्व्वकं or पुरःसरं<BR>affixed; as, ‘with anger,’ कोपेन, सकोपं, कोपपूर्व्वं, कोपपूर्व्वकं,<BR>कोपपुरःसरं; ‘with respect,’ सादरं; ‘with affection,’ प्रीतिपूर्व्वं.<BR>— (Among) मध्ये. To express a person with any thing<BR>in his possession, or a thing in connection with some-<BR>thing else, a compound adjective may often be used; thus,<BR>‘a man with a stick in his hand,’ दण्डहस्तः पुरुषः; ‘a man<BR>with riches,’ सधनः or धनवान् पुरुषः; a ship with two<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=843-b" target="_blank">Page843-b+ 51</a>]<BR>masts,’ द्विकूपका नौः or कूपकद्वययुक्ता नौः.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210422. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=843-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

withal
WITHAL, adv. समं, तथैव, अपिच, अपरञ्च. See LIKEWISE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=843-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

withdraw
To WITHDRAW, v. a. अपनी (c. 1. -नयति -नेतुं), विनी, व्यपनी, अप-<BR>कृष् (c. 1. -कर्षति -कर्ष्टुं), अपाकृष्, अपहृ (c. 1. -हरति -हर्त्तुं), व्यपहृ,<BR>उपसंहृ, प्रतिसंहृ, संहृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=843-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

withdraw
To WITHDRAW, v. n. अपक्रम् (c. 1. -क्रामति -क्रमितुं), अपसृ (c. 1. -सरति<BR>-सर्त्तुं), परावृत्, अवस्था, पलाय्, चल्. See To RETIRE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=843-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

withdrawal
WITHDRAWAL, s. (Taking back) अपनयः -यनं, अपहरणं, उपसंहारः<BR>-हरणं.<BR>— (Retiring) अपक्रमः, अपायः, see RETIREMENT.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=843-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

withdrawn
WITHDRAWN, p. p. अपनीतः -ता -तं, उपसंहृतः &c., परावृत्तः -त्ता -त्तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=843-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wither
To WITHER, v. n. विशॄ in pass. (-शीर्य्यते), म्लै (c. 1. म्लायति, म्लातुं),<BR>नश् (c. 4. नश्यति), सद्, क्षि. See To FADE, v. n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=843-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wither
To WITHER, v. a. नश् (c. 10. नाशयति -यितुं). See To FADE, v. a.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=843-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

withered
WITHERED, p. p. विशीर्णः -र्णा -र्णं, म्लानः -ना -नं, शुष्कः -ष्का -ष्कं,<BR>गतरसः -सा -सं, see FADED; ‘a withered leaf,’ जीर्णपर्णं; ‘hav-<BR>ing a withered arm or hand,’ विकलपाणिकः -का -कं, कुकरः<BR>-रा -रं, कुणिः m., कूणिः, कोणिः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=843-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

withers
WITHERS, s. (Of an elephant, &c.) स्कन्धदेशः, स्कन्धः, आसनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=843-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

withheld
WITHHELD, p. p. उपसंहृतः -ता -तं, प्रत्याहृतः &c., अपहृतः &c., विधृतः<BR>&c., विधारितः &c., निगृहीतः &c., उच्छिन्नः -न्ना -न्नं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=843-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

withhold
To WITHHOLD, v. a. उपसंहृ (c. 1. -हरति -हर्त्तुं), प्रत्याहृ, संहृ, विधृ<BR>(c. 10. -धारयति -यितुं), उच्छिद् (c. 7. -छिनत्ति -छेत्तुं), निग्रह्, विनिग्रह्,<BR>नियम्, निरुध्. See To RESTRAIN, RETAIN.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=843-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

within
WITHIN, prep. (In the inner part) अन्तर्, अभ्यन्तरे, अन्तरे; ‘within<BR>the house,’ गृहाभ्यन्तरे; ‘being within the house,’ गृहान्तर्वर्त्ती<BR>-र्त्तिनी &c., गृहान्तर्गतः -ता -तं, गृहान्तःस्थः -स्था -स्थं.<BR>— (Not later<BR>than) मध्ये, अर्वाक्, see UNDER; ‘within a year,’ संवत्सरमध्ये;<BR>‘within ten days,’ दशाहमध्ये.<BR>— (In the limits or compass<BR>of) गोचरः -रा -रं, विषय in comp., गम्य or ग्राह्य &c. in comp.;<BR>‘within hearing,’ कर्णगोचरः -रा -रं; ‘within sight,’ दृष्टि-<BR>गोचरः -रा -रं, दृग्गोचरः &c., दृष्टिगम्यः -म्या -म्यं, दृष्टिविषयः -या<BR>-यं; ‘within arrow-shot,’ वाणगोचरः -रा -रं; ‘within reach<BR>of the hand,’ हस्तग्राह्यः -ह्या -ह्यं, हस्तप्राप्यः &c., हस्तवर्त्ती -र्त्तिनी &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=843-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

within
WITHIN, adv. अन्तर्, अभ्यन्तरे, see INWARDLY; ‘gone within,’<BR>अन्तर्गतः -ता -तं; ‘being within,’ अन्तर्भवः -वा -वं, अन्तर्वर्त्ती &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=843-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

without
WITHOUT, prep. (Not with) विना with instr. or acc. c., ऋते with<BR>abl. or acc. c., अन्तरेण with abl. or acc. or gen., अन्तरा,<BR>व्यतिरेकेण in comp., व्यतिरिक्तं, पृथक्, अ prefixed; ‘without<BR>ornament,’ भूषणेन विना or भूषणं विना; ‘without feeling,’<BR>रसाद् ऋते; ‘without punishment,’ दण्डव्यतिरेकेण, दण्डमन्तरेण;<BR>‘without delay,’ अविलम्बेन; ‘without beginning or end,’<BR>अनाद्यन्तः -न्ता -न्तं; ‘without doubt,’ असंशयं; ‘without reason,’<BR>असम्भावनीयं; ‘without cause,’ प्रयोजनं विना, अकस्मात् or<BR>expressed by the loc. abs., असति प्रयोजने.<BR>— (Destitute of)<BR>हीनः -ना -नं, विहीनः &c., रहितः -ता -तं, विरहितः &c. or ex-<BR>pressed by अ, निर्, वि &c. prefixed; ‘without money,’<BR>धनहीनः -ना -नं, धनरहितः &c., अधनः -ना -नं, निर्धनः &c.; ‘how<BR>can I go without you?’ कथं त्वद्विहीनो यास्यामि.<BR>— (Unless,<BR>if not, except) यदि न, अन्तरेण with acc., or expressed by<BR>the indec. part. with अ or न prefixed; ‘without you do<BR>that,’ यदि न तत करोषि or तद् अकृत्वा; ‘without drinking<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=844-a" target="_blank">Page844-a+ 51</a>]<BR>any water,’ पानीयम् अपीत्वा; ‘it cannot be seen without<BR>a telescope,’ दूरदर्शकयन्त्रमन्तरेण न दृश्यते; ‘this cannot be<BR>ascertained without algebra,’ वीजगणितम् अन्तरेण न ज्ञायते<BR>तत्.<BR>— (On the outside of) वहिस्, वहिर्भागे, अन्तरेण; ‘without<BR>the fort,’ दुर्गवहिस्, दुर्गवहिर्भागे, दुर्गादन्तरेण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=843-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

without
WITHOUT, adv. (Not within) वहिस्, अवस्.<BR>— (Externally) वाह्यतस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=844-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

withstand
To WITHSTAND, v. a. पर्यवस्था (c. 1. -तिष्ठति -स्थातुं), प्रतिकूल (nom.<BR>प्रतिकूलयति -यितुं), विरुध्. See To RESIST, OPPOSE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=844-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

witness
WITNESS, s. (Testimony) साक्ष्यं, साक्षिता, प्रमाणं; ‘false witness,’<BR>कूटसाक्ष्यं, मिथ्यासाक्ष्यं, अतथ्यसाक्ष्यं.<BR>— (Person who gives tes-<BR>timony) साक्षी m. (न्), प्रमाता m. (तृ), साक्ष्यदाता m., साक्ष्यकारी m.;<BR>‘false witness,’ कूटसाक्षी m., कौटसाक्षी m., कूटकारः -रकः;<BR>‘having witnesses,’ साक्षिमान् -मती -मत् (त्); ‘proved by<BR>them,’ साक्षिभावितः -ता -तं; ‘absence of them,’ साक्ष्यभावः;<BR>‘examination of a witness,’ साक्षिपरीक्षा.<BR>— (One who is<BR>personally present) प्रत्यक्षदर्शी m., साक्षाद्द्रष्टा m., see EYE-WITNESS.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=844-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

witness
To WITNESS, v. a. (See by personal presence) प्रत्यक्षं or प्रत्यक्षतस्<BR>or स्वचक्षुषा दृश् (c. 1. पश्यति, द्रष्टुं), साक्षाद् दृश्, प्रत्यक्षदर्शनं कृ.<BR>—<BR>(Attest) साक्ष्यं दा, साक्ष्येण प्रमाणीकृ, see To ATTEST.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=844-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

witness
To WITNESS, v. n. साक्ष्यं दा, साक्ष्यं कृ, साक्षितां दा, साक्षी भू, प्रमाणीकृ,<BR>प्रमाणीभू. See To TESTIFY.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=844-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

witnessed
WITNESSED, p. p. (Seen in person) प्रत्यक्षदृष्टः -ष्टा -ष्टं, साक्षाद्दृष्टः<BR>&c., स्वचक्षुषा दृष्टः &c.<BR>— (Attested) प्रमाणीकृतः -ता -तं, साक्षिकः<BR>-की -कं, ससाक्षिकः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=844-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

witticism
WITTICISM, s. रसिकवाक्यं, रसिकोक्तिः f., सरसोक्तिः f., सरसवाक्यं, नर्म्मो-<BR>क्तिः f., नर्म्मभाषणं, विनोदवाक्यं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=844-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wittily
WITTILY, adv. सरसं, रसिकोक्त्या, बुद्धिविलासेन, नर्म्मोक्त्या.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=844-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wittingly
WITTINGLY, adv. ज्ञानतस्, बुद्धिपूर्व्वं, कामतस्. See KNOWINGLY.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=844-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

witty
WITTY, a. (Of persons) रसज्ञः -ज्ञा -ज्ञं, नर्म्मज्ञः &c., रसवेदी -दिनी<BR>-दि (न्), नर्म्मवेदी &c., नर्म्मभाषी -षिणी &c., नर्म्मवक्ता -क्त्री -क्तृ (क्तृ),<BR>विदूषकः -का -कं, विदग्धः -धा -धं.<BR>— (Of sayings, &c.) रसिकः<BR>-का -कं, सरसः -सा -सं, रसी -सिनी &c., रसवान् -वती -वत् (त्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=844-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wizard
WIZARD, s. अभिचारविद् m., मायाकारः. See MAGICIAN.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=844-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

woe
WOE, s. दुःखं, शोकः, दुर्गतिः f., see MISERY, SORROW, CALAMITY.<BR>—<BR>(Exclam.) हा, वत, धिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=844-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

woeful
WOEFUL, WOEFULLY, &c. See SORROWFUL, CALAMITOUS, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=844-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wolf
WOLF, s. वृकः, कोकः, अरण्यश्वा m. (न्), ईहामृगः, ईहावृकः, छागभो-<BR>जी m. (न्), जनाशनः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=844-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

woman
WOMAN, s. स्त्री, नारी, अङ्गना, वनिता, योषित् f., योषिता, योषा,<BR>जोषित f., जोषिता, जोषा, नरी, मानवी, महिला, अबला, मनुषी,<BR>मानुषी, कामिनी, वामा, विलासिनी, प्रमदा, मानिनी, वधूः f., महेला<BR>-लिका, महीला, ललना, ललिता, रमणी, रामा, प्रकृतिः f., सीम-<BR>न्तिनी, प्रतीपदर्शिनी, भरण्या, परिगृह्या; ‘a young woman,’ तरुणी,<BR>कन्या, बाला, युवती, यूनी, नवयौवना; ‘assembly of young<BR>women,’ यौवतं, यौवनं; ‘an old woman,’ वृद्धा, वृद्धस्त्री, जरती,<BR>पलिता, पलिक्नी; ‘a woman of good family,’ कुलस्त्री, कुल-<BR>नारी, कुलाङ्गना; ‘a beautiful woman,’ सुन्दरी, प्रमदा, कान्ता,<BR>सुभगा, नितम्बिनी, वामलोचना, ‘an excellent woman,’ वराङ्गना,<BR>वरारोहा, उत्तमा, वरवर्णिनी, मत्तकाशिनी, मत्तकासिनी, स्त्रीरत्नं;<BR>‘a passionate woman,’ कोपना, भामिनी; ‘virtuous woman,’<BR>सती, साध्वी, सुचरित्रा, कुलस्त्री, कुलपालिका; ‘clever woman,’<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=844-b" target="_blank">Page844-b+ 51</a>]<BR>सरखती; ‘woman who has borne a child,’ प्रमूता -तिका;<BR>‘married woman,’ सभर्त्तृका, सनाथा; ‘woman-killer,’ स्त्रीघा-<BR>तकः; ‘woman-hater,’ स्त्रीद्वेषी m. The Hindūs divide<BR>women into four classes, corresponding to the four classes<BR>of men. These are, 1. पद्मिनी, comprising the most ex-<BR>cellent women; 2. चित्रिणी or हरिणी or मृगी, comprising<BR>well-educated, accomplished, and beautiful women; 3. शङ्खि-<BR>नी, comprising women who are tall, neither stout nor<BR>thin, with long hair, irascible, and with strong passions;<BR>4. हस्तिनी, comprising women who are short, stout, with<BR>curly hair and furious passions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=844-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

woman-hood
WOMAN-HOOD, s. स्त्रीता, स्त्रीत्वं, नारीत्वं, स्त्रैणं, स्त्रीधर्म्मः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=844-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

womanish
WOMANISH, WOMANLY, a. स्त्रैणः -णी -णं. See FEMININE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=844-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

womankind
WOMANKIND, s. स्त्रीजातिः f., स्त्रीप्रकृतिः f., स्त्रीजनाः m. pl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=844-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

womb
WOMB, s. गर्भाशयः, गर्भस्थानं, योनिः m. f., योनी, गर्भकोशः, जरायुः m.,<BR>गर्भः, कोषः, उदरं, जठरः -रं, मातृकुक्षिः m., उल्वं, कललः -लं,<BR>चत्वालः, धरा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=844-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

won
WON, p. p. जितः -ता -तं, निर्जितः &c., उपार्जितः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=844-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wonder
WONDER, s. (The emotion) विस्मयः, आश्चर्य्यं -र्य्यत्वं, चमत्कारः, चित्रं,<BR>विचित्रकं.<BR>— (A wonder, cause of wonder) आश्चर्य्यं, अद्भुतं,<BR>अद्भुतवस्तु n., कौतुकं, चमत्कारः, चमत्कृतिः f., चित्रं, विचित्रता, see<BR>MARVEL; ‘a great wonder,’ महदाश्चर्य्यं; ‘wonder of the<BR>world,’ भुवनाद्भुतं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=844-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wonder
To WONDER, v. n. विस्मि (c. 1. -स्मयते -स्मेतुं), विम्मयापन्नः -न्ना -न्नं भू,<BR>विस्मितः -ता -तं भू, सविस्मयः -या -यं भू, विस्मयान्वितः -ता -तं भू,<BR>कुहुकुह (nom. कुहुकुहायते). See To MARVEL.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=844-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wonderful
WONDERFUL, WONDROUS, a. आश्चर्य्यः -र्य्या -र्य्यं, अद्भुतः -ता -तं, चित्रः<BR>-त्रा -त्रं, विचित्रकः &c., चित्री -त्रिणी &c., विस्मापकः &c. See<BR>MARVELLOUS.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=844-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wonder-struck
WONDER-STRUCK, a. विस्मितः -ता -तं, विस्मयाकुलः -ला -लं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=844-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wonder-working
WONDER-WORKING, a. आश्चर्य्यकर्म्मा -र्म्मा -र्म्म (न्), अद्भुतकर्म्मा &c.,<BR>चित्रकर्म्मा &c., विचित्रकर्म्मा &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=844-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wont
WONT, To BE WONT. See USED, HABITUATED, To USE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=844-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wonted
WONTED, a. आभ्यासिकः -की -कं, व्यावहारिकः &c. See CUSTOMARY.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=844-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

woo
To WOO, v. a. विवाहार्थं याच् (c. 1. याचति -चितुं) or प्रार्थ् (c. 10.<BR>-अर्थयति -ते -यितुं), विवाहार्थं आराध् or चित्ताराधनं कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=844-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wood
WOOD, s. (Forest) वनं, अरण्यं, विपिनं, काननं, see FOREST.<BR>—<BR>(Substance of trees, timber) काष्ठं, दारुः m. -रु n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=844-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wood-apple
