wronged
WRONGED, p. p. अपकृतः -ता -तं, प्राप्तापकारः -रा -रं, कृतापकारः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=847-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wrongful
WRONGFUL, WRONGFULLY. See UNJUST, UNJUSTLY.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=847-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wrong-headed
WRONG-HEADED, WRONG-HEADEDNESS. See PERVERSE, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=847-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wroth
WROTH, a. कोपाविष्टः -ष्टा -ष्टं, रोषाविष्टः &c. See ANGRY.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=847-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wrought
WROUGHT, p. p. (Done) कृतः -ता -तं, see PERFORMED.<BR>— (Worked,<BR>elaborated) संस्कृतः -ता -तं, संस्कारितः &c., कॢप्तः -प्ता -प्तं, कल्पितः<BR>&c., सिद्धः -द्धा -द्धं; ‘wrought iron,’ कुशी; ‘wrought gold.’<BR>कोषः, कृतहेमं.<BR>— (Stirred) उत्तेजितः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=847-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wry
WRY, a. वक्रः -क्रा -क्रं, विकृतः -ता -तं; ‘wry-faced,’ विकृताननः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=847-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wry-necked
WRY-NECKED, a. वक्रग्रीवः -वा -वं, विकृतग्रीवः &c., वक्रकन्धरः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=847-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

wryness
WRYNESS, s. वक्रता, वक्रिमा m. (न्), विकृतिः f., विरूपता, वैरूप्यं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=847-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

xantippe
XANTIPPE, s. कर्कशा, कैकेयी, वक्रशीला, दुर्मुखी, पूतना.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=847-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

xenodochy
XENODOCHY, s. अतिथिपूजनं, अतिथिसेवा, अतिथिसत्कारः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=847-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yacht
YACHT, s. क्रीडानौका, क्रीडानौः f., केलिनौका, केलिनौः f.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=847-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yam
YAM, s. आलुः -लु m. n., आलकं, मधुमूलं, मध्वालुकं, सुकन्दः, खण्ड-<BR>कालुः -लुकं, खण्डकर्णः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=847-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yama
YAMA, s. (God of Naraka or Hell, Regent of the South, or<BR>lower world, and judge of departed souls, corresponding<BR>to the grecian god Pluto, or to the judge of hell,<BR>Minos. His abode is in the infernal city of Yamapur,<BR>whither the Hindūs believe that a departed soul imme-<BR>diately repairs, and receiving a just sentence from Yama.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=848-a" target="_blank">Page848-a+ 52</a>]<BR>ascends to Swarga, the first heaven, or descends to Na-<BR>raka, the snaky hell, or assumes on earth the form of<BR>some animal, unless its offences have been such as<BR>deserve condemnation to a vegetable or even to a<BR>mineral prison. As god of justice and lord of punish-<BR>ment, Yama corresponds with Śiva and Varuna, and in<BR>this character is represented as bearing a cord or noose.<BR>Yama is often identified with Death and Time. He is<BR>the son of Surya or the Sun, and brother of the per-<BR>sonified Yamuna or Jumnā river) यमः, यमराजः, यमराट् m.<BR>(ज्), यमनः, शमनः.<BR>— (As Death or Time or the Destroyer)<BR>कृतान्तः, मृत्युः m., कालः, कालान्तकः, अन्तकः, कालकुण्ठः.<BR>— (Regent<BR>of the South) दक्षिणाशापतिः m.<BR>— (Lord of the dead) प्रेतप-<BR>तिः m., प्रेतराजः, परेतराट् m. (ज्), परेतराजः.<BR>— (Lord of deceased<BR>ancestors) पितृपतिः m.<BR>— (God of the śrāddha) श्राद्धदेवः, श्राद्ध-<BR>देवता.<BR>— (God of justice) धर्म्मराजः, धर्म्मः.<BR>— (The impartial<BR>judge) समवर्त्ती m.<BR>— (God of punishment) दण्डधरः, दण्डी m.<BR>(न्), दण्डयामः, अधिदण्डनेता m. (तृ), दण्डः.<BR>— (Bearer of the cord<BR>or noose) पाशी m. (न्), पाशभृत् m., पाशपाणिः m.<BR>— (Son of<BR>the sun) वैवस्वतः, सूर्य्यपुत्रः, सूर्य्यतनयः, अर्कतनयः, अर्कनन्दनः.<BR>—<BR>(Brother of Yamuna) यमुनाभ्राता m.<BR>— (The variegated one)<BR>चित्रः. The pain or punishment inflicted by Yama is<BR>called यातना. ‘One of his attendants,’ कालपुरुषः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=847-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yamuna
YAMUNĀ, s. (A river, commonly called Jumna, which rises<BR>on the south side of the Himālayas, and after a course<BR>of 378 miles, falls into the Ganges at Prayaga or Allaha-<BR>bad. The personified river is considered to be the<BR>daughter of Surya or the Sun, and sister of Yama) यमुना,<BR>सूर्य्यतनया, सूर्य्यपुत्री, अर्कतनया, यमस्वसा f. (सृ), शमनस्वसा f., कालिन्दी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=848-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yard
YARD, s. अङ्गनं, प्राङ्गणं, चत्वरं, अजिरं, see COURT-YARD.<BR>— (The<BR>measure) गजः.<BR>— (Of a ship) नौवसनकाष्ठं, नौवसनदण्डः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=848-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yarn
YARN, s. (Woollen thread) ऊर्णासूत्रं, और्णसूत्रं, और्णतन्तुः m., ऊर्णा-<BR>मयसूत्रं.<BR>— (Long yarn) दीर्घसूत्रं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=848-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yawn
To YAWN, v. n. जृम्भ् (c. 1. जृम्भते -म्भितुं), विजृम्भ्, प्रजृम्भ्, जभ or<BR>जम्भ् (c. 1. जभते, जम्भते -म्भितुं), जृम्भणं कृ, जृम्भं, कृ, विजृम्भणं कृ,<BR>ग्लै (c. 1. ग्लायति, ग्लातुं). See To GAPE.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=848-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yawn
YAWN, YAWNING, s. जृम्भः -म्भणं, जृम्भा -म्भिका, विजृम्भणं, जृम्भितं,<BR>विजृम्भितं, हाफिका, हर्म्म n. (न्), उपपुष्पिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=848-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yawner
YAWNER, s. जृम्भकः, जृम्भी m. (न्), विजृम्भकः, जृम्भणकारी m.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=848-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ye
YE, pron. यूयं (nom. pl. (युष्मद्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=848-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yea
YEA, adv. वाढं, आम्, सत्यं, हुम्, तथेति, अपरञ्च; ‘yea and nay,’<BR>स्वीकारास्वीकारौ m. du., स्वीकृतास्वीकृतं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=848-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

year
YEAR, s. वत्सरः, वर्षः, संवत्सरः, परिवत्सरः, अब्दः, समा, समाः m. (स्),<BR>संवद् ind., हायनः, वरिषं, कालग्रन्थिः m., ऋतुवृत्तिः f., सर्व्वर्त्तुपरिवर्त्तः,<BR>मासमानः, युगांशकः, शरद् f., शरदा; ‘half-year,’ वर्षार्द्धं, अब्दार्द्धं,<BR>षण्मासं, अयनं; ‘last year,’ गतवर्षः, परुत् indec.; ‘belonging<BR>to it,’ परुत्नः -त्नी -त्नं; ‘the present year,’ वर्त्तमानवर्षः, ऐषमस्;<BR>‘year before last,’ परारि indec.; ‘belonging to it,’ परा-<BR>रित्नः -त्नी -त्नं, ‘next year,’ परवर्षः, आगामिवत्सरः, उत्तरवत्सरः;<BR>‘events of the year,’ वर्षफलं; ‘throughout the year, to the<BR>end of it,’ आवर्षान्तात्; ‘for a year,’ वर्षपर्य्यन्तं; ‘year after<BR>year,’ वर्षे वर्षे, वत्सरे वत्सरे, प्रतिवत्सरं; ‘solar year,’ सौरवर्षः;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=848-b" target="_blank">Page848-b+ 52</a>]<BR>‘sidereal year,’ आर्क्षवर्षः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=848-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yearly
YEARLY, a. वार्षिकः -की -कं, प्रतिवार्षिकः &c., सांवत्सरिकः -की -कं,<BR>सांवत्सरः -री -रं, आब्दिकः -की -कं, प्रतिसांवत्सरिकः &c., वर्षैकः<BR>-का -कं, समीनः -ना -नं; ‘half-yearly,’ षाण्मासिकः -की -कं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=848-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yearly
YEARLY, adv. प्रतिवर्षं, प्रतिवत्सरं, प्रत्यब्दं, अनुवत्सरं, वत्सरे वत्सरे, वर्षे<BR>वर्षे, अयने अयने.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=848-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yearn
To YEARN, v. n. वत्सल (nom. वत्सलायते), वात्सल्यं सूच् (c. 10. सूच-<BR>यति -यितुं), वत्सकामा भू, वत्सलीभू, स्निह् (c. 4. स्निह्यति, स्नेहितुं),<BR>उत्सुक (nom. उत्सुकायते).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=848-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yearning
YEARNING, s. वत्सलता, वात्सल्यं, उत्सुकता, औत्सुक्यं, स्नेहः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=848-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yeast
YEAST, s. सुरामण्डः, मद्यमण्डः, यवमण्डः, कारोत्तमः, कारोत्तरः, किण्वः<BR>-ण्वं, नग्नहूः -हु m. n., अभिपवः, कादम्बरीवीजं, सुराभागः. In some<BR>parts of India ताडी or ताली, i. e. toddy or the fermented<BR>juice of the tāḍ or palm tree is much used as yeast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=848-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yell
To YELL, v. n. रु (c. 2. रौति, रवितुं), रस्, नद्. See To SCREAM.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=848-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yell
YELL, s. रुतं, रावः, दीर्घरुतं, दीर्घरावः, चित्कारः. See SCREAM.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=848-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yelling
YELLING, part. दीर्घरावः -वी -वं, दीर्घनादी -दिनी -दि (न्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=848-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yellow
YELLOW, a. पीतः -ता -तं, गौरः -री -रं, पीतलः -ला -लं, हरिद्राभः<BR>-भा -भं, पीतवर्णः -र्णा -र्णं, गौरवर्णः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=848-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yellow-bird
YELLOW-BIRD, YELLOW-HAMMER, s. हरिद्राङ्गः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=848-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yellowish
YELLOWISH, a. ईषत्पीतः -ता -तं, ईषत्पीतवर्णः -र्णा -र्णं; ‘yellowish<BR>white,’ हरिणः -णा -णं, पाण्डुः -ण्डुः -ण्डु, पाण्डुरः -रा -रं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=848-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yellowness
YELLOWNESS, s. पीतता, गौरता -त्वं, पीतवर्णः, हरिद्रावर्णः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=848-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yelp
To YELP, v. a. भष्, रै, रु, रस्. See To BARK, YELL.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=848-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yeoman
YEOMAN, s. गृहस्थः, गृहाधिकारी m. (न्), क्षेत्रपतिः m.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=848-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yes
YES, adv. वाढं, आम्, हूम्, सत्यं, तथेति, परमं, एवं, ओम्, अथकिं, स्वीकृतं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=848-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yester
YESTER, a. ह्यस्तनः -नी -नं, ह्यस्त्यः -स्त्या -स्त्यं, पर्युपितः -ता -तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=848-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yesterday
YESTERDAY, s. ह्यस्, पृर्व्वेद्युस्, गतदिवसः, गतदिनं, कल्पं; ‘relating<BR>to yesterday,’ ह्यस्तनः -नी -नं, ह्यस्त्यः -स्त्या -स्त्यं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=848-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yesternight
YESTERNIGHT, s. गतरात्रिः f., गता रात्रिः, गता यामिनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=848-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yet
YET, conj. तथापि, परन्तु, अपि, किन्तु. See NEVERTHELESS.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=848-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yet
YET, adv. (Over and above) अधिकं, परं.<BR>— (Hitherto) अद्य यावत्,<BR>अद्यपर्य्यन्तं, अद्यापि, see HITHERTO, STILL.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=848-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yield
To YIELD, v. a. (Produce, bear) उत्पद् (c. 10. -पादयति -यितुं), जन्<BR>(c. 10. जनयति -यितुं), दा (c. 3. ददाति, दातुं), प्रदा; ‘fruit,’ फलं<BR>दा or प्रदा, फल्.<BR>— (Give, grant, concede) अनुदा, प्रदा, दा,<BR>वितॄ (c. 1. -तरति -रितुं -रीतुं), अनुज्ञा, प्रोत्सृ in caus., see To CON-<BR>CEDE.<BR>— (Deliver up, surrender) उत्सृज् (c. 6. -सृजति -स्रष्टुं),<BR>विसृज्, अवसृज्, त्यज् (c. 1. त्यजति, त्यक्तुं), हा, विहा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=848-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yield
To YIELD, v. n. वशीभू, वशं गम् or उपगम्. See To SUBMIT.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=848-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yielding
YIELDING, a. (Bearing fruit) फलदः -दा -दं, फलप्रदः &c., फलवान्<BR>-वती -वत् (त्), फलन् -लन्ती &c., फलोत्पादकः -का -कं.<BR>— (Com-<BR>pliant) अनुकूलः -ला -लं, अनुरोधी -धिनी &c., see COMPLIANT.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=848-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yojana
YOJANA, s. (A measure of distance, equal to five miles, or,<BR>according to some, to nine miles) योजनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=848-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yoke
YOKE, s. (For the necks of oxen) युगः -गं, प्रासङ्गः, आबद्धः; ‘of<BR>a plough,’ कुशः; ‘pin of the yoke,’ युगकीलः -लकः; ‘tie<BR>of it,’ योक्त्रं, योत्रं, आबन्धः.<BR>— (Yoke or pair of oxen) गोयुगं,<BR>गोमिथुनं.<BR>— (Fit for the yoke) युग्यः -ग्या -ग्यं, प्रासङ्ग्यः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=848-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yoke
To YOKE, v. a. युज् (c. 7. युनक्ति, c. 10. योजयति -यितुं), नियुज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=848-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yoked
YOKED, p. p. युक्तः -क्ता -क्तं, नियुक्तः &c., संसक्तयुगः -गा -गं; ‘is<BR>yoked,’ युज्यते; ‘a yoked animal,’ युग्यः, प्रासङ्ग्यः, शाकटः;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=849-a" target="_blank">Page849-a+ 50</a>]<BR>‘having yoked the steeds,’ युक्ततुरङ्गः -ङ्गा -ङ्गं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=848-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yoke-fellow
YOKE-FELLOW, s. सहचरः, सहवर्त्ती m. (न्), सहभावी m.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=849-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yolk
YOLK, s. (Of an egg) अण्डमध्यं, अण्डमध्यभागः, अण्डहृदयं, अण्डकुसमं,<BR>अण्डमध्यस्थः पीतभागः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=849-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yon
YON, YONDER, a. नातिदूरस्थः -स्था -स्थं, ईषद्दूरस्थः -स्था -स्थं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=849-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yon
YON, YONDER, adv. नातिदूरे -रतस्, ईषद्दूरे -रतस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=849-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yore
YORE, adv. (Of yore) पुरा, प्राक्काले, प्राक्, पुरस्तात्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=849-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

you
YOU, pron. (For thou, in the sing.) त्वं nom. sing.<BR>— (In the<BR>plur.) यूयं nom. pl. (युष्मद्); ‘of you,’ युष्माकं; ‘you two,’<BR>युवां. The honorific pron. भवान् m. (त्), is often used for<BR>‘you,’ with the 3d pers. sing. of the verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=849-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

young
YOUNG, a. बालः -ला -लं, युवा m., युवतिः -ती f., यूनी f., युव n. (न्),<BR>तरुणः -णा -णं, अल्पवयाः -याः -यः (स्), अल्पवयस्कः -स्का -स्कं, अभि-<BR>नववयस्कः &c., बालिशः -शा -शं, कौमारः -री -रं, किशोरः -रा -रं, अभि-<BR>नवः -वा -वं, प्रतिनवः &c., वयस्थः -स्था -स्थं, वयःस्थः &c.; ‘a young<BR>man,’ कुमारः, युवजनः, बालजनः, तरुणः, रूढवयाः m. (स्); ‘young<BR>woman,’ तरुणी, कुमारी, कन्या, युवती, बाला, नवयौवना; ‘a young<BR>bird,’ see YOUNG, s.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=849-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

young
YOUNG, s. (Young one of any animal) शावकः, शिशुः m., पोतः<BR>-तकः, अपत्यं, पाकः -का, अर्भकः, डिम्भः, पृथुकः, प्रथुकः, वर्करः -री,<BR>कुणकः; ‘a young bird,’ पक्षिशावकः; ‘a young mouse,’ मूषि-<BR>कशावकः; ‘a young elephant,’ गजशिशुः m.; ‘a young deer,’<BR>मृगपोतकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=849-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

younger
YOUNGER, a. कनीयान् -यसी -यः (स्), कनिष्ठः -ष्ठा -ष्ठं, यवीयान् &c.,<BR>यविष्ठः &c., अनुजः -जा -जं, अनुजातः -ता -तं, अनुजन्मा -न्मा -न्म (न्),<BR>जघन्यजः -जा -जं, अवरजः &c., अवरवयस्कः -स्का -स्कं, अवरः -रा -रं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=849-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

youngster
YOUNGSTER, s. कुमारकः, बालजनः, किशोरः, वटुः. See LAD.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=849-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

your
YOUR, YOUR'S, pron. तव gen. sing., युष्माकं gen. pl. (युष्मद्),<BR>भवतः gen. sing., भवतां gen. pl. (भवत्), त्वदीयः -या -यं, भवदीयः<BR>&c., भावत्कः -त्का -त्कं, यौष्माकः -की -कं, यौष्माकीनः -ना -नं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=849-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

yourself
YOURSELF, pron. (Reciprocally) आत्मा m. (न्); as, ‘blame<BR>yourself,’ आत्मानं निन्द; ‘for yourself,’ आत्मार्थं.<BR>— (Emphati-<BR>cally) स्वयं, स्वतस्; ‘you yourself,’ स त्वं, see SELF.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=849-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

youth
YOUTH, s. (Early part of life) यौवनं, यौवनावस्था, यौवनकालः,<BR>यौवनदशा, कौमारं, तारुण्यं, तारुण्यदशा, तारुण्यकालः, सौकुमार्य्यं,<BR>शैशवं, प्रथमवयस् n., पूर्व्ववयस् n., प्रत्यग्रवयस् n., कैशोरं; ‘prime<BR>or heyday of youth,’ नवयौवनं, यौवनप्रौढिः f.; ‘pride of<BR>youth,’ यौवनदर्पः.<BR>— (A young man) तरुणः, कुमारः -रकः, युव-<BR>जनः, युवा m. (न्), बालजनः, अबालः, किशोरः, वटुः m., वटुकः,<BR>वेकटः.<BR>— (Young persons) तरुणजनाः m. pl., युवजनाः m. pl.,<BR>बालजनता.<BR>— (State of being young) तारुण्यं, बालत्वं -ता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=849-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

youthful
YOUTHFUL, a. यौवनवान् -वती -वत् (त्), बालः -ला -लं, यौवनेयकः<BR>-की -कं, अल्पवयाः -याः -यः (स्). See YOUNG.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=849-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

youthfulness
YOUTHFULNESS, s. तारुण्यं, बालता -त्वं, सौकुमार्य्यं, बालिश्यं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=849-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

zany
ZANY, s. भण्डः, वैहासिकः, विदूषकः. See BUFFOON.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=849-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

zeal
ZEAL, s. उत्तापः, चण्डता, उच्चण्डता, उष्णता, उष्मः, तैक्ष्ण्यं, तीक्ष्णता,<BR>व्यग्रता, उद्योगः, अत्युद्योगः, प्रौढिः f., औत्सुक्यं, अत्यनुरागः, अत्यनुरक्तिः f.,<BR>अत्युत्कण्ठा, उत्सुकता, आस्था. See EARNESTNESS.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=849-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

zealot
ZEALOT, s. अत्यनुरक्तः, अतिव्यग्रः, अत्यासक्तः, अतितीक्ष्णः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=849-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

zealous
ZEALOUS, a. व्यग्रः -ग्रा -ग्रं, अतिव्यग्रः &c., उत्तप्तः -प्ता -प्तं, चण्डः -ण्डा<BR>-ण्डं, उच्चण्डः &c., तीक्ष्णः -क्ष्णा -क्ष्णं, अत्यनुरक्तः -क्ता -क्तं, अत्यनुरागी<BR>-गिणी -गि (न्), अत्युत्सुकः -का -कं, उत्सुकः &c., अत्युद्योगी -गिनी<BR>&c., उद्योगी &c., उद्युक्तः -क्ता -क्तं, इष्टार्थोद्युक्तः &c., समुद्यतः -ता -तं,<BR>अत्युद्यमी &c., अत्यासक्तः -क्ता -क्तं, उष्णः -ष्णा -ष्णं, तीक्ष्णकर्म्मा -र्म्मा<BR>-र्म्म (न्), प्रयत्नवान् -वती -वत् (त्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=849-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

zealously
ZEALOUSLY, adv. अतिव्यग्रं, अत्युद्योगेन, अत्यनुरागेण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=849-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

zebra
ZEBRA, s. वनगर्दभः, अरण्यगर्दभः, वनरासभः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=849-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

zedoary
ZEDOARY, s. (A plant) सटिः -टी f., कर्चूरकः, कर्बूरकः, वेधमुख्यकः,<BR>द्राविडकः, काल्पः -ल्पकः, सुम्पलुण्ठः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=849-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

zenith
ZENITH, s. खमध्यं, ऊर्द्ध्वस्वस्तिकः -कं, ऊर्द्ध्वदिशा, खस्वस्तिकं, शिरोविन्दुः m.,<BR>ऊर्द्ध्वः; ‘zenith distance,’ नतं, नतांशः, नतभागः; ‘pointing to<BR>zenith and nadir,’ ऊर्द्ध्वाधरः -रा -रं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=849-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

zephyr
ZEPHYR, s. वसन्तवायुः m., मन्दवायुः m., मन्दानिलः, मृदुवातः, सुखस्पर्श-<BR>वायुः m., सुगन्धवायुः m., चारवायुः m., मन्दमारुतः, वासन्तः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=849-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

zero
ZERO, s. (Cipher, naught) शून्यं, विन्दुः, वटः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=849-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

zest
ZEST, s. रुचिः f., स्वादः, आस्वादः, अभिरुचिः f. See RELISH.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=849-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

zigzag
ZIGZAG, a. वक्रः -क्रा -क्रं, कुटिलः -ला -लं, जिह्मः -ह्मा -ह्मं, वक्राकारः<BR>-रा -रं, कुटिलगतिः -तिः -ति, घुणाक्षरः -रा -रं; ‘zig-zag lightning,’<BR>विद्युल्लता, असिलता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=849-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

zinc
ZINC, s. (Kind of metal) वङ्गं, दस्ता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=849-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

zodiac
ZODIAC, s. राशिचक्रं, ज्योतिश्चक्रं, राशिमण्डलं, भचक्रं, भमण्डलं, भागनं,<BR>रिम्फं; ‘a sign of the zodiac,’ राशिः m., लग्नं, भं; ‘the<BR>twelve signs collectively,’ राशिगणः, भगणः, राशिकुण्डली, मेष-<BR>वृषादयः m. pl. These are, 1. Aries, मेषः; 2. Taurus, वृषः,<BR>वृषभः; 3. Gemini, मिथुनः, द्वन्द्वः, जित्तमः; 4. Cancer, कर्कटः,<BR>कर्कः, कर्कटराशिः m.; 5. Leo, सिंहः, आरण्यराशिः m.; 6. Virgo,<BR>कन्या; 7. Libra, तुला, तुलाधारः, धटः; 8. Scorpio, वृश्चिकः,<BR>कौर्प्यः, अलिः m.; 9. Sagittarius, धनुः -नु m. n., तौक्षिकः;<BR>10. Capricornus, मकरः, मकरराशिः m.; 11. Aquarius, कुम्भः,<BR>कुम्भराशिः m.; 12. Pisces, मीनः, मीनराशिः m., मीनलग्नं, झषः.<BR>Of the twelve signs there are two divisions, one called<BR>उत्तरगोलः, consisting of the six signs, from Aries to Virgo,<BR>the other called दक्षिणगोलः, comprising the remaining six<BR>signs. ‘The rising of a sign,’ लग्नं, उदयः; ‘setting,’ अस्तं;<BR>‘rising sign,’ उदयलग्नं; ‘setting sign,’ अस्तलग्नं; ‘circuit<BR>of the sun through the zodiac,’ भागनं, भगणः; ‘passage of<BR>the sun through a sign,’ सूर्य्यसङ्क्रान्तिः f., रविसङ्क्रान्तिः f., सूर्य्य-<BR>सङ्क्रमणं; ‘of a planet,’ राशिभोगः; ‘passage of the sun or<BR>a planet from one sign into another,’ सङ्क्रान्तिः f., सङ्क्रमः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=849-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

zodiacal
ZODIACAL, a. राशिचक्रसम्बन्धी -न्धिनी &c., भचक्रसम्बन्धी &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=849-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

zone
ZONE, s. (Girdle) मेखला, रसना, कलापः, see GIRDLE.<BR>— (Of the<BR>earth) भूमेखला, भूवलयः -यं, भूकटिबन्धः; ‘torrid zone,’ क्रान्ति-<BR>वलयः, मध्यदेशः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=849-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

zoographer
