age
AGE, s. (Of the world) युगं; ‘beginning of an age,’ युगादिः m.;<BR>‘end of one,’ युगान्तः. The four ages of the Hindūs, cor-<BR>responding in some degree with the golden age, silver<BR>age, brazen age, and iron age, are, 1. कृतं or सत्यं, 2. त्रेता,<BR>3. द्वापरः, 4. कलिः m.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=851-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

