balarama
BALARĀMA. This god is not often regarded as an avatār of<BR>Viṣṇu, but rather as an incarnation of the great ser-<BR>pent Ananta; hence he is sometimes called शेषः or अनन्तः.<BR>He was the son of Vasudeva by Devakī, but was trans-<BR>ferred from the latter to the womb of Rohiṇī, the other<BR>wife of Vasudeva, and hence his name, सङ्कर्षणः. Other<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=853-a" target="_blank">Page853-a+ 51</a>]<BR>names for him are<BR>— (Fond of wine) प्रियमधुः m.<BR>— (Killer<BR>of the boxer Muṣṭika) मुष्टिकान्तकः.<BR>— (Secret in motion)<BR>गुप्तचरः.<BR>— (Strong and good) बलभद्रः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=852-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ballet
BALLET, s. हल्लीषं -षकं. BALUSTRADE, s. प्रग्रीवः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=853-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

