humour
HUMOUR, s. The three humours of the body are, 1. ‘phlegm,’<BR>कफः; 2. ‘bile,’ पित्तं; 3. ‘air or wind,’ वायुः m., वातः; ‘dis-<BR>order of any h.,’ धातुनाशः; ‘vitiation of three h.,’ त्रिदोषं,<BR>सन्निपातः; ‘excess of any of the three h.,’ प्रकोपः, उल्वणं;<BR>‘disorder resulting from vitiation of the phlegm,’ कफ-<BR>विकारः, कफरोगः; ‘of the bile,’ पित्तविकारः; ‘of the wind,’<BR>वातविकारः, वायुविकारः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MWE&page=858-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=mwe" target="_blank">Correction</a>

